package com.darkshamanism.lotcscholar.services

@Suppress("LongMethod", "MagicNumber")
internal object StaticBooksData_ATHERA {

    private fun _ATHERA_0(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("!!!!!!!!!!!", "The Story Teller", "!!!!!!!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("!!Attention!!", "Tarien Arvius", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon IV - A Warning\nTo the Spellcrafter Archon,\nI hope this message reaches you in time. We were deceived, the Seal was a false lead, the Radiant Man, or as he is truly called, the aengul Garzardiel, had\nhis own agenda all along, and Rivel faces imminent attack and possibly annihilation.\nMost of the Spellcrafters in the task force are fully under Garzardiel’s sway, mere puppets to his will. I have broken free of his influence and escaped but in\nturn have lost both my powers from him and my skill with the Arcane. I fear how many of my decisions in the past months have been acts based not on my own judgement but on his influence!\nWhen we opened the Hall we found it littered with\nskeletal corpses: the Forgotten Dwarves were wiped out by a civil war: the ruling caste trying in desperation to give the Seal enough fuel to defeat the Ravager, and the people fighting back. It seems too that the ruling caste won the war and the death\nsimply fueled the Seal further. The city was also filled with hundreds of war constructs designed for raiding the surface for harvesting more souls: I suppose when you’ve enacted a near total genocide on your own people in the name of\nsurvival the deaths of a few hundred surface dwellers aren’t going to bother you. It seems these constructs wiped out the surviving Forgotten Dwarves.\nAs for the Seal, the machine itself is complete, but damaged: we\nsuspect the damage allowed vengeful souls to leak out and possess the constructs, wiping out the surviving dwarves. Garzardiel revealed that the goal of the Forgotten Dwarves was impossible: the Seal could never hold enough souls to\ntrap the Ravager, which begs the question, whatever does he want it for?\nOnce he had access to the Seal Garzardiel took control of the constructs and ordered the elimination of all loose ends, all who knew about the Seal.\nThat means the Spellcrafters of our company that were not fully under his sway and Rivel itself. I attempted to conceal myself, but without my arcane powers it was most difficult. The last I saw of Garzardiel was him headed to the Seal Chamber\nitself, a writhing mongoose held by the neck in his grip. After that I was forced to flee the city, and as I left I realised the direness of our situation.\nThe majority of soul harvesting constructs left for Rivel hours ago: I know not how long\nyou have to formulate a defence against their oncoming assault on the walls.\nI will find the keys and reseal this Hall. My last act will be to return the keys to their hiding places. I don’t know what Garzardiel really wanted to trap in\nthat machine, but Urguan’s Hall must never again be found.\n- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius\n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"A Time Before\"", "Maehr'Celia", "This book has been written by Maehr'Celia, by Memory once again.\n Before time itself there was darkness, a evil like no other capable of destorying any life that may have formed. But for every evil there is good, a light appeared in the darkness, a good capible of creating any life. The two opposite forces battled for \nwhat have been in our time, milleniums. But the light pulled through against the darkness and arose the first life, Time. Time is a life unkown to many, thought to be nothing, but it was Time that created all of what we know today. Time was only one \ncreature, the only living thing in our world, but Time grew weary and grew more lonely so it created us. Every living thing in our world was created by Time. Time controled everything, it controled our lives, it allows to live in its world for a period of\ntime in exchange for on thing, our will to overcome the temptation of the darkness, so the world shall remain in peace. But like all good things, it will eventually come to an end. Watching Time created all this peace and happiness, The Darkness grew sick\nof it. It grew jealous of Time. So The Darkness created something to tempt us to join him, it created sin. The Darkness too form of one of us and tried to tempt us with sin, but we all refused, until one child met it. The Darkness told the child that he \nhave more then this world of peace, he could have the power to control it, so the boy accepted the temptation of sin and became the first evil, The Void. The Darkness named this bou levithan. Levithan tempted others to sin and to join the Void, those who \ndid join became the first beasts, the slaves of the Void. No one could tell who joined the Darkness because those who did appeared to be so normal, except for one small thing, there eyes where a pure white. The Void spread Terror through out this peaceful\nworld for years. Until Time caught up with them.\n-----\n Time soon discoverd the Void and spent years trying to find a way to fight them, until he soon decieded to create his own warriors, the Hope, few us joined with the idea that if they joined him the \nworld would be at peace once more. That was all that Time promised, and so few joined. The Hope was described to wear a pure white robe with blue lines around the neck, arms, and feet. After the Hopes creation, the first war begin, the war for peace.\n Hundreds, upon hundreds of years of fighting took place. The Hope fought as best they could, but they were nearly destoryed. Just as soon as the Void declared its victory, the people stood up, fought back the Void, wiping it out from this world. The \nDarkness retreate to a different world, leaving this one to Time. But Time went after the Darkness, leaving the Hope to protect the land from any new evil that may arise, but they slowly diminished and disappeared in Aegis, leaving the people vaunible. \nSoon a new evil arose, led by one they called Iblees. Iblees tried to conquer the ways of the Void, raising the beast of the dead, but he had much he did not learn. Soon the sages came to fight Iblees, using the ancient ways of the Hope, but they to had\nmuch they did not learn. As they fought and time went by, the Darkness grew stonger and soon will return to our world with the stongest evil ever known, the Void. But it is said that when the Void returns, so shall the Hope, lead by Time himself, to fight\nthe Void once more, But the propechy of the tomes leaves one mystery, which shall win, Good of Evil?\n*sign*\n -Maehr'Celia \n  Follower of Time ", ""),
        StaticBook("\"A Winters Night", "Clan Elder Legate Fili Grandaxe", "It was a cold night, in the dead of winter. The wind was howling like a wolf outside my window, as a blizzard blown down from the north settled in around my small house.\nI sat awake, huddled near the crackling fire, bundled under my pelts, packed closely, as they buried me like a tomb. Despite my care, and precautions to keep warm, the cold cut into me like a knife.\nI sat blankly, staring into the depths of the flames, contemplating whether or not this would be my last Winter.Then I heard a commotion at my door, followed by a thud, then silence.\nShocked by fear, and surprise, I remained seated, unable to move. Slowly as I regained my composure, I reached for my waraxe, sitting at my feet, displacing my carefully arranged cocoon of blankets.\n I do not know how long I waited, petrified with fear at what may be outside my door. My imagination went rampant, as I began to think of all the horrors, and atrocities that may lay outside my door,\nwaiting to pounce on me, and bring a swift end to my suffering on this freezing night.\nAfter a while though, when the fire had begun to die down, almost to cinders, I mustered up enough courage to arise from my seat. The blankets slid off my body down to the hard, unforgiving floor,\nthe warmth they once held, now being sucked away by the hungry planks. I stepped over the pile, and made my way a few steps into the open room before my doorway.\n\nJust after my third, agonizing step, I fell upon a loose board, and the creaking noise that emitted from it almost sent my heart jumping through my mouth.\n“It is only a board” I told myself, breathing heavily “Nothing to be afraid of” I took another step onwards, closing in on my destination, waraxe in hand to fend off whatever evil lay on my doorstep.\nI took another step forward, and my heart began to beat faster. The crackling sound of my dying fire began to get blotted out by the thump, thump, thumping of my own heart. I took yet another step forward.\nAt my door now, I slowly reached for the door knob, extending my left hand, holding my waraxe high in my right.\n\nI groped for the door handle, opening my sweaty palm. I was shaking like a leaf by the time my hand closed around the copper handle. Taking a few ragged breaths before my imminent doom, I closed my eyes and tried to calm myself.\nI began to slowly, ever so slowly twist that wretched knob. I heard a click as the tumblers on the door unlocked themselves.\n\nThe few moments before I opened up the door were filled with fear, and a type of frightful curiosity. I slowly drew open the door. \nThe creaking racket that it made as the hinges slowly began to loosen their frozen grip on the door sent shivers down my spine.\nI couldn't take the anxiety of it all, and in my panic, I threw open the door, sending it crashing into the wall it was attached to, \n and raised my waraxe high, sucked in last gulp of breath and got ready to scream at the top of my lungs.\n\n\nThen, I released a ragged sigh of reprieve as I looked around at the fresh fallen snow on my doorstep. Just snow, nothing else.\nI returned to my chair, and recovered myself with my pelts, and stared into the depths of the embers at the bottom of my hearth left from my fire. I slowly began to snooze,\nand slept with half an eye open that night, jumping into alertness at every creak and shudder my home made. Until I was blessed by the long streaks of the dawning sun, enchanting my small abode in a golden light.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Juicy\" - Poetic", "Immortal Cole", "You know very well who you are, \n\nDont let 'em hold you down. Reach for the stars. \n\nYou have a goal,\nbut not that many.\n\nCause you're the only one, \n\nI'll give you good-\n-and plenty.\n\nI made the change from a common thief\n\nTo up and close with the eldest elf. \n\nThinking back on my one-room shack.\n\nI still have that old hat -\n-With the fat red and black lumberjack, all to match.\n\nNo heat, no wonder nights were cold. \n\nBut I did not give up and I grabbed ahold.\n\n-Cole", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Lennox\"", "Alexandria Fireblade", "[!]A Picture Of A Young Boy, Around The Age Of 16. Standing In A Forest, The Boy Is Smiling, A Girl With Long Brown Hair, And Purple Eye's A Tad Younger Then The Boy Holds His Hand, She's Looking Up To Him, A Name Is Written At The Bottom\n\"Lennox\"\n[!]A Picture Of The Same Boy, This Time He's Shirtless And Holding A Axe, A Pile Of Wood Nearby He Appears To Be Cutting Firewood. His Hair Is Slightly Covering His Face, His Blue Eyes Shining In The Sunlight.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Ondnarch", "Hellio Brasspick", "\"The Fall of Wyrvun\"\n\nLong ago, in ancient times when the world was young and pure, the first snows of the Deep Cold arrived. At first, the mortal races who lived beneath them marvelled at their beauty but as years passed,\nthe cold would not release its icy grip and it held tight as many would perish. The ground froze and crops would no longer grow, as warmth and firewood became ever scarcer. Soon enough,\nthe creator looked upon the world with pity as he saw the suffering of his people. Though without the heart to destroy such a beautiful creation, it was something with the power to destroy all life and thus needed to be controlled.\nt was then that Wyrvun was created, the very embodiment of the ice cold winds and the frost that settled upon the ground. For he was the Lord of the Deep Cold and the elements of his realm each answered to his call.\nAn Aengul of great power,\nat his command were all that made up the realm of ice. Such was his power that he could even contest many of the creator’s divine beings. His love for all that was of the Deep Cold was strong,, and it pained him deeply that the mortal races of the world \ndreaded for it to begin and would soon celebrate its end.\n\nThere then came a day when a darkness fell over the world, and even the realm of Wyrvun was not untouched. It was here that a shadow encompassed Wyrvun's domain, \nand darkness slowly crept upon the frozen north. As the shade grew ever closer to his dwelling, the ice seemed to turn into a deep black, and swallow what light was left. Wyrvun could only gaze upon this darkness and in doing so,\nelt the corruption of the world in which he lived. The ice which light had once danced upon, became dark, twisted and corrupt, a shadow of its former self. Though the fear would not control him,, the voices in his mind started to murmur, \nas they tore at his very being from within.\n\n\"Would an eternal cold not be beautiful? The mortals wish you gone, and yet you care for them! Why should you, Wyrvun, Lord of the Deep Cold, not spread your realm and consume the world?\"\nAs the words were uttered, Wyrvun seemed to fall into a dazed state and for the first time in his existence, he felt an ever consuming fear. It was not in his creation to be either weak, nor foolish and in his fury, the world shook.\nThe mountains responded, and a blizzard which was by far unmatched by any other, crept down from the north, destroying all in its path. As it approached, a gigantic being in the form of a dragon emerged from within, larger than any mountain stood.\nIts form could bend light and surrounding it, a blue glow was cast. As it let out an almighty roar, the temperature dropped and the air seemed to freeze. Wyrvun was bound to no form, but commanded all in the realm of ice.\n\nIn spite of this, the shade stood in the shadow of the dragon, and from it, arose a sinister laugh. Darkness and flame begun to envelope the ground at Wyrvun’s feet and so he raised his wings and flew high above the mountaintops,\nhis presence blocking out the rays of the sun and casting a pulsating blue light upon the north. Though in all his might, Wyrvun was no match for the Lord of Darkness. Something grabbed a hold of his leg and dragged him down into the black abyss below,\nwhere no light shone and only darkness prevailed.\n\nThere he was bound by shadow and fire, and a last roar of defiance escaped him as the once so pure, mighty and beautiful Wyrvun was dragged far beneath the ground \ninto a prison of the darkest magic. What evils happened down there are known to none other than he,  \nfor what came was an abomination of his former self. All that arose from the abyss\nwas a twisted and corrupt being.\nThe Lord of the Deep Cold who once had been so beautiful and pure was now dark and terrible.\n\n\n\"Rise Ondnarch, terror of the north, bringer of the silent cold... Enslaver... Consumer...Devourer.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Spells\"", "ChokoTaco", "         SPELLS\nThis book was recovered from Aegis in the earlier years of magic. Little is known about the author, and his name was smudged out from the original text. Whether it is a reliable source of information remains questionable.\nFirst off. what is a \"spell\"? A spell is a mystic formula. intended to influence or cause events. There are good spells and bad spells. known as blessings and curses. Spells are limitless. and can bring destruction or peace to the world.\nBlessings. these spells bring no harm. They bring love. peace and success. These spells are used to help mankind and protect it from evil. These spells can heal illnesses. repair broken hearts and prevent death.\nThere are many possible blessings.\nCurses. These spells can lead to the destruction of the entire world. These spells can bring forth vicious things such as: monsters. storms. fire and many other  dangerous things. Now that we know what magic is...How is it used? Can we use magic?\nSpells consist of words. or incantations. To use them. the user must read the incantation. Not only that. the user must have what ever is required to use that spell. Some spells require a short amount of life energy. known as mana. \nThe stronger the spell the more mana that is needed to use it. Some spells also require items. such as herbs. in spells that deal with Witchcraft. Only certain races of the world are able to use certain magics, which makes them extremely special.\n To make it simple, some races have mana, others don't. Some races have a lot of mana, others have little to none. This concludes \"Spells\" written by: -Name is too smudged to read.-", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Tale of Alpha\"", "Hellio Brasspick", "\"Frey Upon a Hill\"\n\nA dark night is was, we knew danger was to haunt us when we first heard the words, Teuton, leave the halfling's mouth.\nHis name was Bili Hollowmead, he allowed us to stay at the tavern and drink his ale free of charge.\nA great thing for a halfling to offer to weary and thirsty dwarves. Us dwarves being; Tortek Irongut, Relku Grandaxe, King Hiebe Irongut, and of course, myself.\n\nSo we set out, crossing an ice stricken lake and over a snow topped mountain.\nWe arrived at the supposed Teuton fortress, but alas, it was none of the kind. We pressed on, though darkness seemed to loom around every corner.\n\nJust over the mountain's edge lay a valley. And in that valley was built a massive fort.\nCurious enough, when we approached, the guard suspected us of being Teutons ourselves!  Outrageous behavior! In light of events, we did not wish to terry there anymore as well.So every farther we pressed on, deeper into the valley,  \n where the mountain wall seemed to close in on us. Their peaks got harder to see as dark clouds pressed in to block our view.\n\nAs we went passed some farms, we found a house, a stone house.\nUpon more investigation,\nthe house was as hollow by being burned out from the inside! \nEven more curious.  \nBut then, it was said by Hiebe that we must leave, there was an unsettling tone in his voice, very troubling.\n He began to explain that he had been here before,\non some scouting mission, that it was not safe. This indeed not sit well with our halfling companion, nor did it with most of us.\n\nIt was then did a blood curdling howl pierce the evening sky, like a heavy sword scraping against hard stone.\n This gave a great freight to our companions. The dark clouds that barred our vision before bore us snowfall, slowly at first, but then quickened as the wind picked up. Soon a great storm was upon us, we had no other choice but to flee!\n\nWe ran as fast as we could back through the valley in which we previously treaded. Hiebe called lighting down upon the darkness in our wake. The evening began to turn to a very unsettling night. Faster and faster was our pace,\nnot to give any ground to any beast that might hunt us. We once again climbed the mountain face out of the valley,\nback up to the original building in which we found that the halfling thought was the Teutonic Order's fort.\n\nI called to my companions to take shelter in it's walls, so in we went, out of the falling snow and looming darkness.\nIn this moment, we sat in fear as darkness enveloped the land in it's entirety. Waiting,watching for the beasts of the night\nto come claim us.We all where at the ready; axes, swords, hammers drawn. The King stood his ground, unwavering, in the only opening to the outside cold. Even more howls could be heard from the darkness. Hiebe lifted his hammer above his head. BOOM! \nLighting striked an unknowing wolf in the distance. \n\nThe Irongut called out to the stale, cold air, \"May Urguan's hammer guide me!\"\n\nAs the wolves drew nearer, we began to see their yellow eyes pierce through the darkness,\n reflecting off the torches that where lit within. One attempted a frontal charge but was smited by Hiebe's hammer in a crushing blow that cracking of a skull could be heard at the other end of the valley. The Irongut King gave out a loud laughter,\n not fearing the wolves that beset them.\nAs he finished his laughter, the wolves began to move in on our position, surrounding us. Relku readied his sword as one charged him, biting into his arm as he plunged his sword deep into the beast's furry body.\nThe wolf was dead before he hit the ground, but Relku sustained injures. Tortek moved in to ward off any wolves wanting to get a jump at an injured lad.\n\nAlmost every dwarf had a wolf it was combating now.\nBut then, a wolf jumped right in front of the small Bili Hollowmead. It growled with terrible ferocity, the halfling shuddered. Slowly, but meaning to do so, Bili began to pull out a fang of some kind from his back pocket.The wolf advanced slowly, \n\n unknowing of his actions. The wolf pounced, but Bili was quicker. Before the wolf knew it, Bili had plunged the sharp fang right through his skull, leaving him dead instantly.\n\nOne by one, the wolves began to fall.\n We felt the optimism rising. Soon, a whole heap of wolves lay dead at our feet, it was a most unholiest of sights if I ever did see one. I gave a sigh of relief as I layed down my axe.\nBut alas, it was premature as I saw Bili pointing out to the darkness crying, \"The Alpha is still out there!\" \nWe all turned and looked out into the mysterious darkness, looking back at us where the largest pair of yellow eyes I had ever seen.\n. It was then that the beast gave out the worst sound one could hear. I swear by my beard, that it's foul howl began to peel up the floorboards on which we stood. The foolish Relku, still holding his arm from the bite of the wolf,\nsaid outright, \"I can take 'em!\".\n\n\"Foolish lad!\" I says, \"you already are injured, you'll get yourself killed!\" Ingoring my warning he charged the Alpha, into the darkness. I of course followed after him,\n what would Valen think if I let his son get killed?! Hiebe and Tortek all followed in suit, charging the large Alpha. As we enclosed around him, he turned right to Relku, seeing that he was injured. \n\nStep by step he got closer, until,\nhe turned his large head towards my way. Only then I truely got a good look at him. He was about as big as two dwarves stacked on top of each other, fur as black as the night.\nHis massive claws left large prints in the snow as his massive weight brought the snow to it's deepest layer. I steadied myself, tilted by axe to the side horizontally in defense.\n\nWith one bound,the massive,  horrible creature was in the air!\nIt's mouth ajar for its terrible jaws to come crashing down on my skull! A half a second is all it took, I thrusted by tiled axe right into it's mouth, making give a loud yelp. It's claws just about dug into my skin until the head of Hiebe's hammer \ncame crashing across it's body which sent the wolf flying through the falling snow. The Alpha remained motionless, dead, like the others. \n\nAs I remained laying there, I could here Hiebe picking out the teeth of his fallen prize, 13 of em to be exact.\nI reached for Tortek's hand for assistance up. As Tortek helped me up, leaving my body print on the snow, a cracking sound came from my chest. I stumbled in pain,  reaching for my chest.\nI felt the concern of my companions upon me,\n but I did not let my pain shown.\n\nSunlight shown on our faces as the break of dawn came upon us. To our great relief, we all began down the mountain, thinking of a warm fire and a good ale. Tortek helped me with support as well as the use of my cain.\nAs for that young Relku, I gave him an earful after the foolish actions of earlier. Alas, a beardling will always be a beardling.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Wayward Dwarf\"", "Hellio Brasspick", "\"Carry on my wayward dward\"\n\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink some more\n\nAh\nOnce I rose above the noise and confusion\nJust to get a glimpse beyond this illusion\nI was digging ever deeper, but I dug too deep\n\n\n\nThough my eyes could see I still was a blind dwarf\nThough my mind could think I still was a stark dwarf\nI hear the voices when I'm dreaming,\nI can hear them say\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf,\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink some more\nMasquerading as an alt with no reason\nMy charade is the event of the season\nAnd if I claim to be a wise man,\nWell, it surely means that I don't know\nOn a stormy sea of moving emotion\nTossed about, I'm like a ship on the ocean\nI set a course for winds of fortune,\nBut I hear the voices say\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink some more, more!\nCarry on,\nYou will always industrialize\nCarry on,\nNothing equals the splendor\nNow your life's no longer empty\nSurely industry waits for you\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink\nWhy don't you drink some more!\n \nDrink some more!", ""),
        StaticBook("'The Balrog'", "Arinislia", "'The Taint'\n\n7th of The Grand Harvest, 1475\n\n\n       The day was calm and gentle. The sun was high, shining its rays down upon the Father Tree as the druids went about their day. One of the druid children suddenly runs up, gasping for breath as she appeared to have been running. \nShe looked panicked, saying that she ran into a Dread Lord summoning something in the nearby woods. Suddenly a loud shriek was heard. . All look up the natural carved stairs of the Father Tree to see the Dread Lord stand before them. \n. A ghoul standing next to him along with some followers, the Dread Lord unleashed the ghoul down upon the druids, commanded to kill them all. During this, the Dread Lord then turned and advanced up the tree, \n, telling his followers to block all that dare move up. The ghoul was quickly defeated, but not before spreading its taint on all that it bit along with ones that were near when it exploded. \nIt appeared that if something wasn’t done quickly to cleanse, they perished.\n\n       The druids now advancing further up the tree, the followers were quickly removed before advancing further up. \n. Again the druids were blocked and met with a horrible abomination. The Dread Lord cackled down at them, before unleashing a balrog upon the druids, charging down full force. \nSeveral that were in the way were easily knocked off the tree to their deaths.  The druids seemed unorganized, yet with some coordination from a few within the order, they quickly rooted the balrog and threw it off the tree. \nThe Dread Lord far gone by then yet the top of the tree tainted. The druids advance upward, circling around the taint and focused, using their healing magic to remove the corruption of the tree.\nBelow where the balrog  fell off the tree, several came from different nations and organizations and struck down the abomination where it stood.  With the Father Tree healed once more, the druids descended down and helped cleanse and heal the wounded.", ""),
        StaticBook("*//MENU\\\\*", "Taissa Vale", "      *//menu\\\\*\n\n50% if you're in order \n  \n     *///FOOD\\\\\\*\n\nMushroom Stew - \$20\n\nBread/Fish - \$5\n\nCarrots - \$8\n      *//DRINKS\\\\*\n\nWine - \$40\n\nVodka/Whiskey - \$15\n\nAle - \$6\n\nCarrion Black -  \$10\n\n     MORE THINGS MAY \nBE IN STOCK OR OUT OF STOCK.", ""),
        StaticBook("*A", "Thurak", "Delonna Aeleyelsa, as an elder and far seer of the Orcs. I am wondering if we could meet to dicuss relations with the Orcs about shamanism. Send me a bird with the time you are able to speak to me. RulG, \nMirdautas Vras", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Note*", "Resia", "Izier,\n\nI apologize for making you angry the other night. Please don't take it the wrong way. I did mean it when I said I am not ment for that type of relationship and it's not your fault at all. You didn't hurt me. I'm g;ad to have you as my llir. Please\naccept these fishing rods as a token of my apology. \n\n-Resia Sae'lantae", ""),
        StaticBook("*a notice*", "Thurak", "*A note if found, scribbled out roughly on a creased though recent fold of parchment. It's written in common, although the hand that wrote it was large and awkward*\nThrom'ka. Thurak, Elder of the Uruks and Farseer of the Uzg, is now giving blessings to those who are worthy of them. Find him in his shop in San'Vitar, or send him a bird.\n\nMirdautas Vras", ""),
        StaticBook("*a red scroll*", "Thurak'Yar", "*the parchment is hued a crimson red, making reading the encryption difficult. What you can make out, however, would seem to be some sort of prediction or preminition*\n§uThe Red Realm Will Open\n§uThe Floating Fortress will rise from the sea\n§uThe Organic Island is going to fall along with the Fringelands\n§uThe realm of the Black Wrym shall soon open up", ""),
        StaticBook("*A rotten note*", "The Oogie Man", "Soon i will come~\n\nSoon you will be mine!\n\nI'm talking to you...the oogie man will come and he wants to play with you...\n\nLove,\nThe Oogie Boogie Man\n\nI talk to you...Arch Druid.\n\n      O           O\n.                          .\n .                        .\n   .                   .\n     .             .\n       .       .\n          . .", ""),
        StaticBook("*a small note*", "~5", " *you find a small, neatly written note in front of you, penned out on a plain sheet of paper in a dark purple ink. It seems to make no sense, however, and is only signed by the number, 5...*\nN fr ymj rfs wmt xytqj owtr ytz. Nk ytz wfsy yt kqsi rj, n wjxnij ns ymj Kwnsij Ijxjwy, ns f mtzxj ozxy tzyxqij tk ymj rfns ifyj tk ymj Zzi- Vznyj mfwi yt rqxx, ns kfhy. Nk ytz’wj nsyqqnljsy jstzlm yt ijhnumjw ymnx, ytz’wj ijxjwvnsl tk wjywngzynts.\n\n~5", ""),
        StaticBook("*signed note*", "Thurak'Yar", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~Whuevah hawldz dizz nowt mae rezeeve ash Zpirid Wulk ur Blezzin'\nfrum da zpirid ob der choize frum Thurak da Farzeer. Zend heem ah burd wehn lat wund tu kollekd id, agh zhuw heem dizz nowt.\n     *Thurak'Yar*\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("-The Fairground-", "Ulfrík", "  *}The Fairground{*\n\nThe Fairground is a short story that has been written by Ulfrík. He wishes that whomever is reading this enjoys the little tale. \n\nPlease turn over for the start...\nThe eerie wind rasps through the tattered flag that hangs on top of its ruined tower of a flagpole. As I creep across the abandoned field of ruin, my feet meet with the sodden posters that lie in their graves of despair. The peices of paper drift like-\n-Tumbleweed. Their once vibrant colours are now faded, dead. A sign stands bent diagonally, frozen by the frosty wind. Peeled back paint, laden with spiders, covers the once informative plaque that reads, \"F...N   GR...U...D\". The occasional mocking of a-\n-nocturnal bird echoes across the barren land, beckoning for you to enter the monstrous wasteland of a fairground. \n\n\nThe skeletal frame of a withered ticket booth looms over the entrance. Little pieces of its once grand-\nframe lie strewn about the littered floor. Shudders run down your spine as the cold winds blow. Tickets and various other ruined items rest on top of  the counter. A dilapidated chair lies on its side inside the booth. Once a man sat there, enjoying the -\nsounds and feelings of the funfair. All of those are gone now, they have blown away with the wind. The roof of the three walled structure sits aside its only companion, the dirty floor. shines through the door, it illuminates a dusty wooden floor that -\n-leads to an outside trail.  A strange path of crumbled desolation has been trod by the countless trespassers that choose to dwell in the shadows. Unseen by society, fallen pillars are left to rot and decay. \nStaring down upon you are the tracks of a rollercoaster, it hangs suspended in the bitter  air by multiple metal poles. A forest of rust stands before your eyes. As time has dragged by, the life of the rollercoaster has been sent into retirement. Ten -\n- years of redundancy is clearly shown by the thick layers of grime and dirt. As you tread, the soles of your shoes make footprints on the weed-ridden concrete. . Wild plants escape from underneath the hard stone, their mal-nourished heads break through-\n-ashes on the ground. \nAnother amusement lurks in the gloom, within its frame rests a few scattered bumper cars. Rusted hulls cover the front of their wrecked forms. Once bright paint has now faded into a barrage of dingy browns and-\n-greys. An old, peeled back flooring is left alone in amongst the faded dodgems. Moss grows in the mat's place now, it covers the ground with a jungle-like presence. The ceiling of the ride is tattered and crumbled. Most of what remains lies on the floor-\n-among the rest of the rubble. In the distance, dark figures creep about, scuttles can be heard from the outskirts of where you stand. Almost like someone is watching you, staring and glaring... \n\nThe last exhibit focuses in on your-\n-view. An archway stands there, hunched over. Its black, dark colours seem not to have faded. A wicked doorway is what the arch hides. From inside a feint cackle can be heard it rings through your ears like a scream. As you step toward it the sounds-\n-become louder, growing in size. Do you dare to enter...?\n\n\n\nYou you enjoyed.\n\n   -Ulfrík.", ""),
        StaticBook("...", "An old parchment", "*hastily written words are scralled across a tattered paper*\n\n\"They're trying to kill me. I hear them, talking behind my back. They think I don't know. They think I don't hear. All I need to do is seal myself in when they go on patrol.....\"", ""),
        StaticBook("...", "Joe", "Ah, Conjuration; the rarest Arcane Art known... well, it won't be rare anytime. Of course, once you begin to learn the art, you will be reffered to as a \"Conjurer\". A conjurer is an individual who access the Void and construct living organism which are \nfueled wholly by the mana of their creator. Through the depths of the void, a Conjuration user will be able to summon mighty creatures or placid flowers into reality. Alas, as a conjurer you will be constantly delivering your mana for virtually every \nsecond your ersatz summon exists. You will soon come to a realisation that Conjuration uses the most of your mana unlike any other Arcane Science. In order to uphold the existence of your faux creature in reality, you must feed it precisely a great \nportion of mana to flow within it. As the creature you summon will be downright complex, the process of building it within the Void will be rather tiresome and there is a good chance you may be drained completely of your mana until you reach \nunconsciousness, as that happens your beast will be removed from the physical realm and be sent back to the Void. Yes, you can decide to desist the flow of mana beforehand, in which case the fauna will vanish to no consequence. Now, for you to construct \nan organism within the Void, you must first have a sharp and great understanding of both the interior and exterior of the living you wish to formulate. This can be achieved by oftenly killing and dissecting the creature you wish to summon. However, it is \nalso best to keep very detailed anatomical diagrams of the beast you wish to conjure. Remember to have notes on the animal's exterior, interior and bone structure if you want to have an accurate understanding of it. In the opaque Void, the fabrics which \ngenerate the entity are summoned bone by bone, layer by layer, muscle by muscle and organ by organ the Conjurer crafts and sculpts their being into an exact copy of their previously existing self. As a result of poor research, the Conjurer may fail at\nthis point, producing a being unlike that of its true and real form will result in an uneven and revolting entity which would certainly turn to a sludge once conjured. After a while of practice, the Conjurer would be able to summon the creature exactly \nhow it was before it was slain and have it formed with sheer stability. As it will behave akin to the life form it represents, it will follow its creator's commands. As a Conjurer myself, I would highly recommend you begin to study roses, then petite\ninsects until you grow stronger and confident enough to study anything larger. Think of Conjuration as art. You are the painter and the Void is the frame. What you paint in that frame will need to look beautiful and make sense in the judge's eyes. Bear in\nmind that the \"judge\" is the physicla realm. If the judge thinks your work of art is good, it will be stamped on and crushed and it will appear as an abomination in the mortal plane, you will be smacked in the face for your poot efforts, that smack will \ntire you. Keep practicing and your artistic skills will improve and the judge will begin to continue to accept your art. Overtime, your frame will expand and leave you open to produce which the judge can view. Be warned though, the larger the harder. And \nyes, you can fabricate hybrid fauna. I'll leave that for you to grasp the concept of that alone.\n\n\n-READ THIS NEWBIE-\n\nIf this tome becomes the next Illusion Arcane Art... I swear, as one of the most \npowerful conjurers in this realm, I will stalk and kill these conjurers I was not informed of beforehand with an army of flying honeybadgers... Or a colossal elemental... You better watch yourself, reader.", ""),
        StaticBook("/-Venehopea-\\", "Illmori", "/-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\\         Venehopea\n        City Plan \n\nI. Platform Planning : \n\nFour main platforms - Central Platform (CP), Residential Platform 1 (RP1), Residential Platform 2 (RP2) and Comercial Platform (CoP). \n\nTwo big canals - Hoprive \nand Venriv. Venriv is between CP and RP2 (with size of twenty blocks) and Hoprive is between CoT and RP1 (With size of eight  blocks). Small Canals Everywhere (With size 3-5 blocks). Medium Canals in RP1 (5-6 blocks). \nMost canals in RP1, fewer in CT. \nCT is next to CoT and RP1. RP2 is near to a small farm island (that will be built by us). \nThe bigger Platform is CoT, the smaller is RP1. The second bigger platform is RP2. \n\nCoT is with the size 2/3 of Werdenberg. RP2 is with size 1/2 of Werdenberg. \nCT is with size 2/3 of CoT and RP2 is with size 1/2 of CoT. \n\nThe Bigger Plaza is Plaza \"Tuin\" in CT. \"Tuin\" is 2/3 of CT. On \"Tuin\" there are the biggest and the most beautiful buildings in the city - The Castle \"Illonnis\", the cathedral \"Oschino\" and \nthe highest building in the city - the Tower \"Hopea\". On The Central plaza there are also the local biggest shops, caffes and resturants. The main Plaza have three entrances - One entrance to the street on the side of Venriv, One entrance to the small \nstreets that head to CoT and one entrance to the small streets that go to the docks. \n\nThere are two big streets - \"Main Street\" and \"Sea View\" - main streets is the street that is one of the exits of \"Tuin\" and \"Sea View\" is the street that is next to \nVenriv and Tuin. Main Streets is eight block big and Sea View is five blocks big. All the other streets are 1-3 blocks big. \n\nThe building desines are completely different. There must be not two houses that look the same, but in the same time there must \nbe style. The Cathedral may have a round roof and small towers on it. The Castle would have lots of collonums and warm style. The tower would be with lots of ornaments and details on it's walls. \n\n((Ooc note - it would look like Minecraft Venice", ""),
        StaticBook("1500-1501 Profit", "Adoros Steel", "PROFITS:\n930 Minas - Phaedrus\n100 minas - Adoros\n700 minas - Phaedrus\n100 minas - Adoros\n300 minas - Adoros\n25 Minas - Phaedrus\n175 minas - Adoros\n100 minas - Adoros\n\n-Confirmed by Tyrell\nBlavier.\n\nDEDUCTIONS:\n500 mina-phaed\n400 Rent & Taxes\n510 minas - Phaed\n150 Minas - Phaed\n20 Minas - Phaed\n\nEmployees Produce:\nPhaedrus: 5 chain sets, 3 HQ swords\n\nPure Profit:§\n870 minas\n\nBONUS PROFIT (Unrecorded): 930 minas\n\nTotal Profit: 1800 minas\n\nSTORAGE UNTIL BOUGHT:\nSharp sword 45%, 7 damage.", ""),
        StaticBook("1st Journal", "Unknown", "\n            /\\\n            \\/\n\n         Journal\n*A drawing of everyone in Nerezza. Daren is centre as he is leader, next to Thor and Ulfrik.*\n*A drawing of Alfred's family members, his neice and brother. The names Andreth and Ariana are at the bottom of the page.*\n*A drawing of the keep in Nerezza from the main entrance*\n\n*A drawing of Alfred's father, he has stern look on his face because that is how he always looked at Alfred*\n*A drawing of Zaviel.\nAt the bottom of the page it says in bold letters \"TWAT\".*\n*A drawing of Sage, the best done drawing in the whole journal.*\n*A drawing of the Drunken Monk Tavern, the top half of the page is the exterior. The second half is the interior.*\n*A drawing of the undead attacking Nerezza.*", ""),
        StaticBook(": }", "Feral Elf Kidnapper", "Art,\nPlease save me. He demands that Cerulin be released! Oh yes he does, how awful!\nGive it up, I will love you forever. \nSincerly,\nTitania The Usuruper\n:) : ) :) : ) :) :) :) :) <3\n\nHAHA \nIt thought this was its\nusurper. It is so dumb! It is a filthy false elf.  Left us they did oh yes. Left us to die at the hands of the dwarf demons! Oh yess but now we have it's usurper. Give us the city or she stays in our possesion. OR give us the heads of :\nKalenz\nArtimec \nAelu\nMizziyrn\nDaki'ir\nDwyn\n", ""),
        StaticBook("<3", "Elayne", "It's sweet like nectar of the garden flower,\n\nIt's soothing like the buzzing of bumble bee.\n\nIt's warm like the rays of the morning sun,\n\nIt's the search of love so pure which keeps me on the run.\nIt's the pulse in my vein,\n\nThe thoughts in my brain,\n\nIn every breath that I take,\n\nThe smile my lips make,\n\nIt's in the twinkle of my eye, till the day I die.\nIt's my dreams in my sleep,\n\nIt's springs freshest leaf;\n\nA love so rare like this will always be with me for keeps.\nIt's warmth of my blood,\n\nAs my feelings flood,\n\nAs says my heart's beat,\n\nIts depth touches the ocean's feet.\nEven if its heart searing pain,\n\nWith nothing to gain,\n\nI will feel it as the tear on my cheek,\n\nAnd without words my soul will speak.\nA feeling so sincere,\n\nA bond so strong,\n\nI know my soul will never guide me wrong.\nI would wait till my last sunset,\n\nTill my heart slows down with dull ache,\n\nTill my eyes are wet,\n\nDak, you are my soul's mate.\n\n-=Lain=-", ""),
        StaticBook("=- Holy Magic -=", "PiercingDarkness", "Holy-Magic: Clerical Magic of the realm. \n\n\"Clerical Magic is impossible to learn without faith.\"\n- Prophet Hosper\n\nTold to you by, Mythras Ardere.\nWritten by Mythras Ardere.\nHoly Magic is often taught by the Clerical Order It is said that the magic is taught by masters of it as they grow more powerful. War-Cleric is a form of clerical magic used for combat, and is often used to fight Necromancers.\n§LIt is thought that magic used by clerics is from using their expendable mana from themselves to heal others. But this is false, considering all magic has a power source other than yourself. Except for a select few, such as Necromancy.\nClerics draw their power from a \"Patron,\" or also known as a Aengul. Clerical Magic varies from different patrons, one may be Aerial while another's perhaps, Nemphiisae, because of this it's mainly the beliefs of the user.\nRed-Note.\n\nBecause of the nature of this magic, one may not learn void magic and many other kinds, with priest healing /AND/ war cleric. Because of this it's impossible to wield evocation /AND/ War-Clerical Magic.\nTo continue this, Clerical Magic is often thought to be, \"useless.\" Though, it has it's uses only smart people would know of. The healing of people's important, as is defending the light. Clerics are often heroes who help anyone in need.\nThis magic's often gained through prayer to the person's patron. Thus prayers lead to you being granted energy for your clerical spells from your patron. Prayer and hard work lead to mastering clerical magic.", ""),
        StaticBook(">.>   <.<", "Salamander", "Efficiency\n0x0\nx0x\n0x0\nKnockback\nxxx000000\nxxxxxxxxx\nxxxxxxxxx\nxxx000000\nPlace element at (X)\nFire\nx00x00x\nx00x00x\nx00x00x\nxxxxxxx\nLoot\n0x0000x00\nxxxxxxxxx\n0x0xxxxxx\n000000x00\nPlace element at (X)\nProtection\n00xxxxx00\n00xxxxx00\n00xxxxx00\n000xxx000\nSharpening\n000000x00\nxxxxxxxxx\nxxxxxxxxx\n000000x00\n\nInfinite Arrow\n0x0x0\nx0x0x\n0x0x0\nSilk Touch\nxxxxxxxxx\nUnbreaking\nx0x0x0x\n0x000x0\nx0x0x0x\nUnknown\nxxxxxxxx\nxxx00xxx\nxxx00xxx\nxxxxxxxx\nFishers Luck\n0xx0x\nx0x00\n0xx0x\nHoly Ward\n0xx0\nxxxx\nxxxx\n0xx0", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A Note", "Serpen", "I am the one with a battle of souls.\n\nTwo became one.\n\nOpposing desires collide within, leaving me susceptible to either.\n\nMy salvation can only come from those who are garbed in light \nand led by the keeper of souls.\n\nMy time is limited.\n\nMalice and destruction are beomcing the prominent desires.\n\nDeliverance into the light shall be either the end, or the return of one pure.\nThe green soul fades.\n_\n            _.;_'-._\n           {`--.-'_,}\n          {; \\,__.-'/}\n          {.'-`._;-';\n           `'--._.-'\n              .-\\\\,-.\n              ._..\\\\._\n                  \\\\\n                   \\\\\n                    \\\n-C.A\n[!] A drawing of a black rose seems to be at the bottom of the note?", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] Urgent [!]", "Fjordin Sylver", "[!] This book appears to be written by someone of great penmanship, carefully scrawled in a very deep cactus-green ink with elegant lettering!\nGreetings, outlander! It appears to me you are trying to make a living for yourself in the unforgiving wilds of Athera. Having been in this situation before, I understand the constant danger in doing so. Brigands tend to pillage what little they can find.\nLong ago I founded a settlement not far from here, and coined the future city \"Sylverwood\". Unfortunately, a group of downtrodden peasants in armor swept through the village, killing my citizens and nearly myself.\nHad it not been for my faithful friend who is now part of an Orenian military, I would not have survived. Two decades later, and I am prepared to stake claim of a more worthy piece of land. Found a truly grand city.\n\nI myself have laid out the architectural plans for almost a third of the upper district, which I will promptly begin construction of once the blueprints are complete. Right now, however, I need spare hands on deck to help with the heavy lifting.\nI cannot offer you any material goods, although I can offer you a sizable home with a lavish, and prestigious interior. In the next few pages I will detail what it is we are looking for pre-and-post development, and my name if you wish to send a bird.\nThe community is looking for a mix of skilled and unskilled labor. This city will be the cornerstone of regality and luxury all across Athera, and aspire to provide its citizens with only the finest places to live. \nAnybody who shows ample support in the development of this city will be given a free homestead in the inner-city. Those who do not, and would rather wait until after it is complete will have to pay a hefty sum of Minas to purchase a place to call home.\nOur community is built around the values of comfort, prosperity/wealth, and industry. Piety will also play a role, although people will have the option to practice their own religious beliefs in private or none at all. \nWe plan to vassalize under Oren, although this is more for political prestige and diplomatic reasoning. Chances are we will eventually break away from Oren, although we would rather wait for valid reasoning to do so (to avoid unnecessary bloodshed). \nWe will also have a military, which we plan to coin the Sylver Sword. That will be the offensive reserve of shock-troopers, infantry, skirmishers, and cavalry. Our archers will be the Sylver Shield, which will be a mainly defensive and learn siegecraft.\nThere are a number of general professions across Athera that people take up arms in. The most needed unskilled labor in terms of most important to least important will be detailed on the next page. After that skilled labor:\nMiner -\n[x][x][x][x][x]\nBreeder -\n[x][x][x][x][ ]\nFisher -\n[x][x][x][x][ ]\nChef -\n[x][x][x][ ][ ]\nFarmer -\n[x][x][/][ ][ ]\n* We are going to be an industrial fishing community. Farming hardly needed *\nStonemason -\n[x][x][x][x][x]\nTinkerer -\n[x][x][x][x][x]\nLeatherworker -\n[x][x][x][x][ ]\nWoodworker -\n[x][x][x][ ][ ]\nBlacksmith -\n[x][x][ ][ ][ ]\nAlchemist -\n[x][ ][ ][ ][ ]\nEnchanter -\n[x][ ][ ][ ][ ]\nBlacksmiths are obviously important to a society, and the maintenance of a military, but they fall off their use in our society due to the lack of miners. Once we increase in population, unskilled labor will balance out with skilled labor.\nLeatherworkers play a key role in the maintenance of our ranged military (and in fact I wish to branch cavalry in the direction of horse archery). Studded armor is very important to an archer or light infantry by increasing their effectiveness.\nI personally recommend picking two unskilled labors as professions, whilst choosing two skilled labors as your remaining professions. If you already picked your professions, no sweat. That means in some way you will be more vital to our success initially.\nIf you wish to send me a bird, my name is Fjordin Sylver (christian2142). I'm almost always available to recieve messages, but if I don't respond within ample time try sending another. We can then meet at a convinient location to talk in person.\nSincerely,\n\nFjordin Sylver\n\n- Potential Ruler of Sylversands -", ""),
        StaticBook("[1] Sealed Note", "Aislinn", "[!] The letter is sealed with a wax seal, the outside having clear, written instructions:\n\n\"Open when you need me, but I'm not here.\"\n\n\n[!] You tear open the letter, because who carefully opens letters anyway? \n\nIt begins:\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Dearest Love,\n\nI'm writing this for you because I know there will be times where\nyour mental and physical willpower will be pushed to its limits, and then some. We live in a cold, harsh world, and keeping yourself together can be tough sometimes.\n\nI hope I'm always here to help, but just incase, I am leaving you these letters.\nIn my experience, everyone reacts differently to the hardships of life. Some people become cold and resist everything. Others become very affected by what happens to them, and they internalize it. They allow things to change them.\nIt's my hope that you do neither. \n\nBy becoming cold and shutting yourself away from others, you deprive yourself of the most precious need - the need to be loved, to care for and be cared by others.\n\n\nIf you allow things to change you, you will become like me. Your mind will become twisted, and you will lash out at others.\n\nYou'll lose control of yourself. It's an awful path to go down, and I love you too much to see that happen.\nI know you, and I know that no matter what happens..\n\n*A note is scribbled in to the side* (Aside from spilling a tray of freshly baked cookies)\n\n..you'll be able to persevere through it. You're a strong woman.\nPeople may offer their help, but know that you don't need it.\n\nYou have everything you need within you, everything you need to overcome whatever obstacle you face.\n\nAs always, I love you, and will love you forever.\n-Aislinn", ""),
        StaticBook("[2] Sealed Note", "Aislinn", "[!] The envelope is addressed to 'Cheza', sealed with wax. Instructions indicate it be opened during dire circumstances.\n[!] The wax seal breaks off easily, and you slip a piece of parchment from the envelope. You begin to read the note..\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Dear Chezzy,\n\nMy memory has never been the sharpest. Sometimes I do or\nsay silly things. I can say with 100% certainty, however, that I have never had the good fortune of being with such a fantastic woman as you.\n\nHave you ever had a moment where you saw something so stunning, so beautiful, that time \nitself seemed to come to a halt? It happens to me every time I gaze into your eyes. \n\nI get lost in them, as if I were trapped in the vast expanse of the night sky. \n\nWords just can't describe how I feel when we're curled up\ntogether, looking at each other. Every moment of you reminds me why I am so happy to be alive, and I wouldn't trade a second of it for all the wealth in the world.\n\nIt is my dearest hope that we will grow old together, if such a thing is even possible.\nIf not, you and I better die wrestling bears or fist fighting crazed necromancers. Our story deserves an equally glorious ending.\n\nBut here I am, being negative and speaking about endings. When I met you, it was like a new beginning for me.\nEven if I had just known you for a short while, you'd have made my troubles melt away for every moment we were together.\n\nFor whatever reason, I'm not by your side right now.  I better have a good reason, or you can slap me viciously when you\nsee me again. Still, I want you to know that you are always in my thoughts. Should something happen, my last thoughts will be of you. Should something not happen, I'll still think about you.\n\nI'm a little bit obsessed, but that's just what being in \nlove is. I truly do love you, Cheza.\n\nWith you always-\n\n-Aislinn.\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("[3] Sealed Note", "Aislinn", "[!] The small, folded envelope seems to bulge, clearly something more than just a letter inside.\n\nIt's addressed to Cheza, and is sealed.\n[!] The wax seal on the envelope breaks off, almost too easily. The first thing you notice is a small, silver ring fall out, along with a letter.\n\nUpon closer inspection, the ring seems to be made of a C+A pattern, running\nin a seamless, perfect circle to form the ring.\n\nYou scan the letter next, which reads:\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Dear love,\n\nI had something made to remind you of us. Sometimes our material things are taken\naway. Other times, our friendships and relationships are shattered. There were times where it felt like my soul was chipped away.\n\nBut there's one thing nobody (except a gorgeous mental mage such as myself) can take away, and that's\nmemories. This ring can serve as a reminder of all the good and happy times we had together. If you ever are really sad, all you need to do is look down at this ring.\n\nIt's a symbol of our unity, like other rings. Our love isn't going to end, and as long\nas you remember me, I will be there to help you. \n\nDraw strength from it. Use that strength to find happiness, or to overcome whatever has temporarily struck you down.\n\nKnow that I've always wanted the best for\nyou. Whether it was with me or someone else, you truly deserve to be happy.\n\nYou may not think it, especially now. Others may tell you that you're worthless, but know that to me, you were, and always will be my world. My everything.\nYou're more precious than the largest gemstone, or the heaviest gold crown, or even the most extensive hair collection. But that'd be cutting it close..\n\nBe proud of yourself and who you are. You're a wonderful individual, and you\nalways will be.\n\nI love you.\n\n-Aislinn", ""),
        StaticBook("[4] Sealed Note", "Aislinn", "[!] There is a large envelope that is sealed with a wax stamp. \n\n- To Chezzy. Open if necessary.-\n[!] You open the envelope, and a small collection of drawings fall out, a note scattered amongst them. It reads:\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Dear Chezzy, if you're reading this, you must be having a bad time. I had hoped that you would read these all\nin order, and if you have gotten this far, I hope I haven't done anything to warrant the need to read them all.\n\nHopefully we're reading these over together, and laughing about how silly this idea was.\n\nRegardless, I know time can sometimes wear on the memory of a person, so I wanted to save some of our memories for you.\n\nWith love;\n\n-Aislinn.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n[!] The first drawing is that of Aislinn and Cheza, when he proposed to her. The scene was reconstructed as best as Aislinn could according to his memory.\n\n[!] The second is a portrait of Aislinn. It seems to have been \ndone in a mirror, since the mirror is sketched along with himself. He seems.. content.\n\n[!] Another drawing shows Cheza healing an injured man. The expression of gratefulness and thankfulness is ever-present on his face.\n[!] And the final picture is Aislinn, Cheza, and Crona together in a family picture. Crona looks too badass to be described.", ""),
        StaticBook("[L] Lost Page 1", "Freema", "[!] You've found an ancient page lost from it's binding. This page\nglows a faint greyish aura around it. You cannot seem to make any sense of the dialect it transcribes.\n\n\nOOC:\n\nYou have found a lost page of the Compendium, on the forums in Storyline Events. Please post a picture of this book in hand, and you will be contacted for a special event.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Bear Tale.", "The Scribe.", "Once upon a time, a group of hunters went into the forest to kill a wolf that had killed a farmers cow.\n\nBeing untrained, they were lost within the hour, and found themselves lost in the forest, with night quickly approaching.\nThey approached a cave, a great grown bear bursting out and attacking them. The slaid it, through their combined efforts. They ignored the cries that came from the cave, instead walking off.\n\n\nThe next day, a young dedicant\nwas in the woods, lost on her way back to the grove. However, she heard the calls from the cave, and sought to see what they were. Entering the cave, she found the bear's cub, injured and starving. The cub tried to attack the dedicant, but \ncould not move with its wound. \n\nOver the course of several days, the dedicant brought the cub food, and nursed the cubs wound. She gained the trust of the cub.  She brought the cub back to her home, and watched over its recovery.\nSeveral weeks past, and the cub was healthy and fit to leave. The Dedicant took the cub into the woods, and sent him off. \n\nOf course, however, the cub would not leave.  No matter how she tried, the \nbear would not leave. The bear cub followed her everywhere, it would not leave her side. The two were friends for the rest of the bears life. He protected her, and she took care of him. And those hunters... They did not fare so well.\nThe moral is simple; Do good, and good will come to you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Blessing", "Zane Capette", "May the light of your soul guide you. \nMay the light of your soul bless the work that you do \nwith the secret love and warmth of your heart. \nMay you see in what you do the beauty of your own soul. \nMay the sacredness of your work bring healing, light \nand renewal to those who work with you \nand to those who see and receive your work. \nMay your work never weary you. \nMay it release within you wellsprings of \nrefreshment, inspiration and excitement. \nMay you be present in what you do. \nMay you never become lost in bland absences. \nMay the day never burden. \nMay dawn find you awake and alert, \napproaching your new day with dreams, possibilities and promises. \nMay evening find you gracious and fulfilled. \nMay you go into the night blessed, sheltered and protected. \nMay your soul calm, console and renew you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A bloodied tome", "Jonathan Dunharrow", "Malghourn's mother was not a nice lady. She doesn't like blood magic.\nThis is, your knowledge of blood magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Book", "Anonymous", "It was the raw and wild duo of earth and natural growth: the Aenguls Cernunnos and Cerridwen. These two incorporeal beings are the patrons and deities of which Druids call upon for influence over nature. With the elven\npenchant for similar ideals as the Druidic Aspects, the two factions frequently blend. In this, the Druids exist.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Book of Songs", "Ketiley Strong-Heart", "*It is clear to see that this book was written in coal, but had rather eloquent, fluid, and graceful appearance to each letter.*\n\n\n        A Book of Songs\n\n           Written by:\n\n        Ketiley of Orvar\nAge of The Fallen\n\n\"We drink to our youth\n'Til the day's come and gone\nFor the age of scourge\nIs now gone and done\nWe'll drive out the fallen\nFrom this land that we own\nWith our blood and our steel\nWe will protect our home\nAll hail to Bloodborn\nYou are the High Chief~\nIn your great honour we drink and we sing\nWe're the children of Savaar\nAnd we fight all our lives\nWhen the Isle comes to beckon\nEvery one of us dies.\nBut this land is ours\nAnd we'll see it wiped clean\nOf the scourge that has sullied\nOur hopes and our dreams\"\nMay It Be\n\nMay it be an evening star\nShines down upon you\nMay it be when darkness falls\nYour heart will be true\nYou walk a lonely road\nOh! How far you are from home\nMornie utulie (Darkness has come)\nBelieve and you will find your way\nMornie alantie (Darkness has fallen)\nA promise lives within you now\nMay it be the shadow's call\nWill fly away\nMay it be you journey on\nTo light the day\nWhen the night is overcome\nYou may rise to find the sun\n\nMornie utulie (Darkness has come)\nBelieve and you will find your way\n\nMornie alantie (Darkness has fallen)\nA promise lives within you now\nBarid and Morvan Orvar\n\nOne day when I was on the misty mountains\n\nFar al a leò ro ho bhi ò\nHoireann is ò ho rò bhi o ho\nHi rì ho ro ho bha ò hug ò ro\n\nI saw a wonderful sight\nThe Clan Orvar's ship passed by\nAway from Alaskr Country.\nTowards joyful Ovarii\nWhere the feasting takes place\nDrinking wine from night to day\nThe piping of the tall, lovely drones\nThe sweet harp being tuned alongside\nRusset silk being worn by the ladies\nBarid The Reaver, the great hero\nand Morvan the great Heir.\nMy Dashing Darling\n\nOnce I was a gentle maiden,\nBut now I am a spent, worn-out widow,\nMy man strongly ploughing the waves\nOver the hills and far away.\nHe is my hero, my Gallant Darling,\nHe is my heart, a Gallant Darling;\nI've found neither rest nor fortune\nSince my Gallant Darling went far away.\nEvery day I am constantly enduring grief,\nWeeping bitterly and shedding tears,\nBecause my lively lad has left me\nAnd no news is told of him, alas!\nThe cuckoo does not sing cheerfully at noon\nAnd the sound of hounds is not heard in nut-tree woods\nNor summer morning in misty glen\nSince my lively boy went away from me.\nNoble, proud young Gorundyr,\nYouth without gloom, of pleasant countenance,\nA swift-moving fist, nimble in a fight,\nSlaying the enemy and smiting the strong.\nLet a strain be played on musical harps,\nAnd let many quarts be filled on the table,\nWith high spirit, without fault, without gloom,\nThat my lion may receive long life and health.\nGallant Darling for a while under sorrow,\nAnd Savaar completely under black cloaks,\nI have found neither rest nor fortune\nSince my Gallant Darling went far away.\nI Want Tomorrow\n\nDawn breaks; there is blue in the sky.\nYour face before me\nThough I don't know why.\nThoughts disappearing like tears from the Moon.\n\nWaiting here, as I sit by the stone,\nThey came before me\nThose rays from the Sun.\nSigns from the Isle say I'm the one.\n\nNow you're here, I can see your light,\nthis light that I must follow.\nYou, you may take my life away, so far away.\nNow I know I must leave your spell\nI want tomorrow.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Case Study", "Falyen Darylus", "The Radiant Man - Powers and Subjugation of the Mind\nThe Radiant Man, a suspected incarnate aengul, has aligned himself with parts of the Spellcrafters of Rivel with the goal of uncovering the Forgotten Dwarven artifact known as\n“The Seal”. To those who follow him, the Radiant Man grants incredible powers. They are akin to holy magics, but are incapable of healing yet also functional against those who could not in any way be described as dark creatures. It seems to be Holy\nMagic without the requirement of being holy: an excellent addition to any Spellcrafter’s arsenal, especially when so freely given and easily mastered. Or so it would seem.\nIt appears to draw upon the Radiant Man’s power is to open one’s being\nto him: the more power one draws and the more frequently one draws it the more the Radiant Man is capable of influencing, or even controlling, one’s thoughts. We have carried out extensive experimentation on the two members\nof the Radiant Man’s following of Spellcrafters when they returned to Rivel to analyse the tomes from the Archive. Their behaviour was normal, yet they wholeheartedly refuse to accept the possibility that their minds are not fully\ntheirs, and mental magical probing is being blocked by a power beyond our own.\nPart of the danger of this is the slippery slope: once one opens one’s mind to the Radiant Man the Radiant Man can influence one to draw a little more, giving\nthe Radiant Man a little more control and thus the influence required to push one to draw slightly more power. This could rapidly lead to a complete inability to refuse the commands of the Radiant Man, and hypothetically could turn into what I\nrefer to as a “Subjugant”, an individual wielding untold power via the Radiant Man yet completely slaved to his will to the point of lacking independent thought: simply an extension of the Radiant Man’s desires. Such a being could prove\nincredibly dangerous, and I recommend total disconnection from the Radiant Man of all of his Spellcrafter followers as soon as they return from their venture to the Hall.\n- Senior Researcher Falyen Darylus\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Clasped Tome", "Assa'rai", "Dear Eilistrae,\n\nI hope this finds you in good hands, for this seems to be the best manner in which to speak with you.\n\nEnclosed within the chest you will find one other item of interest.\nWith the return of your Mate I don't know if you will value it much at all, or if you will even notice this box for several weeks.\n\nI had intended to give you this necklace after the ball but... it seems such is not to be.\nI imagine this probably comes out of my own ignorance, assuming facts that were not quite right. I am presumptuous, naive, and... I shouldn't really fault you for it.\n\nRegardless, my heart is about to bleed onto the page so I should\ncut this short, I hope you will accept this gift. I will be around if you need me, but I would like to ask you to be transparent with me.\n\nI love you, but if you do not return the emotion I will be fine.\n\nI simply want you to be happy.\n\n- Assa'rai", ""),
        StaticBook("A Coin", "Miru", "I wish I wish:\n~For a special world for you and me,\nA special bond one cannot see,\nIt wraps us up in its cocoon,\nAnd holds us fiercely in its womb,\nIts fingers spread like fine spun silk,\nGently nestling us to the fold,\nLike silken threat it holds us fast,\nBonds like this are meant to last.~\n\nAnd a new clothes.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Consul's Mind", "Menithrian", "^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    -_=-*(S.A)*-=_-\n           1510\n\n -Consul Menithrian-\n\nRegarding the affairs\n     of the Druidic\n          Order\n\n\n\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ \nMy formal opinion is one with the Republic's: the Druidic Order has survived and flourished, despite being surrounded by times of spite and war - we've all been familiar with them. This they did by keeping themselves apolitical, or so it feels so. This \nis better off not being tampered with. \n\nThe Druidic Order preserves the roots of nature, and branches out throughout the plains of Mother Nature herself. To leave its peaceful nature is something the Republic wouldn't condone, and \nundermine its value as a neutral core. \n\nRight then, Official words done. The Druids, to me, have done my time here in Salvus a good - by supporting us in all aspects of nature, we've tried to nurture: our ponds glimmer off the glowing trees we\nhave in our gardens. We have a few of them in the City, and they've proven themselves to not dictate Druidic ways to Salvus - although the two are very compactible in ideal. We both mean peace, we both strive to keep the nature of the place, and to keep \nthe favour we hold for people on equal terms. It's those factors that have allowed Salvus, me and the Druids to all get along. \n\nI'd like a grove in Salvus, for what it's worth - as a glimmering beacon of hope, and a sign that \nSalvus represents all good - in a world where the bad has tried to empower. If it must be political, then surely should it be more tied to a place that strives to keep its ideals alive - than tree cutters, and warmongerers. We must prove that it doesn't \ntake a blade to speak. This sounds much like the Republic's view, probably for reason.. \n\nTo me, the Druidic Order can prove great friends to everyone, that respects its ideals.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A crumpled note", "Unknown", "[!] The handwriting seems rushed, dirt marks litter the note.\n[!]\n\"My savior, I have written, in haste! Jonathan has started to keep a closer watch on me since of the meeting, he may be suspicious. You need to locate a ruin, an old crypt which has a -\n-sword inside it. It is a hunter's weapon, a weapon of legend! The Draoidheil Marbhaiche. Ask around for old ruins, and do not enter alone. You will need a party of adventurers to progress... More details will come soon, justice shall be swift\n-Falgor\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A crumpled note", "[!]", "\"The blade which sings of tales of gold, it becomes your destiny soon. Though Jonathan keeps watch on the blade, it is his bane, after all... Please proceed with caution, more details are going to be outlined. But for now, I shall hope you have not -\n-forgotten the task I have given you. For, you will save a large amount of people from the Draiochta's torment. It lies beneath the ground, the blade surrounded by waters, blessed by them.\"\n-Falgor", ""),
        StaticBook("A Crumpled Note", "Anya", "*The letter is written in untidily scrawled handwriting, seemingly bearing a number of spelling mistakes and grammatical errors.*\n\nTo Aleksandr Carrion, Imperial Prince of Oren and Duke of Karovia,\n\nYou must know that the boy who gave you this letter is\nmy son. His name is Ivan and he is a blessed child, hardworking and unspoilt. For the last seven years, he has lived on almost nothing but bread and soup. Lucky enough to have survived his early childhood, I have often found myself fearing for his life.\nNow were he to remain with me any longer, he would surely not live to the age of forty.\n\nThe reason for which I tell you this, is that as much as I regret to say it, his father is also your brother, Yakov Carrion. Many years ago, I lived in Petrus, a\nresident of Shadow Alley. There, Yakov would often visit the local tavern, gambling and drinking away his father’s fortunes. At the same establishment, I frequently found myself trying for work and through a series of events, I was left bearing his child.\nAt the time, I dared not tell him for fear of my son being taken away from me.\n\nYet now I must look towards the future, knowing that the boy must never learn the truth of who his father really is. The life I can provide him with is nothing compared to\nwhat you can offer. Indeed I beg of you. Have mercy on his soul and take him as your own. He will not be of any grave difficulty for you to raise and bring in to live among your people. Even a bastard would live a better life than a street rat.\n\n- Anya.\n*Tears appear to have smudged the ink slightly at the bottom of the page.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A crumpled note.", "Unknown", "elvalah'akal thill kinal.\n\nelvalah'akal myumieral igne'sae ito Haelun'or.\n\n\n      kina ito Valah\n\n Maer'sae Hiylun'ehya. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dark Past", "Netphreak", "[!] A story, that never ends.. Everyday more words added to this series and everyday his own words come to life. [!]\n\nA lone Necromancer scans the tree tops for any sign that the 'one of the night' would be there, smiling down upon him with that \n-face that melts the roughest of hearts. Behind her mask, something dark and mysterious, something the lone Necromancer himself has come to witness.\n\n\"She wanders within the shadows, and upon the trees, searching.. For what though..?\"\nThe lone Necromancer.. A man of many faces, a man of many names.. So known to the world yet.. All they see is a vessel, the darkness that haunts him day and night.. Remain concealed within his mind.   \"The curse, will forever stay with me until my death.-\n-I've come to accept the fact, I can no longer offer my heart, for the rare times I have.. Heartache comes in return.\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer himself, sits within the tree tops of Lenniel, writing the story you read now, while watching the stars-\n-roll on by, looking to the soft sounds below, the insect life, sound of the water, even the echoes of the wind seem to tell tales of past times.\n\n\"The stars are beautiful, each one so unique, yet a sight we take for granted.. I've found myself many a-\n-time just, watching.. Beauty just outside of my reach, for a Beast cannot tame such beauty.\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer, once again scarred by another with a blind mission. To find the other Necromancers and destroy them. A hole in his right-\n-hand gives detail of the pain he took, to protect those who don't even acknowledge his existance.\n\n\"Bound by blood, although I loathe it, I must protect my bretheren, even if it costs me my life.\"\nThe lone Necromancer sits at his desk, next to the room of his precious and delicate Flower, to write down the events and continue the story.\n\n\"My heart aches, I long to seek her, although I've made promise... I must keep it, for her sake.\"\nA promise, something that should be soul bound, yet so easily broken, although this lone Necromancer takes promises seriously.\n\n\"A man of trust, although trust I've broken in the past.. I've still yet to fix, I'm only a mortal.. I can -\n-only do so much.. They expect much from me.\"\n\nWithin the shadows of his safe haven, he rests, he ponders, he weeps, he listens.. What questions come to mind.. Will that noose take him today? Will that Rosary Pea stop his heart? -\n- \"Many times, I've pondered how I would end my life, to keep the Monks from reforming my body, around a soul that should have never been created..\nI wanted to, I tried to even.. I have to stay strong.. For my little Flower...\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer calls out her name in the midnight hour, although no words escape his mouth, his curse keeps him still.\n\n\"This thing, this monster in my brain.. I can see their faces, eyes like a sea of emerald, combined with the 'one of the night'\n- A motherly figure, embracing the Flower as if her own.. How I wish for such a dream to become truth..\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer creeps through the night, without a purpose, wandering aimlessly.. Will there ever be light to this darkened soul?\n\"As a Necromancer, I find myself.. Around beings of the dark, but.. Sometimes I wonder.. If the dark beings are really the evil ones.. All we want is to be left alone.. And these people of 'light' scream theirs diety's name and slash us with their blades-\n-I can't see how we are the evil ones, when we do what we do to survive.. Yet, the ones of 'light' slaughter us on sight because of some false sense of pride, or perhaps... Fear.\"\n\nWithin the Necromancers humble abode, a room of-\n-steam, books and iron.. A room to simulate the very nature that a Necromancer steals, life..\n\n\"This room was never meant for one person, but to be shared, to have filled with laughter and tales of happiness, this..-\n-Will not come to pass.\"\n\nAs the lone Necromancer climbs into the pool, many scars exposed, some of ink.. A skull within a rose.\n\n\"Each scar, tells a story. Whether it be a hooded Elf-\n- using claws to cut the left cheek and forearms, or it be a lover impaling a shovel in the stomach.. A hole in the right hand, to try and expose the secrets never to be spoken.. Although, the scars that tell the best or the worst stories.. Are the ones -\n-unseen by the naked eye.\"\n\nA flip of a lever, the Necromancers' hand did manipulate, as the sound of a thousand horses come crashing down with a final 'clank!' To isolate, and keep safe the Necromancer within the steel cage. -\n- \"Visitors are rare these days, though it seems my kind of visitors are generally hostile.. Precautions have been taken.. Gates are needed.\"\n\nWalking through the forest of frost, the lone Necromancer unites with the Inferno-\n- A mission they both have, to gather the power of a nation of frost, such a thought seems impossible.. Although, the combination of Death and Inferno proves too much for any political power.\n\n\"We, have influence in a nation of frost-\n-it wasn't too hard, although I can't help but feel a bit of loyalty for them.. The thought crosses my mind, can I find purpose here?\"\n\nFrom above, a creature of darkness screeches down amongst the living.-\nA predator, watchful and swift flies through the air, with a letter in its husk.. The last to be sent with meaning and promise, a ring lay inside to signify the last promise.\n\n\"It was.. A day of confusion, I found myself in a situation that I could not-\n-comprehend.. The 'one of the night' stood there in front of me, hand extended.. Her face was cold.. It was empty, almost... As if Death itself was manipulating her actions.. Someone succumbed by the pain and loss of loved ones.. I cannot blame her..\"\nThe daylight shines upon the ground, yet the lone Necromancers face remains a shadow, a pair of bloodshard eyes watching, scanning, manipulating.. \nA face once filled with joy and peace.. Now cold and dark. -\n- \"It wasn't always like this, the days were like any other, sunny, rainy, hot or cold.. The obscure side, that only very few know about.. Remain concealed, some things the rain cannot wash away.\"\n\nWithin the walls of a newly built Conclave the lone Necromancer rests upon a tree, writing down the story..\n\n\"Some areas are peaceful, and quiet.. Whilst others, even with silence speak horrible stories..\"\nAnother day, another mystery, another adventure, even though for the lone Necromancer that adventure is of domestic grounds. Although he has run into 'the one of the night' to see the Oceans of turquoise and emerald.\n\"She was... Different today, we held an embrace and I couldn't turn away, to invest whatever of my heart I have left.. It seems like something I've missed my entire life. Love is something that I've never fully understood, it's something people speak of-\n-all the time but yet.. It's power is beyond that of the gods. Should a Necromancer like myself feel this emotion? It's so intoxicating.. I find myself wanting to just please her, make her happy.. I wish I can.\"\n\n\nAt the humble abode, the lone Necromancer readies his new tactics against any possible form of attack.\n\n\"For security reasons, I'm sure you know I cannot write down my exact measures, I'm sure you would understand.\"\nAt the City of Walls the lone Necromancer spots an unusual child, silent, brave, tough. Her eyes almost screamed for attention yet, she remained quiet and attentive.\n\n\"This child was... Interesting I should add, it was an unusual-\n-encounter, I've never had such with a child before.. She actually reminded me of myself when I was a young boy, my mother would always tell me to stay silenced when being spoken to.. I saw this in that little girl, she finally spoke after we've had the-\n-battle of the stares.. She said to me, 'Those who I care about deeply.. Are my family.'\n\nHow I can relate to this little girl.. As the only one's I have left as family, are the closest to my heart..\"\nThe lone Necromancer sits aside a warm fire, the 'one of the night' across from his view as he writes. She is soothing someone in a very calming manner..\n\n\"I myself would have not used such measures.. But I think I should change for the better.\"\n-------------------\"I fear I don't have much time left, Battou has gotten stronger whilst myself weaker.. I fear, those I love will outlive me, and my absence will cause them pain.. I would love to say I lived a good life, but I would be lying..... -\n- I have come to find joy within my life, I consider myself extrememly lucky that Poppy and Lilith found it worth their while to know me.. I think it's safe to say we brought a little joy to one anothers lives...\n\nI guess... This story will have to end-\n- As we all have an expiration date set.. I didn't think my time would be so short, but I love the ones in my life.. Lilith, Poppy.. Heck even Joe..\n\nSo, my final chapter.. Until Death Do Us Part..\n\n[!] Pherak's Signature [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dedication", "Hreidmar Strongbrow", " -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n Carve for Me a Rock\n \n      A Dedication      \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHreidmar Strongbrow\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI want to build a hearth\n\nA tribute for my new kin\n\nI need your help,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve again.\n\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI need a place of shelter\n\nBeneath the skies of blue\n\nI need desire,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve for you.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI want to keep my craftsmanship\n\nWithin your holy\nfount\n\nI need the strength,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve your mount.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI have to keep my heart\n\nSecured in my new home\n\nI need the will,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve a dome.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI need to feed my\nmind\n\nAnd ensure it is overfilled\n\nI need knowledge,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve the hill.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI need to build a door to you\n\nAnd hold it with a\nlock\n\nI can't do it without you,\n\nCarve for Me a Rock.\n\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("A Diary", "Anonymous", ". . .\n\nDay 832: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks.\n\nDay 833: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks. Chopped wood.\nDay 834: Had tea. Ran out of crumpets. Hunted rabbits successfully. Played with rocks. \n\nDay 835: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Rocks went missing. Tended farm.\n\nDay 836: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Rivel split apart, torn asunder by arcane forces and floated into the sky. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks.\n\nDay 837: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks.\nDay 838: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks. Tended farm.\n\n. . .", ""),
        StaticBook("A Diary", "Griffon \"Greenfingers\" Trowelpot", "*The diary reeks of rotten cabbages and ancient parchment. Many of the pages are ruined; only two entries remain...*\nEntry 7568\n\nThe weather here is getting worse...I've been hearing strange noises, both from inside and out. I think there is something in the swamps... Something different...\n\nMaster's been working on an experiment. I'm \nnot quite sure what it is, but he says he will need my assisstance within the next few days.\n\n*A sketch has been drawn here of what looks like a brewing stand*\nEntry 7569\n\nI am on my way to the lab. Master says it is time for me to help him with his experiment.\n\nI don't want to ruin any of my nice clothes so I have taken my old coat that I wore in my wandering days.\nMaster has told me to document his experiment.\n\nHe says his work involves some leaf of alabaster, a blistering toad and mandragora as well as some other things that are too complicated for me to scribe.\n\nHe has got all of these things spread across the \ntable, and he has asked me to sit down.\n\nHe had asked that I bring a club of sorts; I brought the one I used to hunt that boar all those years ago.\n\nHe is holding it now, I assume that he will be using it to grind up the asd   iohasd     aisudh  .....\n*The entry stops abruptly, all traces of further entries have been ripped out. Drops of dried blood are dotted about the final page, accompanied by the smell of Tippen's Root*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Diary & Story", "Lyra", "This is Violetoins Diary!\n  \n\nIt is my real diary.\n\nYou just bought this book!\n\n\nMany copies will follow if this book sells well. Then i shall start writing useful books!\nDear Diary, Lyra is trying to kill me! If you find this i'm probably already dead! \n\nSomeone help! Anyone  just dont let Lyra find me!\n\nOh No, she's coming...\nShe's going to k...\nHello, this is Lyra. I like following Violetoin all around. This book might be useless. Indeed it is. Still i shall write a story at the next page. Thanks for shopping!\n-=-=-=-=--=-=-=-=-= The Evil Bird\n    \n        &\n          \n          The Alchemist\n------------------- Written by Lyra Moonstone\n-------------------Copyright is probably owned by Lyra.\nOnce upon a time, in a little, little town a bird was sitting on a tree next a big wheat field. The wheat field was laying next to a few houses and a blacksmith building. Many people were strolling around carrying logs and stone. The people of Astruagan \nwhere building the town since they started it last month.\nThe bird sat in the tree on a twig. It was one of the rare species. The Mad Chicken. Its so rare you can only see it in special trees! So a few days later, someone new joined the town. \nHis name is Joseph. He was an Alchemist and made potions for everyone in town. Everybody was healthy until the Alchemist went chopping trees to get more logs for houses. When he started chopping the special tree of the bird Magma\nMagma jumped out of the tree, pecking on the man's head. It started to bleed heavily and he screamed for help. Everyone ran to him and helped him. He died later. R.I.P. Joseph\nA message to Magma. Bad bird. \n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=  \n\n\n\n\n         THE END\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("A Draft Speech I", "Andria Ith'ael", "Greetings Mali'thill ulliran,\n\nAyelmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya'Haelun'or I hereby withdraw my challenge for the position of Sohaer. I request that those who voted for me vote for who they truly believe will cause maehr'sae hiylun'ehya better\nthan I. I shall remain as Okarir'mali, provided Elheial'thilln let me. I wish to attend... \n\n[!]The writing seems to become messy before abruptly stopping", ""),
        StaticBook("A Fish-Scented", "The Lord of The Fish", "*Distorted words are scribbled onto the page, large blotches of water blurring certain sections*\n\nDear Gazadiel\nI am worried about the water...it feels...different... Only yesterday I was taking a swim and a great shark came at me \nwith hatred in its eyes...not a hatred that is natural...\n  It is a hatred brought about by something very dark...something that has come from aoihsd oihasdioh oihaosind oihasihd ihasd \nI went to aiojsd iohasdiohdiojmsjoijsdoij what I\nfound chilled me to the scales...\n   Beware of the sewers...they contain giant vicious man-eating fish!\nTake care, and may the light of the pufferfish lead you along the right river..\nYour Friend,\n The Lord of the Fish\n*The entire letter reeks of mouldy fish*", ""),
        StaticBook("A folded note", "Gerald Elgan", "\"Brothers, I apologise for the hasty depature. But the Aeldin sect of the Sparrow has called upon me. Since Robert's departure, I have been called upon to train in these lands and help other follow the path. Shall I lead back to my old roots, eh? Do not-\nthreat, nothing is an eternity. Except ol' Adeon, bugger never dies. When I get back, if this isn't as bustling as the old sect in Kaedrin, I may have to throw some fisstech at poor pigs. Atlas, Morris, Delonna, Adeon, Ikur and Valahan. And of course the\n-chivay. You have served me well. Ensure the next generation is primed up for the job.\nFarewell, may we meet in the future.\n\n-Gerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("A Forest Poem", "Nivndil Duskhollow", "Puerith'leyu.\n\nThe trees they stand,\nA clamour of souls.\n\nTheir voices born on\nWinds, are old.\n\nBoughs up high,\nFairy halls.\n\nRoots below,\nSilent foot-falls.\nThey stand and wait,\nFor times unborn.\n\nTo whisper secrets,\nBefore words were forged.\n\nAmongst their trunks,\nBeneath canopy dome.\n\nTo bathe in twilight,\nThe trees my home.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Formal Request", "Majystur Laurenzo", "\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*       A Formal Request\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*          Dedicated To:\n\n      The Courtship of\n      Lelien Aeléyèlsa\n&       Zeus Ith'ael\n\n\n\nUpon the birth of your precious offspring, I request permission to sacrafice it to an unnamed god, or unseen evil presence at the peak of Dun'Suldur.\n\n\n\nAt the completion of the sacrificial ceremony, I plan to promptly dedicate a song upon the forsaken organ to the bonding of your child's soul, and that of the unquenchable lust for chaos of the iniquitous phantom.\n\n\n\nDo you accept this proposal?\n\n[] Yes.\n\n[] No.\n\n\n\nI patiently await your response, and hope that you find my proposition reasonable and acceptable.\n\n\n\n*The message would be left without a closing signature, nor any other signs of who initially wrote it.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A found Journal", ":", "An Itharel's journal:\n\n\nIt's interesting really, even after ascending to a height of Demi-Godhood that many a Valah would dream of and many a Mali, Uruk or Bortu might envy...I feel little difference and yet I still fear it. The loss of my soul...not the literal soul I remind \nyou...you being me in the future. I fear it because...well look at my cousin...I hardly see a scrap of him left in that hollow golden shell...\n\nSo starting from this day I'll note the simple things...the taste of bread, the trees...\nthe coitus, the masonry, the books I read and poems that made me cry...that way I'll have memories to cling to...the pile of experiences that define us as people and thus will save me. \n\nI pray my mortality does not leave me too quickly...I must also \ntell Mia...and Skale...and those ignorant of this matter. It's a saddening truth and a cruel one for them and myself...but alas it is so...\n\nI am bound by the chains of service until I'm cast aside.\n\n\nYet another is lost. I can't blame him, the stress is damaging and the sights can drive any man past sanity...or good...\n\nIt would have been me had I not *several words have been erased as if the reader couldn't decide*\nwell...if I wasn't what I am...\n\nSeems as soon as we lose one, we recieve a new one. One of Katari's creatures...now one of Hesh's....I named him grandmaster.\n\nThe new Cleric is Luna. Impure but...pretty...\nalas the frailty of mortality. Like a small sculpture of glass and china. Fascinating yet...so delicate.\n\nSo this Rose tavern is clearly going to be nutcase central, perhaps I can fix that....maybe not.\nI see interesting folk here, the Gwyn individual appears again...she seems less...brute-ish.\n\nAll sorts in here actually. Old faces and new...one of Ivanus' past.\nSo for those interested, this is how you can be an Itharel:\n1. Man up- Ivanus.\nWell...I would note that usually sitting on a Shrine's altar would be...most...cruel.\n\nHowever...this particular one is in Lenia's name...so I doubt she'd mind.\n\nBesides I'm a walking steamboat of Tahariae's favour\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("A gift", "Mariane'a Fournier d'Avenese", "I have walked across the land to find you the perfect wedding presant and I think I found it. Hope you like it\nlove \n-Mariane'a", ""),
        StaticBook("A Gift!", "Navarre", "Halflings debate long into frosty nights over the best methods to brew tea. I present to you my favorite type of kettle, a dark-wood carving. This will instill a rich flavor into your dark teas, thicken and sweeten your white and green teas, and deliver \nimpeccable taste to any brew you fill its walls with. \n\nEnjoy! \n\n-Navarre", ""),
        StaticBook("A Halfing's Tale", "Timothy McPatt", "~*~Prolouge~*~\n\n1st Deep Cold, 1461\n\nLife as a Halfling is hard. Don't believe me? Well, this is my own personal account of my life and such throughout Anthos and the Fringe.\n\nI suppose I should start with my birth...\n~*~Chapter 1~*~\n\nI don't mean to sound cocky, but you could say my skills were apparent at the first appearance of my naked body!\n\nI was born to a simple home in Lenfarthing, the son of a farmer and clothes maker. Rumors were always circulating around the\nvillage about Momma and Pappy making love so loudly that it made the Dark Elves shiver in their sleep. That made me a proud, little one.\n\nAnyways, on the night I was born, the clouds gave way to a stunning and vibrant light. Some say it was just a full -\nmoon, but I beg to differ! I think it was a sign that I'd be a unique child!\n\nWhen my Momma gave her final push, I slipped from the Doctor's hands and happened to hand atop an anvil. It was then that my destiny was decided! I'd be the best Smith in all of\nAnthos and the lands after! And, as you can tell, so I became!\n\n~*~Chapter 2~*~\n\nGrowing up in Lenfarthing is the best upbringing anyone can ever hope for. Filled with fishing, smithing, eating, music and anything else you could possibly want!\nI myself enjoyed playing the fiddle and fishing on warm, summer days. The winters were filled with smithing practice and educational skills. I was reading and writing at an early age, even writing the name of our family above our Burrow's door! Such fun!\nMy smithing skills were improving, and my father was wanting me to improve and learn to sell what I made. So, he began taking me with him to the nearby city of Kingston to help sell Momma's clothes and his crops.\n\nLearning to be an adequate salesman, I \nbegan searching for instructors in the art of smithing! Thankfully, Kingston saw many travelers, many being dwarves!\n\nLearning day to day with helpful travelers improved my skills and made me aquire a new assortment of useful mental tools.\n~*~Chapter 3~*~\n\nThe day finally came. The day I was both hoping for and dreading. Reaching a mature age, I told my parents I wanted to move to Kingston and help craft armor and weapons for the soldiers.\n\nMy father was strangely upset about this, telling\nme that it was not the best choice. He was a very peaceful man, and was fine with crafting things for show. But he knew that the tools I would make would be used for cleaving heads off and such. I was young and foolish, not even taking this into account.\nI began my life in Kingston by making simple yet beatuifully crafted tools and weapons for citizens.\n\nThe life was good, even taking me to far away places to smith! One time, i was even in the dwarven capital! Learned a lot there, I did!\n\nBut, like anyone with a sensible mind, I had to return home sometime!\n\n~*~Chapter 4~*~\n\nReturning home was met with warm hugs and kisses! Those of Lenfarthing hardly remembered me, but we are nothing without love!\n\nI noticed my parents were\nabsent from the crowds. I asked where they had gone to discover they had left to sell their items along the roads of Anthos!\n\nHow excited I was by this, yet still a little sad for not having seen them on my return home. But, of course I'll see them again!\nI didn't stay long, leaving back to Kingston to finsih up the orders I had promised. Then, well, Setherien came. And you all know how that ended, so... Fringe!\n\n~*~Chapter 5~*~\n\nWe all know how we came, here, so I won't waste your time there! Ha!\nEntering the Fringe, I did what most did; wander. For years, I wandered the lands and lived day to day on few coins and fruits.\n\nThe life was fun and hard! Even learned much about surviving out there!\n\nBut, eventually I realized that I needed some coin,\nso I seeked work in all of the lands. The only one were I was met with open arms was - strangely enough - Kaldonia!\n\nSer Mizu Silverblade offered me a job as his Houses Blacksmith! A grande opportunity! I was extremely excited for such a job!\nStarting off with mass orders of armor and swords, the Elders of the House were astonished at my quality and care put into making their gear. My first payment was 2,500 coins!\n\nI work there now, but of course the story ends when I want it to! Ha!\n~*~Chapter 6~*~\n\nWorking for the Silverblades has made life... weird. Between getting kidnapped, fighting and saving Orcs, my life has never failed to be interesting there!\n\nBut even with so much excitement, one must never forget their roots! That is\nwhy I returned to my people, currently living in Ivybend. Once more, they accepted me with open arms and even built me a cozy, little Forge!\n\nLiving a simple life is the best, and it is the path of the Halflings. I read, create and steal sheep! Oh, what\na life it is!\n\n~*~Epilogue~*~\n\nLife among our races are all different! But none compare to that of a Halfling. Why, you might ask? One, simple fact:\n\nWe live like we always have.\nNo war or politics get in our way as we live day to day with farming, smithing and other trades that make us a people.\n\nNone are corrupt or angry! We are who we are. And what we are... are Halflings.\n\n- Timothy McPatt,\n  7th, Deep Cold, 1461", ""),
        StaticBook("A Healing Lesson", "Lillith Winterleaf", "A Fundamental Lesson in Effective Druidic Healing\n\n~Scribed by Lillith Winterleaf, Sequoia Druid\nMy name is Lillith, the Sequoia Druid, and I was taught this lesson by my Guide back on Asulon, Jena, and it seems to have been lost somewhere along the way, so I will give this knowledge back to the Order, as is my duty.\nIt is an effective technique that takes very little strain on the Druid themselves as you only augment what is already present instead of drawing from your own essence. This allows it to be repeated almost indefinitely without the need for resting \nfrequently to restore oneself.\n\nIt is a simple bandage and medicine of a sort, but only in the hands of an attuned Druid is it potent enough to be an effective method of healing, and one does not need to be a healing-focused Druid to perform this task.\nAll you need is bonemeal and fresh lily root, and then a large leaf, vine, or lilypad. I personally have found lilypads to be most receptive and effective, but I have used all three successfully. You must grind up the bonemeal and lily root into a fine\npaste, add water as needed to reach a consistency of a thick paste.  If using a vine as the bandage, you need to butterfly cut it down one side and fold it open so it is large enough to serve as a bandage.\nApply the paste to one side of your chosen bandage and place it over the wound. You can use multiple such bandages for larger wounds, but keep them all the same plant or you will need to augment each separately in the next step.\nOnce the wound is covered, place your hand upon the center of the bandage and focus on the mixture beneath, asking the nutrients and life within to mend flesh and bone. You should feel when the mixture responds, it will grow lukewarm. You then focus upon \nthe bandage plant, asking it to aid in the mending and remain on the flesh until the healing is done. The plant should glow a faint green for a moment and then adhere to their skin, and you should be almost unable to distinguish where the edges of the \nplant end and the flesh begins, they should be quite literally fused.\n\nOnce this is done, there is nothing more to do but wait for the wound to heal, this usually takes an hour or two for most wounds. If there is significant muscle damage it can sometimes\ntake a day or two.  Once the wound is healed the bandage should release itself and fall away, it is perfectly normal for the skin beneath to take on a greenish hue for a few days until a few layers of skin have been shed.\nYou should be able to perform this task many times without tiring, as it requires very little from the Druid, the energy needed is drawn from the living essence of the mixture and bandage. If you put more energy and focus into it, the speed of healing is\ngreatly increased but this will begin to draw from the Druid and will tax you after only one to three uses, depending on the skill and fortitude of the Druid.\nOther substances can be used for the mixture, I have experimented with many substances and have found bonemeal and lilypad roots to be among the most potent and most readily available ingredients,\nand I usually use lilypads as the bandage as the pad is left over from harvesting the roots anyway.\n\nI highly recommend having bonemeal in your mixture if possible, I have found every mixture without it to be far lacking in potency, sometimes\nwith no healing effect at all. Always include bonemeal when possible.\nOther viable substitutes to the lily root include:\n-wheat (fresher is better, over an elven week after harvest seems to reduce its effectiveness.)\n-Tippen's Root\n-Halfling's Grass\n-Blaze Powder (makes the mixture sting to the touch, painful to the recipient, use sparingly)\n-Cactus Green (makes the mixture odorous, strongly so, but is fairly potent.)\n\nThe only viable replacement for bonemeal that I have found to be just as effective in mixtures lacking bonemeal has been living slime, usually found in swamps. This can also be mixed with bonemeal for the most potent mixture I have found, \nusually halving previously stated healing times. However, slime is rarely a readily available ingredient and so should only be used for the most dire of cases if available.\n\nThis is by no means a comprehensive list, other substances can be used and I have\ntried others, but they generally were not strong enough to make suitable replacements. All flowers were nearly pointless to attempt.\n\nI hope this helps many of my brothers and sisters in the Order. It is a fairly simple task and one I feel is a vital base\nfor any aspiring healer, as I know from personal experience how taxing Druidic Healing can be and how much it can take from you if you are not careful.\n\n~The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Winterleaf", ""),
        StaticBook("A Journal", "Anonymous", "Day 1: Today I begin my trek to Mount Thahn, the colossal mountain in the centre of the world. It is an intriguing target for scientific study as it is a frozen tundra, yet is surrounded by temperate to hot lands. This is a\nmystery I shall solve, and which will catapult me to recognition in the guild and that fool Havery will finally see me as a proper rival.\n\nDay 3: Arrived at Mount Thahn. Was rudely thrown out of the dwarven\ncity built upon the upper slopes for attempting to enter the Remembrancer's library. Apparently the dwarves take issue with having their doors broken open with axes, but they shouldn't lock their knowledge away like that! Not\nfrom me, anyway. They can lock it away from Havery all they like.\n\nDay 4: A little prospecting soon deduced why: the mountain stone is rich in thanhium, a heat-absorbing ore. The ore has many useful \nmagical properties, including use as a power source for enchantments. I will hire some miners at once!\n\nDay 5: Sadly, setting up a thanhium mining operation could prove difficult. The dwarves have\ndiscovered and claimed the thanhium. All of it. They haven't actually dug it up, but a foul smelling dwarf informed me at swordpoint that it's all theirs. Should I attempt to steal it from under their noses, they'll likely respond by\nby force of arms. I will search for a place where we could potentially mine the ore without them noticing.\n\nDay 8: I discovered a cavern today. It seemed to warm as I went down, as if the thanhium\nwere... missing. Surely there should be more of it as one goes down? It's as if it's already been dug up, but the dwarves live on top of the mountain, not below it. I will venture deeper tomorrow.\n\nDay 9: I found\na huge door at the end of the cavern. It looks dwarven, but different, like it's centuries of architectural development ahead. Could the dwarves have developed time travel and invaded the past? I wouldn't put it past them. That being\nsaid, stealing their time machine and claiming it as my own invention... Forget beating Havery, this could send me right to the top! I must open this door...\n\nDay 13: No luck opening the door.\nDay 17: Still no luck opening the door. This sure is a low technology door for future dwarves, though.\n\nDay 20: It has occurred to me that the future dwarf theory is, to put it as the orcs would, a load of\nskah. The door isn't a future door, it's an ancient one. Have the dwarves devolved? I could believe that, they must have lost their brilliance with their height. Still no luck opening the door, but I suppose we could tunnel around it. Heard\nwhat sounded like people skulking around.\n\nDay 21: This discovery is remarkable! I can't write it down in fear that I will lose these notes and Havery will steal my discovery. We collapsed the\ntunnel we dug and I will hire a full expedition to loot this place. We need to get out quietly though, as the dwarves are onto us. I've heard they can be so quiet that they can sne\n\n*The journal stops abruptly here.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Last Testimony", "Felix Pyre", "It was John Vilcan. He was the one who did this to me.\n\nI was helping Laurinia with something in her house when suddenly I blacked out. When I awoke I was on a bed in some basement, missing my tongue. I saw him face... John was there with a knife in hand.\nI was able to push him off me before he did anything more, but when I was about to tackle him, something struck my face, not sure what, not sure who did it. But I suspect Laurinia...\n\nI need you to do me a favor... I cannot live like this, I can't recover\nI need you to end my pain, my misery. But you need to make it look like a murder, otherwise the Monks will not heal me. There is a knife on the table beside me ((There's actually furniture down here lol)) When you're done, burn this note.\nBut memorize its contents in its entirety. I need you to explain everything that I've told you... Then we find this bastard and we end him.\n\n((Just erase everything and leave the book in my mail instead of actually burning it, I wanna keep atleast one.))\n\nFor- Alfred Orris", ""),
        StaticBook("A legend is born", "Shel'Yar", "At least I have chicken.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Azorella", "Dear Ah'Visaj,\nIn the interest of providing various educational opportunities to the general Meritorious, I wish to request a number of brewing stands for any student who wishes to pursue practical knowledge in the alchemical arts.\nA mere two stands should be adequate for this purpose although ingredients will later need to be procured. A Will ((atles)) of Alras appears to be willing to supply both. If possible, perhaps you could contact him? He is familiar with myself and should\nbe eager to trade if such is requested. I have a small supply of minas, about 750, at my disposal if some funds are required.\n\nahernan llir,\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya,\n-Azorella Coulissante\nOkarir'indor", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Edward Dustin", "Dear Madame Carys Dexeraux,\n     Hello, I am Edward Dustin, vassal of the highly esteemed Vladovic House. I've noticed your beauty from afar many-a time when visiting my younger cousin, The Grizzly. I had wanted to speak to you sooner, but hadn't \nworked up the courage to do so until recently. I wished to make known my intentions of courtship to you, to get to know your pleasant self better. I'd be delighted to spend some time with a delicate flower like yourself, and I believe it would benefit\nboth of our House's standings should this simple courtship turn into something... more serious. Should you want to inquire about my whereabouts, I reside within the Vladov keep nearest to the main stone road. Feel free to send a carrier message. \n- Edward Dustin, second oldest son of Yukanol. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Aenor Calithil", "*The handwriting would seem vaguely familiar*\n\nIsabella  Flormai, or rather Deathsbane,\n\nIt has taken me many years to get to this point, to forgiveness. I have denied, bargained, been angered, and now i am ready for forgivness. We had\nmany, many good years together, before things started to fall apart. I remember when i first heard that Aislinn had taken you, and I feel as though that is where it began to decline. \n\nI understand that I am not completely innocent in this matter. It was \nthis that took me many years to realize. I did not place myself in your shoes, not realizing what it must have been like for you. I left without any notice, without any word. I was gone, and you lost faith. Do I blame you? Not entirely. \n\nI returned, \nthough, do you remember? I tried to make you love me again, and I thought I had succeeded when you said you'd wait for me for twenty years \"As you did Kalameet\". Yet it didn't take you a year to leave me. Why? It is a question I've always wondered, yet I \ndo not have the answer to. I have an idea, as stated before, but not entirely. \n\nI do thank you though. You raised my child when I could not, both physically and mentally. You also aided me, helping ease my mind when it was at its worst. You also\nmended my leg all those years ago in Kalos. Do you remember Kalos Izzy? Back when the world was easier, free of worry, of pain? I wish it could have stayed like that. But we all had to grow up at some point, didn't we? \n\nAnd now I ramble, reminisicing of\ntimes which cannot be brought back, as much as I wish. You may be asking what is the point of this letter? I suppose it's that I forgive you Isabella, after all these years I forgive you, and I am sorry. I am sorry for all the grief I caused you back in \nAnthos. But these are probably just empty, aren't they? I wish I could say this directly to you, but Mithras does not believe you would be willing. Maybe some day I shall see you around Leyulin, and should you wish to speak, I suppose I will be willing.\nVan'ayla, Isabella. Ame nae evareh.\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter.", "Rose Little", "*the text is very messy, with scribbles and ink spills and the occasional spelling mistake*\n\nHi there Jacob,\n\nI am here hoping you could do me a favor, you will be paid of course, but let me explain first..\n\nI have recently bought a bakery, here, in\nPetrus, plot a5 on Market Street. The official opening ceremony has not happened yet as not everything is 100% ready, but it is still open in case there are hungry mouths to feed.\n\nI need menus written, and I was hoping you could write them for me? You\nwould obviously be paid, I was hoping you could propose a price though, as you are the one doing the work. I will provide you with all the details and everything that you need to write.. so no worries there..\n\nIt's not TOO urgent, although I would like\nthem AS SOON AS POSSIBLE! I will willingly pay you extra, for faster work.\n\nOnly one copy is needed, on a book like this (of course much more neat and professional!).\n\nThe details are still in the works, as I need to arrange supplying the ingredients..\n... so I will give them to you when I receive your reply.\n\nSpeaking of which, please reply as soon as possible.. just put your reply in my donations box outside the bakery please.\n\nAnyway, hope I didn't leave anything out.\n\n\nYours truly,\n\nRose Little.\n\n===== + =====", ""),
        StaticBook("A life..........", "Lurk", "His body lay there with his guts torn out, I stand at the back watching our leader as he tears bits of his skin off and eats them.\n\nHe pulled out a slimy liver of the man and slurped it down his throat!\n\"T'ats what yer get fer tryin' ter assassinate me'h yer focks\"\nhe said with bits of kidney spewing out his mouth!\n\"A'h loike ter eat me hostages alive,\" he smiled a creepy grin.\n\"He chewed into the mans face tearing away the muscle and cheek bones.\nThe man screamed for his life, his voice boomed over the forest.\n\nOur leader dug his nails into his face ripping it open a bit more, He started to swallow the flesh until we heard footsteps nearby.\nThe leader rubbed some blood over his chest and pretended to be dead, the rest of us fled behind the trees.\n Orcs came out grunting, \"Oooh look at t'at we got ourselves a'h dinner.\"\nI took my bow off my back and aimed it at one of the Orcs, I slowly put the arrow on and Fired at the Orcs head.\nThe orc fell down with a loud slam.\nThe rest of us jumped out killing the other 2 Orcs.\nOur leader got up and thanked me then kicked the Orcs bodies to see if they were really dead.\nWe walked back to Petrus and our leader went into the Tavern, his blood stained outfit caused some curiosity, so people were\nasking if he was stabbed.\nHe didn't reply to none of them who asked, but instead slurped his Ale, I guess to get the taste of Internal Organs out of his\nmouth.\nI wandered out of Petrus and headed to the streets to the Temple.\nA man named Arthur stopped me and guided me into his Tavern, owned by Vinnie The Chef.\n I brought a couple of Ale's and stayed there writing, until I noticed a little girl\nwalk through.\nI decided to make a joke \"Yer 'ere fer Ale?\" I said, unfortunatley the father didn't take it Swell he told to the daughter to go\nplay outside onto the porch.\nHe started to get angry so before he could punch me I decided to punch him straight in the nose, blood dripped down from nostrils\nas he stood there holding it, tilting his head back.\nHe told me to get outside so I withdrawed my sword and was ready for a fight.\nI looked at him angrily, A women poked me with her sword and I can't remember much after that apart from he put his hands onto my neck behind me.\nArthur told me the story later on.\nI decided to walk back to Petrus and go to my Leader, but 6 Elves stopped me they wanted my swords, my bow and everything I had\nin my bag.\nLuckily for me, my group wasn't far behind the Elves and they came out of the trees chopping off the Elves heads, blood squirted\neverywhere.\n((Okay that is the first part of my Journal I will make the second one soon))", ""),
        StaticBook("A loose paper", "Unknown", "§L         __      ,-/\n     .\" \\ `.   / (\n    ( \\\\`\\\\_|_;   \\\n     \\\\ _,' // ) ``)\n      `/ // /// ',/\n      (// /_,'_,-'\n       `'-'.l_l_\n\nT͜HESE͡ AR͡E ̡NO͞\n  ͝RAM̴B͟LING̷S\n\n  ALL ҉IŚ LOS͡T͞\nT̶HĘ AE҉N͡G̕U͏L͢S ͞H̸AV̨E LEF͝T U͠S\n\n    _\n__(.)<\n\\___)\n             _\n         __(.)<\n         \\___)\n\n       _\n   __(.)<\n   \\___)\n     (_(\n    ('')\n  _  \"\\ )>,_     .-->\n  _>--w/((_ >,_.'\n         ///\n         \"`\"\n\n THE COCKATRICE\n       COMETH\n\n     THE BONDS\n    ARE BURNING\nBURNING  BURNING", ""),
        StaticBook("A Minor Test", "Athe'lor", "As thanks for mentoring me, I offered to teach you the language I have been studying as of recent. The Cervitaur, Plazea taught me only a few words of her language, albeit I believe I have discovered on my own how to re-create words myself; keep in mind,-\nthis did not take me very long, and I do not expect it will take you very long either. Your task is to speak the phrase I am going to write  for you, after you manage to turn it from Common to Cervitaur. \n\n\"Your name is Athe'lor.\"\nOn the following pages will I write down a few of the words I was taught, and I will include only the words necessary for you to dissect and learn on your own properly. \nYou - Yui\nWater - Wedas\nLanguage - Lelriera\nSometimes - Runadainar\nGoodbye - Ruunfirra\nNo - Lu\n\nI truly believe that with these words you can discover how to say \"Your name is Athe'lor\" If you manage to succeed in this task, I will-\nreward you by teaching you the language as promised. If you cannot, I shall merely wait until a time when you can. This offer extends until the day I pass into the void, where Aegis awaits me.\n\nTo Tiuth,\n\n-Athe'lor.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "Robert Mallister", "*The small note read*\n\n\"The father of Regina's Child is Guy De Bar, and currently resides within his castle\"\n\nSigned, unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "Teyvani", "A note:\n\nGreetings Mages' Guild Representatives, I am Teyvani, a mali'aheral who is seeking to learn more about the ways of Magic.\n\nI have been trying to teach myself \nsome fire evocation for what seems like a month, but to no avail. I was wondering if your organization would accept me as an 'apprentice' of sorts to be taught.\nThank you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "BrandNewKitten", "Dear fellow Arcanist,\n\nI am sure you are well aware of the rampant outburst of magic through our realm. I tell you now that I fear it. Such a surge of magical mana and in such a concentrated location could lead to a cataclysm.\nIt is here that I write to you to explain my fears in hopes that you will head my words. I have bestowed upon you and one other the knowledge I have pulled from the void. It has been referred to commonly as Arcane Evocation and mana manipulation.\nAs I have explained the magic deals with pure magical energy in a very pure and volitale form. It is this energy that I fear could destroy the realm if not handled with care. I fear that the magic might grow and the extreme surge of \npure energy will cause a rift our world and the void.\n\nI ask that the meeting of the true arcanists be brought forth. \n\nIatrilemar of Lin'evaral\nKalameet of the Mages College\nand Titania, High Princess of Malinor.\n\nWe shall discuss the terms of use and set up boundaries for ourselves along with discussing how we must keep it's existence relatively secret or at the very least vague.\nI hope to hear from you soon.\n\n-Iatrilemar Elervathar\n\n((PM on the forums. Meeting can be IG or on the forums. I am fine with either))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Viktor 'The Grizzly' Dustin", "Neighbor. Edward is not a bad man, nor is he usually a liar. If what Rickard said is true, he was trying to impress you because he most likely felt inferior to you. I am certain that he wouldn't try to say anything untruthful without good reason.\n\n-Grizzled Bear", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Damasus Visaj", "WKH EXWWHUIOB KLGHV ZLWK WKH KDOIOLQJV.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "Taynuel", "Decorate your office, it looks boring~\n\n:*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Nicolas Fireblade", "\n\n\n\nYou have commited crimes against your people, you have    been marked for death.\n\n\n\n\n\n  The blood of our enemies\n           shall be spilt.\n\n*a bloody handprint is here* \n\n              We know.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Anonymous", "*The pages seem to be written in a near-illegible scrawl*\n\nBark of iron, deep in the south. The rip in the world that we must embrace! It gives gifts! It gives wonderful gifts to those who serve!\nA blade most perfect! So perfect that it does not belong in our world!\n\nAll it takes is a few drops of blood! A few drips from your wrist, and it shall awaken! And when it does, it will look upon you with\nsuch favour! The sweetest favour! It is an impossible thing, but it is a wonderful thing! Seek it out, brothers and sisters!\n\nSeek it seek it seek it deep in the south, for amongst the Islands of the\nAnkulos Peninsula, it waits for others to appreciate its luminescence!\n\n*A second piece of writing by a different hand is scribbled below the first*\n\nDo not trust it. The tree is evil in a\nway that I cannot comprehend. Take only its first gift, and then never return.\n\n*A third piece of writing by yet another hand is scrawled at the very bottom of the page*\nTake nothing from it! It wants only to consume! It consumes everything! It will consume you! I can't get it off me I can't get it off me I can't get it out of me only flame will end it\nBurN th TrEE\n*The writing trails off to nothing*", ""),
        StaticBook("A note.", "Kalenz Uradir", "Tiuth may take the Meteor.\n\nElsohaer.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note...", "Vladimir Tahorran", "Dear friends,\n\nWith the departure of my dear husband-to-be, I feel as though I can no longer remain in this city. The area holds too many memories for me.\n\nAs such, I have chosen to depart in search of a new home.\nI take only a small handful of food and a tent under which to sleep to aid in my journey.\n\nI bid you all farewell.\n\nSincerely,\nVladimir Tahorran", ""),
        StaticBook("A Page", "Anonymous", "The 5th of Snows Maiden, 1302\n\nWe, the Order of Nine close upon the sanctuary of the heretic known as Ezekiel Cunningham. He appears to have sealed himself in an underground cave of sorts.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Painting", "Immortal of Soth", "--------------------------------------------____--------------/      \\-------- ----/         \\------- ----| ~     ~  |------- ----| O /  O   |3------ ----|  /_       | ------ ----|            | ------ ----\\  \\__/   |------ -----\\______/------", ""),
        StaticBook("A Parchment Roll", "The Soothsayer of Argul", "I COME TO FOREWARN OF DEATH, FOR IT IS IMPENDING. [*The words are scratched into the parchment, the non-specific threat crudely scrawled.*]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Peculiar Paper", "Damasus Visaj", "This paper seems to be thick and made of a hide... It has the texture of a human skin. \n\nThere are three circular symbols at the top, and words written in blood towards the middle and bottom of the paper.\n\nIt reads:\nThe one that signs this paper vows to teach themselves the magic art which created this same contract. \n\nIn two years if the one who signed does not feel that he has learnt enough, will have his eyes rot and fall from his sockets. \nSigned with a drop of blood.\n\n-A drop of blood sits on the hide of skin, obviously signed. -", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem", "Anonymous", "The Great Serpent of Earth and Stone\n\nAn unquenchable thirst for earth and stone,\nIt sits down low beneath the soil,\nFar beyond the mortal’s reach,\nWide it may open its vicious maw,\nWide it may open its vicious maw,\nShaking the mountains as it moves,\nIt slithers far off and devours many,\nBeware the Vermianae, children of mine,\nFor it asks not even a name before it turns dwarven\nflesh to gore.", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem", "Patriotic_Fool", "Roses are red,\n\nviolets are blue,\n\nI flay people,\n\nthe end.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of Nature", "Baine", "Nature is what we see,\nGeese that form a V in the sky.\nThe pedal of a flower that wave good bye in the wind.\nA wood pecker that pecks to no end.\nThe wheat that waits to be harvest and sold at the untold shop.\nThe tree that can spare no more but a \npear. \nNature is what we hear\nThe tree's branch that falls on to the abandoned ranch.\nThe clucks of chickens when they see a wild dog in the fog.\nThe hiss of a cat when they've found their prey in the ray of light.\n\nNature is what we feel.\nThe thorns on a rose bush that over grows.\nThe moarnful rabbit that's fur rubs against your leg.\nThe tall grass that is vast.\nThe tree that maybe gone soon.\nThe roots that someone played the flute on.\nNature is beauty. \nThe flower that grows in the sight of delight.\nNature is life or death.\nThe vultures that threaten to end the rabbit's life with one nasty bite.\nThe deer that lies injured near a wild dog unable to see through the fog.\n\nThe luck that a duck has when a hunter can not swim.\nNature is everything.\nA tree in the meadow that is ready to be carved into a bow.\nThe bird that sings to all beings.\nThe giant mushroom that grows in harmony near ebony.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of Nature", "Endrai Denthrular", "A poem of nature\nBy Endrai Denthrular.\nOh great tree and forest amongst the main circle       How strong your bond must be with the druids that co-exist with you\nYour leaves are as beautiful maybe even more beautiful than the ones at the Spring Circle near Haelun'or\n\nAnd your roots, deeper than any grove in all this world\nHow great your bond must be with the druids that reside with you.", ""),
        StaticBook("A poem.", "'Allastor'", "A poem.\n\nNature is beautiful.\n\nFrom a very small ant.\n\nTo a very large tree.\n\nNature is beautiful.\n\nFrom a pretty flower.\n\nTo a funky fungi.\nEveryone should see.\n\nFrom a pile of rocks.\n\nTo a bundle of leaves.\n\nNature is beautiful.\n\nFrom a prickly cactus.\n\nTo a very smooth stone.\nNature is beautiful.\n\nWritten by: No Name.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Prophecy", "Amarie Deathsbane", "Heard this Prophecy at the Standing Inn:\n\nProphets- \"The Fallen One moves against you... The Fallen One readies... his sizzling ill humane unholy fire may set upon you as his test comes to a close... The Fallen Daemon Galah, he exits the words of the \ntruest of evils. Khorvad may on the soonest reveal true might, the brimstone and hellfire of old. Many of you are merely Decsendants of the frightened that fled Origin, the Origin was consumed by his hatred, and his hatred will consume many a land more...\nGreatest of the Daemoir! Foe of Ibless, Galah lend me thy ear! Lend me thy mouth!  Lend me they echoed ramblings of old!\"\n\nGalah, the Daemon- \"The Prophecy of the eldest Aenguls, Kaegan shall fall. Kaegan shall burn, the Ancient Ones put to rest once and \nfor all. The Fallen One has tried to break it, but he shall fail, he shall fall upon one of you in the room's blades... Some of you will perish, others of you will stand in harmony, one of your blades has the ability to pierce the Fallen One.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Recommendation", "Valmir Audane", "To whom it may concern,\n\nI am a career mage and a man who has studdied the arcane arts for nearly a century but I have always had close ties with the druidic order.\n\nI have recently met a lad named Felix Reed.\nThis young boy was very passionate about the order and knowledgable of the inner workings and tasks of the druids.\n\nWe have been conversing for a lengthy period of time and I am pleased to say that this boy is the type of person I feel\nrepresents  the druidic order very well.  Should I set my mind on whether or not I give up my magical studies for that of bound with nature that may be obtained through the Order Felix would certainly have been an aspect of my decision.\nIt is with nearly three hundred years of experience behind me that I would say he would make a great addition to the order.\n\nSincerly,\n~Valmir Audane", ""),
        StaticBook("A Remark of 1501", "Silv'ar Vanguard", "The Founding of Tahu'nor\n\n1500 Sun's Smile\n The Elves of the Valley went to the Salvians to ask to make sure their land was not going to be taken from them and a deal was made for there continued ownership of said land\n1500 The Deep Cold\n A Salvian's begain to complain about our land and wanted to change and move our homes from the valley. We created a deal to allow them to do this and for our homes to be move furter down in the valley. Though this deal was void due to \nthe man who made us this deal while being a part of the Salvian goverment did not control said land even though concessions had already been made on our part. The man's name was Tahjeet mumbee, Note this name may not be correct. He offer was a lie and he \nknew that he did not have the power but he wanted our homes moved and we thought the deal was a true so we did only to be meet with great angry later on by the Syndicate leader.\n1501 Snow's Maiden\n The Syndicates leader had become more more unreasonible and after two more deals had been made and made void he simple wanted us to move off our land and move into the city. Though our leader had had enough of the salvian's lies.\n1501 Malin's Welcome\n Ante'ame approched the learder of Salvus to try and end this madness for a deal that would last and could not be made void with out exetreme cause. Though there learder, Who's name I can not think of. Was not a man who wanted to make\nany consesions to us and wanted to us to obey there wishes. This was the start to an event which lead to our breaking away and forming Tahu'nor.\n\nDuring the meeting above Ante'ame's advisor was murdered in cold blood by the Salvian's. it was complettly\nout of no where as our we were about to agree to a deal with the Salvian's. Now of corse this is what I was told by Ante'ame.\nIt wasn't till I returned home that I saw the horror of the salvians... Our leader was hung by her arms of the brige connecting \nSalvus to our cliff. The syndicate learder with help from the Salvian leader's guard hung her there, to only be cut down when a I arrived. I questioned the Syndicate leader he simple lied to me telling me that's what she wanted. After her fall she was \nnot awake so about 20 or so minutes after she was cut down she begane to shout from down below. I of corse was still talking with the mad man of a leader. Hearing all of this he told me to stay he would go and helper her. Of corse not beliving him I \nFollowed him down only to see him try and killer her again.  I stopped him just barly and thanks to a mage who will not be named for his own protection Saved her. This marked the event that went to far we acted.\n1501 The First Seed\n We formed Tahu'nor\na Elven town on the cliff we're we lived and we sent a letter to the salvians with a offer we did seek peace but we were only met with swords. They came and killed all but one elf who was able to get away by -\nclimbing down the cliff face. He went to Oren for help because if he did not the other's would never be safe and our freedom would be short lived. Oren offered us protection as long as we joined the wood elven state under Orenian rule.\nWe found the terms \nto be quiet favorible to our death at salvus hands and soon enough Oren declared war on Salvus and we won our freedom. \nSnow's Maiden 1502\n Tahu'nor made serveral deals with the syndicate clearing there learder and his guild. Though at this point I was sent to petrus to only come home to Tahu'nor being gone and all the other elves dead.\nThis is the Story of\nTahu'nor and her people.\n\nMay 1501 Never be forgotten. May the Martyr Salvus made never be forgotten.\n\n-Silv'ar Vanguard\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Report", "Alderiki", "The Advanced on a Door Forever Sealed\n\nWe advanced upon the great doors of Urguan last night to find them sealed entirely. Reports from our spies within the area assured us the dwarves would not\nseal the door for their strange soul rending machine they call “The Seal” had consumed all but a fraction of the city’s populace, by order of the dwarven government. These informants did tell us that some remained at the\ngate, a skeleton crew who they believed were to few in number to seal the great door. Evidently, they were wrong for when we arrived we came across a hall which was impenetrable. Those left inside had seemingly\nprefered to leave themselves to the horrors within, rather than answer to our eldritch might which would bring them justice for their crimes.\n\nBeyond the wall, sickening screams were heard for days, and then\nsilence. What brought them their final descent into death remains unknown to us. Was it thirst? Starvation? Or something far more sinister which lurked within?\n\nFor days the most powerful of my\nkindred assaulted the wall with the elements: Fire, earth, wind and water but nothing could break its eternal watch. And so, days later, we left. The war had been won, but the mysteries which lay within the walls had forever been\nlost.\n\n-Alderiki", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "Avern'len", "===================\n\nDarkness, fear, even pain have long been foreign to me,\n\nNow I am just an unnatural stain, dead as a cut down tree.\n\n===================\n===================\n\nYet, friends, in the name of love, I've fought the stigmas set.\n\nFor the sake of my blue eyed dove, an oath I shall not easily forget.\n\n===================\n===================\n\nA promise made beneath the birch, upon our humble mountainside.\n\nAnd so I wish to resume my modest search, and overcome this unnatural divide.\n===================\n===================\nWhat proof is there beyod simple words, perhaps my protection over your woods.\n\nI stood against dragons, Harbingers, and Scourge hordes, a dire trial by simply mere swords.\n===================\n===================\nAllow me to retack the path, my former kin, to reach enlightenment, attunement, take a totem- even then.\n\nI wish to atone for my involuntary sin, and take the path to Druidism again.\n===================\nA Request\n\nAvern'len San'taelah", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request .", "Rilkor Niwarsay", "-------------------A Special Request\n------------------- From Rilkor Niwarsay the Loyal\n\n   I have heard of many reputable blacksmiths of the lands of Athera. My father was a blacksmith himself, skilled in his craft he made many a blade.\nAlthough this may be true, I am in sure of a worthy blacksmith to uptake my special task at hand. Not only will I be requesting a blade forged with legendary craftsmenship, altered to be able to defeat even the best of swordsmen, but I am also offering a-\n-chance. A chance for you to make a name for yourself as the most grand of all blacksmiths to walk the lands. If you wish to uptake my task, as I will pay you with not only renown, but with what I can offer as material payment. Whether that be minas or-\n-priceless items of fortune. It is all subject to whether or not you want to prove your skills.\n\n   And so he spoke, and if you wish to uptake the task, that is up to you. By means of contact, you have my name. See to it and become praised.\n--------/\\----------------/--\\--------------|-../\\..-|-------------|-..|.||.|..-|------------/--|.||.|--\\----------/--/-@}--\\--------/---]-\\.'.---\\------/-//[=__=]\\\\-\\-----\\--|[|[|\\---/:]:]:--/----|--\"\"\"./\\/\\.\"\"\"--|-----|/============\\|----|\\------------/\n*Etched into the previous page is an unfamiliar house symbol, much like the coat of arms of the Old Apostolic Kingdom of Aesterwald, but different, featuring a white eagle overlayed infront of a Sword. The eagle holds a scroll in its claws. It reads:-*\n\"Loyalitat gegenuber der Gerecht, Mutig auf die Starke, Ehrenwerte auf die Integer.\"\n\n\"Tapferkeit vor dem Feind.\"\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A Ruined Book", "Iron Seals the Book", "Brethren, my alchemical studies into the forgotten beasts has gone mildly well. My travels in the other land, though, have brought us a wealth of information.\n\nI wish to make contact with you soon, however the hours draw dark, and I must depart to  \nmake the final arrangments. \n\n\nLive and be Reborn", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sealed Book", "a sticky substance seals the book", "I have arrived back from my journeys amongst the frigid lands. Many thoughts have been had, and many things were learned. Our kin is different, and my time with the ice snake taught me even more about their heros.\n\nOur old friends, the \nIrehearts still thrive, and I learned much about them. Their loyalty is still flickering, and is possible to flare up again. Their governing body seems weak and feable, my time with their hero gave sight to this.\n\nWhile with the \nworshippers I saw much. I learned of the new generation that see as we do. It is too bad that our Ice Dragon was corrupted once again, he was one of the stronger ones we had purified.", ""),
        StaticBook("A sealed note.", "Delonna", "King Maric.\n\nIt is with great displeasure that I am unable to deliver these in person. \n\nWhile hunting the Hydra beneath the Embermoor with my Marked Men brothers, I was gravely wounded.\n\nI'm told the Clerics did -\n- their part, however will still be recovering for a long time. \n\nThus I hope this reaches you well, and that you may put it to good use.\n\nIncluded are a number of enchantment scrolls, arrows, and a basic enchanting table which I will give instructions -\n- for using.\n\nMuch of the magical energy required has already been applied, so you should be quite capable of applying the enchantments as you wish.\n\nSimply place a single single on the enchantment table, and you will be able to imbue a piece of armor -\n- with little effort.\n\nAttempting to apply more than one will result in the enchantments conflicting, negating one. \n\nAttempting to apply the enchantments to Carabarum based armor, or already enchanted armor will require an experienced enchanter.\n((Put the book in the enchantment table and shift+rightclick it while holding the item you want enchanted.))\n\nI hope these are of use to your cause.\n- Delonna.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sealed Scroll", "Caliph Faiz Kharadeen", "Dearest David Campos or any Salvian official,\n\nI hope all is well within the nation of Salvus, may prosperity continue to reign over your lands! I bring you news over the terms of allianceship between our two humble nations.\nThe council meeting of advisors has just finished, and I write this letter fresh after the meeting. \n\nThe council unfortunately have come to the decision of declining any sort of allianceships/defensive pacts\nat this time. 9 against the idea of a defensive pact while 3 in favor. It is a unanimous decision, I am afraid. \n\nEach one has brought up convincing arguments agianst a defensive pact, such as how both our militaries are not prepared\nfor warfare, and the many disadvantages to going to war if it comes to it. We spoke long and plenty on it, and I have to agree with my advisors on this. I am no leader if I desregard what my people want. I am sorry.\n\nMay peace be with you and your people, perhaps in the future things can turn in a different direction.\n\nSigned by,\nCaliph Faiz Kharadeen\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("A short journal", "Mercenary", "1505     Fjólar Stigrssøn\n---------------------------------------\nToday I found a city with lucious crops and kind people. I have found out that they were recently pillaged by Oren and there armies. While I was in Siegrad the Lord was rude as expected.\nHe seemed quite eager to get rid of me after I revealed that his father was responsible for my fathers kidnapping. I make this accusation based on Oren's symbol. It was the same on on the letter when my father was kidnapped.\n------------------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("A Silver Writ", "Eleron", "I, Eleron Haler'Ante of the Ancient House Sylvari, do hereby grant the Vanguard Elrolas the ability to recruit Lumi'drim and commission uniforms, within reason.", ""),
        StaticBook("A slim grimoire", "Unknown", "     ＦＡＬＬＥＭ´ＲＯＣＨ\n       ＢＨＡＫＴＡＬ\n         III\n  III     I     III\n   I   I  I  I   I\n   IIIIII I IIIIII\n     I  II II  I\n     II  III  II\n      IIIIIIIII\n        IIIII\n        IIIII\n        I I I\n          `     '\n           [!]\nAn odd grimoire with tattered black leather\ncover sits in your hands. By the looks of it, it probably has something to do with magic, but the entirety of the book is written in an odd language that aches the head of those who can't read it.\nHazk,\nmerin'gnu vegaati zu'nokion. \n\nRe'nokion talsh vokarl\nya'pelosr therthe'pelosr-bhaktalserthek-unkra zu'gathan.\nE\nOdurnur blothr zu'kraemsal\n\nDu\nPelosr'basular koneg\nqsuzph'dvemd\n\nDo'nekaro kuram savurr'zu bhakthal.\n\n[]  []  []  []  []  []  [] \n\nKraemsal lerikah odurnur ubyz'fikt koneg vurrsht-chelion\nil do'jhorvastur \nsavurr'vegaati qsuzph'dvemd\n\naza uvot, do'varsku -\nO'ag'vokarl\nE\nDo'odurnur bhatti'dvemd\n\nDu\nDo'kree haurz qsuzph\nkon kreoz'bhaktal\n\n           [!]\n  Pictures have been\n  drawn alongside the\n  instruction.\n            [!]\nThe first picture seems to have an odd lump of rock.\n\nIn the second one, some sort of hollow figure has been molded from the ore.\nVe\nDo'kree thur'hadan\nfhi al'kraemsal\n\n   o  -->  ö\n   O        []/\n\neg zmask, a'kyoni Kha.\n\nCul\npelosr'basular koneg'qsuzph\nZin\nDo'infinst qsuzph egodar burz'fhi yatha\n\n\n     Undere dayn!\n\nqsuzph lerikah ezg saiz undere aldunr lerikah al'kraemsal.\n    ö \n  \\[] -> ,;     ✔\n            [!]\nAnother set of pictures are on the side. In the first, the figure is made to resemble a kharajyr.\n\nIn the second one, the kharajyr shrinks considerably in size.\n\n\n\n\n\n             ☬\n\n\n\n\n\n                   -1496\n                   - Z.C.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Spark", "Athe'lor", "The Founding of Electrical Evocation\n\nSalamandra (or Regaki, I should state), founded Electrical Evocation in a year not known, though was approximated to have been sometime during the races stay in Elysium. However, the tale stretches backward into \nthe deep roots of Asulon, where the possibility for this, all began. \n\nRegaki was the violent, and dangerous figure that was a terror in the night for the common man, elf, or dwarf alike. Never was his skin shown, and this caused many to believe he was a \ndemon, manifested, or perhaps the physical embodiment of the tortured soul of a great wizard, returned from the grave to slay all mortals. Nonetheless, a hooded figure left a note for Regaki, knowing it would be found. The directions on the note lead to a\ngrand, isolated tower where the robed figure would wait for him. Atop the tower did the shadow stand as the demon approached, rain and thunder battering the two of them with no effect. Rock, fire, and water beckoned to the command of the ghoul, -\nshattering the defenses of the robed figure; yet, still, the robed figure appeared to refuse to fight back, aside from casting minor defensive magic to protect himself. It was apparent Regaki would triumph, but in the last moment, bolt of lightning \nreigned down from the heavens, attracted to his golden mask. With ear-piercing howls and shrieks the demon squirmed as the gold melded to its face, until Regaki fell silent.\n\nWhen he awoke, he could not feel his face. He touched it, but the gold was hard,\nand no matter how hard he tried, the mask would not yield from his head. \n\n...And so some great time passed, before Regaki could be called Salamandra again. With extensive research into his mask, it was concluded that the lightning's energy had been\nabsorbed into the golden pieces, at least somewhat. Over time the mage found himself able to draw this energy from the mask, and bend it to his will. Before long the mask's power would wane, however, so he made it his obligation to create electricty\nhimself. The Undead had been capable of doing it in very large quantities, so perhaps he too could create lightning, albeit not as efficiently. \n\nThis was the founding of Electrical Evocation.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Strange Letter", "Ouity Deathsbane", "In the heart of the first home, so long ignored\n\nRests a doorway which time has decored\n\nWith vines and a waterfall,\n\nThe skeleton key reveals our true past.\nHave ye what it takes to join in this rite?\n\nThat ascent or descent depend on your plight,\n\nGo now, seek quickly, for ye hear the call.\n\n*A diagram of the massive mother tree\ndecorates the rest of the page, while the sun shines brightly over the main section, the trunk and canopy, the underside of it is shroued in shadow, and barely discernable. A few simple diagrams of a femur bone rests beneath.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Study of Air.", "The Scribe.", "A Study of Air.\nAir has always been a curious element. It is said to be the element of the free-minded. Those who wish harm upon others and seek to delve into chaos shall not find themselves working with the air around themselves easily as a manipulated\nelement. Now, as many of you prospective mages are probably jumping up and down, I am going to say now; This is not a book on how to learn Air Evocation. It is merely a study of the properties of air observed over time.\nAir is a gas. Much as when water is heated to a boil it turns into a gas, air is constantly in a gasseous state. However, the boiling temperature (temperature at which liquids turn to gas) of air is far, far lower than any witnessable temperature upon any\nrealm the races have currently visited. I believe that if we visited a realm where air was a liquid, it would be covered with insurmountable oceans, and we would all drown.\nAir moves from high concentration to low concentration. Upon working with a bellow, I was able to pump more air into a box than currently resided with in. After opening the box, a breeze was produced. The opposite was produced upon\nusing a bellow to remove air from a sealed box. A slight breeze was created blowing into the box. \nIf one places a leather bag into a large jar, and seals the bag upon the lid of a jar using thick rope, one shall find that pulling that bag up from the jar\nis a difficult task. This is due to the amount of air within the jar. The air on the outside of the jar is exerting force due to its concentration, while the air on the inside is extering less due to its lack of concentration.\nThis is also an effect of \nsuction. The lesser amount of air tries to pull air to it to equalize the concentration, but it cannot pull the air through the leather.\nAir is finite. There is only a certain amount of air within a certain amount of space, and that air can be exhausted through breathing. \nAir is comprised of multiple elements, though I do not know what they are. This was a rather unfortunate experiment to test. I locked a squirel in a contained box, and then submerged the box underwater. Obviously, the animal died as\nthe air in the box ran out. But, when I opened the box underwater, bubbles were created, leaving me to believe there was still gas located in the box. The question is, if the squirrel inhaled all of the air, what was left?\nI hypothesize that \nthe lungs of creatures only use the majority of air to breath, and other trace elements are left over as they are not needed by our lungs.\nAir can absorb heat just as a solid or liquid can. Upon heating a rod and holding it in a room, the space around the rod remains heated, obviously, but when the rod is removed from the room, the air within the room is still heated.\nThis next section is comprised of recounts of scientific interviews about air.\nThe properties of air are weight, color, density, air mass and pressure.  ~uncited mali'aheral. ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Thank You Note", "Faye", "Thank you for your time and the ability to stay in this room.\n\nI ower you but I don't know when I will see you.\n\n~ Faye", ""),
        StaticBook("A Theif v1:book1", "homijoe", "Clerics\n-Theifs guide\n<vol. 1\n\nLenfarthing farms,\nacross to the homes and over the two bridges, one made from Oak and thinned branches, another made from a tree root itself..\nA third, leading past..\nThe Dark forest, spiders amidst and mushrooms and webs of great, holds the trail of which to follow. Mages live here, up the stone hilltop to \ntheir home. Sheep's wool, a farm, and a gatehouse with streaming fountains of crisp water.\nThe second gate, may not always be open, be weary of guards and mages about. The stove rom, on the right... two store cuboards guard chests with simple single padlocks, a trapdoor leading to the great storeroom..\nGuarded by many a locks of steel...\nTo the left, a homely passage with a golden chest without any locks atall... an easy find.\nStraight through past the shrine room, a chest stands in the center... Locked but within holds armor of gleaming iron infused with light abound. Staffs and Axes too\nLastly, the barracks... homes of guards and tennants mustered about carelessly. Doors unlocked and chests unstowed, and easy pick of litter when it comes to fine linen or apparel worth stealing. The masters room is guarded by doors and padlocks.\nDifficult\nOn your travels....\nbe stealthy, speak to noone, if perchance you are caught....\n\"I wish to speak to the master of this establishment on a merchantry business offer...\"\n\"Perhaps I may stay longer?\"\n\n-Spriggar Stormhammer\n\nCompany Owner and servant of his Kingdom of the Dwarves\n\nUntil we stand, we forever hold ourselves as fools, frightened, weak..\nUntil we fight we will not be free.  *1445", ""),
        StaticBook("A Token", "Salamandra", "Snowy peaks and mountain tops did guide the lad on his way; through wretched cold and face-freezing snow was the price that he had to pay. Although the path was broken and battered, his robes soggy and tattered, the boy continued on, and his spirit never \nshattered.\nLong had he waited, oh yes, to rejoin the Mages Guild. Ambros as arch-mage, missing before, had returned, and he was thrilled. Months did he stay there before the guild came to fall, then the boy packed his things, his miserable rings, and flew\noff on erroneous wings. Abominations took the guild, so the boy had nowhere to go. Nothing to do, no friends to turn to, the boy would wander where he did not know. Darkness and shadow followed him, wherever the lad went, until a being of bone sucked out \nhis soul, and the threads of fate were sown. Regret, sorrow, and anger, filled his narrow frame. He hurt not a soul in his madness, though his death was assured, all the same. A cleric ended the lich's existance, though the bones did not fight back; and \nso is the story of the clerical order's high prophet, braxis's false glory.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tome", "Anonymous", "The Stonekin\n\nThe Descendants of Urguan were a hearty people, sturdy in form and idealogy. With this, of course, came those who were a tad too zealous for their own good. with a culture and lifestyle idolizing\nthe mountains and rock, there came a group almost religious about their love and adoration for the peaks of stone that were about the lands. With this exaltation for hte strong and grand, this group turned more passionate\nthan expected; the loose collection of arcane artists within the cult gathered with the most devout and ardent to the order of Faith of the Mountain Leaders with an idea that would further their works, believed\nto bring them to divination. They tried to make the perfect being, and after several decades of experimentation and testing, something was made.\n\nThe Faith of the Mountain\nproduced numerous of these creations after their original birth, seen as the most true and correct embodiments of their emotions for the glorius mounds of compact perfection.\n\nThese supposed\n\"supreme beings\" were far from so, but anyone may think what they will. In truth, these men made one of the first collaborations of the natural elements into an entity; an elemental. These beings are the\ntrue works of stone masonry in its most primal and gruttal fashion. Morphs shaped of pebbles to boulders, these things lacking sentience were none the less exalted and glorified, called gods and avatars\nfor their creative powers, able to format all things earthen. Although, they were correct in partial; they represented the mountains, the rocks, the unmoving and forever tough. And it was so, the Stonekin outlasted the children of\nUrguan. It is said that, to this day, they remain in the last shrine of the Faith of the Mountain, home to the last trio of Stonekin, the elementals forever locked away in their own tor, a crag made just for these three men\nof gem and subsurface grain.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Traitor", "Thomas Broderick", "Subject 1: Screams the Barry, whispers mumbling voices to himself and gets unconsious easily.\n\nSubject 2: Broken knee from a warhammer, squeezed thumbs. Blue eyes, blonde and he said his name was HELP!\nSubject 3: Thomas Broderick, a traitor he screamed for help yet not realising that he was underground where no voices could be heard.\n\nI cut off his ear and left it to bleed he was unconsious for 2 hours until he awoke.\n\nI grabbed him by the throat and punched him in the nose. He pleaded mercy but I took an arrow and placed it gently in the fine strings of the bow and shot at his Crotch. He screamed in intense pain, blood dripped down his trousers I smiled as I saw his \n\nface.\nI made him sign the book and then I scooped out is eye balls with a rusty spoon and plopped them in a jar. I sewed a pair of buttons there instead. \nI forced him to sign his signature just before I performed the surgery.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Treatise", "Aluuvia", "    When we are born we are placed on one side of the divide or the other.\n    Only the Creator's first were in the grey and not all still are.\n    We feel ourselves pulled towards one side or another. And if not pulled we are pushed away from one, by \nit's own inhabitants.\n    It is wearisome to be alone on one side of imbrication. To think that that above us may be lurking in the murky in-between.\n    And so we pull our Gods over as well, giving them places and powers and loves and hates,\nand all the mortal fallacies and things Gods care nothing for.\n    When we make our Gods more like us, do we make them less like Gods? But what many refer to as such are merely the Creator's First.\n    His first Creations.\n    But perhaps they do not mind so much.\n\n\nBeing named Gods.\n    There are reasons not to wander towards either horizon.\n    To the East it is bright and distanct. Pleasant to be sure, a luminescence that works it's way under the skin, into the being.\n    One can make no objections to this and wonders who could.\n    To the West it is dark and silent. \nComforting to be certain, a gentle stillness that calms the bones, the mind.\n   Another can make no objections to this and wonders who could.\n    Then there stands those who have crossed the border.\n    Those who have been both East and West, seen the sun rise and the sun set, and settled upon one or the other.\n    Then there are those who have crossed the border.\n    Those who have been both East and West, seen the sun rise and the sun set.\n    And settled upon neither.\n    We sat ourselves down in the grey in-between, where the sun never rises and the sun never sets.\n    But it's rays are not of light nor of coming dark, in the middle where we lurk.\n    I have watched people come and people go. Some have stayed to linger, others left too soon.\n    Many more simply walk right over me, never looking down as to them I make no sound, no noise nor purpose to be heeded.\n    I cannot say I blame them. It is loneliness in the place where two things meet but neither be. Sometimes it feels there is no one here but me.\n    No one wants to be alone and so no one wants to linger here.\n    If others embrace the light, you may too.\n\n    If others seek the dark, you may too.\n\n   For some the light blinds, wherein the dark they find solace.\n\n    For some the dark frightens, where in the light they find safety.\n    But the light blinds me and I find no solace in the dark.\n\n    The dark frightens me and I find no guardian in the light.\n\n    I was not born here, in the middle grey in-between.\n\n    Here I shall stay.\n    It is easy to find excuse, a circumstance of birth. Sunrise or Sunset, a preference is a choice.\n\n    Not an affliction.\n\n    Not a disease.\n\n    We just make us in-between.\n    Then there is North and South. Still and shifting. They are neither East nor West, sunrise nor sunset.\n    For the few that pass from East to West, South and North is a horizon all must cross between.\n    But there are those who don't.\n    There are those who linger.\n\n    Those who cling to the South refusing to pass the border, relishing the warmth of the sun and the cool breeze.\n    Those who wander the North, walking though all else around is still and silent.\n    At the very center there is that and in and of that are they. We pass through but do not linger for as we pass we are not even cognizant of doing so for the sake of never really being there.\n    And of those some may push against the veil that cloaks that center, pressing this way or that, North and South meaning nothing to them, but East and West of significance, for that is where we are always regardless of all else.\n    Some seek those by sunrise, others those by sunset. They reach out and they reach through, invisible to all, without a face or flesh or bone. They set us about, against the other one's, pick us up and drop us down.\n    We are reflections of them, in our search for power. Some of us in our judgement.\nOthers in our reach across the horizon, ever searching for companionship to join us, on our side of the divide.\n   Here I benefit, in the in-between.\n    For here I may simply stretch my arms out to either side and offer my hands.\n\n\n\n    And I know in time someone will always place their hand in mine.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Verse", "Anonymous", "The boarman walked on the mountain high,\nTo the altar they built long ago,\nHe knew in his heart twas his time to die,\nFor the shaman said it was so.\n\nBut his heart did not race in fear,\nHe knew why he must now go,\nUp on the slopes of the mountain high,\nTo the altar they built long ago.\n\nSick we was not nor old in age,\nBarely past his twenty-first year,\nYet he went to the altar to gods of\nrage,\nOf flame, fure, fire and fear.\n\nHe climbed upon the icy peak,\nThe altar lay just ahead,\nIt was time to discard this body weak,\nHe would die but would not be dead.\nHe carved the circle in frozen mud,\nIn the center of a dwarven bone,\nHe marked the ring with elven blood, Intermixed with the thanhic stone.\n\nHe struck the ring with his ancient spear,\nAnd the altar lit in voidflame,\nThe thanhium burned purple and clear,\nAnd thus over the mountains it came.\n\nHuge white teeth and huge black wings,\nHellish thunder in flight,\nArchon of terror, devourer of kings,\nThe dragon flew through the night.\n\nThe boarman stood with spear in hand,\nAs the mighty beast did near,\nHe stood in thanhic ring of flame,\nHis heart devoid of fear.\nThe dragon swooped and in one sweep,\nConsumed the boarman whole,\nBut this was not the sign of boarman weak,\nFor this battle was of the soul.\n\nThe dragon writhed, its mind\naflame,\nTwo minds fought for control,\nThe beast did falter in infinite pain,\nConquered by boarman's soul.\n\nVictorious he roared with fiery breath,\nHis new wings took\nhim to the sky,\nAnd then he tumbled and fell to his death,\nFor boars know not how to fly.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Warning", "फ़थेर् अच्मेद", "य़ोउर् किन्द् इस बुत् फ़िल्थ्. \nथे दय ओफ़् योउर् देस्त्रुच्तिओन् इस अत हनद\nओउर् अर्रोव्स् शल्ल् ब्लोत ओउत् थे सुन अस थेय रैन दोव्न् उपोन योउर् पितिफ़ुल् लिवेस\nथेरे इस नो एश्चपे\n\nवे अरे चोमिन्ग\n\nआल्लहु अकबर ", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wish", "'Finek", "I wish for the land that was my home,\n\nEvery rock, and every stone.\n\nFrom where the water ever flowed,\n\nFrom where no greater kindness was ever shown.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wish", "Tenyalenya Chamfhaer", "I wish to become a mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("A wish", "Tippen Oaklend", "I wish to know what my totem will be when I become a druid, and when will I become a druid?", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wish", "Rilkor Niwarsay", "   \"Even though there are many things that I could wish for in this moment in time, I wish for great fortune and success to my children. Even though I was not there with them in the time of their infancy and childhood, I could not as I was a man of-\n-great valor of Aesterwald. At the time, Aesterwald was at war with many. I feared for my life as I slew many men. I only wished for the day that I would meet them later on in life. I am not sure how many more of my sons and daughters there are out there-\n-but, I have met two of them so far. They are more than what I expected. Prodigies of myself. Even though it does not seem that I should believe in this wishing and luck /thing/, I do. And so, as I toss in this coin, I wish for great success upon my-\n-hopefully everlasting family name. May the Niwarsays live on. Große Tapferkeit, Große Ehre,\nGroße Gerechtigkeit.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A wish", "Aerion", "I wish to have eternal life.\n-Aerion", ""),
        StaticBook("A worn diary", "Sillice Nightingale", "Day 1 of the journal.\n\nI met a small elf named Leyun. She saved me from a room I was locked in. She helped me remember Aeras who I promised I try and remember. She then told me he visits this other circle. I still dont understand two circles. Or druids \nbut she led me here where I met a druid named Izzy. She had white hair and yellow eyes and was very nice to me. This person named Art was here too but he seemed to sad. My name is Sillice from what the others tell me and I forget things. I just hope this \ndiary helps me..\n\n5th, First Seed 1493\n\nI found Aeras again and remembered him. It took me a while but I did it. I...still cant remember anything in my past though. A strange human came into the grove. he frightened me then\nattacked this weird creatured that wandered it. It was made of mud and looked like a woman. but the mud didnt attacked back and actually looked scared. I do not know what to think.\nDays have passed..months..now years..only memories I hold lie within this diary of mine. Even now, I cannot even remember why I hold onto it so. The name 'Aeras' in my mind yet like an echo, its been slowly fading away. I wondered back to what looked like\na grove, but it was charred and the air hurt my lungs. I started crying, but I didn't know why. So I left and kept walking. \n\n\n1st Malin's welcome 1498\n\nIt's nice here. So many beautiful things in this small grove. There is another further down the hill. Even the elf city looks nice. I might look around some more to see if I find what I am searching for. Aeras....who is he?\nI found a small village. Oakhearth is the name. Its so nice and peaceful here. As if I were in a dream. I felt like I was being watched then a high elf appeared from the trees. She was so beautiful and elegant. The Owl Druid is what she called herself.\nDruid....it sounds familiar. She was very quiet then gave me one of the houses here for me to live in. I didn't want to impose on her for a place yet she dissappeared once more. I felt being watched again yet somehow I wasn't afraid. Like protected. \nIt's summer. The little farm within the village is so beautiful with the wheat growing. I was trying to harvest some when a male elf started talking with me. Adorellan..that was his name. He looked familiar yet I didn't know why. Like a friend long lost \nto me. He knew me and of my past. He then told me my real name.\n'Winteer'\nThat name...it scares me, but I do not know why. He took me to the druid grove and then I remembered, he took me before and hurt me. Forcing me to remember something I did, but I\ncouldn't remember. Those eyes still scare me. Haunt my dreams. He said his sorry to me and wanted to help me get my memory back. He went to the druids up on the tree. The tree was so pretty and beautiful, almost like a dream. Lillith, that was her name. \nShe was angry and was going to hurt him. She was frightening me. I thought druids were suppose to be friendly...Adorellan lead me away from her and we left the tree.\nDeep Cold, 1499\n\nI guess I haven't written in here in awhile. I have such interesting adventures it would seem yet I can only remember on paper. I am currently tending a farm in the dwarven lands....I think? I am unsure. It is quite cold here\nbut I do not mind so much. It's peaceful. The word 'Druid' again. It appears I am always finding them. My memory is slightly returning. I remember the villege I live at and I visit there often. A merchant just moved in there. I hope he likes the place as \nmuch as I do.  \n\n\n\n13th, First Seed, 1503\n\nI recrieved a letter today from that high elf that helped me. I am starting to remember people some. I was asked to bring some crops to this cleric named Ramza at the druid grove. He was friendly.\n  \nThis place is so dark...a voice. I followed it here. A voice of distress, echoing from this cave. getting louder as I drew near. The voice I could make out more. The sound of a female in distressed. I called back but all went silent for a moment before\nshe started calling again. The cave was dark but I hestiently went. I want to help. It was so long and deep then I tumbled and fell and here I am...where? I don't know. like an old library of sorts. A cave-in it appears happened here. No one has been here\nin a long time. I dont think I can get back up the rumble, but that voice...its soothing and soft. echoing in this room...calming me, but I can't find her. Perhaps i will look around more when I recover some more from the fall. I just hope my bread last \nuntil I am able to climb out of here or someone is able to find me...", ""),
        StaticBook("Abandon", "Chirr'taliame Mantisuku", "Abandon, \nChirr Mantisuku\n\nYou left me when we were young.\n\nLeft me with my falling tears.\n\nI felt like I was no one.\n\nFor so many painful years.\nI cried at night wishing you were there.\n\nHow could you do this to me?\n\nDid you not see how that was unfair?\n\nLife was a horrible mess.\n\nMy heart so bad I couldn't rest.\nFalling tears that fall.\n\nShow that I've been through it all.\n\nThe cause you leaving me.\n\nWe are together now but it isn't the same.\n\nHeart aches and you are to blame.\nIf you saw me crying maybe you'd regret what you've done.\n\nRight now I will live my life as no one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Abstract", "[Sohaer] Kalenz", "The Valleian'Acal of Larihei and the effects on the physical body.\n\nLomanih et al.; Malin's Welcome 198\n\nIn this paper we will attepmt to categorize, without searching for too through an explanation, the effects of enchanted\ngold-infused pools. We will begin with the physical alterations and come to accept that continued exposure to the pools will only lighten one's skin and hair tones while potentially increasing a subject's height. We see that neither of these effects are\nharmful to the physical body.\n\nWe will also conclude that these pools bolster an Elf's magical prowess and their natural talent to channel the Tanya that flows through our earth. We will illustrate why this increased acuity only has\npositive effects, and the suggestion of hallucinations or a clouding of judgement is beyond preposterous.\n\nFInally we shall discuss the benefits of bathing in the pools and encourage all of Malin's pure children to do the same.\nThis shall be done by introducing a concept known as the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, which will be the driving philosophy behind our arguments.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ack Toran", "Agor Floreck", "===================     To my Firstborn\n        son Sarco\n            [!]\n The page is stained in teardrops, and written in red ink is \"To Dargrind, my new heir, rest in peace Sarco. Cratus ack paz.\n       GENESIS\n===================Goren cratus ack mundo ack carraig, aquis, infernus, ack aer. Goren cratus arbor ack carraig, aquis, aer, ack vita. Goren cratus bestia ack carraig, infernus, aer, ack vita. Goren... *the rest of the page is burned*\n            [!]\nThe next few pages of the book are burned, or torn out, until the 13th page\n*this page his torn out\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is torn out*\n*this page is burned*\n  AUTHOR & HISTORY\n===================The author of this book is Agor Floreck, who lives in the small town of... *this part is covered in blood* with his children Sarco, Dargrind, Kip, and Goreck, *the next few lines are covered in blood as well* \n            [!]\nA small note flutters out of the 14th page of the book, which is charred and burned. The note reads \"By order of the Uruguan, this item has been confiscated and it's owner hung for herecy, -signed Norid Grandaxe\"\n   *this page is covered in blood, and is charred in burned, but the word Ack Goren, Corpus ack Brathmordakin! can be read, and it's translation, For Goren, Death to the Brathmordakin!", ""),
        StaticBook("Ack Toran", "Dargrind Floreck", "Irst, Goren cratusari ack carraig, ack bluud, un ack vita. Goren cratusari ack arbor ack bluud un ack vita. Goren cratusari ack structa ack vita un carraig. Goren cratus ack bestia ack bluud un ack carraig. Goren cratus ack alves ack bluud un arbor.  \nGoren cratus ack Dwas ack bestia un ack vita. \n    EN ACK GENESIS\n*Goren has decreed that the next chapter be translated into Common*\n\nAfter the Genesis, the Dwarves and the Elves lived in peace, that was, until the void was discovered.\nThe void is what was before our realm, that of Goren, and contains all the pure energy that our world was born from and into. From this void the Elves who tapped into it found immense power. They dominated all the tribes of the world, and soon, called \nthemselves gods. They soon forced their people to bow at idols of them, the most horrible crime, and used the void to control those who dissobeyed. In the beggining, the universe was young, and the void was full of uncontrollable power. Corrupting power.\nOne Elven King became too ambitious, he gathered and enslaved all Elven mages under him, forcing them to tear open a physical hole into the void. He wanted to be able to draw all the voids energy into him. and use it to challenge Goren, and become a god.\nThe mages were barely able to tear a fist sized rift, when Goren wrenched open. A blast of power destroyed the entire city, corrupting all those inside. They were no longer Elves, but High Elves, filled with the corrupting power of the void. \nAs time would progress, the void would become controllable, but at this time, the void was pure evil. The elves blamed the king for the opening of the hole, and worshipped him as a deity. The High Elves amassed armies, to force their false god onto the \nworld. They realized that they could not breed fast enough, learn fast enough, build fast enough, and progress fast enough for them to conquer the remaining Elven and Dwarven kingdoms, so they made Humans. Horrible expiriments took place, and the void was\ncombined with stone to create an altar. At this altar, the High Elves plunged each other into the void, and saw what happened. Eventually, they succeded and made their perfect slave race. Humans bowed to the High Elven creators, and called them gods.\nGoren decided that the High Elves had gone too far, and out of bone, fire, mud, blood, life, beast, mushroom, and metal, bore the uruk! A great war began, one that lasted thousands of years, until, the High Elves, in a last ditch attempt, tricked the Uruk\nWarGoth into a meeting with their leaders. He used his snake tounge to convince the Uruk leaders to turn on the Alliance of Goren. Soon all races were conquered under the High Elves, and Goren was to be eradicated. That was, until, the Human Uprising. \nGoren came to the Human Lords, as they had no kings, as a burning tree. He told them that he was the one true god, and created everything. He did not have much time, and merely told them to revolt, before bestowing on the golden swords.\nThe Swords were blessed by Goren, and could kill a High Elf with just a touch. It protected the users from magic, and thus, all High Elven attacks. The Human Lords gathered their armies, and told them of a great Creator. The armies amassed, alone.\nAll other races had been conquered, and were being forced to believe in the High Elven King as god. When the day came, the Human armies had a \"festival\" outside of the Elven capital. It was to \"honor the god king.\" The day of the battle, the great warhorn\nof Goren was sounded by the Human lords, and the city walls crumbled, as if by magic. The elven armies were strong, and it seemed that the Humans would lose, until, Goren appeared as a bright fire in the sky. He rained lighting, fire, locusts. He \nshook the world, and made it crack. He made the seashore on which the city was located stand up 100 feet high, and roar down upon the people. He made the hills surrounding the valley shoot darkness, and fire. At the center of the carnage, was a circle of\nThe High Elf Kings, Surrounding their god. Using all their power, they banished Goren into the World. This was their last mistake, for as they did, the Human lords drove blades into their hearts. Goren's physical form was lost in the ground, while his \nspirit form remains to guide and protect us in life. The Human lords never knew Goren's true name or the true history of the World, only the Dwarves did. The Dwarves who saw two powrful beings fight, made new gods, new stories. Only the few who lived far \nfrom all others remained loyal to Goren. These were Dwarven believers. Soon the Creator, Brathmordakin, and the rest went down in history as the things that destroyed evil. Goren only remained in the hearts of a few.\n   *EN ACK EXODUS*", ""),
        StaticBook("Acts of Petrus", "Lord William Harcourt", "The Lynch-Tuvian Act of 1471\n \nIssued and Confirmed by Tuvya I\nSection I.\nThe Maer of Petrus\n\n-Appointed by the Emperor Himself, Maer Lynch of Petrus is the civil governor and holds the highest authority within the capital next to the Emperor.\n-He shall hold the power to pass civil acts and mandates to further the city and her people. He shall also act as the Decurion of the guard regiment and ensure their efficient operation.\nSection II.\nThe 2nd Petrus Reserves\n\n-The 2nd Petrus Reserves will be the occupying and outlying guardforce of Petrus.\n-Their duties will include:\n1. The maintenance and Protection of the Gate of Humanity (Petrus).\n2. The maintenance of Logs of all crimes and warrants\n3. The defence of the City and the Emperor.\n4. The safety of the citizens of Petrus.\nSection III.\nThe Council of Petrus\n\n-Per order of the Maer of Petrus, the council of Petrus shall act as the civil lobby for the advancement of the capital of humanity.\n-The offices of the serving members are as follows:\nThe Sheriff of Petrus\n\n-Generally a ranking officer of the 2nd Petrus Reserves, the Sheriff is a skilled lawyer and soldier. \n\n-Using both law and steel to enforce the Emperors will. He holds the authority to pen and issue warrants on any unlanded citizen of Oren so long as sufficient evidence is given.\n-The Emperor always holds the authority to pardon a warrant.\nThe Guildmaster\n\n-The Guildmaster represents the labor guild of Petrus, he regulates the trade and employment alongside the Maer.\nThe Bishop of Petrus\n\n-The Bishop of Petrus is the third and final member of the council, his responsibility lies in enforcing the will of the Creator and His Servants.\n-His is tasked with the maintenance of the Cathedral, Cleansing of heresy, and voicing the will of the clergy to the church.\nSection IV.\nEstablishment of the Coin Guild of Petrus\n\n-The Coin Guild the roster of active stall owners and laborers in Petrus, they voice and discuss the trade of Petrus as well as present cases to the Maer via the Guildmaster.\n-Membership of the Guild extends beyond merchants, any aspiring trader may apply to join the guild.\nSection V.\nOpportunity\n\n-The Maer of Petrus is currently looking for able bodied statesmen, merchants, soldiers, and builders. If you are looking for an opportunity to gain a lower officer within the government of Oren than look no further.", ""),
        StaticBook("adawdada", "Odin Ireheart", "adjhagdawdhjawdawjkdawldkawbdnwajdwa", ""),
        StaticBook("Adran's seeking", "Elindor", "Adran seeks to become an apprentice. He seems to have what we demand.\n\nNo preference.\n\n[[creeperslayer779]]\n\nIf we don't grab him the Clerics probably will.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunian Poems", "Hamish", "Open your eyes and watch the sky,\nto see the blue and the white,\nand view the stars that roam up above\nand watch the birds in flight.\nTo see the seasons change with time\nand the people grow and age,\n\nto see the kindness in their hearts\nand their dark eyes that hold their rage.\nOpen your eyes to notice the difference\nbetween the rumours and praise,\nfrom the people who honestly care\nto those that could not be more blasé.\n\nTo notice the change from black to grey\nfrom purple to blue, orange to red,\nand see green turn to yellow,\nthe rich comforted and the hungry get fed.\nOpen your eyes to watch the pain\nthat others hide from the rest.\n\nThey might be the man on the street\nor the masquerade, best dressed. \nNotice the seasons wash the air new\nto make room for their colours, \nand make the people change their clothes\nas well as watch out for others.\n\nOpen your eyes to their lives going by,\nto their hopes flickering and fading,\nthe things they want most leaving\nand their dreams gone from trading.\nWatch out for a puddle of tears\nnear a gravestone of the loved,\n\nand see those who longed to be touched\nas they keep their fingers gloved.\nOpen your eyes to see the compassion\nthat seems to flow in this realm,\nfrom the caring and the kindness\nto the comfort that can overwhelm.\n\nBut also take note of the depression\nthat sits at the bottoms of the lakes, \nthat rots on the tree branches\nand in the corners of the crates.\nOpen your eyes to see what I see, \nthe final realisation; \n\nthat with every new begining\ncomes yet another civilisation.\nBut just rest and take it all in,\nwith your eyes wide open\nand see this shattered realm like me,\nwith my heart completely broken.\n\n\nShattered,\nThe fact that I am broken,\nBroken,\nEven with what I said;\nTattered, \nMy heart is thankful for use,\nSmashed,\nEven though all out my heart bled.\nHalting,\n\nMy world, but seems to keep spinning,\nCrushed,\nAs my mind searches for support;\nImperfect, \nHe is gone forever as they said,\nUneven, \nAnd I did not have the energy to retort.\nDisturbed,\n\nThey told me, when I asked what happened,\nSnapped,\nThey said, when he fell with my heart,\nDefeated,\nHe was, as he was carried outside,\nCracked,\nThey described he was not that smart. \n\nStopped, \nas I cannot hear it anymore,\nDestoryed,\nmy heart to the very core,\nAltered, \nas I think its beat has changed,\nDefective,\n\nand it has made me beyond poor. \nIs,\nwhat a time that this has been,\nWhat,\nI have been through is too much,\nI,\nonly wanted to see him again,\nFeel,\n\nhis heart and his touch.\nMy,\nThree, dear Three, bless him,\nElton,\nfor he was my net under the ledge,\nIs,\nhe really, truly with you now? \n\nDead,\nand gone, straight over the edge?\n\n\nHis green eyes never leave my gaze\nand his beard will always be brown,\nhis kilt never lost its colour\nas he kept not a trace of a frown.\nHis high stature has yet to be forgotten\nwhat with his boom laughter and grin,\n\nand his highspirits not only with his family\nbut also in the tavern with his gin.\nHis comforting words kept me going\nas his form took shape in my mind,\nfor it was I who kepts his memories,\nit was I that he never left behind.\n\nI cannot say I enjoyed all of it\nfor that man saw too many wars,\nbut he also had his moments of triumph,\nand those he loved dearly of course.\nHe kept his mind straight and level\neven under the most pressure,\n\nhe always knew where his place was\nand respected those who were lesser.\nSometimes he forgot right from wrong,\nbut then again, we all to at some point,\nand yet he knew how to keep people motivatied\neven though he was hard to dissapoint.\n\nAnd though I miss him still to this day,\nwith years gone since he passed,\nI still wish Hanrahan was here with me,\nbut for now his memories will stay glassed.\n\n\nI tried to paint you with the finest paints,\nto bring your green eyes and brown hair,\nbut the picture simply slipped from my mind,\nand on the canvas you were not there.\nI had the colours perfectly mixed,\nmy brush poised and ready, \n\nbut when it came to shaping your face,\nI could not keep my hand steady.\nI ended up painting a landscape;\nit was one that I knew all too well,\nit had trees in the back and buildings around,\nbut little did I know that I fell.\n\nI watched my hand with curiosity,\nnot knowing what it was doing, \nand suddenly I forgot where I was,\nand even the tea I had brewing.\nI forgot my life and all my memories,\nI forgot who I had lost,\n\nI only knew about the place at hand,\nand I could not see the lines I crossed.\nI backed into my own painting\nof the trees and of the buildings,\nand backed right into the old Clinic of ours\nand I found the stash of old kindlings.\n\nI relit the fire just behind the counter,\nand leaned on it as I looked towards the door,\nI had washed the floors and that silver bell,\nand waited for your arrival once more.\nAs I stood in the Clinic of Memories\n\nI seemed to trick myself,\nbut at the time I could not see you\nas I restocked the shelf.\nYou walked in quietly as you always did,\nand I hung my coat on a hook.\nBut I could tell that I was not alone\n\nas you stood in that corner and looked.\nI turned around to see your expression,\nthose green eyes sunked into your face,\nand when you told me simple words that calmed me,\nthey helped me find my place.\nYou stepped closer and hugged me,\n\nyour words were soft and kind,\n\"You will be all right, I promise,\" you whispered,\nand suddenly it was I who was hard to find.\n\"Can't I just go back to the Clinic?\"\nI almost cried as you came near,\n\n\"Yes, anything you want, I promise,\nbut for now, Arial, you must stay here.\"\nSomething happened just then, \t\nwhen you promised I would be okay.\nI knew that the person I was then\nwould not be the person I am today.\n\nFor now I know that Arial\nwas the one who you wanted to protect,\nso she took her things and kept them safe,\nleast she be the one I forget.\nAnd now your dreams can come true,\nfor your daughter now walks these lands,\n\nand I can assure that Arial will be all right, \nbecause she is in your own hands.\nShe may call herself Annabelle,\nbut that is only for your sake,\nbecause she knows your daughter is in her\nand her soul was always yours to take. \n\nBut I did lose myself in the Clinic that day,\neven though it was just a painting.\nAnd even though it was all in my mind,\nI know it was real and Arial is still waiting.\nShe will wait for you until the end of time,\nuntil the brush is steady,\n\nuntil your face can be painted again\nand until you think she is ready.\n\n\nPostscript.\n\nA collection of poems\nwritten by a famous Adunian poet in the late Anthosian period.\n\nLet her memory be charished by all those who read her delightful words.\n\n-Hanrahan Brae", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventure Book", "Illmori Chalkeus", "The Travelers Guide II\n\nI. Tourism : \nThere are lots of places around our great lands, but only few of them are good for tourism. The Tourism part of the book is for the persons which want to enjoy their travels \n\n~~~\nDrinks and Foods Tourism : \n\nIf you like the food and the drinks, then good places for you are tha famous inns - The Red Rose Inn and The Viridian Pub. But you can find good foods and drinks into the cities too - Haelun'or (have alchemists), Petrus, \nWerdenberg (may have tea and sweets shop (but not sure)), The Dwarven Lands (The place where the famous Dwarven Ale were born) and The Cloud Temple (there is a pub). \n\n*Side Note* - If you go into a famous pub, you risk to get robbed or hurted by the ->\n-> bandits.\n\nEvents Chasing Tourism : \n\nIf you like to be where the events are, then you may go on the places below. In this section you may find where most things happen and where the social live is mostly. \nThe Famous Inns (However you must be sure you have no problem with bandits), Petrus, Haelun'or, Cerulin, The Cloud Temple and Sometimes the small villages and towns in Oren. \n\nPeace and Silence Tourism : \nIf you want to go away from the society and -> \n-> the peoples, then you can go in one of the place below. However it may be boring and not so interesting.\nKorovia, Nerezza, Dul'Sildur (it is not a city, but it is castle with nice view), The Dwarven Lands, The messa lands. \n\n*Side Note* In Nerezza, ->\nDul'Sildur and the Dwarven lands it may not be so peaceful, but there aren't lots of peoples. \n\nMistery and Adventure Tourism: \nIf you search for adventures and misteries, then you can go in : Dul'Sildur, Petrus, The Old Druids Groove, ->\nThe lands near the wilds, The messa lands and The Dwarven Lands. \n\nII. Travels : \n\nIf you search for peaceful paths, points where to stop and rest or places where you may do comunications with other travelers then this is your section.\nPaths and Roads : \nThere aren't lots of paths and roads around our beautiful and magestic lands, but this may be useful for the new adventurers. \n\nThe Stone Road (Main Road), The Cerulin Road (Next to the Red Rose Tavern - To Cerulin and The Asylum), -> \nThe Werdenberg Road (East from Petrus, to Montfort, Werdenberg, Dragon's Peek and other keeps and towns), and lots of other roads (sorry there are few roads here) \n\nResting Points : \n\nIf you traveled much and want to rest somewhere you may try in : ->\nThe Famous Inns (But be careful for bandits or evil things), Werdenberg, Petrus, Asylum (Not so good place for resting in), The Cloud Temple, Akovia. \n\nPlace Where You May Talk With Other Travelers : \n\nIf you need information or News you may find them in:\nPetrus, Cerulin, Haelun'or, The Famous Inns (As i said - bandits and maybe false information), Nerezza, Werdenberg, The Dwarven Lands, The Uruk Lands, The Cloud Temple. \n\nIII. Specific Interests \n\n\n\nStudying (Reading, Magics, Writing, etc.) : \n\nIf you want to educate yourself then try in: Petrus, Haelun'or, The New Druids Grove, The Dwarven Lands, Asylum, Dul'Sildur (Be careful studying necromacery - it is dangerous and bad) \nStudying (Gardening, Tea Making, Masonry, Architecture, etc.) : \n\nPetrus, Cerulin, Haelun'or, Wardenberg, The Viridian Inn (But have bigger chance to learn anything in Haelun'or, Petrus or Wardenberg), The Cloud Temple, The New Druid's Grove\nFighting, Joining Millitary or Wars : \n\nHaelun'or or Petrus are the best for these interests. \n\n-=-=-\n\n*Final Notes* \nGood Luck Dear Adventurer, i hope you will find what you was searching for. \n            Illmori Chalkeus", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventure Book 1", "Tantaparo", "CREATE YOUR OWN............\n.............ADVENTURE...............\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nYou are stranded alone on an island. Do you check for other inhabitants or begins to find food?\n\n#1 - Pg. 2\n#2 - Pg. 3\nYou check for inhabitants, finding a cave with a lit torch. Do you look inside the cave, or do you run away quickly?\n\n#1 - Pg. 4\n#2 - Pg. 5\nYou begin to find food, locating two odd herbs: A red one and a blue one. Which do you eat?\n\n#1 - Pg. 6\n#2 - Pg. 7\nYou look inside the cave, finding ugly orcs and dwarves. Do you try to kill them or do you try to befriend them?\n\n#1 - Pg. 8\n#2 - Pg. 9\nYou run away from the cave, finding a huge monster. Do you try to fight it or run into the cave?\n\n#1 - Pg. 10\n#2 - Pg. 4\nYou eat the red herb, slowly beginning to cough up blood, until you die.\n\nRestart.\nYou eat the blue herb, filling your stomach's hunger. Regaining strength you decide to build a boat or a house.\n\n#1 - Pg. 11\n#2 - Pg. 12\nYou attempt to kill the orcs and dwarves, dying quickly to their blades.\n\nRestart.\nYou attempt to befriend the dwarves and orcs. They like you and decide to give you a blue herb.\n\nGo to Pg. 7\nYou attempt to kill the monster, hurting it, but netting yourself a short death.\n\nRestart.\nYou decide to build a boat, riding out into the ocean. Soon, a tidal wave comes, crushing and suffocating you.\n\nRestart.\nYou decide to build a house, the dwarves and orcs helping you. You stay alive and survive.\n\nGood work!", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegian History", "The Pine Druid", "    Aegian History\n\nThe Age of Founding and the Before Times\n\nDuring this time, Druids were brought together and the Druidic Order was founded by Wayward Druid Respiren Knox. The records of these times may never be fully\ndeciphered, however. Although we know of some of the first Druids in Malinor, such as Respiren, Swifthide, and Native, very few details are known. Perhaps someday the past regarding these times will be revealed.\nThe First Age of Reconstruction\n\nThe First Age of Reconstruction was ushered in by the initiation of Dragon Druid Apollan into the Order. Apollan was the first to express interest in joining the Order after reading\nthe \"Myth of the Great War\" and spent long hours in the Druid grotto after he was famously murdered outside the gates of Laurelin by a bandit. Apollan quickly moved up the ranks. Meanwhile, the Order gew. After initiating Apollan, Respiren expressed \ninterest in 'rebuilding the Order'. Everyday, new citizens of Aegis would show up in the grove wanting to become Druids. Most were immediately innitiated. As the Order grew, so did a number of things including property and knowledge. During this time the \nOrder gained a lodge in Ravenhold, as well as one in the Laurelin docks. Additionally, two stalls were bought at the Laurelin Marketplace and hundreds of books were added to the Order's library.\nThe Age of Abandonment\n\nUnfortunately, due to extremely casual and non-uniform rites of the Wayward Druid, people were joining the Circle, only to wander into the wilderness never to be seen again. With no established Hierarchy\nthe Order lacked organisation and purpose. This was made apparent when an Elf named Rowan arrived. Archdruid Rowan, arrived from a far off forest, seeking to re-establish his lost Circle, the Druids of Mother Aegis. Rowan is likely the only citizen to \nhave argued with the Order's ways. His only backing for title of Druid was that he 'had a love of nature'. When Rowan became annoyed by the fact that he had to be initiated in order to be allowed into the inner library he stormed off claiming he would \nstart his own order somewhere else. Rowan was last seen entering the wilds outside his home in the Ravenlodge, and was never heard from or seen again. Fortunately the dark Age of Abandonment was brought to an end by the light of the Dawn Druid Maiavel.\nThe Age of Reformation\n\nThe Age of Reformation was brought on by the ideas and drive of one Maiavel. With her determination, she was able to rally the remaining Druids to create an official lore, hierarchy, rules and sense of order.\nThe Second Age of Reconstruction\n\nDuring the second age of Reconstruction many more books were written and a Grand Tree in the Laurelin Grove was planted. New Dedicants were brought in but less frequently than in the first age, and the \ninitiation process was more careful and uniform. During this age, the current Hierarchy was established with Apollan as Archdruid.\nThe Age of Knowledge\n\nThe Age of Knowledge was ushered in by Petyr, the Salmon Druid. His creation of the \"Dedicant's Vow\" and the \"Attunement Ceremony\" greatly helped the Order as did his other ideas, including spearheading the wiki.\nThe Age of Mushroom Transgressions\n\nThis age was brought about by the conflict caused by the deffering ideals in the Order. Some Druids were becoming increasingly annoyed at the restriction that came with having a grove in the \ncity (where trees/mushrooms could or could not be planted and the structure of the Druid tree). Other Druids argued that it was their duty to promote balance, and that the runway growth of mushrooms flowing from the grove was nowhere near \nnatural. Some Druids wanted a new grove to be created outside the city and far away. Others wanted the grove to be close. Still others did not want a new grove at all. However, it is important to note that most of these arguments were caused by \nmisunderstandings, which is why this age is sometimes called the Age of Misunderstandings or the Age of Confusion.\nThe Age of Renovation\n\nIn the end, most mushrooms were removed from the grove when Maiavel stamped her foot and the mushrooms instantly broke (but were unthoughtfully left on the ground, only to be swept up by Deltaro). A new, \nsecret grove was set up in the wilderness outside Ravenhold, (notable work from Mahten and Aeaira whom spent days working on the road leading to civilization). The Laurelin Grove continued to be renovated and improved on, with notable work\ncontributed by Lunar Druid Bircalin and Dedicant Deltaro.\n\n\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Aengudaemons", "Beranabus Seregon", "What is an Aengul and Daemon? Well.. In my studies I have looked through a plethora of ancient texts, and manuscripts made long ago some brought over from the times of Anthos, others I have discovered in these times of Athera, and others. I have infact \nmemorized for this small journal upon the thesis of an aengudaemon. Now.. It seems that aenguls and daemons are called neither instead infact are simply called aengudaemon in common tongue.. Though I have yet to discover the name inwhich\nthey call themselves, I would assume that is a word translated in our tongue having a queer meaning. Much like the common word for Mali is Elven. I would theorize the same can be said of the aengudaemons. Now, this text will have much rambling in it, as \nis a form of writing called \"Dreamscape\" so if it is too randomly paced do but ask dear reader and I may speak to you in person of what an aengudaemon is.\n\n Now, unto the text. And Aengudaemon is the term coined of a being from another realm\nof which we call the seven skies, Aether, and other terms. Some call them the Aengudaemons, others gods, the dwed cal them the brathmordakin. Now, some people worship them like a divine being, and for good reason in the aengudaemons innate capability\nin magic. Though, we will get back to the magic portion I will say that it is infact true that they need naught to be followed. As, all they are are aliens. Now, to some this is heretical though t'is true. They are but beings created by the creator long \nago eons prior to the descendants of Malin, Horen, Krug, and Uruguan. Meaning they have far more time to attain such powers. Now, simply what these beings are, are those what I believe to be but beings who have ascended to a higher tier of being.\nas are told in stories of descendants transforming themselves into these aengudaemons. It could be assumed if such is true that not all are born in the seven skies but infact may ascend to such a rank, and will of being through arduous work. Meaning, you \nor even I may become such a being in the future if we truly aspire to be it. Therefore, the aengudaemons are infact not beings we should necessarily 'worship' but I believe we should instead befriend them. Friendly bonds are much more potent than that of \nfaith, for to one I may worship, our connection is simply that, they are those that I follow zealotically, and they may give me insight upon things.. Possibly boons.. Though boons are but powers, and borrowed.. But friendship. Now..\nThe reason I say befriending is because an aengudaemon is much similiar to us. Some should be feared yes, but in the end of the day. They are a being of our entire.. Verse of planes of existance. Perhaps gods compared to man in the feats they are able to \nperform, though that needn't mean we must worship them. Though, that doesn't mean we musn't follow them. For I myself am a follower of the tenants stated by Aeriel. I am not a worshipper, a meer listener of her word. Much, like a pupil may follow a \nteacher. Now, moving back to their magical capabilities. It appears to me that the aengul and daemons have achieved a state of being that is far beyond some folks contemplations. I may delve into it more in different volumes, though I would assume it ties\nin on their apparent abilities they have created themselves. For there are many things folk draw from. From the void, from an aengul themselves, from lifeforce, spirits. And even some from their very souls. Perhaps there are more places to draw from that \nwe haven't touched upon, that gives them the powers to preform such grand feats. Or even possible that their very souls have been enriched by some even greater force. to achieve such a state of being. Things aengudaemons are able to do are creation. Of \nanything truly, a pocket dimension which they may think up. A race, a magic. raise the dead. Simply any feat with a flick of the finger some are able to do. Though most fall into certain catagories and set powers which they are able to do, or grant upon \nthose which they grant their boons to. For example Aeriels domain over souls that pass into the seven skies after death in our realm. With that, she is able to cleanse souls from tainted and otherwise unnatural sources such as a soul with two souls one\nartificial the other their own. And remove one soul from the body of another. To allow them control over their own. Now this may sound complicated or otherwise unimaginable but I have infact seen it with my own eyes.. Quite wonderful thing to see.\nOther things that seem to exist are folk with blood of the aengudaemons themselves, further bonding our people with theirs, and would lead some to believe that they mate much like we do. As it is said, and proven that my family itself hails as descendants\nof some vague aengudaemonic being. Though in my years of study I have yet to uncover who or what they are. Though one can only imagine what it would feel to discover an ancient relative from long ago. Still alive today.. Besides that, but misc things can \nbe said upon the aengudaemons. It seems they are broken into 2 catagories of standard aengudaemons and greater ones who have achieved even greater powers called arch aenguls or arch daemons. Though, it seems \nthey themselves do not consider themselves aenguls or daemons. And it is our people who call them which, upon our social views. Most commonly a daemon is considered bad when in truth the only difference it seems to be is that daemons interact more with \nother realms and are more prevalent in every day life whilst aenguls prefer to stay in the backround though most of the time are considered benevolent. Even though that is untrue. What more can be said about these ominous beings besides that they should \nnot be feared nor worshipped, instead I believe if our people are to move on and achieve greatness, we should instead find peace, and friendship with these alien people. Closer bonds, learn from them much like a student would a teacher. For worshipping or\nfear can only last long, though it is possible friendships to last an eternity..\nThank you for reading the first addition of the Theory of Aenguls and Daemons. If I gain more insight upon these beings or choose to ramble more in my writings, I shall make \na secondary addition though for now. I bid you good night. And thanks for reading.\n             Signed\nB.B Seregon", ""),
        StaticBook("Aenor Calithil", "Aenor Calithil", "I am not one for deities and the likes, but oh, how I wish to start a family. Not a dysfunctional, crazy family, but one I can be proud of. I wish to stand by, and truly believe that family is the strongest of bonds. Please, something, someone, hear me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeran's Wish", "Aeran", "Dryads", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeromancy", "Great Ser Arhadir Owl", "Aeromancy\n\nBy Master Of Air Ser Arhadir Owl\nDate 23rd of The Amber Cold, 1474\n\nChapter 1: How to use Air Evocation\nChapter 2: Extra Information\nChapter 3: Spells\n\nChapter 1:\n\n1. The first step you should take to learning Aeromancy is by observing the wind itself in action, but to do this in a windy area where you can see what the wind does to nature. \n2. The next step is to learn how to clear your mind and focus just on the void. \n\n3. After these first two steps you must learn to pull from the void, you do this by clearing your mind and focusing on the void and by thing about the wind itself which you have been studying.\n\n4. Slowly you will be able to bring small amounts of Air from the void into the world. During this stage you will find that your body is weaken and you may faint a few times trying to hold a connect to the void or by trying hard spells.\n5. Once you learnt how to pull Air from the void you can start using it practically. one of the first spells you can learn is Force push which is a basic burst of Air, this can be used to blow out torches and maybe even push people back a bit.\n6. From here it is up to you to develop Aeromancy better to learn new and intresting spells.\nChapter 2:\n\nQuestion that people have about Aeromancery's and what they can do with Aeromancy.\n-Aeromancer’s cannot control Air in the natural world only control and summon Air which they have summoned from the void.\n\n-Aeromancer’s cannot fly because the cannot hold a stable connection to the void while moving that fast.\n\n-Aeromancer’s do not have the ability to change the weather.\nChapter 3:\n\nBasic:\n-Force Push: The most basic of all the spells this essentially allows of an Aeromancer to push a target away or knock them over.\n\n-Air Ball: Another basic spell which allows for the Aeromancer to summon a ball of Air which can be fired at targets at different speeds.\n\nAdept:\n\n-Tornado: This is a much more defence spell which allows the Aeromancer to summon a tornado around a person or the Aeromancer him or her self,-\n- this tornado can protect from distance attacks (Best against other elemental magic attacks) or weak melee attacks. \n\n-Air Jump: An Aeromancer can fire a blast of air underneath him or her self which can then propel the Aeromancer up a few meters.\n\n\n-Air Burst: This spell fires a blast of air out from all around the Aeromancer which can be powerful enough to knock over many targets all out the Aeromancer.\n\n-Air Stream: This spell is when an Aeromancer fires a constant stream of Air which can push objects or people back, even knocking them over or stopping them from moving.\n\nAdvanced:\n\n-Air Leap: The same as an Air Jump but allows you to jump much higher with much more precision.\n\n\n-Speed Run: While the idea of this speed seems easy it requires a lot of concentration for a mage to be moving at a speed and be usings his or her magic, this spell allows for the Aeromancer to run slightly faster than normal.\n\n-Air Bolt: This is a sudden and extremely power blast of air which which can be fire long distances. When this bolt hits it can knock a person out cold or even break bones.\n\nThis concludes the Tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeromancy", "Glacio", "Study of Air Evocation\n\nAir Evocation, like all evocations and forms of magic, require you to be able to connect to the void. The Void is the source of all magic, and is the most fundamental part of evocation. To connect to the void, you must meditate and\nbe able to clear your mind of thought. By doing this, you should be able to connect to the void.\n\nIn order to evocate air and wind, you must first understand your element. This involves studying it until you know it inside and out, both literally and \nfiguratively. You will need to know it very well to be able to evocate it.\n\nSome ways to study it include breathing it, touching it, smelling it, and tasting it every place you can.\n\nFinally, when evoking this element, you\nwill most likely fail the first times, and you will experience extreme fatigue. You must envision actually taking the element from the void, into existance. However, after you lose focus with your evocated element, it will cease to exist again.\nYou cannot manipulate existing air, and magical air does not act different other than the fact it was created by you, and can be controlled to an extent.\n\nSo, connect to the void, learn your element, practice...\n[!]A picture of a feather floating in the wind fills the rest of this page.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aheral Hst. V1", "The Scribe.", "Mali'aheral means blessed Elves. The Mali'aheral ancestors bathed in a golden pool. This is how they gained their appearance and conciousness that is kept today. The Mali'aheral have a tendency to dislike the other races. Many \nbelieve this is a burning hatred, and that the Mali'aheral seek to rid the world of the other races. However, this is not true. The Aheral merely are annoyed at the chaos and lack of intelligence of the others.\nIn Aegis, elmaliaheral resided in the leafy cities of Laurelin. Upon the High Council, only one Mali'aheral sat, Prince Toren. He alone stood as a bastion of order against the chaos that was seeping in from the rest of Malinor. However,\nit can be assumed he may have actually been impure, as the strict and just laws of purity had not been established as of time he lived in. \n\nPrince Toren was tasked to feed all of the Elves of Malinor. As such, \nhe grew one of the largest farms to ever be seen in the lands og Aegis. He named it the Laurelin farm. That is, one is afraid, all that is known of the people in Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Air Evocation", "Ayche Raven'kor", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocatonist Alatar of the Mage Academy\n\nRecopied By\nAyche\n\nTable of Conents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\n\nChapter 1: \nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by absolute darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas.\n\n\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' \nconcept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found.\n\nLearn how to blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to paint your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self.\n\n\nWith the art of air evoction, you manipulate it. Wind is unpredictable and one\nof the best studied branches of arcane magics, You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it.\n\nIn order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a  region of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it.\n\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch how the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or carries it away.\nChapter 3:\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; you may begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\n\n\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this. A small amount of wind may be conjured. \nWarning: You may pass out a few times upon first connection.\n\nChapter 4: After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal.\n\n\n\nThe first and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large and forceful push at the enemy. \n\nSecondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado.\n\nA skilled air evocationist can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most objects out of your sphere. That concludes this tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Air Evocation", "princetonlax21", "This selection will offer insight into the subtype of evocation named Aeromancy. I do not particularly enjoy the name, so please do not use it.\n\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocationist Alatar of the Mage Academy.\n Table of Contents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\nChapter 1:\n\nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by complete darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas. Hypothetically, \nanything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. \n\nThe first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' concept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found. Learn how to\nblanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to create your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\n\nWind and Air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self. With the art of air \nevocation, you manipulate it. Wind is very unpredictable and one of the least studied brances of arcane magics. You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it. In order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a\nregion of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how the pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it. \n\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch \nhow the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or carries it away.\n\nChapter 3:\n\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; You \nmay begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void.\n\nFirstly, you must find a place of peace. Next, use your blank canvas to imagine a air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very \nblood. Though combining all of this, a small amount of wind may be conjured. WARNING: You may pass out a few times upon first connection.\n\nChapter 4:\n\nAfter you have mastered basic connection, you can \nmove onto some of the key spells in a air evocationists arsenal.\n\nThe first, and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large and forceful push at an enemy.\n\nSecondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado. A more skilled air evocationist can can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most object out of your sphere. \n\nThat concludes this tome. Feel free to \ndiscover your own path in the special art of air evocation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aisilnn Log", "Domainoft", "Aislinn's Medical Log\n===================\n\n\n*A crude drawing of Jex lies here, various parts labelled, and a few injuries also drawn on as well.*\nSubject took multiple puncture wounds to the side, lower chest, and shoulder. A slashing blow to the back of the head and piercing of the temple was the cause of death.\n\n\nI opened up his chest and cut open the large bone in front of the heart. It was difficult, but expected. After all, the heart is extremely important, and should be protected.\n\nI examined the heart and lungs closely.\nFrom what I already know, it /is/ possible to repair a punctured lung. When a lung is pierced, I suppose blood and other fluids fill up, causing the person to 'drown'.\n\nAnother thing I noticed is that arteries and veins, which obviously transport blood \nthroughout the body, are quite elastic and stretchy. If one was cut, it /may/ be possible to sew or cauterize it shut, preventing rapid blood loss. \n\nMaybe if it could be pressed or squeezed somehow, blood loss could be migitated \non severed limbs and the like. Although now that I think about it, it would be preferable to bring the person to the monks, to save the limb.\n\nAs for the eyes, I have seen dozens of eye injuries. Despite my careful work, I cannot understand \nnor comprehend how the eyes work, or how they could possibly be worked on or fixed. \n\nA shame, really.\n*Another drawing, better this time, is made of a large, muscular Valah*\nSubject died due to severed throat. Too much blood loss, artery cut.\n\nI checked the heart and lungs carefully, noting the position. \n\nA note on the stomach - I found that it holds food, as the throat appears to lead to \nit. However.. once the stomach branched off into the long, spiraling organ, I became stumped. I'm not even going to attempt to fathom how food is digested.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alch Notebook I", "Laerden", "The Alchemist's Notebook\n\nForeword\nThe Realm of Anthos is filled with all types of herbs, creatures and phenomena to which are the delight of the many alchemists which fill it.\nSwamps and plains; hills and deserts can be found all around the continent, and in each of them a plethora of regents await to be found. With that being said and done, I welcome you, reader; to the Alchemist's Notebook on each (though not every) of\nthese very regents in their corresponding habitats.\n\nThe Southern Desert\n\nGoblin's Ivy\nKnown for its hardiness and abundance, Goblin’s Ivy covers dunes, caves, buildings and trees seemingly without preference or deterrence of any of the nearby inhabitants. The sludgy,\nOrc-Hide hue that colours the vine is, to be blunt, abhorrent, and its lack of appeal is only increased by its near uselessness in alchemy. With that being said, though, every regent has its function, and Goblin’s Ivy’s would be as an obvious \nsymbol Earth, resilience, and life. It can be used somewhat effectively in Stoneskin Potions, Potions of Fortitude, and even Potions of Strength. It’s been seen to have been used in poisons too, strangely, though any such are \nuseless in practicality and cause no more than mild nausea. Finding it isn’t a challenge, even in the vast expanse of the Badlands, and harvesting it is done simply enough by cutting off a length of the vine with a \nmachete or a similar knife, and keeping it in your satchel with all the other regents you have collected. When used in potions it can be extracted into water through boiling, or crushed finely in a mortar and pestle, though the second is advised in oils.\nBlood Lotus\nWith a blood like colouring and a blood like taste, the aptly named Blood Lotus is a desert crawler considered to be a valuable regent when traversing the dunes in search of a symbol of Fire. It’s widely accepted that heat and\nstrength are the two main things the plant represents in alchemy, and can be used in many potions in need of a more (And I use this lightly) calm portrayal of fire. It has been said that Blood Lotus can be brewed into an invigourating ale\nor even eaten crushed as a nutritional spice, and is commonly fed to people weak with sickness to help keep up their strength. It can be easily found in the mouths of caves and caverns and harvested by bottling the plant and \nkeeping it alive until use. It wilts and becomes useless quickly; as is the tendency for flame-related flora.\n \n\nThe Northern Icelands\n\nFrost Vine\nFound in the deepest cold of the North, it is only natural that Frost Vine be known as a symbol of Water- But more importantly so of ice, calmness and release.\nIt blends well into its chilly landscape with a light blue, and almost grey skin, and would seem to prefer to live in the shade of a tree, sheltered from the North gales. It can be used well in Oils of Frost and Potions of Mending,\nas one of its more useful attributes is a handy numbing agent that can be observed simply by a few minutes touch. After being crushed and extracted into water it becomes more potent, and is as quick and powerful at numbing \nas any alchemist or healer would need it to be. Harvesting can be done by bottling the vines and perhaps keeping them cold, and it should be said that growing Frost Vine away from the North or any other cold ecosystem\nis nearly impossible due to its fragile nature.\n\nElrow Berries\nA strange plant to say the least, Elrow berries are one of the only symbols of Fire that can be grown naturally in cold climates such as the North. One would seem to ask why when first told this fact, though by only a simple taste \nof the Devils of the North would they find out. Similar to chilli’s in nature, the berries burn the eater’s tastebuds and dry his throat nigh instantly upon consumption; leaving you craving for water or some other release from the aching \nElrow Berries bring. A mouth full of snow is a common enough cure for ‘berry burn’, and any nearby Frost Vine or Serpent’s Stalk would work just as well in the case of any snowless expanse. It can be used in potions and poisons alike \nas a symbol of power, anger and destruction, as that is simply what follows after eating the Berries of Elrow. They can be harvested without worry from any bush found in a cranny in a rock up North, though tend to lose some\npotency once dried. To dry and crush the berries is the best way to use them in a potion, though ample warnings should be given for any ignorant lab assistants; as even after processing they possess the same spice as they would naturally.\n\nElf's Hair\nAs rare as any growable regent can get, and as hard to spot as a Signus in a snowstorm, the Elf’s Hair Vine may only be seen once or twice in a whole year of searching, as many Alchemists find out to their dismay.\nFound atop mountains or hanging precariously over cavern edges, these wisps of vine and blossom are rivalled only in their potency by their beauty. The petals of the plant are of a soft, creamy white, and are indeed the most useful part of \nthe plant- In an alchemical sense, at the least. They hang loosely off the vine they grow on, and with any strong gust of wind are blown off and away; drifting over the air to populate some sparse piece of land far away. It is undeniable that \nElf’s Hair is a symbol of Air, speed, and grace, and it has been said that it an essential in any potent Potion of Swiftness. To harvest it one must be very careful- a stray bump could mean losing your rarity to the winds. It is the petals\nand the nectar that are most potent part of the plant, so plucking the whole blossom would be the simplest and easiest way. The nectar can be infused slowly with a potion, drop by drop, and the petals crushed; which \nis the most unfortunate part of using this reagent. Commonly, after the blossoms have been used, the vines wilt, die, and succumb to the winter winds.\n\nThe Midland Marshes\n\nDwarven Pumpkin\nAs swampy a plant as one could rightly get, Dwarven Pumpkin is a valuable symbol of Fire, power, and destruction. It can be easily spotted amongst the swamps and bogs by \nthe murky orange leaves that surround it; these being the main part of the plant you will want to use- and the brighter, the more potent, in this case. It’s usually found basking in sunlight in a rare clearing in the Marshes, which indeed\n is a great need of most herbs representing fire. Though commonly used for its potency in potions revolving entirely around fire, Dwarven Pumpkin also has a use in many other potions such as ones of fortitude, in which \nits representation of power grants a concentration boost to your armour-for-your-armour. Harvesting it is done by pruning off the leaves of brightest orange, and keeping them uncrushed in your satchel. They should be used soon after \nharvesting, in potions, by crushing them thoroughly and pouring the juice slowly into your concoction. It’s not a naturally toxic plant- but neither is it particularly pleasant to eat; with a bitter, clinging aftertaste.\n\n\nSaffvil\nThis plant, looking more like some clump of dilapidated weed-grass than a useful ingredient, is one of the few regents in the Marshes which is more repugnant to harvest than Mandragora. Found among the rotting carcasses\nof recently deceased swamp beasts, or sprouting from beneath decomposing mushrooms, Saffvil is a vile floral parasite and decomposer with a very handy use in potions needing a strong symbol of Earth, resilience, and decay. \nPoisons are the strong suite of this lacklustre herb; it has long been known to be a critical component in some of the more deadly brews, and indeed induces a blood clotting effect in most potions it is used in- though this can be \nremedied by including the nectar of the swamp blossom plant in your concoction, or any other strong symbol of air and speed. Harvesting it can be done by a simple uprooting of the whole, grassy mound, and washing it clean \nof any contaminations, to avoid impure potions (the bane of any alchemist intent on keeping their eyebrows). The easiest way Saffvil can be used in potions is to infuse it by a process similar to tea making.\nLeave the regent in a pouch soaking in your base ingredient until most of the plant has lost its colour, and dispose of it afterwards.\n\n\nSwamp Blossom \nFound growing in the crowded treetops above the Midland Marshes, this purple stemmed perennial produces strange, transparent nectar known well for its interesting properties, and its use as a symbol of Air, speed, and motion.\nThe liquid will not diffuse into water in great quantities without great heat and effort, and seems to refuse to behave as anything aqueous should. It glides across skin, and most any other surface it comes into contact with, \nand only seems to be interested in sticking to itself- Quite the opposite of water, in fact. Growing naturally on the branches of high-reaching swamp trees, Swamp Blossom can be spotted by its curved purple-green petals and the \npreviously mentioned burly, mauve-hued stem. Swiftness Potions and Potions of Mending are what this plant is of most use in, as both require a powerful symbol for speed. To harvest this plant this plant is difficult-\nOne must wait for first the plant to be producing its nectar, before slowly letting it collect it a water skin, or a vial. Consumption is practically harmless, though not advised- As Swamp Blossom is much more valuable \nas an alchemical regent than it is a barely nutritional, foul tasting pallet cleanser.\n\n\nMandragora\nOne of the more deadly plants inhabiting the swamps of Anthos, Mandragora is quite the prize of any herbalist; and is rather impressive on display. In several stages of its lifecycle, this parsnip shaped fungi releases toxic spores \nwith a hallucinogenic and eventually fatal effect on most creatures when inhaled. The meat of this plant is the most useful in potions involving clarity and regeneration, and is a somewhat strong symbol of Water \nwhen properly harvested. The plant’s brown coloured leaves can be used in soups, brews, or a rather nice tea- Though all have a chance of fatality or intoxication if boiled or cooked incorrectly. Harvesting this plant, as would be expected, \nis nigh impossible for any unknowing alchemist; two to three weeks after the Mandragora’s spores are released is the safe time to harvest, eat, and use it in potions. This can be done by simply uprooting the wholething, and separating the leaves \nand ‘meat’ later on at your alchemical workstation. The best way to brew Mandragora into a potion is to grind it up with a Mortar and Pestle, sprinkle it through your base, and later filter out the chunks.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Alch Notebook II", "Laerden", "The Great Anthos Forests\n\nTippen's Root\nA purple flower found growing beneath rotting trees and on the sides of hills, Tippen’s Root is one of the more common alchemical reagents in the great forests of  Anthos. \nCharacterised by its thick, deep digging roots and yellow spotted skin, this plant is the favourite of ‘healing’ alchemists everywhere, due to its almost uncanny blood coagulating properties. When crushed and made into an oil\nor balm, the root of the Tippen’s plant is capable of stopping the bleeding of most any wound (Within practicality, of course) in only a few moments. Though limited to only stopping bleeding, not actually healing the wound or cleaning it, \nas is a top priority in healing, its balm is a must to carry around in case of emergencies. Due to its natural endurance and blood-stopping abilities, it’s a brilliant symbol of Earth to use in Potions of Mending, and can mostly \nbe used in other concoctions needing strength or balance. Another interesting property of Tippen’s Root in its crushed form is an awful, putrid smell; though this can be found useful in situations where someone sleeping or unconscious needs to \nbe woken –unhappily, indeed, but woken all the same.\n\nNight Sap\nA golden sap found seeping out of growths of birch trees, Night Sap is regarded as the most deceptive alchemical regent in any of the four base biomes. Upon consumption, the thick, honey like substance proves to be a powerful \nsleeping agent- lulling you into a warm slumber only minutes after drinking it. Its taste, though sometimes over exaggerated, is perhaps the most pleasant effect this ingredient will give you; it’s soothing to the throat and calming to the\nmind, and slows your breathing and heart rate as if you’re now instantly lying in a soft featherbed, ready to sleep. Upon waking, however- Generally two to four hours later- you will soon come to realise that aching pains now \nplague your body. On most occasions after awaking from Sap Sleep, the unfortunate victim will find themselves too groggy or in too much pain to move- and will be racked with headaches and muscle pains for days after the experience. \nApart from the natural effects of Night Sap, an alchemist will find it useful as a symbol of Earth, endurance, and strength, and is commonly used in poisons to give them a good, addictive taste. Consumption is not advised, and harvesting \nis as easy as collecting the weeping sap in a vial from an affected tree.\n\nAlabaster Leaf\nA plant appropriately named for the colour of its foliage, Alabaster Leaf is a fairly common alchemical ingredient found growing around felled trees, in the drier regions of forests. It’s difficult to spot and identify save\nfor its alabaster hue, but is easy enough to grow in a grove once a herbalist gets a sample. If eaten, the plant can be found to be slightly poisonous; having the effect of nausea and throbbing headaches on those unknowing foragers who consume it. In \nbrewing potions, Alabaster Leaf is useful as a symbol of Earth and fatigue. Simply cut off the leaves and store them dried or fresh in your satchel to harvest the regent, and later crush them to add to your potions, oils, or balms.\nSerpent's Stalk\nAn emerald cluster of reeds usually found thriving among small ponds or beside slow flowing riverbanks, Serpent’s Stalk is an average symbol of Water, and is best used in potions revolving around calmness and relief. \nBrews such as the Potion of Mending would indeed find the mild herb as a key ingredient with a more placid representation.  When crushed and mixed with water, the plant’s stalks have a somewhat similar effect \nas the Frost Vine plant; soothing the pain of recent, minor burns when applied directly to the skin. The best way to harvest the plant is by cutting as close to the base as possible, and leaving it to regrow. Crushing the \nplant and infusing it into a potion’s base is the best way to get the most concentrated effects of Serpent’s Stalk; and though eating it is not advised, it’s not poisonous in a sense that you would think of with the name it holds.\n\nFlame Tongue Root\nFound in the more dense parts of forests and groves, this reagent is more easily defined by its deep crimson rose like blossom that is most commonly completely covered in a plethora of spines and brambles. Upon touch,\nFlame Tongue is physically hot, and when administered to wounds it coagulates the blood much like Tippin’s Root does- Though with an almost unbearable burning sensation in addition. Spores are released from the plant’s formidable spikes \nwhich cause continuing pain and irritation long after touch, and simply refuse to be washed off- though a mixture of Serpent’s Stalk or Frost Vine will relieve your affected skin and wash off the spores quite easily. The most potent parts of the herb\nwould be the roots; being known as a somewhat competent symbol of Fire for potions involving power, pain, or torment. Harvesting the plant must be done with gloves and heavy clothing, as many would-be-alchemists find out the hard way. \nUprooting the whole plant and keeping it in a leather pouch is the best way to transport it back to storage, as even though the spines aren’t as potent as the roots, they are sometimes useful in the more mild types of poisons.\n\nAdditional Entries\n\nMiner's Helmet\nA cave dwelling mushroom found all around the continent of Anthos, Miner’s Helmet is a large, abundant fungi preferring to live down deeper in cave systems than many \nherbalists would wish to go. Somewhat weak as a symbol of Earth, this subterranean growth is still useful in brewing for its use in potions needing resilience, strength, and poison. The plant is poisonous if consumed \nwithout proper processing; undetectable save for in the first few minutes in which the victim will be plagued by a series of violent twitches, the mushroom will stop your nervous system in only a matter of hours. The top \nof the mushroom is covered in a fine, but deadly toxic slime, which must be used in poisons only. Harvesting this plant should be done with utmost care; with gloves, a mouth covering, and a safe, sealed container.\nWhen preparing the fungi for brewing, make sure to properly wash and boil the meat of the plant for about fifteen minutes, as this should remove any of the more deadly parts of the plant while keeping the head \nsafe and pure for potion making. Crush and infuse the pulp into your base, and filter it out later, as is common procedure for mushrooms and roots.  \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Alch. Notebook 1", "ilikefooddude", "The Alchemist's Notebook\n\nForeword\nThe Realm of Anthos is filled with all types of herbs, creatures and phenomena to which are the delight of the many alchemists which fill it. Swamps and plains; hills and deserts can be found\nall around the continent, and in each of them a plethora of regents await to be found. With that being said and done, I welcome you, reader; to the Alchemist’s Notebook on each (though not every) of these very regents in their corresponding habitats.\nThe Southern Desert\n\nGoblin's Ivy \nKnown for its hardiness and abundance, Goblin’s Ivy covers dunes, caves, buildings and trees seemingly without preference or deterrence of any of the nearby \ninhabitants. The sludgy, Orc-Hide hue that colours the vine is, to be blunt, abhorrent, and its lack of appeal is only increased by its near uselessness in alchemy. With that being said, though, every regent has its function, and\nGoblin’s Ivy’s would be as an obvious of symbol Earth, resilience, and life. It can be used somewhat effectively in Stoneskin Potions, Potions of Fortitude, and even Potions of Strength. It’s been seen to have been used in poisons too, strangely,\nthough any such are useless in practicality and cause no more than mild nausea. Finding it isn’t a challenge, even in the vast expanse of the Badlands, and harvesting it is done simply enough by cutting off a length of the vine with a machete or any \nsimilar knife, and keeping it in your satchel with all the other regents you have collected. When used in potions it can be extracted into water through boiling, or crushed finely in a mortar and pestle, though the second is advised in lards and oils.\nBlood Lotus\nWith a blood like colouring and a blood like taste, the aptly named Blood Lotus is a desert crawler considered to be a valuable regent when traversing the dunes in search of a symbol of Fire. It’s widely accepted that heat and\nstrength are the two main things the plant represents in alchemy, and can be used in many potions in need of a more (And I use this lightly) calm portrayal of fire. It has been said that Blood Lotus can be brewed into an invigorating ale, or\nor even eaten crushed as a nutritional spice, and is commonly fed to people weak with sickness to help keep up their strength. It can be easily found in the mouths of caves and caverns and harvested by bottling the\nplant and keeping it alive until use. It wilts and becomes useless quickly; as is the tendency for flame-related flora. \nThe Northern Icelands\n\nFrost Vine\nFound in the deepest cold of the North, it is only natural that Frost Vine be known as a symbol of Water- But more importantly so of ice, calmness and release. It blends\nwell into its chilly landscape with a light blue, and almost grey skin, and would seem to prefer to live in the shade of a tree, sheltered from the North gales. It can be used well in Oils of Frost and Potions of Mending, as one of its more\nuseful attributes is a handy numbing agent that can be observed simply by a few minutes touch. After being crushed and extracted into water it becomes more potent, and is as quick and powerful at numbing as any alchemist or healer would need it to be.\nHarvesting can be done by bottling the vines and perhaps keeping them cold, and it should be said that growing Frost Vine away from the North or any other cold ecosystem is nearly impossible due to its fragile nature.\nElrow Berries\nA strange plant to say the least, Elrow berries are one of the only symbols of Fire that can be grown naturally in cold climates such as the North. One would seem to ask why when first told this fact, though by only a simple \ntaste of the Devils of the North would they find out. Similar to chilli’s in nature, the berries burn the eater’s tastebuds and dry his throat nigh instantly upon consumption; leaving you craving for water or some other release from the aching Elrow\nBerries bring. A mouth full of snow is a common enough cure for ‘berry burn’, and any nearby Frost Vine or Serpent’s Stalk would work just as well in the case of any snowless expanse. It can be used in potions and poisons alike as a symbol of\npower, anger and destruction, as that is simply what follows after eating the Berries of Elrow. They can be harvested without worry from any bush found in a cranny in a rock up North, though tend to lose some potency once dried. \nTo dry and crush the berries is the best way to use them in a potion, though ample warnings should be given for any ignorant lab assistants; as even after processing they possess the same spice as they would naturally.\nElf's Hair\nAs rare as any growable regent can get, and as hard to spot as a Signus in a snowstorm, the Elf’s Hair Vine may only be seen once or twice in a whole year of searching, as many Alchemists find out to their dismay. \nFound atop mountains or hanging precariously over cavern edges, these wisps of vine and blossom are rivalled only in their potency by their beauty. The petals of the plant are of a soft, creamy white, and are indeed the most useful part\nof the plant- In an alchemical sense, at the least. They hang loosely off the vine they grow on, and with any strong gust of wind are blown off and away; drifting over the air to populate some sparse piece of land far away.\nIt is undeniable that Elf’s Hair is a symbol of Air, speed, and grace, and it has been said that it an essential in any potent Potion of Swiftness. To harvest it one must be very careful- a stray bump could mean losing your rarity to the winds. \n. It is the petals and the nectar that are most potent part of the plant, so plucking the whole blossom would be the simplest and easiest way. The nectar can be infused slowly with a potion, drop by drop, and the petals crushed; which is the most \nunfortunate part of using this regent. Commonly, after the blossoms have been used, the vines wilt, die, and succumb to the winter winds.\nThe Midland Marshes\n\nDwarven Pumpkin \nAs swampy a plant as one could rightly get, Dwarven Pumpkin is a valuable symbol of Fire, power, and destruction. It can be easily spotted amongst the swamps and bogs by the murky orange\nleaves that surround it; these being the main part of the plant you will want to use- and the brighter, the more potent, in this case. It’s usually found basking in sunlight in a rare clearing in the Marshes, which indeed is a great need of most\nherbs representing fire. Though commonly used for its potency in potions revolving entirely around fire, Dwarven Pumpkin also has a use in many other potions such as ones of fortitude, in which its representation of power grants a concentration\nboost to your armour-for-your-armour. Harvesting it is done by pruning off the leaves of brightest orange, and keeping them uncrushed in your satchel. They should be used soon after harvesting, in potions, by crushing them\nthoroughly and pouring the juice slowly into your concoction. It’s not a naturally toxic plant- but neither is it particularly pleasant to eat; with a bitter, clinging aftertaste. \nSaffvil\nThis plant, looking more like some clump of dilapidated weed-grass than a useful ingredient, is one of the few regents in the Marshes which is more repugnant to harvest than Mandragora. Found among the rotting \ncarcasses of recently deceased swamp beasts, or sprouting from beneath decomposing mushrooms, Saffvil is a vile floral parasite and decomposer with a very handy use in potions needing a strong symbol of Earth, resilience, and decay.\nPoisons are the strong suite of this lacklustre herb; it has long been known to be a critical component in some of the more deadly brews, and indeed induces a blood clotting effect in most potions it is used in- though this can be remidied by including \nthe nectar of the swamp blossom plant in your concoction, or any other strong symbol of air and speed. Harvesting it can be done by a simple uprooting of the whole, grassy mound, and washing it clean of any contaminations,\nto avoid impure potions (the bane of any alchemist intent on keeping their eyebrows). The easiest way Saffvil can be used in potions is to infuse it by a process similar to tea making. \nLeave the regent in a pouch soaking in your base ingredient until most of the plant has lost its colour, and dispose of it afterwards.\nSwamp Blossom \nFound growing in the crowded treetops above the Midland Marshes, this purple stemmed perennial produces strange, transparent nectar known well for its interesting properties, and its use as a symbol of Air, speed, and motion. \nThe liquid will not diffuse into water in great quantities without great heat and effort, and seems to refuse to behave as anything aqueous should. It glides across skin, and most any other surface it comes into contact with, and only\nseems to be interested in sticking to itself- Quite the opposite of water, in fact. Growing naturally on the branches of high-reaching swamp trees, Swamp Blossom can be spotted by its curved purple-green petals and the previously mentioned\nburly, mauve-hued stem. Swiftness Potions and Potions of Mending are what this plant is of most use in, as both require a powerful symbol for speed. To harvest this plant this plant is difficult- One must wait for first the plant to be producing its\nnectar, before slowly letting it collect it a water skin, or a vial. Consumption is practically harmless, though not advised- As Swamp Blossom is much more valuable as an alchemical regent than it is a barely nutritional, foul tasting pallet cleanser. \nMandragora\nOne of the more deadly plants inhabiting the swamps of Anthos, Mandragora is quite the prize of any herbalist; and is rather impressive on display. In several stages of its lifecycle, this parsnip shaped fungi releases toxic spores \nwith a hallucinogenic and eventually fatal effect on most creatures when inhaled. The meat of this plant is the most useful in potions involving clarity and regeneration, and is a somewhat strong symbol of Water when properly harvested.\nThe plant’s brown coloured leaves can be used in soups, brews, or a rather nice tea- Though all have a chance of fatality or intoxication if boiled or cooked incorrectly. Harvesting this plant, as would be expected,\nis nigh impossible for any unknowing alchemist; two to three weeks after the Mandragora’s spores are released is the safe time to harvest, eat, and use it in potions. This can be done by simply uprooting the whole thing, and separating the leaves and\n‘meat’ later on at your alchemical workstation. The best way to brew Mandragora into a potion is to grind it up with a Mortar and Pestle, sprinkle it through your base, and later filter out the chunks. \nPart One Complete.\nSee The Alchemist's Notebook Part Two for Regents in the Great Anthos Forests, and Additional Entries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alch. Notebook 2", "ilikefooddude", "The Alchemist's Notebook\nPart Two\nThe Great Anthos Forests\n\nTippin's Root\nA purple flower found growing beneath rotting trees and on the sides of hills, Tippin’s Root is one of the more common alchemical regents in the great forests of  Anthos.\nCharacterised by its thick, deep digging roots and yellow spotted skin, this plant is the favourite of ‘healing’ alchemists everywhere, due to its almost uncanny blood coagulating properties. When crushed and made into an\noil or balm, the root of the Tippin’s plant is capable of stopping the bleeding of most any wound (Within practicality, of course) in only a few moments. Though limited to only stopping bleeding, not actually healing the wound or cleaning it, as is a top \npriority in healing, its balm is a must to carry around in case of emergencies. Due to its natural endurance and blood-stopping abilities, it’s a brilliant symbol of Earth to use in Potions of Mending, and can mostly be used in other concoctions needing \n strength or balance. Another interesting property of Tippin’s Root in its crushed form is an awful, putrid smell; though this can be found useful in situations where someone sleeping or unconscious needs to be woken- unhappily,\nindeed, but woken all the same. \nNight Sap\nA golden sap found seeping out of growths of birch trees; Night Sap is regarded as the most deceptive alchemical regent in any of the four base biomes. Upon consumption, the thick, honey like substance proves to be a \npowerful sleeping agent- lulling you into a warm slumber only minutes after drinking it. Its taste, though sometimes over exaggerated, is perhaps the most pleasant effect this ingredient will give you; it’s soothing to the throat and calming to the mind,\nand slows your breathing and heart rate as if you’re now instantly lying in a soft featherbed, ready to sleep. Upon waking, however- Generally two to four hours later- you will soon come to realise that ach