        StaticBook("Calendera Clover", "Averroa", "The Calendera Illisium Clover-An Anesthetic\n-Averroa Dewhurst\n\n  As written in the Study of the Effects of the Calendera Illisium Clover, Calendera demonstrated potential in use as a painkiller-having\npotency in grown elves at just 50μL. A fellow scientist, Lucion Sullas, suggested creating an anesthetic from the clover, and for the past year I've been trying various mixtures, combining the clover infusion with everything from spider venom to pumpkin\nwine.\n  After undertaking these studies, I've discovered that the painkilling properties of the clover are heightened when combined with the latex of the common poppy. In addition, the combination works as an effective anesthetic, potent\nfor an hour on average. However, I have yet to conduct these studies on creatures other than mice or chickens, so the following should only be used in practical applications after further research.\n  To prepare the Calendera Illisium Clover infusion: Simmer 10mg of fresh clover in one liter of water for 4 minutes. (The clover can be found among the roots of large trees near the Nawari Gypsy camp as well as in certain Elven forests.)\n  The mixture and how to prepare it: Mix 700mg of poppy latex with 20mL of simmering water and simmer for 3 minutes. Turn of the heat and quickly add 10mL of the Calendera infusion while the solution is still hot and stir quickly until well mixed.\n  50 microliters (μL) seemed to be the optimum dosage for the mice I tested on. After scraping away some of their skin and applying salt water to increase their pain, this dosage caused them to cease squirming and fall into a sleeplike state.\nHowever, about 0.05% of the mice became asphyxiated and nearly died at this dosage, leading me to believe that some creatures are more sensitive to the mixture than others. In addition, as I gradually increased the dosage, the chance of\nasphyxiation also gradually increased until an average lethal triple dose of roughly 150μL.\n  When I performed the same procedures on chickens, I found that a higher dose of 1.5mL was required to have the same effect. Similarly, a triple dose of 4.5mL was\nthe average lethal dose.\n  From these results, I hypothesize that body mass influences the amount of dosage required for the desired result. As the mice weighed 20g on average and the chickens weighed roughly 3.2kg on average,\nthe dosage may be proportional to body weight. As such, it may be practical to weigh patients before giving them their appropriate dose, if possible.\n  Hopefully these results will assist others in further research as well as healers in treating\npatients with more severe injuries or scientists hoping to prod into living organisms.\n   -§iAverroa Dewhurst", ""),
        StaticBook("Caliphate Report", "Silv'ar Vanguard", "First note of the Caliphate. There is a man here named Haadi Mubdee. I wonder if there's any relation to the Magistrate or the Sentinel.\nFrom what I can tell they only have one smith in the whole city. This whole city seems to be made of small alley. \nThe gate of the city is made of dried wood. Seems fairly weak. All of the cities water seems to come from a lake found near the castle.\nFrom what I can find most of the towns water is run through underground areas that some time surface. There's a \nsmall part of the city kept seperate it's called the home of the Kha. After talking to a citizen she told me they get there water from the ocean. Though this lady is the only one I've found so far. End of report. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Calvin's Lease", "Rezgiez", "10th of The First Seed of 1473\n\nThis note is to signify the agreement between the Boyar of Drak Thalas under the Barony of Llynch de Bar of House de Bar.\n\nThe agreement is thus, that the leasee will formally be know as a\ncitizen of Drak Thalas and agrees to the required quota of four (4) bundles of logs each elven week.\n\nIn return the leasee will recieve:\n  1 Unfurnished home\n  Free food weekly\n  50 minas\n  A say in the bi-elven weekly meeting if they\nso wish.\n\nSignature of leasee\nCalvin\n\nSignature of council member\nRezgiez", ""),
        StaticBook("Camping.", "Edwyn Lynderly", "\n\n\n  Camping, the mildly exciting adventure of Edwyn Lynderly.\n\n\nWritten by  E. Lynderly.\n3rd of Sun's Smile.\n\nI've never been one who wishes to camp. Sure, I dont mind the outdoors. Quite the opposite, and yet sleeping overnight is miserable conditions has just never offered any appeal to me. However, this is the task set for me and thus \nI must complete it. I write from within my sleeping bag, small candle flickering hopelessly to be right. It took me far too long to find a place to set up, thus causing the sky to glow orange as dusk set upon us. So I had no time to set up my damned tent\nand I lay upon the damp flooring, cold and miserable. Bloody camping.\n4th of Sun's Smile.\n\nWell, I'm not longer miserable nor wet.. But, I am very tired. After having maybe.. 10 minutes of sleep? I awoke to the rays of sun piercing my apparantly non existance eyelids. Refusing to have no sleep once again I spent\nmany a hour establishing the tent packed into my bag by Arin. Quite frankly, it's not bad.. Splash cramped however it'll do the job. I soon turned my attention to my ever grumbling stomache. I quickly went about summoning up a fire, fortuantly I have\nexperiance doing such.. So, placing it aside a fell tree which I'm hoping will become a moderately comfy bench.. Then I encounted another issue, I didnt exactly have anything to cook. Unwilling to go hunting, I decided to eat some of the grain granted to \nme by Arin, mixed with water to form a slush of disgusting, flavourless bollocks. Damned camping.\n11th of Sun's Smile.\n\nWell, been a few days since the previous entry to this thing. Been keeping myself occupied in this isolated place. First, knowing my food supply wouldn't last the next few saints months I went about creating a farm.. I have some\nknowledge upon farming, along with observing that Felix chap tend to the fields perched atop my rock. I miss that rock right now. So I have some grain slowly coming to form, I have plenty of time to tend to it and it's growing with signicant haste. Along \nthe creation of the farm, I've began forming that of a basic chair from wood. I have never practiced carpentry and have already broken about five designs. However, as night descends and my farms become shrouded by that of darkness it keeps myself busy, \npulling me further from the insantity that isolation brings.\n15th of Sun's Smile.\n\nAt last! My mighty mission to build that of a chair has been complete! It stands up all by itself and everything! However, with that complete I'm once again bored during the night. I cant even glare meaningfully off into the\ndistance because well, it's all bloody dark. Maybe a table. Yes! Let's build a table.\n17th of Sun's Smile.\n\nApparantly tables are much easier to construct than that of a chair.. Four legs and a large plank. Brilliant. They're so easy infact I built two. I hardly had use for one nevermind a second. So I threw once inside the tent with \nme acting sort of like a desk, I'm writing this entry on it currently, however I dont have a chair to go with said desk. Back to square one I suppose.\n18th of Sun's Smile.\n\nTried making another chair. I'll just move the one I have made around.\n22nd of Sun's Smile.\n\nI've had a nice few days suprisingly. I haven't bothered with constructing something.. constantly watering my grain.. tending to the fire.. Instead, I moved my single chair down to the beach and sat. I glared at the opposing \ntree line, rolling waves of the river, occasional critter that hopped by. I suppose this is where the appeal of camping is, being able to disconnect from the stress of reality and merely.. observe. We often take for granted what surrounds us, yet if we\nallow ourself a single moment here and there.. It's relaxing.. It may have taken me close to two saints week to realise such, but thats not important. Camping isn't that awful.. I do miss my bed though.\n23rd of Sun's  Smile.\n\nBloody chair broke again.\n26th of Sun's Smile.\n\nUnfortuantly my relaxing experiance sitting upon the bank was abrubtly forced into an end today.. The weather had been lovely since I came here, sure the occasional drizzle of rain but otherwise fantastic.\nAnd yet, today, for some unknown reason.. Rain came down in bucket loads. It still hasn't stopped now! My crops have became flooded, my flooded, my fire flooded, my rebuilt chair taken away by the flooding river. Whatever the cause of this madness I sure\nhope it ends it's terrible rage soon. I had some food stocked within the tent at least, so I shan't go hungry.. I quite enjoying observing the flames that rested below my feet at night, the heat against the freezing winds of night, the calming light it \nprovided. Now I sit in this shite tent, the only light source a shite candle, the only heat source this shite blanket. Times like this make my want to pack up, and buggar off to a nice tavern for the night.. Probably once close by, they're bloody \neverywhere. Only if Arin could whitness the misery I'm going through right now.\n28th of Sun's Smile.\n\nI awoke this morning to not that of the downpour of rain against my tent, but that of a bird chirping. Finally! It had cleared from the skies and in it's place the lingering sun that felt like cotton against my raw skin. This was\nnot the only thing to give me a pleasant grin this morning however.. For as I left my tent, a stag stood within my now flooded grain fields, feeding on whatever was left. I was amazed, I've never seen one in the wild, it stood proud.. strong.. graceful. \nI would have watched it for hours, yet unfortuantly my clumsy foot hit that of a stray twig and it soon pelted towards the tree line. Interesting how despite having the strength to easily overcome me, it cared not for the threat, rushing away instead\nof engaging the threat.\n3rd of The Amber Cold.\n\nThe Amber Cold.. The tempreture may become chilled.. Rain more often.. Animals less present.. And yet, I care not. I'm watching the trees around me change in this influential stage of nature.. Leaves turning brown \nupon the tips of their branchs, frosty morning grass, early sunsets that seem to dominate that of the other seasons. You dont get to whitness this transisition under normal circumstances and it's brilliant. It's almost exciting to awake every morning and \nlook outside, seeing which leaves have browned.. what colour the sunrise may be.. Questions I've never even care of, yet when 'forced' into this situation I do not regret a moment.\n5th of The Amber Cold.\n\nThe tempreture sure drops quick come this month.. The days are fair, enough to still operate on and yet the nights bring my arms to shiver and legs to.. quiver? Aha! A rhyme! However once again I care not of this \ntempreture drop.. For, I can sit by the fire and allow it's warmth to lick against my skin. I've almost become addicted to the sensation, I'm reliant on the poor sod.\n8th of The Amber Cold.\n\nI've started packing, should be all done by tomorow. I've spent.. nearly two saint months lingering in these woods? Oddly I shall miss it, it's offered me a different perspective on the outdoors in general.\nFor although many of it is there to harm you.. Cold.. Animals.. Even that of poison plants, just as much is there to help you. Such as the fire! Without it, the nights would have frozen my body solid.. I suppose thats why the druids have such belief in \nbalance, for it can be seen all around us. Despite all of this time here, one moment stuck out to me.. When the stag wondered into my camp, it's just a wonderful creature and yet often a rare site to the eye for it easily darts away when we approach. A \nshame those of certain aspirations tend to hunt the creature.. That may be why he was inclined to flee. I've even managed to fumble up some skills during my time here, for one I can now.. sort of tend a farm.. Build a chair.. Put up a tent.. Perhaps one \nday I shall return to me small settlement I have created here.\n\nCamping isn't that bad, it turns out.", ""),
        StaticBook("Canons of Honour", "Berilac Goldworthy", "      \"Canons of Honour\"\n\nAs written, the following cards explain the meaning of Aesculian honour - Bastokarla - as based upon the Resol'nare, six, last commandments of St. Elam left to the Descendants and upheld by followers of Fjordin Sylver.\nBa'jur - Education.\n\nSome believe that children are a blank card. Some others find faith in the belief that we are born, and die, with certain knowledge encrypted in our heads like incantations upon a blade. Education means many things. Sometimes, it is\nteaching skills, abilities. How to plow a field, write and read, hammer the red hot ferrum. We learn, and so we forge ourselves. But as we are young, we've usually little to no true ability to discern evil from good - and to choose the right path for us \nto follow. Children are aenguls, but aenguls easily misguided and even more so easy to destroy. It is up to us as parents and Askalians whole to uphold the traditions and pass them onto the new generations, meaning that so long as at least a single \nchild of Sylver lives, true honour will never perish. \nRaise your child to be strong and resistant, capable of looking after itself and it's fellow generation, teach it kindness for any good hearts and despisal for the signs of vileness - of weakness and \nyou shall know that you are following the right path. \n\nBeskar'gam - Armor\n\nA warrior is more then his armor, and that is to be remembered. But for the Sylva'ada, armor is a sign of solidarity and honour, it represents everything that we are or want to be\namong the Descendants - it is meant to be pure and strong. It is a sign of companionship, for in the armor, we all are the same, men and women, Descendant races all alike - so that we can always tell ourselves from aruetii.\nAra'nov - Defense\n\nDefense means many things for our people. It means standing up for our ideals, people and things we love. \n\nIt also means our ability to defend ourselves and each other that we pride ourselves in - for just as our bodies are shielded\nby our armor and training, our souls remain pure and strong, burning bright whereas those of the degenerate are but fickle lights above the swamp. \nIt means something we all should remember - that a true warrior isn't an aggressor. A true warrior is a\nprotector, a defensor. We must value the lives bestowed upon the oyu'baat, the multiverse as much as we value the ability to take it, lest we all become degenerates and bootlicks to Iblees, and forsake our ideals and the one, true honour.\nAliit - Tribe\n\nBack, long before the colony was settled, each of us had a different past and a different story to tell. Misfits, deserters, outcasts, united together by a hope for prosperity, led to the first of our fatherlands by the vision of our \nbeloved leader - and soon, did we realize, that what lives we had before didn't matter greatly - we were free from our sins and from our past. From our secrets and our downfalls. We weren't who we used to be. We were children of Sylver, and we were born \nanew to work for bettering of ourselves, each other, and oya'baat itself. We fought, we bled, and we grew accustomed to each other. Whomever we were before, we were one people - if perhaps a people missing identity. Resol'nare provided us with that, and \nwe proudly upheld the name of Sylva'ada, swearing to protect each other and our homeland, our business and families. \nSylalat - Language\n\nA grandchild to the speech of Bastura, Sylalat was developped for the simple mean of creating a personal, private form of communication to strenghten our identity. Simplistic, gender-neutral and highly dependant\non context, it remains in our grasp as something to wield with just as much pride as we wield our weapons, as we don our armor. Sylalat gives us the ability to speak without aruetii intrusion on our privacy, leaving any Sylva'ada truly\nfree in speech and manners, while also providing us with a single language we can use, for regardless who we used to be, where we came from, what tongue do we speak, one can always know that there is at least one common ground for us to speak in - one \nthat we all know and remember for days that were, and those to come.\nWield it with pride, and you shall do honour to each other and the legacy you leave for your children to carry.\nSylva'alor - Our Leader\n\nDerriving from the tradition of Basta'alor, the Sole Ruler of Honour, men and women of Sylvaestina who became Aesculians call their single leader Sylva'alor, in honour of the ambitious governor who brought them all together \n- Fjordin Sylver, a wood elf born and a Orenian bred, who, with the wise king Olivier de Savoie's blessing began settling magnitude of individuals in the area of mesa that'd later be known as Provincia Sylvaestina. \nSylva'alor isn't a king, and he isn't a lordling, in spite of the habit of Orenians calling the ruler of clans \"Lord Sylvalore\" or just \"Lord Sylver\" - the man or woman assuming that rank isn't just a blueblood. He or she is the first among equals, the \nparamount example of ideals that tied us together, burning with the same spirit that made first of us follow our beloved leader - he or she has to be a warrior, general and patriarch or matriarch at once. While the family may be staying\nautonomous in many a case, governing itself whenever it be necessary, it was and always is our duty to rally to our leader's call - to answer the call of the one we deemed worthy to be the living avatar of our honour, our faith and our indomitable \ndetermination to survive and combat Iblees and his bootlicks at any chance possible. We are Sylva'ada, and we shall carry the title of children of Sylver with same pride an aruetii may call himself a Vladov or de Sola. We are one people, even if many.\nThree Daemonic Warnings:\n\nOne - Never hurt children, for they are the greatest gift Descendants were given above all else.\n\nTwo - Always repay in kind. For kindness, kindness, for joy, joy, for sorrow, sorrow, and for blood, blood.\nThree - Remember that regardless of who you are, and how unremarkable you may be, you are always one of many - and together, you can achieve so much more.\nFor those seeking guidance: On traditions.\n\n\"Sha'kajir\" - \"Over a meal\" - as a people that rarely have a good chance to feast together, it should always be perceived as a celebration. Some of us do truly view it as the most extravagant and noble way\nof debating over matters, or deciding for a business contract, usually over meals usually taking longer to eat, such as snacks and soothing wine. \n\n\"Darasuum\" - Eternity.\nLove and marriage.\n\nLove is a quirky little thing. Can be infatuation. Can be \nsome charms being cast down like sunlit sprinkles of dust. But sometimes, that feeling is true and overcoming - and when the two feel like it, they may wish to take another promise for each other. Some of the romantic traditions among our folks include \nthe heads of respective families blessing the two and aiding them into an exchange of gift, after which comes the exchange of words:\n\"Mhi solus tome, mhi solus dar'tome, mhi me'dinui an, mhi ba'juri verde.\"\n\"We are one when together, we are one when parted, we will share all, we will raise warriors.\"\nFamily and adoption:\n\n\"Aliit ori'shya tal'din\" or \"family is more then blood\" pretty much sums up the sincere belief that blood ties may have worth, but in the long run, don't mean as much as those we choose to establish and uphold. \nThat is also why among us it is possible for children to denounce parents unworthy of their love - and as such, carry out a parental divorce, shedding any allegiance they owed to them - sometimes so that they can ensure the cin vhetin, pure start, not \nunlike the \"first turn of the screw\" rule, of their life among Sylva'ada - where they might be adopted. Traditional ritual includes sharing sangu'gal, bloodwine, with following words: \n\"Ni kar'tayl gai sa'ad.\" \"I know your name as my child.\"\nFor bloodlines and lineage mean little to those that never rest in their war with Iblees. Gar taldin ni jaonyc; gar sa buir, ori'wadaas'la, as the saying goes, ranging back to the first days of Sylvaestian rebirth:\n\"Bloodline is not important, but you as a parent, are most important of things.\" or as some interpret it, nobody cares who your parents were, only the parent you will be - emphasizing the importance of our role in raising the future generations, and \nstating clearly that an individual is judged by more then his ancestors. \nRemembrance - no man or woman has truly passed away while they are remembered - and while the joys of paradise may be at their reach, we, who sweat for the divine work, rarely remember that - knowing only the bitter emptyness that was left in our heart at\nloved one's passing. Some find comfort in aay'han, meditation of balance - joy of solidarity and companionship of fellow Sylva'ada filling their hearts, while still tearing those with memory of the brothers and sisters lost, a sensation at the verge of \npain. Bittersweet it is, and some of us simply find ourselves in remembering - every day, once, at the passing of hours, do we kneel and praying, do we carry out the remembrance of ours, contemplating on our future in heaven.\n\"Ni su'cuyi, gar kyr'adyc, ni partayli, gar darasuum\" - \"I am still alive, but you are dead. I remember you, so that you are eternal.\", do we say, speaking out all those we wish to remember, whom we held dear, respected or loved. \nRet'lini - while the canons are your guide, you must remember, that the only constant in the multiverse is change - and that over, even if our honour shall still apply, many things may change - and you shouldn't struggle. For the beauty of shereshoy, our\njoy and thirst for life and combat, lies in countless means to interpret it - and our ability to cull down the poor interpretations, and uphold those worthy of passing onto new generations. I, for one, Berilac of clan Nightgrove, wish you, children of \nSylver and God, good luck. K'oyacyi. Oya Sylva!", ""),
