        StaticBook("Cervitaur", "Athe'lor", "Basic records of the Cervitaur language, or Relriera.\n\nYes - Irrar\nNo - Lu\nHello - Harru\nGoodbye - Ruunfirra\n[Good = Ruun]\n[Firra = Bye]\n\nBad - Fen\nSometimes - Runadainar\nIs - Air\nAlso - Erru\nAnd - Eln\nUnderstand - Ilnasrdeln\nLanguage - Relriera\n\nGrass - Rserr\nWater - Wedas\n[Run = Sil]\n[Running = Rasirr]\nFlowers - Llruwas\nStuff - Rdillll\nBook - Fuuc\n\nKill - Cairr\nEvil - Ayair\nL turns into R\nS turns into R\nO turns into U\nA turns into E\nE turns into A\nB turns into F\nD turns into N\nI turns into AI\nU turns into I\nN turns into L\nF turns into LL\nG turns into R\nA - E     B - F\nD - N     E - A\nF - LL     G - R\nH - H     I - AI\nK - C     L - R\nM - N     N - L\nO - U     R - S\nS - R     T - D\nU - I     W - W\nY - RR\nThrough simple calculation and study, I have confirmed that the translation from Cervitaur to Common can be found by replacing letters with combinations of other letters, as shown on the previous page. The previous page does not contain a few letters-\nfrom the Common language, and this is because I was not taught any of the words in Cervitaur that included said letters for me to translate.\n\nThis concludes my very minimal study into the Cervitaur language. More may follow.\n\nAthe'lor.", ""),
        StaticBook("CH Handbook", "Saithor", "Introduction\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are a guild of Spellswords, Sellswords, Mages, and Scholars all alike, all seeking the same goal, knowledge, power, wealth, and fame.\nThe Hearts of this guild are brothers and sisters, bound by oath.\nPaths\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are divided into three categories. Knights, Mages, and Mechanists. No matter what path you pick, your brothers and sisters will protect you. And no matter what they pick, you will too.\nPeople of Honor\n-------------------Sonoren Klaren: He is the Ace of Hearts, our leader\nTalimeracahe: He is The Red Joker, second in command\nEdwyn Lynderly: He is the maker of the Crimson Hearth, the guild hall of the Crimson Hearts.\nTrainers o' the Paths\n-------------------Olympus: Trainer of the sword\nLelien: Trainer of the magic\nVirgo: Trainer of the Mechanists\nSaithor: Trainer of the bow and of the Realm\nRules\n-------------------1) Ye will protect your brothers and sisters\n2) You will obey all orders\n3) Knights will remain loyal\n4) Mages will heed to heal\n5) Mechanists will procede to prosper\nPath o' Knight\n-------------------The path of the Knight consists of the noble warriors of the Heart. They are the men and women who seek to be armed with a sword, those who know how to use one, and those who wish to know. They are loyal to the Hearts\nPath o' Mage\n-------------------The path of the Mage consists of the arcanic people of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the arts of magic. They heed to heal us, and will continue to do so.\nPath o' Mechanist\n-------------------The path of the Mechanist consists of the artisans and merchants of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the most money and fame they can get. They will procede to prosper.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chamber Proceeds", "Alexander Bedevere", "-Outer Chamber Rules- Prerequisites:\n -Each Guild in attendance may have only one representative sitting in house. \n-Every meeting, your chosen representative may change if it suits  you better, but we prefer it stays the same.\n\n-If you miss a congregation, then know your voice will not be heard, for any debates taking place that day.\n-Failure to conduct one's self appropriately in Council may result in temporary or permanent expulsion, so be respectful \nand follow these court proceeds.\n\nChamber Procedures:\n\nAt the beginning of each meeting, the Tribune shall first take a quick roll call, then proceed with announcements.\n Announcements can include numerous things such as events, legislation or ongoing issues. All of which are expected to be discussed over the coming hours amongst the outer chamber.After announcements, the Chamber is in session,\nand each topic will be debated over. Opinions issued, solutions, ect. Proceeds go as follows. The Tribune will first state the issue at hand, then ask for opinions. \n-One raises their hand prior if they wish to speak. \n\n-Chamber men will not speak, in any circumstances, over each other. If done, you will be issued a verbal warning.\n-While a speaker is debating, you shall demonstrate full and absolute attention to them. This means do not raise your hand if someone is \nalready speaking.\n-If an issue needs to be discussed, then the court may vote on debating it in full at a later date.\n-If it's decided that the issue does not need to be discussed further, then the Tribune will ask if the Chamber can move on.\nOnly speak if you feel this matter needs more discussion. It is at this point that the Tribune will decide whether or not the Chamber proceeds. If there are more than three whom oppose it, then it will be discussed further.\n\nThis process is repeated with the next topic, and the next. Until you have reached the end of the list.\n\nOnce all official matters have been discussed, the Tribune will ask if there are any questions, or if anyone would like to add on.\nIt goes in order, starting from his rightmost chair, to his leftmost. If your name is called, but you've nothing to say, simply say, \"Pass\". If you've been called on and you wish to speak, then stand and begin speaking. If it's a matter of debate,\nthen it will be voted on whether or not we should discuss it next meeting. It needs a minimum of 30% to pass. Once passed, it will be added to the court for next week's meeting.\n\nFinally, after all voices have been heard, the Tribune will finally dismiss \nthe court.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chest Locks", "Hadrien Blade Valdeg", "I need locks on certain chests in the Storeroom (upstairs) of the Valdeg Lumber storefront (they will be marked with signs). They should only be availible to me, Hadrien Valdeg, ((OKUDKREESH))", ""),
        StaticBook("Childish Diary", "Irsia Tehrani", "  ><><><><><><><><><><\n\n\nThings to do before I\n            die\n\n\n\n     Jean Briarwood\n1) Drink   unchaperoned.   \n\n2) Swim in the river in underclothes.\n\n3) Smoke Cactus Green\n\n4) Get married.\n\n5) Dress like a man for a day.\n6) Break into a lock box.\n\n7) Steal from a woman.\n\n8) Get revenge on Christopher Blackwell.\n\n9) Pierce her ears.\n\n10) Get a tattoo ", ""),
        StaticBook("Chimera Notes", "Briar Ophiuchus", "[This book contains various notes, based on Nienna's chimera research.\n\nThere are unfamiliar formulas for life essence, and a design to make an asterwaldian eagle and phoenix chimera for Yaen.\nThe writing shows that briar was probably drunk.\n\nScrawled in a corner is a little note, briar saying he loves yaen so much, and is afraid to say no to him cuz Yaen might leave.]", ""),
