        StaticBook("De Shroom Guide", "Madpen Brookflint", "De Purpose of this book is te ca'alouge any an' all fungi, fungus, shrooms an' differen' 'ypes of Mycelium. This lis' will undoub'udly be expanded as Me colec's more specimens. Each Specimen will be ge'ing a pic'ure an' description. -Madpen\nDe \"Shroom\" clasification be given te a fungi when i' meets cer'ain cri'eria. -------------------I' mus' 'ave a stalk of some sor', an' a distinc'ive cap. This 'oo par' structure is wha' seperates it. Shrooms are usualy found in groups, or clus'ers.\nBoomafool Shroom or\nBooming Fowl Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom is fairly common, i' grows on rocks, s'eep 'ills or under 'rees. It has a large pocket of a very ligh' gas in i's stalk. This pocket is esential. When de Boomafool begins to spore, i'\nde'aches from de ground and floa's upwards. It will either hi' a tree and de'ona' or i' will get blown away. When i' takes a blow, de top section explodes releasing the spores. De spores of de Boomafool are very small and liable to ge' stuck in ye eyes.\n\n\n_______________/~~_________\n            \\____\n                    \\____\n\n\n\n  __\n/##\\\n_||||||________________The Boomafool -Maddy\nRepiluca or\nCreeping Glow Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom is fairly common in caves, generaly on limes'one it grows in spall 'oles in de wall. A Faint glow is produced by spots on i'. De Repiluca is often used in mixings of Acui'y. \n_____________\n                   \\\n                     \\\n                      |\n                      |\n                      |\n      /++\\    ___/\n_____||||||___/\n\nThe Repiluca\n-Maddy\nNote: The Repiluca clones ocasionaly.\nBlack Capped River Shroom or Umbra-oom\n-------------------The Umbra-oom is much larger then previous Shrooms. It 'as a long an' curved s'alk with a bell shaped hood. I' is normaly found next to rivers as i' consumes river bir's tha' crash in'o it. The Umb\nra-oom can be harvested in large chunks, and will consume an' disolve anythin' tha' falls in'o i'.\n-------------------I' is safe less you fall on de 'op. Then ye should be screaming.\n\n\n    __________\n   /              \\\n   |                |\n  /___________\\\n        ||||||||||||\n         ||||||||||||\n          ||||||||||||\n            |||||||||||\n             \\|||||||\\\n            /||||||||||||||\\\nThe Umbra-oom\n-Maddy\nSafron Tree Shroom\nYellow Cap Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom be of'en confused with a Frazzlebush when i's small. I' is covered in a thick layer of vines and pe'als. Should any par' of the pe'als be eaten de consumer will become very agressive and \nwill have a craving for more. De pe'als are a mix of safron an' a bright white.\n        #######0##\n      ###0#########\n      ########0####\n      0############\n      #############\n      ####0########\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\nThe Safron Tree Shroom\n-Maddy\nFireball Shroom\nSpotted Orb Shroom\n-------------------There is nothing much to say about this shroom. Despite i's name i's no' flamable. I' is of'en made in'o soup or use' in a salad.\n\n\n       _________\n     /              \\\n     |                |\n     |                |\n     \\_________/\n         |||||||||||||||||\n         |||||||||||||||||\n         |||||||||||||||||\nFireball Shroom\n-Maddy\nDining Plate Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom comes in many sha'es and sizes. It 'as a long stalk and a reli'ivly flat and 'ard cap. I' is of'en used as a pla'e when a good one is no' available, as i' 'as no effec' on de consumer.\n\n\n___\n  |\n\n        __________\n        |_________|\n              |||||\n              ||||| \n              |||||\n              |||||\n___     ___\n  |         |\nGiant Cluster Shroom\n-------------------Las' bu' no' leas': This Shroom is a sigh' te be'old. Much like de Spotted Orb Shroom bu' this one grows in massive pods. I' 'as no inherent use bu' 'as been used as 'ousing an' is considered sacred by many.\n    _____________\n  /_____________\\\n           ||||||||\n ___      ||||||||\n/__\\     |||||||||\n  ||||       |||||||||\n           |||||||||    ___\n           |||||||||   /__\\\n           |||||||||     ||||\n           |||||||||\nGiant Cluster Shroom\n-Maddy\nOther Tomes of de Fungi by \nMadpen Brookflint:\n\nA guide te infec'ions, fungus an' Myceliums\n\nRiver Fish o' Maliner\n\nA Guide te 'oilet makin'\n\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Deadly Diseases", "daelaris", "A collection of my limited knowledges in the medical field of infectious diseases.\n\nBo'dank is an extremely contagious disease. It is a bacterial infection of the respiratory tract. It is airborne and spread by inhalation. The symptons are the worst -\n- part of Bo'dank.  Those with Ki'katta are more susceptible to the disease. The symptons are as follows:\n\nFever\nChills\nCoughing\nItchy throat\nBuild-up of mucus\nEye pain\nConfusion\nThis disease is so widespread, that it will typically happen once to every person.\nKi'katta is another contagious disease, a key denoter is that people infected are more susceptible to Bo'dank. Doctors have little idea on the origins of the disease, but it typically is not fatal. It will leave those inflicted in pain for up to weeks.\nSymptoms are as follows:\n\nFever\nAbdominal Pain\nRedness of the eyes\nDehydration\nCramps\nWeakened Bones\nDiarrhea\nGrish is one of the nastier diseases, caused by poisoning from raw or rotton meat. The devestating part of this ailment is the extremely high mortality rate, a massive seventy percent. Those who do survive will have to deal with many side-effects, such -\n- as mental impairment, vision loss and numbess of digits or tongue. This is a result of little blood flow to the nerves. Symptons are as follows: Constriction of blood vessels,\nanxiety\nvertigo\nstrange vissions, dreams, hallucinations\nBlackened skin.\nEasily the deadliest disease in all of the realms, the plague strikes quickly and it hits hard. It has a high fatality rate and was first recording in year Thirty-seven of Asulon, in Seventis. The infected began to die in mass numbers, quickly spreading -\n- spreading to nearby settlement. All attempted cures have failed, the monk's magics unable to cure it. Many nations implemented quarentines, and, with time, the disease subsided. There are several variations of the disease.\nGreen-spot variation:\n\nGreen dots that cause itching.\nNumbness.\nWeakness, Fatigue.\nMemory loss and bi-polar mood swings.\nVomiting, typically with blood.\nCoughing up blood.\nBlack-Spot Variation:\n\nShivers, tremors and muscle spasms.\n\nExtreme Paranoia.\n\nCoughing up blood.\n\nHemophobia.\n\nInternal hemorrhage, fatal.\nWheat was also infected by this disease, and all types of beasts suffered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Gemmy", "{OOC}[SM]-SparehoeCakes", "Dear Gemmy,\nI found your island. The house is pretty, and you got a good ass interior designer, you go girl. It's cute as fuq. \nAND IT'S ON A PRIVATE ISLAND LIKE OMG YOU DON'T EVEN KNOW. \n\nYours Truly,\n-SparehoeCakes", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Kelthran", "Abigail", "-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Dear Kelthran,\nIf you are reading this please take this as a token for actually saving me from staying uncoinsious on the ground near the gates of the elcihi. I...would like it if we could...go on a...date to have conversation on such \ntopics. I..\nI'm just really thankful that you saved my life, and for that I should repay you llir. If when you can, you can send me a letter or a bird so that we can meet somewhere in private...\nAheran again Kelthran.\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n[!]You see the signature of Abigail at the bottom with a small symbol of a thumbs up, and a heart next to it.", ""),
        StaticBook("DEAR MILO", "Dalek348", "8========D ~ ~~~\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Rabbit", "Damien Menrow", "Dear Rabbit....my legs are getting weak..... chasing you....\n\n\n\nAnd the snowfields.... Wouldn't seem so big.....if you knew....\nThat this blood on my teeth....it is far beyond dry...\n\nAnd I've captured you once....but it wasn't quite right...\n\nSo I'm telling you.... That you'll be safe with me....\n\nOooooooo.....\nOh Rabbit....my claws are down now so don't be afraid....I can keep you warm...as long as you can just try....to be brave!\n\nYes I know I'm a wolf...and I've been known to bite....But the rest of my Pack...I've left them behind...\nAnd my teeth may be sharp....and I've been raised to kill....\n\n\nBut the thought of fresh meat....it's making me ill!\n\nSo I'm telling you.... That you'll be safe with.......\nMe....Oooooooo...\n\nSo Rabbit....please stop looking the oth... Other way...\n\nIt's cold out there.... So why not stay here... Under my tail....?*", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Strangeskin", "Mungo Proudfoot", "Deah Strangecolored skin,\n\nMe is tire' o' ye tryin' ter ea', kidnapp, 'ang, cu' in 'alf, drawn, burn and cook me.\n\nThis is a be..beoutiful place and ye ruin i'!\nSo while ye is readin' this lettah, me is scapin'.\n\nBa bye mistah!", ""),
        StaticBook("Dearz Burglarz", "Zargloth", "Ug! Mi nub likez bein'z robbedz, Mi sickz 'ndz tired ovz latz tryinz to kilz mi, \n\nso whilzt latz readinz letter miz scapinz", ""),
        StaticBook("Death Potions V2", "Jistuma", "\n\n*~Death\n\n          Potions~*\n\n\n\n\n\nVolume II – Pain\n\nIn the clutches of the underground rivers of the realms of the end, the drinks of the shadow ones, they make you closer to join them. Their tendrils and teeth suck the soul from your very being, dragging you onto their lands by chains.\nPain\n\nLow fires torment and blacken the bodies of the filth. Only through pain shall they know the reasons of the malevolence. \n\nGoblin’s Ivy to start up the brew, add it to water and let it heat. Green it will become, not the color to hold, the Night sap much then be added, to make it sweet and taste good. The more you add the more they’ll like the taste.\nThe Nether fires shall then come, Blazing powder to bring it forth. From the beasts of the lands of heat you must gather their rods, and grown them into thin powder without harm. Slowly the powder is mixed, slowly the sulfur combines.\nIt is strong, magical of the lands. Blessed by the darker flames of below, their skin shall breathe fire. Their heart shall only feel pain for the sins they have not done. \nFire Skin poison ingredients:\n\n- Blaze Powder \n- Cactus\n- Glistering Melon\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant Poem", "[Teen] Dedicant Veren", "The leaves rustle as the wind blows strong\nFlowers blossen and trees grow tall\nThe Druids protect this beutiful place\nWhile the Aspects guid with strength and grace \nThe druids watch the void grow strong Trying to protect the things we love\nAs nature listens, so sutle and quiet\nThe world grows on forever strong\nBy:\nDedicant Veren", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant Poem", "Veren Ibar'ker", "A Sheepish Writer's First Poem\n===================By: Andwise Peregrin\n\n\nFor all to marvel and recognize\nThere once was a mighty fine sheep\n-\nThe best one you would ever peep\n-\nSo I took the sheep and dyed it blue\n-\nA wonderful shade , color, and hue\n-\nI met the sheep on a glorious day\n-\nI thusforth named the sheep Maylarenray\n-\nI looked to the sky and saw an arch of hues\n-\nSo I took the sheep's wool and with dye imbued\n-\n\nThat was when I realized what changed my life\n-\nI recognized I didn't use shears, I just used a knife\n-\nI had pained the sheep yet profitted from its toil\n-\nBut isn't that how most people are, taking\nfrom nature, for personal gain, regardless of how the Aspects a affected, people take and take and use the soil\n-\nSo I demand that we as people across the realm give thanks and respect to the world we have.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant's Vow", "Tristanm1", "The Dedicant's Vow\nScribed by Salmon Druid Petyr\nI will walk the forest with my new kin, I will swim the river of truth, wherever it takes me. As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need, I will help preserve the balance, even as dusk approaches. \nI vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant's Vow", "12werbles12", "           ~*~\n  The Dedicant's Vow\n\nI now walk the forests with my new kin. I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me. As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need. I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk\n approaches. I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\n\n   by:\n   Salmon Druid Petyr\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will walk the forest with my new kin.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges his or her official ties to be with the Druids of the Druidic Order.\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges loyalty to the Order and thereby promises to speak the truth and never with deception.\n           ~*~\n\n\"As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need.\"\n\nWhile under the guidance of the Aspects and the elder Druids, the Dedicant pledges to return the favor of respect and service.\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk approaches.\"\n\nThe Dedicant pledges devout service, no matter the time nor obstacle he or she may face.\n           ~*~\n\n\"I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\"\n\nThe Dedicant does just that; he or she vows to uphold his or her duties and their pledge as a Dedicant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deed to Helgrind", "Ragaros Sheepskin", "*Written in all charcoal.*\n\nDeed to Helgrind-\nThis deed here for somereason gives you the ability to stay and live here on this land. While it's all land, for some reason this paper gives you the power to live here. Only a piece of paper!\nAnyhow, it gives you control of this region. Safe Winters.\n\n            -Clan\n               Orvar", ""),
        StaticBook("Deed: Sol Azirus", "Menithrian", "    -_=*(S.A)*=_-\n   \n    THE SALVIAN\n     CONSULATE\n        1510\n\n Deed on land of the\n  Republic of Salvus\n\n    Writ by Consul\n      Menithrian\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nDeed recipients: \n\nSol Azirus\nLinda Rose\n\nDeed entitlement: \n\na large plot of land, based off of the central road of Camp Tahunor. To be purposed as a manor\nfor its inhabitants. To include seperate physical decorations: a fox kennel, treehouse and capacity for Valaise operations. The Valaise shall include activities in breeding and carpentry - whilst maintaining effort on using existing supply chains. \nThe land is hereditary, passed to direct descendants of the recipients. Where an heir of this nature does not emerge, the land shall be reclaimed by the Salvian Authorities - with its associated Valaise, as a State-owned Venture.\n\nA fixed lump sum of\n10000 - 6750 to be paid instantly by Sol Azirus, with the remainder paid in due time. \n\nAll Standard laws and ideals are bound to this land - still soverign, in the name of the Republic. \n\nThe land may be leased to others, as long as..\na quarter of the lease is paid, as a duty, to the Salvian Authorities. \nBy signing this deed are all these clauses assumed legally binding, with breaches on this deed being a Republican offense, facing heavy fines.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nSIGNED: \n\nMenithrian.\nSol Azirus\nLinda Rose", ""),
        StaticBook("Defense Contract", "Tahjeet Mubdee", "<<><>Iron Corps<><>>\n{}Defense Contract{}\n\nThe Iron Corps will provide the Golden Glyph with a total of 30 bows and 167 Lapis Blocks. \n\nThe Golden Glyph will then enchant 15 of the bows with infinity, power, punch and\nfire. \n\nAnother 15 bows will be enchanted with power, punch, and fire.\n\nThis is to be completed by the 14th of the First Seed 1510.\n\nUpon completion, the Iron Corps will pay 1300 minas to the\nGolden Glyph.\n\nParties participating in this contract are the\nIron Corps and the Golden Glyph.\nIron Corps\n-Tahjeet Mubdee\n\nGolden Glyph\n-Mark Voltaire", ""),
        StaticBook("Defunct Writing.", "The Scribe.", "Why Poetry is Defunct.\nPoetry is the most useless form of writing. It seeks to convey a message in the form of a both a riddle and a rhyme. This is highly inefficient, as the message is deluded by the ornamentation used to create it in the\nfirst place. How can the message originally intended to be read keep its integrity when it is laden with unnecessary words that mean to weave into song? \n\nA song is perhaps a poem, but it is a preformance,\nnot an arrogant rendition of a message that is to be translated. Songs are set to music, and are designed to be entertainment, but poetry is just mindless babble with no point.\nA painting and a paper are very much comparable. Both try to convey a point or image, and do so by being as detailed and well set up as possible. However, a painting is not layed upon another painting, and then glued together with interweaving locks.\nThis would be the pinnacle of madness. This is what poetry is to sensible writing.\nPoetry is defunct.", ""),
        StaticBook("Delivery Birds.", "The Scribe.", "DELIVERY BIRDS.\nHow is it that birds are able to find the recipients of letters without knowledge of who they are needed to visit? My theory is that birds can be trained to detect the soulstones of those who need letters delivered to them. If this is true, can\nall animals sense soulstones?\n\nAll musings of course. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Denial of Hope", "The Eternal Librarian", "\n\n\n\n\n  A Denial of the\n Mystification of\n        Hope\n\n  by Amras Yavelty\n\nIt is prudent to mention that my writing doesn’t intend to deny hope as a valuable emotion of the being but instead explain it as a natural occurring phenomena and not a religion justifying emotion. It seems that hope arises whenever the 'self is\nunder siege’ from within or externally. When I use the phrase ‘self under siege’ I mean the being in which hope occurs is undergoing an emotional, physical or mental conflict as a result of internal or external factors.\nThe problemwith hope is that it often misleads the being into identifying hope as an inner sixth sense that gives out or provides some kind information about divine entities and their bond with beings. Hope indeed is a strong emotion and is one that\nseems to arise even in the most direst of situations. This is explained easily because hope is, none the less, an impulse of the being to maintain it alive and relevant in the world. It is, after all, a common use of hope in Druid religion in which it had\nbeen used to indirectly justify the beliefs and cults regarding their gods. \n\nIt is a foolish notion a sir tends to disregard that hope is not a product of the mind, but instead an impulse of the being to survive, a reflex, therefore it cannot\nbe used in the rational process. It is from this statement that I can conclude that any justification of religious beliefs and cults through the false definition of hope are irrational and untrustworthy in their nature and is by all cost all logic is to\nbe avoided by the Mali'aheral.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desc. Leaves", "Callax", "           -=-=-=-=-=-\n          Descending\n              Leaves\n           =-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nAs the tree grows older, its roots wither and from the lack of nutrient the tree, too, withers. The tree, stiff and hollow, is parched and barren. Its leaves descend, becoming fewer and fewer. Like the leaf, I descend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Bezerkers", "Durza Volkihar", "The Orcs of the desert are bezerking abominations.They crave war and fighting. the majority of fights i have been in and have witnessed have been created by orcs.They do not speak a normal tounge.Their tounge isnt as elegant as the elfs or a simple as the\nmen of oren or the dwarves.Their language is called the blah.The blah shouldnt even be considered a language at all, it is just a series of grunts and guttaral sounds.They often resort to eating people to stop there endless hunger for meat and blood.\nThere are three types of Orcs:\n\nThe Uruk: The Uruk is the most common of the orcish blood.They have a very limited volcabulary and a limted brain size.They are very skilled in combat though.\nThe Goblin: The goblin is considered the smartest of the race of orcs but the weakest and smallest. What they lack in braun they make up for in brain size and wit.\nThe Olog: The Olog is the strongest and powerful of all the orc's. They are the dumbest of all the orc's. They do not possess the ability to think. They are mindless beasts built for one pupose, war\nIt is obvious that the orcs are a race that only cares about war. The only execption for that is the goblins who would rather tinker with devices than fight every creature they come across. The word negotiate is not in their vocabulary.\nIf you share these views come find me.\n\n\n[!] A red eagle is drawn here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Creatures", "Professor Franklin Gavin", "         The Jabbernack and the Scaddernak\n\n\n This devastating beast plays a bigger role in transportation throughout Orcish lands than anything else. Although, even though it is mainly used in transportation, do not let that \nfool you. The Jabbernack is still an extremely deadly foe to even an Orc, its razor sharp teeth and claws will end a foe in seconds. Jabbernacks are solitary creatures and are incredibly hard to breed, only a select few are able to breed Jabbernacks.\n  The Scaddernak\n\nMighty War beasts, having been used by the Orcs for hundreds of years to fight. They can be tamed only by master hunters and those foolish enough to try. They can easily tear\nanyone who crosses their path in two. Scaddernaks are huge, dark creatures that resemble a mix of spider and scorpion with eight legs and a giant pincer. hey have two\nclaws bigger than an entire Orc and enough strength to smash down a fort in seconds. They are usually black or sandy coloured.\n KNOWN SCADDERNAKS\n\nLurgoi-Scaddernak of the Lur clan, tamed by\nBer'lur and given to Craotor. Took a bite out of Fort Krug when it got hungry. It was brought to Asulon on the Mighty Orcish Boat and it resided inside Strigzgoi for a small while until it feasted upon a hut,  it was then moved to the Lur Camp\n and it is in a slumber there until someone awakes it. The Previous Scaddernak of Ber'lur, now belongs to Craotor.\n\nThe Kar'ak Scorpion\n\nA pre-historic, rogue breed of Scaddernack, previously thought to be extinct.\nPossibly the last of it's kind. Slain by great warrior Tythor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Design Proposal", "Belegar Grandaxe", "'ail, King Fimlin. T'is is Belegar Grandaxe, newest member of t'e engineer's guild and I 'ave two build proposals fer yeh. T'e first is w'at I loike teh call t'e \"Auto Furnace one t'ousand\". It is an automated furnace t'at can process an unlimited amount\nof materials wit' an unlimited amount of fuel going into it and it will automatically put t'e products into a c'est. I can s'ow yeh an example of t'is (we got one in Ekren, now known as t'e Garden of S'adows now t'at Beros left). If yeh want teh c'eck it\nout just let meh know. T'e second is a little more impractical and niche, and I am not sure t'at yeh will find a use for it but 'ere it is. It is an auto sorter fer items t'at are put into it. It can sort out w'at ever items yeh want it to and place t'em\ninto a desired c'est or even into a furnace or somet'ing of t'e like. I can also give yeh more of a explanation in person if yeh need it. If yeh 'ave any questions feel free teh ask. T'anks fer yeh time.\n\n-Belegar Grandaxe", ""),
        StaticBook("Devotion", "Lielle Des'nox", "The time without you, it has been long\nAnd my heart still sings the song\nOf sorrow without you here,\nBut I'll forever hold you dear.\n\nMy devotion will not be swayed,\nAnd I miss you more and more each and every day\nThat passes by without you here.\nForever, I'll love you, my dear.\n\nYour laughter and smile,\nThe sounds of our children, \nHolding you both in my embrace,\nThings are things I miss the most.\nYou will forever live on in my heart.\nAnd whenever I do depart\nFrom this world at my life's end,\nI will be with you again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 2", "Greenfingers", "*The top half of the entry is ripped off*\n\ngrow several, deadly plants in various locations around the land.\n\nI keep seeing strange symbols and phrases dotted about the walls of the house and all over these notes.\nThey say things such as \"...Filthy Tree huggers...\", \"...Vicious felines...\" and \"...Stupid long-ears...\"\n\nPerhaps these are clues as to who he means to inflict these plants of his upon...or perhaps they are merely the crazed writings of a madman...\nEntry 5600\n\nThese notes are unlike anything I have ever seen...\n\nI have been studying them for a while now and these plants he plans to create are horrific.\n\nThey seem to be bred\nto do nothing but fight. The Master really has lost the plot...\n\nThere is something else about these plants...they are incredibly tough. He seems to want to have them posess a thick skin that, in his words, \"Will deflect an axe as easily as a troll\ncan throw a feather.\"\n\nI managed to find the section upon how to get past their deadly hides...\n\nIt involves using a blade imbued with\n\n*The entry is torn apart here...*", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 3", "Greenfingers", "*The entry is scuffed and ripped at its top*\n\na combination of Night Sap and Mandragora Leaf...however there is something else...\n\nIt needs something much darker...much more magically influenced...\nIt requires a soul...my soul in fact...\n\nWhy would the master need my soul? Why can it not be anybody else's soul? Has he made me a part of the plant?\n\nHow can he have? He hasn't taken any of me for... *It trails off*\nThe experiment that made me into what I am...\n\nThat is how he somehow implemented parts of my very being into those monstrosities of his...\n\nBut wait...it requires blood too...\nI cannot give my own blood...not now that I have none...\n\nI shall have to find others...others who can help, lest these foul creations that master wishes to grow inflict death and pain across the entire land...", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of L.S.", "Lucion Sullas", "   -==One's Diary==-\n\n            L.S.\n\nI have decided to embark upon an expedition to the Bortu lands. I tire of the ceaseless politics, what with the Mali'ame rabble-rousing and so-forth. Thankfully, \nI was not the only individual who balked at the thought of a mass-slaughter. Phaedrus will have to be placated in some other manner; further trivial responsibilities ought to be sufficient. \n\nThat, I hope, shall be the end of it.\n   -==Entry One==-\n\nI managed to smuggle my way between Uruk and Bortu lands, seeking this supposed geological anomaly. One admits that he is no avid climber, but I managed to reach an abandoned Bortu watch-fort on the cliff-face. Bortu\narchitecture is certainly robust, though one wonders what they planned to observe upon this sheer cliff-face. Never-the-less, the actual entrance from the Bortu capitol has been collapsed, thus I doubt I will be disturbed. I will continue my search\nupon the next day. It is peaceful, to say the least. No grumbling Mali'ame to disturb me, or the nonsense of Uradir to irritate me. I suspect this trip may last longer than previously planned.\n   -==Entry Two==-\n\nI have found the cave! The geological anomalies certainly did not disappoint. The crystalline structures are quite unique in their strange formation. Multicoloured and brittle, I can't imagine how they managed to\nsurvive the Bortu's habitation of the surrounding lands. Perhaps they do not plunge within this mountain? I dare not take samples in case I destroy the formations entirely. But I shall perform rudimentary tests until a satisfactory method of extraction\ncan be formulated. Larihei willing, I shall find a way.\n -==Entry Three==-\n\nI am beginning to suspect the formations are magical in nature. You can imagine my utter disappointment. There appears to be no beginning to the crystals. They practically 'sit' upon the rock; balancing precariously \non the cave itself. Some sorcerer must have found a way to manipulate trace sources of minerals in the stone, and concentrate it into singular structures. I recognise one of the formations as pyrite, but the others are alien to me. Not that I particularly\ncare, mind. Magical origins are desperately uninteresting. I shall end this expedition early, and return home. I hope the Mali'ame have quietened down. Their screeching is most tiresome.\n  -==Entry Three==-\n\nWhat have I done?\n\nThey're killing us. Declarations have been signed. So many nations are resolute in our total extermination. They have taken the city. Golden tear-drop tattoos, and halflings\ncalling for our mass-murder. No-one deserves this. If only I had remained in the city, I might have done something. Curse my distracted mind, and curse me for the death of my people.\n\nThere are no words to describe my horror. I must flee, and\nruminate upon what to do.\n   -==Entry Five==-\n\nThat filthy, mud-skinned, traitorous animal. I should have killed him for his entreatment of Uruks. He is the one who formulated it all. I will not let this stand. I will wait, and I will study. I shall build something to\nannihilate him and the rest of his murderous brood. His harlot druid and child along with him. They will all pay for what they have done. \n  -==Entry Six==-\n\nIt has been some time since my last entry. I have been travelling, mostly. Hiding in locations far from the monsters in the West. Currently, I am observing what appears to be an Undead fortress. At least, I suspect it is. \nThere is a primal dread in my heart when I look upon the floating mass. This descrepit fortress itself makes me uneasy. It is said Mali'aheral are sensitive to magic, and if that is so, it would explain why I can taste something foul in the air. Then\nagain, this whole swamp is naturally unpleasant. I shall move on within the next week. This place is simply too unnerving for me to concentrate.\n\nSo far, I have made little progress in my weapon. Trying to re-create a steam-golem from\nscratch is difficult, to say the least. If only I took Triarch with me.\n  -==Entry Seven==-\n\nUpon my last day in the swamp, I was greeted by the mud-covered, shambling form of my golem Triarch. The fellow was in need of significant repair, but transmutation makes such things trivial. He was carrying a sack of new blades, and \nnote from that traitorous ball of faeces Dak'ir. I ought to enchant them with lightning, and kill the beast, but I cannot risk giving away my continued existance. He mocks me with this letter. He will die slowly.\n  -==Entry Eight==-\n\nI find myself near the edge of the 'civilised' world. I have not seen an Akovian hamlet for quite some time. I am mostly apalled, however, that I am incapable of building any death-machine without a golem core. The one within Triarch\nis confoundingly complex. When I sketch the runes, they seem to change upon my next viewing. I have my doubts that I will ever reverse-engineer one of these accursed cores. I shall have to build my own version from scratch.\n  -==Entry Nine==-\n\nI have returned to Elven lands. I expected to see grand trees dotting my people's lands, but instead I discovered a sheer cliff-face, surrounded by silver walls. I had first thought that the Mali'ame simply copied our architecture, but\nthe guards at the gate were Mali'aheral! They were dressed in the regailia of the Sillumir! There is a town below them, filled with the Mali'ame and Ker. Have we re-established control? How did my people survive? I shan't approach yet. It may be a trick.\n  -==Entry Ten==-\n\nI am currently watching a vicious battle. My people, and what appears to be the humans (though I don't recognise the sigil they march under) are attacking the Mali'ame and Bortu in some underground facility. I must say,\nI felt all-together too pleased to see them slaughtered. I hope Phaedrus was among them.\n\nMy people were victorious. I have not seen anyone other than my kindred and humans exit the facility. This certainly put a spring in my step, \nthough my disgust of our wayward 'cousins' has dulled somewhat. My work on building a coreless steam-golem has turned out fruitless, anyway. One simply cannot create an operating system complex enough to be the match of any average soldier. However, I did\nmanage to design a simple book-publishing mechanism. I suppose I might build one, and send it in commemoration of their victory. I shall have to find more metal.\n -==Entry Eleven==-\n\nUradir lives. This frightens me. What if he blames me for what happened? What if he tries to have me killed for it? I did not sanction his wholesale slaughter of countless innocents. Even in retrospect, I still cannot summon \nenough justification to do so, even when knowing what they would do. I will not be thrown in his acid pit! I will not be a scape-goat for his schemes! I shall remain away for now. I cannot risk returning while he is there. I will still send the Automated \nPublisher to the library, though. \n\nI have sent Triarch on his little errand. Hopefully they will be too confused to follow him. My situation has become confusing again. I must ruminate once more, for a time, and consider what I will do next.\n  -==Entry Twelve==-\n\nI have decided to settle inside a system of caves nearby the city. I must say, the previous occupants were not the most pleasant home-makers. The corpses are certainly quite disconcerting. However, their most important\nfeature is that they are gone. This camp has some food that isn't charred elf, so for now I will remain. I am keeping my crossbow close by, however.\n\nThe ice formations also inspire curiosity. Another distraction from my decision,\nbut I will not simply allow such oddities go unstudied.\n\n\n-==Entry Thirteen==-\n\nEven the close proximity of the fire does not melt the ice. Though it is magical in nature, no doubt, I am still interested in how it was formed. The cave is not particularly cold, thus I am confused as to how the ice remains solid. \nMore curious, is that even grass and flowers grow quite close to it. I have named the orange flower Norbert, as it is my current favourite.\n\nLooking over my previous entries, a thought struck me. There is no water close by to this ice, \nand it remains solid despite natural forces acting against it. It reminds me of the crystals in the Bortu cave, which also seemed to stand despite where they are. Could the ice and crystals have been 'frozen' in a less literal sense into their state? \nWhere did the water for this ice even come from? There is moisture and a pool some ways off, but this place is noticeably devoid. Could miniscule traces of water (humidity? Condensation?) have been dragged by the inhabitants towards this place? Then their\nnatures changed so inexorably that they now stand, as if a part of the stone itself? I must study further.\n\nI am also painting the rear of my cavern. I am improving.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of life.", "Unknown Alchemist", "It is of remarkable that this drenched and idiotic Aldemar Wilkins has gained such influence and wealth from only a discovery. I lament of his position, as he may soon be killed for having such grand and important information for the humankind that he may\nbe captured and imprisoned, then harmed until the location of the mystical fountain of youth is. This is what I would think would happen, but the man is smart. He hides behind his followers, which many are fighters and pilgrims and would protect him from\neverything that would happen to him. Even as to pay to be his defenders, they wish to be close to him, to gain his trust and then his information. They wish to live forever, and such is the reason they treat mister Wilkins is receiving such praise and\ndonations. I have once felt what it would be like to live such live, even as one of the Mali kind. A potion, perhaps one of the most foolish ones that I had made, it carried with it no love of mine, but the payment, it was astronomical. A simple poison,\none to slowly kill a man as if it was a weakness. Simple to create but such is not what I practice the art of alchemy for. I was able to trick the woman which wished to buy it, charging 10000 minas for such idiotic and simple poison. There are so many\nhat on their own could do so, she would quickly know of them and do the task, only for that logic did I accept to do it. The minas, I had not before had so much of them. I was able to buy all that I had always wished, building a proper laboratory, buying\nland which I could built it and a house for my own, brewing stands, cauldrons, herbs of the rarest of kinds. Even with all that, I still had so much left. I decided to try what the noble humankind wasted their minas on, food, drinks, accessories and\nclothes. I was ecstatic, such men truly know how to live. Soon enough I had no more minas, and had to return to the poor alchemist potion maker life, selling rudimentary potions on a day to day basis. I wish to return to my wealthy days, and become like\nsuch that human Aldemar, which lives the grand life without much trouble, getting everything given to him. I have time, a long time to achieve it, and I will get it through means I enjoy. I could trick the humans with potions that appear to make their\nlife eternal, but they would soon find out. As such I will instead study and look for the real cure to humans mortality, Panacea. It is a myth of all alchemist, but of all the myths it is the one that feels like it could be true. \n\n\nThis will take years of study, but I have time.", "")
    )

    private fun _ATHERA_2(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Digest of Law-P1", "Adolf Ruhr Von Manstein", "Liber ex Iustitia\n\nBy Adolf Ruhr Von Manstein\n\nA Book Concerning Laws and Customs.\n\nA Universal Law Code.\n((Based off of the Digest of Roman law by Justinian of the Byzantine Empire))\n1.\"If anyone unlawfully kills a servant or slave of another, or a four-footed beast of the class of cattle, let him be condemed to pay the highest income the object could produce in one year. It should be double that value if the defendant denied his \nliability.\n\nUnder the category of cattle come asses, cows, pigs, horses, sheep, goats and chickens. Not coming under this category are dogs, bears, and other such beasts.\"\n\n\n2.If a slave or servant is wrongfully killed, then the slave's family is to be released as freedmen, and the servant's family or friends are to be given 600 minas.\n3.Accordingly if I kill your slave or servant who is lying in ambush to rob me, I shall go free, for natural rason permits a person to defend himself against danger. This law permits one to kill a thief caught in the night.\"\n4.\"If someone kills anyone else who is trying to go with him with a sword, he will not be deemed to have killed unlawfully: and if for fear of death someone kills a thief, there is no doubt he will be free from charge.\"\n5.\"If a man kills another in a boxing-match or in a formal duel supported by seconds, which is approved by both liege and head of house, then one does not full under persecution.\"\n6.\"According to the law lay down by Celsus of the Old Oren Kingdom, if a doctor operates negligentrly on a slave or servant, he must pay 200 minas to both the slave or servant and their respective liege.\"\n7.If one misuses a harmful drug that is prohibited by their liege, he is to pay 200 minas also.\n\n8.If a mule driver should he negligent and run down a slave or servant with his mules by accident, he must pay 200 minas.\n9.If one man should hold a slave or servant while another kills him, he must is equally held accountable.\n\n10.If one should damage another landowner's or home owner's property, he is to pay the income of the entire property \nfor one month. This applies on both accidental and purposeful damages.\n\n11.If one should make the food or wine or drink of another sour, poisonous, or otherwise useless, he is to pay the 600 minas.\n12.If someone stains clothes, he is as liable as one who damaged property. He must pay the full price of the clothes. \n\n13.If one of your servants or slaves has a miscarriage due to you striking them, you are to give the slave or servant 450\nminas, and the slave should go free, and the servant offered a place of equal pay in the service of another liege. In addition, 150 minas should be payed to the perpertrator's liege. \n14.If you should cause the miscarriage of another's slave or servant, then you must pay the owner's 300 minas, the slave or servant 300 minas, and your liege 150.\n15.If you would cause the miscarriage of a mare, you must pay 600 minas to the owner.\n\n16.If one would harvest the crops of another before they are ready, they must pay the income of all their agricultural produce\nfor 2 months. Furthermore, if one would damage the land so that it is infertile, you must either pay 10 minas for every pace (Block) damaged, or give the same amount of land, or a piece of cattle for every 10 paces. Or they must pay the same amount of \nland rendered infertile, the infertile land being given to local liege. \n\n\nOn the Principle of Theft\n\n1.It is the mere intention of stealing does not make a man a thief. And accordingly, a man who has recieved someone else's property for safekeeping and then denies his obligation is not liable for theft\nwithout more ado, though he is so liable if he conceals that property in order to appropriate it for himself. Theft is a dishonest handling of a thing in order to gain by its use or posession. Such conduct is against the law of nature.\n2.There are two degress of theft:manifest and non-manifest.\n\n3.A manifest thief is one whom was caught in the act. That is, one who is caught with stolen goods on him. It matters little who actually catches him, be it the owner or \notherwise. A man is a manifest thief until he acrries the stolen goods to where he intends to use or profit by them.\n\n5.Therefore irrespective of whether he is caught in a public or private place, so long as he has not yet borne the\nthing to the place he was making for the charge will be that of a manifest thief.\nBut if he got his loot home, even if he was caught with the stolen things in direct possession, he is not a manifest thief.\n6.For although theft may be committed many times over by successive hamdlings of the stolen goods, it was thought right to determine whether or not a theft was maifest at the time of original thieving.\n7.What sort of a thieft a non-manifest theft is is clear, for a stealing now within the meaning of theft must be non-manifest theft.\n\n8.Once someone has a right to bring an action of theft, continued handling of the stolen thing by the thief will not give\nhim any further right of action for theft even though there may be an increase or growth of the stolen thing meanwhile. One could bring a vindicatio against the thief, and therefore the right to recover his goods. Therefore, one would be without charge if\none brought a formal vindicatio, or revenge, approved by the liege of the recovering man.\n\n10.Anyone who's interest is that the property should not be stolen can bring an action for theft. (Marius)\n11.Celsus states that a purchaser has no action if a vendor does not hand the  item purchased over. However, if the purcahser takes the thibng before purchasing, he is liable. \n12.Slaves, servants, or sons, legally in our potestate, or power, who committ theft against us are not liable for theft. The father must deal with him himself, through disownment, punishment, etc.\n13.A child can be liable if they are old enough to be capable of dishonest intent;and moreover sicne a child can committ theft he can also be liable for unlawful damage. However, the fine is directed at his head of house.\n14.A man who steals land is not liable, but the original owner may declare a formal vindicatio in front of his liege, and thereby be allowed to take the law into his own hands, and take the property back. Injuries are not liable in this situation, but for\nevery man or woman killed, regardless of social status, 500 minas must be payed by both sides to the state.\n\n15.Anyone who steals a deed or contract is liable for theft.\n16.A tutor is charged with the administration of his pupils' property, but he is not granted any power to appropriate any objcts for himself, and, in doing so, he is liable for theft.\n\n\n17.Any man, regardless of being caught in the act, who aids a thief, is liable to be charged as a non-manifest thief.\n18.Charges for theft are as such:\n\nManifest Theft\n\nDouble the value of the objects(s) stolen.\n2 Years in prison and/or a flogging of 100 lashes.\nNon-Manifest Theft\n\n1 and 1/2 of the value of the objects taken.\n\n50 lashes.\n19.If theft is commited with violence or attack, the thief must pay 4x the original value. In addition, if he breaks into one's property, he must pay double that.\n\nIf violence is used, they shall have a flogging of 125 lashes.\nConcerning Injury.\n\n1.An injury may be defined as any physical harm done to another, with verbal harm being an insult.\n\nAn insult is either inflicted upon the person or relates to someone's dignity or dishonour.\nA person may suffer an insult on his own account or through others-on his ow account against the head of house or mother of a family; and through others when there is a natural succession, as where it is directed at my slaves, my wife, or my daughter-in \nlaw, for an insult is directed at us when directed at one of our relatives. \n\n3.There are many types of insults and injuries. These include:\n\nStriking,\nbeating, \nverbal insults, \ngestures such as the biting of the thumb, \nReligous insults.\n\n3.There is no set punishment for insults, as it depends greatly on the social class and severity of the insult. \nOne may organise a duel is neither parties seem clearly guilty, however, those below the gentry, females, and those below the age of 14 cannot duel. Both parties, the judge, and their liege must agree to allow the duel.\nFines are unacceptable to those of the gentry and above, but they may be given to a clear guilty party of the peasantry or small landowners.", ""),
        StaticBook("Digowen Part 1", "Jallentime", "One cold winters morning, upon the breast of new fallen snow, there stood a proud spruce forest of irrefutable infamy. There is nothing immediately discernible about these woods; the trees carried the same burdens of frost and insects as any other for\nmiles around. But what this forest did have, and that was quite unheard at the time, was a name. Digowen Woods was the name given to it, or at least that was the name etched into the sign just outside. If you decided to follow this sign you would find\nyourself upon the shambles of an old frontier road, long since buried under mounds upon mounds of soil and brown pine needles, only apparent from the trees whom still could not breach the stone laid so very long ago. It was peaceful here, in inherently\nominous. On this particular day a tattered huntsman trudged his way through the thicket, scattering leaves and pine-cones at his feet as he dragged a chain of cold, metal traps behind him. He stopped only a moment at a time, his eyes gazing at the\nlandscape around him and the ghostly breaths emanating from his throat, before he would lay down his trap and pull back the jagged teeth around it. The huntsman's pattern continued well on into the day, until the sun passed well over it's perch in the sky\nand began to refract it's light upon the forest floor. Golden brown sunshine danced throughout the canopy, signaling the forest creatures that night would soon belong to the predators, of whom Nature did not count it's intruder.\nThe huntsman, sadly, realized the error he had made too late, and found himself far from home, in a world not his own. He dragged his coarse leather boots through the rotting needles, clearing a small section of the forest floor to himself as the last\nbeams of light shone through the mist above him. He laid down on this small amount of luxury, and stared skyward at the cloudless midnight above him, his mind slowly counting each star and naming them off to himself. Soon his eyelids fell, and his dreams\novertook him. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Dire Wolves", "Art Camoryn", "Dire Wolves\nD.O.C Euclid\n\nAppearance: \nMuch like in form to their canine cousins, the Timber or Lur wolves, however, Dire wolves are far larger, the size of bears. Their jaws are longer and fur thicker.\nBehaviour:\nMost notably, Dire wolves always travel in packs. Seldom will you find them on their lonesome. They are fiercely protective of their young. In combat A direwolf will take advantage of combat in number, using powerful hind legs and jaws to rip \nlimbs from your body, the size of it's body provides massive force for ramming, additionally. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Direction.", "Tyrell Blavier", "-Trip to the Abyss-\nDirections & Instruction\n\nGo due west from Salvus until the hellish land scape of the world is met. There you stay careful and explore this red and burning land until a great lake is found.\n\nWhen you find the lake, attack pigmen and go underwater. Kill them while swimming so that they may not hit you.\nGather the gold and other material that they drop. Attempt to get atleast 16 aurum nuggets. /STAY AWAY FROM OTHER PEOPLE AT THE ABYSS/", ""),
        StaticBook("Discourse: WvsK", "Cyrus", "Distinguishing\nWisdom from\nKnowledge\n\n-A Book Humbly\nWritten by Cyrus-\nIt woulde seem odd that there would be a distinction between Wisdom and Knowledge, seeing as the Elven word for both is 'Maehr'. Nonetheless, there is still a rather important distinction between the two.\n\nKnowledge is defined as the collection of\nhard facts, cold information, and solid statistics. Knowledge is very useful for writing books and looking smart around others in casual conversation or in heated debate. It is a useful tool in many situations and I encourage everyone to never cease\nlearning.\n\nWisdom is defined as the useful and efficient application of things known. Wisdom is very useful in making decisions (an activity done by everyone nearly at all times). This increases the usefulness of knowledge in a way\nthat cannot be explained by words as much by experience.\n\nWithout proper and appropriate knowledge, Wisdom cannot exist. Likewise, without Wisdom, knowledge is like holding a knife and not knowing how to cut your roast. Wisdom comes through\nexperience and knowledge through study and practice. Both are useful in everyday interaction and rare situation alike.\n\nTherefore, I entreat you to never stop reading, never stop experimenting, never stop failing (in the\nhope that you not repeat said mistake), and never stop trying. If you do these things, both Knowledge and Wisdom will be yours.\n\n-Maehr'sae Hiylun'eyha-\n~Cyrus", ""),
        StaticBook("Dishwasher", "Alexandria Fireblade", "[!]A picture of a man, with brown hair, and grey eyes smiling is drawn here, the man is holding us a dead rabbit, the man holding a sword in his other hand, the tip dripping with blood.", ""),
        StaticBook("Documentation", "Draoen", "Documentation- I found a Void Mage who says he is Fire Evocationist. His name is Cirimas Elendil. We went traveled next to the manor into an open field where he could use the magic safetly.\nHe begins to extend an arm with an open palm facing upward. He seems to be inhaling sharply. Cirimas looks like he is focusing, a pool of sweat begins to roll down his face. A small fire erupts just above his palms. It grows bigger as he breathes.\nThe flame grows in size, about the size of an apple. After he was done the fire fades and nothing was left. The man looks tired and has fallen into the grass. The man was very polite and I thank him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dominus Tecum", "Guru Pinya", "In this book I shall write of the Order of St. Amyas and their error. The Creator teaches Divine love and mercy, yet these men give no unbeliever the chance to convert or see the truth. These men are HERETICS, they claim that they are setting an example \npersecuting pagans, and heathens! What fools! I have been following them and making religious observances. One accused me of being a sodomite! They do not even realize their error of their religious fallacies and indoctrinaztion! Another moment\nI listened to a conversaion of theirs! Two soldiers called a church 'the house of God' when it is merely a house of worship! These foul mouthed, idiotic hypocrites don't even realize the blasphemies they utter. They suggest that God is incompotent and \nis limited to such a small building! On several occasions I was forced to correct them in their ways IN FRONT OF OTHERS. What an abomination. They also do not realize the meaning of Church! I have spoken that I wait for the Church, and do you know what \nthey replied? 'The Cathedral is in the town square!'. The Church is not a building! It is the mystical body of the Creator and it is made up of all the believers! The fools even tryed to take away my Creator-given freewill! They use FORCE to spread the\nlove of the Creator! A farmer of hate will never sow a seed of love! It is impossible and contrary! To the foolish men in the Order of St. Amyas, change your ways before God's wrath is brought about for your hypocracy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Don't Steal.", "Lorien Vesitza", "((I swear, if you aren't Ciera/thesilentrogue/Ashy....I will turn you into putty. The location of this chest is OOC, and cannot be discovered via RP unless Meta-gaming is done. I WILL KEEEELLL YOUUU. In all seriousness, don't steal this item. I will\nrepeat, but in bold, red and capital letters, so that it may stick in your head.\n\nDO NOT STEAL THE ITEMS IN THIS CHEST\n\n§uIf you are Ashy......................\n\nHai <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 1", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: I thank you dearly for reading the first four chapters of \"Double Dragon!\" I wish to specially thank Valeria Yule for all her support. Now, onto the story!\n\n\n\n================Amnesia Can Be A Bite In, Fuqua, And The Demon In Her           Hair.\n================\nChapter One: \nNew Folsom. Not a bad place to live. But then again, it wasn't exactly a good place either. Crime ran amok and the guards were crooked. The Mob ran this town and everyone in it… but it's practically the only place left to live.\nMy name is Fuqua, at least thats what Shamone says it is. I can’t remember anything besides him and his… Somewhat rude entry into my life. Everythings still blurry about him, but from what I can gather, Shamone and I are connected permanently. \nLiterally. I’m hiding him under my hat right now. He says he’s a parasite and that he’ll just be taking some of my food every now and then. Theres only one problem with that. His mouth is on the back of my head and he’s using my hair as his arms and legs…\nI guess you could say that ever since he’s latched onto me, its just been one big, long, bad hair day… Well… Heres my story…\n\nChapter Two: A Rude Awakening.\nI woke up in a room in New Folsom’s Tavern, The Rusty Nail, with a skull splitting headache. I lazily sat up, rubbing my face and then scratching the back of my head. “Hey! Watch the hands Kid!” A brutish voice said. \nI screamed in surprise, leaping out of the bed and turning around to find… Nothing… There was no one be found… I stood there, extremely confused. Where had that voice come from? \nAs I pondered this thought, the voice called out again “Hey babe, when can we get some food, I’m starvin up here!” I yelped and spun around, now for sure that someone was here. “W-who’s there!?” I asked worriedly. My heart was beating a mile a minute. \n“I’m right behind you, can’t you see?” The voice said. I slowly turned, scanning the room for any signs of life, but all I saw was a pile of clothes next to the bed. “Are you invisible?” I asked, still looking around carefully.\nThe voice laughed in a deep gruff tone, being easily identifiable as male. “I wish! But hey, its fun messin with ya! I’m on the back of your head!” The voice said. I froze, as I reached my hands up to my hair, \n“The… Back of my head?” I asked, more than worried. He responds “You bet! Be careful reachin around back there; don’t want ya puttin my eyes out!” The tough sounding voice laughed heartily, deeply amused by this. \n As my hands slowly trailed up the back of my head, they glided against… A tongue!? I pulled my hands back terrified and disgusted, hopping around the room and shaking the slimy saliva off of my hands “EWEWEWEWEW!” I exclaimed in a frightened voice. \nThe monster spat, like he was trying to get a bad taste out of his mouth. “Ew yourself! You taste as if you haven’t washed in days! Which makes sense, I was wondering when you’d wake up.” The monster retorted. I paused at this last piece of news, \nnot jumping around anymore. “What do you mean by that?” I asked, now more worried than scared. “Well… When I formed a symbiosis with you, ya just kinda conked out. Sorry about that, but a parasites gotta eat ya know!” The beast replied. \nI tried to remember what had happened, but the further back I went, the less there seemed to be. In fact… There was almost nothing. My head was empty and devoid of memories! I couldn't even remember what I was wearing before that monster was put me under!\nI rushed over to the pile of clothes, picking them up and examining them. They appeared to be some type of uniform for girls. The full uniform consisted of a white, long sleeved button up shirt with breast pockets and sleeve cuffs,\na black skirt that reached my lower thighs, a pair of high black stockings, reaching about 3 ½ inches away from the bottom of the skirt. Underneath the clothing there was also a pair of dark brown leather loafers.\nI pulled the clothes over my underwear covered body, before angrily asking the thing on my head “Just who are you anyways!” The monster snorted and said “The names Shamone. Nice ta meet ya Ms. Fuqua.”\nChapter Three: My Hair Eats Weird.\nAt that time, I was pissed. I mean, I had some kind of demon thing in my hair! It was just so… Gross. I growled in anger, trying to pull the parasite off of my scalp, but to no avail.\nI sighed and decided it would be best to try and just cope with the thing. I made my way to the bedroom door to exit, when a flash of white on the coat rack caught my eye. It was a hat! A white bowler hat with a black ribbon around it to be precise.\nI snatched up the hat and slipped it on over my head and Shamone. “Hey! I can’t see!” He shouted out in protest. I hushed him promptly, punching the hat in on my head, knocking against Shamones large crooked teeth. \n“I’m not giving out food for free. The least you could do is lay low and not make me look like a freak.” I said, to Shamone. The parasite mumbled to himself before going silent under the hat. I nodded my head, before heading out the door,\npast the empty hallway to the stairs heading down. It was a normal bar scene for midday… Unoccupied and desolate. Except for the massive rusted spike sticking out of the ground. It took center stage of the bar and was about 4 ½ feet tall. \nI thought to myself 'That is one serious accident waiting to happen.'  Before heading to the bar counter “What do you have for food?” I asked the bartender. The man looks up from cleaning a glass out with a rag.\n“We got some steak and some bread leftover from chefs last cooking session. If ya want that, it’ll be 20 Dollops and 15 Schments.” Said the bartender. I held a hand up, about to ask what that means, \nand then figured it must be the money that this place uses… Or even that I used to use. I digged in my breast pockets, pulling out a couple of paper folds with numbers on them and a few coins. The numbers on the coins read 25 and the bill read 50.\nI handed everything to the man, hoping he would sort out what he needs and give me back my change. The bartender nods his head, taking a portion of the coins, and going to get the plate of food from the slightly heated oven.\nThe aroma of warm steak and bread wafted over to me and my recently acquired demon. Shamone squirmed under my hat as the smell came his way. I pulled the bowler down tight, slightly smothering Shamone, as he gnashed his teeth in complaint. \nI coughed loudly to try and cover the noise he was making, going to take the wooden platter of food from the man. “Thank you sir.” I said as I made my way over to the corner of the bar as fast as I could. \nI sat down at a corner table and immediately began to dig into the bread, tearing hungrily at it, having not eaten for at least a day I knew I would probably regret eating all this food in one sitting at some point and not saving any for later. \nShamone growls lightly and says “Kid… I’m gettin impatient with my food. I can steal from your stomach when I want, but that takes longer.” I sighed deeply, leaning against the table, not really wanting to feed the monstrosity on my head.\n“Fine… Here, quick.” I said as I grabbed up the steak with a knife and fork, cutting it in half and holding up the piece of meat behind me, then swiftly tilting up the hat. Shamone darted forward, \nchomping up the steak and slinking back under the hat, chewing sloppily. I looked around the room to see if anyone had noticed, and thankfully the bar was still deserted. \nI continued to eat my food, as a man walked in, heavily armed and armored, going to talk to the bartender.\n\nChapter Four: Milk Goes Good With Murder.\nI finished my food, getting up to give back the wooden platter to the bartender. I sat down at one of the stools next to the counter, “Got any anything to drink? I asked curiously. \nThe bartender nods his head “We have beers, whiskeys, wines, you name it, we probably have it.\" The bartender said, examining the large stock behind him. \"Hmm... Do you have any milk?\" I asked, seeing if they really did have everything a bar could have. \n \"You're in luck, got our last pint in stock. That’ll be 10 Dollops.” He said as he went into the back to get the milk. I retrieved the money from my breast pocket, setting it on the counter and relaxing a little. \nThe heavily armored man who entered earlier scooted closer to me, as the bartender returned with the glass of milk, a straw sticking out of it. I latched onto the straw, holding the glass in both hands, as I drank deeply from it.\nThe taste of it was wondrous! It must have been a favorite of mine from before… Well I suppose since before I met Shamone. As I was about half way done with my milk, the armored man, for some reason, decided it would be a good idea to try and hit on me, \nand slung an arm around my shoulder. “Hey pretty lady, how about I get you a real drink for a real good time?” He says with a smug grin. “Uh, no thanks, we already have a drink.” Shamone said for me. The armored man just smiled and said “Deep voice huh? \nI can dig it...\" I was about to speak up, before Shamone acted up again “THATS IT, HE HAD HIS CHANCE!” The parasite shouted. My hair exploded upwards, Shamones maw stretching wide, his two yellow glowing eyes staring hatred at the armored man. \nThe man stumbled back, “A p-parasite!?” He was barely able to get that out, before spikes and arrows of hair grew from my naturally short black hair, going to slam into him at an upwards angle, tossing him into the air. I turned around in surprise,\nKnocking the rest of the milk over, the glass shattering onto the floor. Time seemed to slow, as I saw the man land on the spike, and soon afterwards impale himself upon it. His chest bursted outward, as the huge spike impaled him, bits of gore flying \nHere and there. He grabbed at the big spike in his body, struggling briefly, before the life in his eyes faded to nothingness. I stood there, shocked at what had just happened, as my hat floated back down onto my head. I quickly pulled it on over the \nParasite. \"Guards! We have a monster in here!\" The barkeep shouted, alerting the nearby populace. I ran out of the bar and into the crowded streets full of staring eyes. Tears sprung to my own eyes as I passed the still bleeding corpse on the rusty nail \nIn the floor. This day had gone from bad to worse...\n\n\n\n================-End Of Part One-\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nArt: ----------->\n======Character Art\n((http://i.imgur.com/rn780uy.png?))\nFuqua, our main protagonist in Double Dragon!", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 2", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: The adventures of Fuqua and Shamone continue in “Double Dragon!” part two! I hope you enjoy this series, as I have enjoyed writing it. Onto the story! \nChapter Five: A Shaky Relationship: I rushed into an alleyway, far away from The Rusty Nail, tears streaming down my face.  I raced about halfway down the alley and ducked behind a large garbage bin, sliding down the wall in exhaustion.             \n“What the hell!” I exclaimed angrily at Shamone. “What! No one touches my host! No one…” Said the riled up hair monster. I shook with rage and disgust. Because of this random, /thing/, in my hair, someone had died, and now I was probably a wanted \nCriminal! I reached up and pulled my now short hair and growled angrily. “Owowow! Hey kid cut that out! That’s my face you're pullin!\" Shouted Shamone. This only gave me incentive to pull harder, which I did at first, but then stopped after a while.\nI took the hat off my head so I could talk to the parasite better, “Shamone, I can take care of myself. I don’t need you making me public enemy number one by murdering a random person for offering me a drink!” I nearly shouted at the hair demon. \n“Hey, I didn’t know there was a gigantic spike in the bar, you covered me up with a hat.”Shamone replied in a snarky voice. I sighed in aggravation, standing up and heading out of the alley, going to put the hat back on when Shamone spoke, \"Look out kid!\"\nI spun around, heeding the parasites warning to find a dark robed figure about 6 feet away holding some sort of syringe. The figure chuckled, before charging forward… Straight towards me! Instincts kicked in, as I ducked low and swept my leg under the \nRobed person. The figure fell instantly, having not expected any resistance from his prey. I quickly stood up and stomped on the hand with the syringe, shattering both the syringe and breaking the attackers hand. I cringed at the sound of crunching glass\nAnd bones, “S-sorry!” I said, backing away slowly before dashing out of the alleyway, holding my hat onto my head as I ran. I felt something pull at my mind at that time. As if someone were trying to invade it. I quickly shook that feeling off, thinking \nHow ridiculous that would be. I ran all the way to the edge of town, bumping into people along the way, now in a more slum like area than before. I leaned against the outer city walls, placing my head in my hands “What am I gonna do…” I asked helplessly.\n“Get us some food?” Shamone asked. This ticked me off beyond belief. He had just ate a big portion of my food, murdered someone and!... Possibly saved my life… I calmed down quickly having realized this last piece, but was still slightly disgruntled with \nShamone's behavior. “I don’t have much money left… We need to get a job.” I said, pushing off the wall and walking forward, keeping a careful eye out for anyone that looks like they may be a guard. I lifted my hat briefly, readjusting it.\n“Why don’t we just beat the crap out of people for money?” Shamone suggested. I very nearly smashed my hat in along with Shamone, but decided to give him a chance to explain “Do what?!” I asked in bewilderment. \n“Yeah! There’s a fighting tournament, look to your left, there's some posters on that shack.” Shamone said, shedding light on his strange answer. I turned and went to examine said poster. It read: “Beuwolfs fighting tournament! Go toe to toe with a mass \nOf fighters! Make it past them, and you’ll be able to take on the legendary fighter returning from retirement after a whole 2 years! Beuwolf! Each fight will wager 50 Dollops, and the winner shall receive both payments and a portion of the betting money!\nNext week at the Julius Fighting Center!\" I looked at the poster and blinked. “Are you sure about this Shamone?” I asked. “Of course!” The parasite said cockily. I stood up to my full height of 5’4” and thought ‘This is gonna be one hell of a week.’\n\nChapter Six: Displayed Powers.\nAfter getting out of town with a full stomach... Well partially full. Shamone had already begun draining my stomach of nutrients and food. I decided that if I was gonna beat this famous fighter and a bunch of other \nPeople, I had better train… But first I had to understand, what the hell Shamone was, and what he does. After meandering along the paved road for a while, I came to a stop and sat on a nearby stump. The fallen tree next to it looked recently cut.  I \nThought to myself 'Better make this quick.' I tore the hat off my head, the monster underneath snorting awake “Sngh, what! I swear I didn’t do it!... Oh it’s just you kid.” Shamone said slightly panicked. \"What are you exactly?\" I asked curiously.\n\"I mean, you've been on my head for about a day now, and killed someone for me, but all I really know is your name.\" Shamone snorted in response. I could hear a faint buzzing in my head… Although I’m not sure what it was. The buzzing stopped as Shamone \nSpoke up “I’m a parasite kid! I take nutrients from ya. But, don’t worry; this isn’t me just bein' greedy. It’s a symbiosis! You’re me, and I’m you. I already gave you some powers. I mean, hell, you beat the crap out of that one guy in the alley with just\ntwo kicks.\" I rolled this around in my head for a second “So… besides boosting me, what else do you do? Do you have special powers?” I asked. “Well… I guess I can show you now that I’ve formed a full symbiosis with ya.” Shamone said with a dark chuckle. \nI would later regret asking that. Suddenly, my hair shot to the ground, forming into claw like feet at the bottom, as a pair of large bat like wings formed off the side of my head, flapping mightily as the legs of hair sprung off the ground, shooting me \nInto the air. I screamed and clung onto my hat for dear life, as both me and Shamone flew through the sky. \"Hell yeah!\" Shamone shouted in his rough voice. Soon after our take off, gravity took its reigns upon us, as Shamone wrapped thick tendrils of hair\nAround my entire body. We slammed into the earth, my hair cushioning my fall like a pillow. I continued to scream, as my hair retracted back to its short lengths. I had closed my eyes and not realized that we had hit the ground yet… I opened my eyes \nEventually after I heard Shamone sniggering behind me. I looked around, stopping my childlike screaming as my cheeks glowed red with embarrassment. Shamone grew out my hair again, the delicate looking curls pushing me off of the ground\nAnd onto my feet. My heart felt like it would explode at almost any second now.\nChapter Seven: Learning The Ropes\n“Could you show your powers in a way that doesn’t involve a heart attack?” I asked shakily, still scared out of my wits. Shamone laughed harshly “Sure thing babe! Try punchin and kickin a few times! \nI’ll help ya out when I can in combat! I mean hell; you need to win that tournament to get that food money- I mean uh, prize money!” Shamone replied. I took a deep breath and steadied myself. I set my hat on the ground next to me, then got into a spread\nOut fighting stance, readying myself for a brawl. Spiky tendrils of hair grew from my scalp, making my hair go down to the middle of my back… It felt strange having longer hair. Maybe less so if it hadn't been grown by some parasite on the back of my \nHead. I punched around a few times, while Shamone added in the extra whip of a hair tendril every once in a while. When I was about to finish up punching, I sent out a particularly harsh right hook. Suddenly, all the hair that Shamone had grown out, \nExpanded and surrounded my arm. The hair spun around my fist rapidly, turning it into a huge spinning drill of a punch. I arched the punch upwards into an uppercut, and launched it upwards, the hair following suit and even pushing past my hand, going \nHigher than I could reach. The spiky tendrils of hair came back down behind me, as I went directly into kicking. I swung my back right leg up and forward, as a long length of hair followed directly underneath it like a second foot, effectively doubling my\nKick. I got back into my fighting stance thinking hard. That buzzing sound was back in my head as I eventually of thought of something interesting to try. I dashed forward, jumping up and springing both of my legs forward in a flying double kick. As if \nReading my thoughts, Shamone threw out two tendrils of hair, shaping them into horse hooves, and slamming them into the ground, blasting me forward at incredible speeds. I landed on the ground, having to go into a roll to stop my insane amount of forward\nMotion without injury. As I started to roll, Shamone did something entirely unexpected “Roll em up!” He said, before swaths of hair surrounded me, covered in small blades of hair on the outside, and spinning us both forward. After about two seconds of \nRolling, Shamone suddenly undid the ball of hair around me, as my appendages shot free and I stumbled back onto my feet. I was speechless as to what had happened, panting heavily. “Good job kid! I think now’s a good time to get somethin to eat! I'm \nHungry!\" Said Shamone, licking his nightmarish teeth with his long tongue. I stared at my hands before reaching up and smacking the back of my head, rapping against some of the parasites teeth. “Tell me when you're going to do something like that idiot! I\nShouted at Shamone. “Ow! Dammit kid! I was just helpin! “The parasite retorted. “Well could you help in a way where I don’t die?!” I practically screamed at him. “But you didn’t die. You’re perfectly fine.” Shamone said, trying to speak some sense to me \nBefore I smashed his chompers in. I calmed down some, huffing and walking back to where I left my hat. I picked up the white bowler and dusted it off, pulling it snug over Shamone again. He didn't resist that time, knowing full well that he would be \nGetting food soon... Hopefully. I really wish I had saved some of that bread. I walked briskly down the road again, admiring the trees as I made my way to… Wait, where was I going? I had no idea where this road led to, if anything. I looke back and \nDecided that heading down this road must be better than going back to a town where you're probably a wanted criminal. I mean the worst that could happen to me out here is that I could be killed, but at least it wouldn't be in the name of justice.\n\n\n\n\n===================--End Of Part Two--\n===================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCharater Info-->\nFuqua: Age: 16 1/2, Height: 5'4\", Weight: 142 Lbs. Likes: Eating, Coffee, Milk, Reading, Learning, Dramas, Romantic Novels, Cats. Dislikes: Shamones Behaviour, Seeing Innocents Getting Hurt, Hair Getting Tangled, Being Lied To, Side Effects of \nShamones Parasitism. \nShe's a kind and caring girl, who has to deal with her now living hair and having no memories to speak of. She's an average fighter who is amplified greatly by her parasite, Shamone. She protects her friends with a fervor unknown \nto most. Her anger is quick to rise, as are the rest of her emotions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 3", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\" Volume One Part Three.\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: Hello once again dear reader! Our story will be taking a slow progression in action, so do be patient with the  frequency of the fighting sequences. Now, onto the story!\nChapter Eight: Look Before You Leap.\nAfter walking along the road for some time, an alluring scent caught my attention. It was coming from within the woods to my right. I decided to investigate and see if I could ask someone if there was a nearby town\nOr if they were willing to part with some food. I followed the scent of cooking food with my nose… It smelled like… fish! Delicious smelling fish at that. My stomach growled at the same time Shamone did \"I smell food kid, were gettin some of that!\" The \nSwath of hair said. “Yeah yeah, I’ll see what I can do with this little bit of money. Hope its enough for at least one fish.” I replied, squinting my eyes and looking through the trees, trying to see any signs of civilization. After walking a little \nFurther in the brush of the forest, I spotted what looked to be a clearing with a log cabin in the center. The area seemed to glow in the dimming afternoon sun. My eyes lit up at the prospect of meeting someone new and possibly getting something to eat.\nHowever, as I entered the clearing, I stepped on a large net and slipped, landing flat on my face. The trap was quick to activate, as the net snapped around me and hoisted me high in the air below a sturdy tree branch. Me and Shamone thrashed against the \nNet, but it was no use. Neither of us had a tool to cut us free. That’s when she burst through the cabin door. She had short, spiky, burnt orange hair, and stunning carrot orange eyes. She bore identical triple clawed scars  on both of her cheeks, and a \nLarge scar going all the way around her neck, just above a leather collar with a golden bell. Her skin was tanned and she wore a sleeveless suit. It had a tiny skirt, but left her legs otherwise unbarred. She wore a utility belt around the skirt, with \nSeveral pouches attached to it. She wore thick golden looking wrist guards that covered her forearms with a leather pad, not covering her fingers, as well as leg guards covered her feet to her toes, and went up to her upper thighs. The most striking \nFeatures about her though, were her strange cat like additions, including high perching chocolate colored cat ears that flicked from time to time, a tail of the same color that looked more sharp than it did fluffy, and long claw like nails on her feet and\nHands. She looked triumphantly at me, caught in what I assume was her net. “Ah ha! Like a mouse in a mousetrap! I knew I would catch a bandit sometime!” She said, briskly walking towards my entrapped self. “Nonono! I’m not a bandit! I-I just smelled food \nAnd wanted some!\" I said, frightened for my life. She just sneered at me “Oh yeah? How are you gonna prove that!” She said, as she reached behind her and… Pulled off her tail? I looked on in confusion, as she snapped the tail once. It straightened out \nInto what looked like a rod of metal with a single bladed edge, looking sharper than that of any steel... How was I gonna get out of this one?\n\nChapter Nine: Fish And Playfulness.\nI held my hands out through the resistant net meshing, \"Please you gotta believe me! I don't even know if I'm from around here! I don't know anything!\" I said, on the verge of a panic attack as the cat lady stood \nUnderneath me, the tip of her tail sword poking against my stomach. The woman sighed, before jumping up and slashing the netting above, dropping me to the ground. I smacked into the earth, all the air in my lungs being forced out of me from the harsh \nImpact. I gasped for air, closing my eyes and waiting, thinking I was going to be slain by this cat person any second. When I finally opened my eyes hesitantly, I found the cat lady bent over in held in laughter, her tail back where it belonged. She \nStarted to laugh uncontrollably, as I looked at her in suprise. \"Y-you aren't going to kill me?\" I asked meagerly. \"Oh my god! The look on your face! Ahahah, that shit is priceless!\" The woman said, now in a lesser fit of giggles, slowly standing back up \nTo about 5'8\". \"The names Natalia FoRune! Sorry about that little net of mine, tends to catch more people than it does animals. What's your name miss?\" She says, reaching out one of her clawed hands. I took up the hand and pulled myself up, while I \nGrabbed my hat with the other and  tightened  it back on my head \"F-Fuqua... I don't know my last name... But thanks for not killing me.\" I said, as my body unstrung itself from the stressful situation it just went through. \"My pleasure Ms. Fuqua.\"\nNatalie said. My stomach growled even louder than before, as I placed a hand on top of it to try and calm it. \"I don't mean to be rude but um... Would you mind if I have some of your food? I can pay for it of cou-\" I said, before Natalie cut me off. \n\"Ep ep! That's absolutely fine. You can come join the family for dinner! I'll bet they can't wait to see what the cat dragged in this time!\" She says, laughing joyfully at her terrible cat joke, letting go of my hand and heading towards the cabin, \nMotioning for me to follow. \"Well, go on kid! Free food!\" Shamone said, urging me on hungrily. I bopped my hat, startling the parasite. \"Oh be quiet you!\" I said jokingly to Shamone, before following Natalia. The air behind her smelled of... fish and \nPlayfulness... If that can even have a smell.\nChapter Ten: Meeting The Parents\nNadalie threw open the front door of the cabin, \"I'm back!\" She said in a sing song voice. I followed behind slowly, peeking my head through the door. There was a large table, chock full of food, with the main course \nbeing fish and rice. I licked my lips in anticipation of a meal, while Shamone nearly coated my hair in a layer of drool. There were two people sitting at the table, one male human, and one female kharajyr. The female had the same burnt orange hair as \nNatalie. I waved shyly at the pair \"Well who's this cute thing you dragged in?\" The kharajyr asked with a giggle. \"This is Fuqua! She fell into one of my hunting traps so I decided to let her eat with us! Hope that ain't too much of an inconvenience!\" \nNatalie said loudly, going to promptly take a seat, patting an empty one next to her. \"I'm Sixis FoRune, and this is my husband, Roger FoRune, make yourself at home Fuqua!\" Said the kharajyr, gesturing to the man to signify his name. I was more or less \nTransfixed on the swishing of Natalie’s tail than focused on making my way to my seat or replying. So, unsurprisingly, I tripped and stumbled over my own two feet and barely caught myself. I glowed with embarrassment, I shuffled into the chair next to \nNatalie \"So... How does your family eat?\" I asked politely. \"Dig in!\" She said, not even using the fork next to her and snatching up a whole fish, then chomping into it with fervor. Her mother did the same, but Roger picked up his fork and ate with a more\npreserved manner. I decided I was to hungry for eating normally, and grabbed up an entire loaf of uncut bread, tearing into it hungrily, before reaching out with my left hand to grab one of the grilled salmon, biting off large chunks of delicious fish. I \nKept eating like this for a while, alternating between the meager varieties of foods. After eating my fill of food (And Shamones) I leaned back in my chair. The rest of the family at the table stared at me, as I looked around slightly put off by this. \nThen Roger started to applaud, the others joining in quickly. I looked around at them, very confused. \"Uh... Why are you guys clapping?\" I asked with a suspicious look on my face. Natalie stood up, giving me a standing ovation, sticking her fingers in her\nMouth and whistling loudly, while Sixis laughed. Richard was able to explain to me \"You ate a third of the food!\"  He said in a smooth voice, a grin on his face. I looked down at the table, and discovered the lane of food in front of me was cleared. My \nFace grew very flustered, as I apologized in rapid fire succession. Natalie just slapped me on the back laughing \"That was awesome! I haven't been out eatin in a long time! Well played Ms. Fuqua.\" She said, her tail swishing happily. I breathed a \nSigh of relief and smiled. It looked like the day was about to go from worse, to ok for me... Maybe tonight wouldn't be so bad.\n\n\n\n===================End Of Part Three\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParasites--->\nParasites Explained: Parasites are strange creatures, pre dating back to before the beginnings of all the races. They once posed a major threat to the minor gatherings of people, but now, being surrounded by people in major cities, have decided to change \nTactics... At least most of them have. They have now adopted to leaching off sentient beings for nutrients, while maintaining their own powers. These powers are partially transferred to the host, giving them superpowers and abilities, whether they were \nWanted or not. Attempting to follow the example of natural parasites, people created synthetic parasites, although, they were not at all ethical in any way possible. The host controlling synthetic parasites often were mutilated in order to control them, \nand more often than not, end up holding more than on parasite in their body, which leads to soul corruption. Soul corruption occurs when multiple parasites are taking from the body. They begin to leach at the persons soul, instead of the hosts food, \nLeading to mental instability and insanity. Synthetics are able to be detached from the body, while most natural parasites cannot. \n\nCurrent Parasites In Novel: Shamone; An unruly mop of black hair, residing on the back of Fuqua's head. His rude attitude and composure usually annoys his host. He is one of the most powerful parasites in brute strength.\nFishtail: Manifesting in Kharajyr's only, has taken a special exception to Natalie, as she is half human, half Kharajyr. Her mixed blood had a strange effect on the parasite, giving her near immortality in the way of undying flesh. Natalie still ages and\nHas shown no negative effects to the parasites presence. Fishtail himself is unable to speak. He takes the form of Natalies ears and tail, infusing himself into her at a young age. Her orange fur in those areas had turned to a shiny brown.\nHis own ability is to be able to sharpen and stiffen, depending on the circumstance. Fishtail may also be detached by the tail only, functioning as a sword at that point. He does not give his host physical buffs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 4", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: The action begins in part four of \"Double Dragon!\" I hope you enjoy, and as always, Onto the story!\nChapter Eleven: Moonlit Melee\nAfter helping to clean up the large meal, I asked if it would be any trouble if I slept somewhere in their home. \"Follow me! I gotcha covered!” Natalie said, then led me to her room. She rubbed the back of her head\nSheepishly when we arrived \"Eheh, we don't really have a guest room, but I have two beds in mine so uh, guess where you're sleeping tonight!\" She said with a sly smile. I looked in the room with a grin on my face, \"Thank you so much for everything \nNatalie; I don't know how I could repay you.\" I said. Natalie waved her hand at me \"Forget about it! We're friends now right?\" She replied,walking into her room and throwing open a chest in front of the bed to the right. She rummaged around in it before \nPulling out a big net, exactly like the one that I was trapped in previously. She began to head back out of the room \"I just gotta go put this up, be back in a second!\" She said as she dashed down the hallway and out the front door. I giggled softly, \nLooking out the window to watch. She glowed slightly in the light of the full moon, giving a peaceful aura about her. She unhooked the cut net, before attaching the new one, standing back and resetting her trap. I saw some movement out of the corner of my\nEye, and when I looked over to the source, I saw the glint of a metal blade cut through the darkness. Bandits! I pounded on the window, desperately trying to get Natalie’s attention, but my racket making must not have been loud enough. The bandit was \nGetting closer, and now there were two! I sprinted out of the room, throwing my hat off “Shamone wake up! We need to save Natalie!\" I shouted at the parasite. He startled awake,before my hair grew out in thick cords, now reaching my lower back. Long hair \nHovered up and down my back, as I burst out the front door, \"Natalie! Watch out!\" I called out, warning her of the bandits. She looked to me, then around her, jumping back as she spotted the bigger of the two bandits already bringing his arming sword \nForward diagonally, aiming for her neck. She wasn't fast enough. The blade cut straight through her, cleanly decapitating her head from her body. I watched as her head flew through the air, landing on the ground, her body collapsing beside it. The clunky \nMan laughed \"I gotcha bitch!\" He shouted. I stopped dead in my tracks, holding my hand to my mouth to stop me from screaming. Sudden anger and sadness filled me to the brim, fueling my drive to take these guys out. I dropped my hand into a fist, stomping \nTowards him loudly as he laughed \"What are you gonna do little girl, kill me?\" He said amused, raising his bloody sword. I grimaced and bared my teeth, \"I'm not gonna kill you... I'm just gonna beat the shit out of you!\" I yelled, before charging at the \nMan, reaching into my hair and grabbing Shamones jaw, flinging it forward. His mouth shot outwards in my right hand, covering my arm in hair, forming the gaping maw of an alligator's mouth at my hand, outwards. The action took both of the men by suprise \nAnd the one that struck down Natalie swung at the hair, only to have his sword bounce off the thick cord back towards him, smacking his muscled chest but not cutting into him. Shamone bit the bandits left arm fiercely, piercing through his clothing and \nTearing at his flesh with his gruesome teeth. He cried out in pain, twisting his body, trying to escape the wicked bite. I swung my left fist as hard as I could, lengths of hair covering it up and spinning rapidly as tiny blades of hair grew on the now \nSpinning drill of a punch. He brought up his sword with his right arm, his left being disabled by Shamones teeth, attempting to block the powered up punch. My fist slammed into the flat of the blade, pressing it hard against his chest. I roared in pure \nUnadulterated rage at the man and the drill punch sped up while the sword starting glowing orange with heat from the intense friction acting against it. The man grunted and struggled with the blade, barely staying in place as his feet began to drag \nAgainst the dirt. \"Behind us!\" Warned Shamone. I shouted in fury, retracting the drilling arm and alligators bite, swinging my head forward, while a loud buzzing played in my ears. \"Gotcha!\" Shamone said as he responded to my actions, and thick cords of \nHair shot out with the headbutt like action. The hair ensnared the bandit in front of me as I lifted my head along with the bandit, and flung him behind me. The bigger bandit landed on the small frail one behind me, being crushed by his comrade. I turned \nTo face them, my hair flowing in thick swaths behind me “This is for Natalie you bastards!” I screamed and proceeded to kick the living hell out of both of them until they were poor, sniveling excuses of men. They moaned in pain and agony, as I looked at \nThem to make sure the bandits were down for the count. \"Don't you dare try to escape.\" I said in the most threatening voice I could muster. They coughed in response, writhing on the ground. I looked back to where I thought Natalie's body was and... It \nWasn't there. I looked around frantically, a panicked look on my face. Who would steal a body?! Then I heard something that made me believe I was going insane. I heard Natalie’s laughter. I looked to the source of the laughter and very nearly fainted. \nThere stood Natalie’s headless body, but she held her head at her side like a helmet. \"I didn't know you had a parasite! That's awesome!\" Her head said with a smile. Tears brimmed at my eyes and my knees grew weak \"This can't be real, you were killed!\" I \nSaid, not believing what I was seeing. She laughed again \"Haven't you heard that cats have nine lives? Well, I guess you could say this cat has quite a few more lives than nine, but the puns still there.\" She said, raising her head up over her exposed \nNeck. She plunked her head back down where it belonged, twisting it left then right. She smiled and spread her arms wide, as if it was no big deal that her head had come off. It was at that moment that the night had become too much for me to handle. \nI fell onto my knees, as my vision quickly went dark, and I blacked out.\nChapter Twelve: So That Really Did Happen?\nI woke up in a bed, still fully clothed from the feel of it. I was laying on my right side, with Shamone facing the rest of the room. The bed smelled of fresh laundry and, not surprisingly, cat hair. The \nEvents of last night came crashing down on me, as I sat up quickly and threw the covers off myself. I looked around the room to find that Natalie was nowhere to be found. I got out of the bed and grabbed my hat which was sitting on the bedside table, \nSlamming it over Shamone, right as he was greeting me with a \"Morn-\" Poomf. Covered. I heard his teeth clicking together in annoyance. \"Kid, take it easy, your friends fine. She said she was gonna get a small catnap in then go make breakfast... Speaking \nOf which! It's food time!\" Shamone said greedily. Even after hearing this reassuring news from Shamone, I rushed out the bedroom and to the kitchen. There I saw Sixis and Roger, weeping over dramatically \"Oh whatever shall we do! Our one and only \nDaughter was slain last night! Oh woe is we!\" Roger said, trying to hide a grin, while Sixis just started laughing. \"You-you’re laughing about your daughter dying!?\" I exclaimed in disbelief. Roger waved his hand \"She didn't die Fuqua! She has a parasite\nTo. Although from what we know from our chat with Shamone (\"He was still awake when you passed out by the way\" added Sixis.), Fishtail is a much different type of parasite.\" Robert said, as Sixis picked up where he left off \"Shamone helps you in combat a \nLot more than Fishtail, and can talk, but he can't grant you the ability to remain alive even after having your limbs cut off!\" Sixis explains. I eventually caught on to what they were saying \"So you mean to say that she's-\" I asked, before being \nInterrupted by Natalie herself \"Indestructible! Pretty much!\" She said, bursting into the dining room with huge stacks of pancakes on platters in both hands, balancing a bottle of syrup on her head between her long cat ears. She set the platters of\nPancakes on the table, then snatching the syrup off her head and placing it in between the fat stacks. I ran forward and grabbed Natalie in a hug \"You scared me half to death!\" I thought when your head got cut off, you were done for!\" I exlaimed, being \nVery upset. \"Eheh, sorry about that, probably should have mentioned that sooner. But for now, why don't you sit down and we can have an eat off again. I won't let you beat me this time!\" Natalie replied with grin, hugging me back briefly, before gently \nPrying me off. I nodded my head, “What about the bandits? What happened to them?” I asked. “Oh, them, I took care of it, told them that if they came back, their head would be the one on the ground. Then they just ran off.\" Natalie responded, sitting down \nAt the table.  \"Stop messing around babe and get ta eatin! I'm starvin up here!\" Shamone yelled, vibrating my skull. I took the hat off my head, letting my short hair free. Now that the family knew of Shamone there was no real reason to hide him \"Fine you\nGreedy hog!\" I shouted back, then sliding into the seat next to Natalie. The rest of the family chuckled at our bickering, as we all began to eat. It looked like a return to normalcy for me... Wait, wasn't I supposed to train for something?\n \n\n\n\n================End Of Part Four\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCharacter Info-->\nNatalie FoRune: Age: 17 1/3. Height: 5'8\". Weight: 127 lbs. Likes: Making friends, Sunlit naps, Bowling, Golf, Parkour, Subjecting others to terrible puns, Robbing from the rich, Giving to the poor, Potatoes.\nDislikes: The mob, Feliz, Sushi, Guards, \nBullies, Marsupials, Loud noises, Lemonade, Getting caught.\nA feline feral, Natalie FoRune is an excelent thief and swordswoman. She makes use of her ability to not die of mortal wounds to her advantage, often stopping large groups of bandits from robbing\nA singular person. She is the mix between a human and a kharajyr, and has the traits of both. Her parasite, Fishtail, is her primary weapon of choice, her second being her claws. Her playfulness while fighting is a key signature of hers, often throwing \nOff enemys at how she laughs in the face of certain doom and death. She has been known for taking off her own head and placing it in random places, either to spy on people, or scare them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 5", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: As we near the middle of Double Dragons story, I would like to thank my editor, Laria Mogun, for helping me write this entire thing! Now, onto the story!\nChapter Thirteen: Somewhat Unprepared.\nAfter helping clean up again, I slapped on my cap and rushed out of the front door, Natalie following close behind \"Hey! Where ya goin!\" She called out to me. I halted and turned around \"I gotta get ready for \nThis fighting tournament coming up!\" I explained, about to dash off again, when Natalie placed a hand on my shoulder. I turned around to see her with a slightly concerned look on her face \"Who's training you for this fighting tournament exactly?\" She \nAsked. I raised a finger and opened my mouth, then closed it, realizing I had no real plan of action. \"No one... Just myself and Shamone I guess.\" I responded with a shrug. Natalie grabbed both of my shoulders and shook me vigorously \"You had that kind of\nPlan and you were going to enter a fighting tournament!? Do you want to die!?\" She yelled, the hair on her head sticking up like an angry cat would. I just shook there, apologizing over and over... For what, I wasn't sure, but I'm sure I was about to find\nOut. Natalie let go of one of my arms, but now held onto my right wrist as she pulled me along, \"Come on! I got a friend in New Folsom that can teach both of you how to fight.\" She said, as I was dragged along. \"Alright fine, but could you let go of me \nFirst?\" I asked, pulling my hand away as Natalie released it with a sheepish grin. \"Sorry, but seriously, joining a fightin tourney without training? Do you even know the top fighter there?\" She asked me. \"The poster said something about a guy named \nBeuwolf... Doesthat sound familiar?\" I said in response. She laughed half heartedly, \"Even if you somehow made it past the slew of fighters that are in the tournament, there would be no way you would beat Beuwolf in a fight, parasite or no parasite.\" She \nSaid, walking on ahead, her tail moving back and forth slowly. My eyes were drawn to the wagging tail once again, as I followed Natalia down the path. \"Why wouldn't I be able to beat this guy? Is he good?\" I asked curiously. \"He's one of the top fighters \nIn the realm. Best wrestler out there too. If he got a hold on you, it'd be lights out in seconds.\" She said, looking up to the sun briefly, noticing it nearing it full arch. \"Ah crap, we gotta get movin, you do not want to be on the road by mid-day.\" She\nInformed me before beginning to jog along the road. I picked up my pace as well, keeping behind her \"Whys that?\" I asked. \"Well, let's just say that the kingdoms military does their combat training on random people on the road... It isn't pretty.\" She \nSaid in a grim tone. I shuddered at the thought, keeping up my pace with Natalie. I really hope I wasn't going to be the poor sap that was going to end up as target practice.\nChapter Fourteen: Caution, Flying Objects Overhead.\nAs we approached New Folsom, a small worry built up inside of me. Were the guards looking for me? 'Guess I'll find out soon enough.' I thought  to myself as we passed through the front gates. The two\nArmored men on both sides of the entrance nodded to Natalie, and glared at me, but didn't make a move. I let out a deep sigh of relief, \"Thank the gods...\" I said under my breath. Natalie looked back with a curious expression, \"Whys that?\" She asked. I \nCrossed my arms behind my back and looked at the clouds \"Oh, no reason, ahaha!\" I said, awkwardly. Natalie gave me an odd look, shrugged, then continued walking. She held up her left index finger, remembering something, \"Oh right! Macron might be around, \nSo watch yourself.\" Natalie said. \"Who's Macro-\" I was about to ask, before something strange caught my eye. A flying fruit stall! And it was flying right at me! I jumped away from the stands destination, its destruction onto where I was standing \nFollowing soon afterwards. \"Hooly shiiit!\" Natalie said with a smile on her face. She looked down the slightly populated streets along with quite a few other onlookers. There appeared to be a man running at full sprint down the road, several large mostly \nWooden objects landing all around him. The man dashed past me, and not long after was a slender blonde man in a tailors outfit. The blond man was carrying an entire pull cart, complete with horse harnesses, and running after the other man at a good clip.\n\"I gotcha this time Grigs!\" The blond man shouted, before spinning and throwing the wooden cart with ridiculous speed. The cart slammed into the running man, hitting his entire body, the force of the impact shoving the man to the ground. The cart itself \nSpun sideways along the ground, crashing into a building and shattering a couple of windows on the street level shops. The blond man walked up to the now halted running one, and picked him up with one arm by the collar \"Now, when will I have my money \nAgain Grigsy?\" The blond said with a snarl. I turned my attention away from the situation, looking to Natalie, who continued to watch \"Is that Macron?\" I asked, slightly scared at the raw power the man displayed. She shook her head, \"That indeed is, Oh \nOh! Look, this is the best part!\" She said excitably, pointing at the pair of men. I looked back at the scene to see the body of a man hurtling towards me. The person slammed into my left shoulder, shoving me to the ground on my butt. The man continued to\nRocket along at incredible speeds, landing face first into a stack of tomatoes on a produce stall, sending food merchandise flying everywhere.  I looked on in disbelief at the thrown man to Macron. How could that lanky man be that strong?! Macron smirked,\nLooking at the havoc and destruction he caused, before sticking his hands into his pockets and walking down the street. Natalie held out a hand to me “Nice one! First time in town and you’ve already been nailed by one of Macrons human missiles. Man, I \nWish I was that lucky.” She says cheerfully. I took her hand and pulled myself up.  \"What's that guys deal anyways?\" I asked, a bit miffed, then looking over to find the thrown man hobbling down the street, covered in tomato guts. \"Well, he's only a\nLittle bit nuts, but he only hurts people if they piss him off, so just stay out of his way and you should be fine.\" Natalie suggested. I dusted myself off, \"That's not who's gonna teach me right?\" I asked, looking at all the strange civilians around me. \nNatalie laughed \"Nyahahaha! No, he may be powerful, but Macron has no form. I'll be takin you to the guy who taught me. He used to be in the guard before, well, they became consumed by the mob. Now he's a private eye. Damn good one at that.\" Natalie said \nAs she began to walk further downtown. I followed behind her, watching the sky's for any more flying objects. Wouldn't be the last time I saw them, that's for damn sure.\n\nChapter Fifteen: Ivan’s Detective Agency\nNatalie led me to a rundown building with a swinging sign in front of it. The sign read: \"Ivan's Detective Agency.\" In big bold letters. She pushed open the door and walked inside, beckening me to enter. As I \nStepped inside,  the putrid smell of years of tobacco smoking assaulted my nose, complimenting the old vintage look and dim lighting of the room. There was a man in his 30's by the looks, leaning back in a chair behind a desk, a lit cigarette in his mouth\nHe had black hair and a slightly pale complexion. He opened his eyes from his probably light slumber and groaned \"Oooh, it's you again.\" He said with a playful smile. Natalie smiled back at him \"It sure is, and I brought a friend this time!\" She said \nCheerfully. I waved meagerly at the man \"Hi.\" I said, just as meagerly. The man sits up in his chair, peering at me \"She looks a tad bit familiar... What's your name?\" He inquired. \"It's Fuqua, what might yours be?\" I asked in response. \"The names Ivan \nMalark. And the girl pointing a crossbow at you from the corner is JuJu.\" Ivan said nonchalantly. I looked in suprise in all four corners, catching her in the corner to the right of the front door. She had black hair, put in a clothed and pinned together \nBun, along with gray eyes. She wore dark green combat gear, black kneeguards, along with fingerless black gloves. She looked to be of eastern descent.  She held an extremely large crossbow with a scope attached to it, and was aiming at me. I held up my \nArms in surrender. JuJu lowered her oversized crossbow and laughed at my reaction... Only there wasn't any sound coming from her. \"She's mute, just don't be rude about it and she won't shoot you.\" Ivan said, getting up out of his chair and walking around \nhis desk. \"Anyways, what brings you around this time Natalie? Got any leads on case 47?\"  Ivan asked Natalie. \"Nah, I do have a request however.\" She responded. \"Oh? What might that be kitty cat?\" Ivan said playfully. Natalie smirked \"I need you \nTo train my friend here for a fighting tournament. The one at the Julius Center.\" Informed Natalie. Ivan let out a loud whistle, before shoving his hands in his pockets \"She got anything going for her now?\" He asked. Natalie responded by yanking my hat \nOff, an already awake Shamone underneath \"Finally! Now I can see who's talkin!\" The parasite said, looking around. Ivan looked a little taken aback and then smiled \"A parasite, of course. How else could you beat Beuwolf.\" He said, as JuJu walked closer \nAnd poked my hair with a curious expression. \"Watch where you're touching toots! Wouldn't want any 'accidents' now would we?\" Shamone said, grinding his teeth. \"Shamone! Don't be rude!\"I said, bopping the parasite on the teeth, Sampson shooting back a \nRetort immediately afterwards. Ivan just sighed \"Oh boy, this is gonna take a while.\"\n\n\n\n\n===================--End Of Part Five--\n===================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHuman Government->\nAfter the Great Disaster, the humans tossed aside their differences and banded together in the form of one super government, ruled by its king and royal family. They formed handfuls of massive citys along the Courier Road, guaranteeing safety to all of \nTheir populace. They adopted a single currency, but largely function on bartering and trade. A few grand citys have been lost over the century, the most noticable being the old capital of Maplecrest. \nThe Canyon Kingdom of the humans is the largest government in the realm, and thus holds most power. It is currently ruled by its princess, Renoir Canyon. She fights alongside her troops, The Black Shield, helping any innocents she may find.\nThe only real challenge and enemy's the massive kingdom holds, is the Mercoli Mafia, and the ever present danger of The Swarm returning.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur's Brood", "Thurak'Yar", "Dragur's Brood\n\nAnd one of the few stories known of them.\n\n\n\nRe-Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 21'st of The First Seed, 1489.\nThe Dragons all descended from Dragur, an Arch-Daemon of the land named Asulon. Dragur’s true form is that of a dragon, so the appearance of his offspring is of no surprise. Dragur raised the first of his brood in his volcanic lair, and taught them\nvast knowledge and wisdom. Like their father, the dragons are capable of morphing into a humanoid shape. The majority of the brood are wise and indifferent to mortals, sometimes posing as scholars or mages; spending their time distributing their \nknowledge of the realms with the races of this world. However, a certain sect of Dragur’s offspring exists, known as Drakes. The scales of these drakes have turned to a shade back as night. These Drakes, unlike their brothers the Dragons, are heavily \nopposed to mortals, sometimes spending time in humanoid form purely to destroy them or to spread corruption in hopes of turning them against each other.\nAfter the creation of his brood, Dragur fell into a deep slumber within the volcano, and\nhas yet to be awakened. In spite of this, the dragons are overseen by a Matriarch, or \"Queen\". \nAs the brood grew, they began to scatter across the land, some going off into the mainlands, or even farther into the opposite ends of the world. Some stayed close to their birth home, such as the Matriarch as well as Velketzar. Velketzar was the first \nborn male of the brood. While Xandraza was born with the mind of Dragur, the yearning for knowledge and learning, Velketzar was born with the strength, pride, and sense of wanting to protect. This Dragon worked closely with the past civilizations \nof Asulon, ensuring that peace was kepy between them and that they prospered. In his humanoid form he was known and respected greatly across the lands. Always possessing an astounding amount of patience, he thought things through\nfor the best possible outcomes.\n\n*The shade of ink turns from old to fresh, at the start of a new paragraph. It seems to be a new entry*\nHowever, as much as he wanted it to, no everything could stay in the peaceful serenity he so desperately worked for… There was just some hate in the hearts of beings that one could never come to change, for Velketzar, he felt pity\nupon these. Few of the brood saw how he aided these creature, as they were so far beneath them, and while some attempted to understand, others simply refused to care at all, and shunned him for his passion. But alas, it wasn't simply his own kind\nthat acted in such a manner. The humanoids he helped, some sought greed over all, and despite how much they already had in this world, nothing satisfied their thirst for gaining more wealth of power… Thus lead to the day of betrayal. \nThe day when some of us cast aside the trust of us and stole knowledge for their own personal gains came too soon. After that day, Xandraza and Velketzar sought out what they could together but could only find so much. Velketzar’s pride\nhad been dealt a heavy blow. He was born with the sense of urge to protect, and he felt he had failed to aid Xandraza in the protection of her vast collection of scrolls and books. Depression fell upon him greatly; he stopped visiting the civilians, and \nalthough she tried her best to console him and tell him that, indeed, in time, together they would perhaps be able to recover that which was stolen, Xandraza’s words would not reach him. His emotions slowly began to consume him. \nOne day after Xandraza returned to the island, filled with happiness after reclaiming another book in ruins, her eyes befell Velketzar and her heart sank. Once a bright healthy ruby shade of red, his scales had begun to dull in colour, and had saturated \nnearly to a dank brow. Bringing him outside so he could see for himself in the light of the sun, Velketzar finally understood what he was becoming. His head grew clouded with his emotions, as Dragons, it is known, have the strongest emotions \nof all creatures. Sadness and rage overtook him, and blinded by this the urge to halting his protection against corruption grew. And then he stopped, and began to think. Pondering on the best possible outcome, as he always did...\nAnd so Velketzar changed into his true form, and with determined rage, he destroyed the mountain on the east side of that island that was their home. For what reason? It didn’t occur to Xandraza what he was doing before it was too late. He was making \na clearing for himself. Once he had enough space, he stood at the edge of the island, looking out to sea. And then it began. First, his claws, spikes and horns began to harden and turn to stone, then his wings, arms and legs went next... All turning \nto rock. He did this to himself… But why? \"Do not think ill of me.\" He said to Xandraza who watched, mortified and as still as the stone he was becoming. \"I do not wish to become one of them. I wish to stay in the good of your heart. I will guard \nthis island so that what has happened may never happen again, and I hope in time, my scales will return to that shine and hue you love so dearly. Goodbye.\"\nAnd as the final whip of his tail slammed into the side of the volcano, it too then turned to stone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drake's Tail", "Sol Azirus", "      Drake's Tail\n            and\n        it's uses\n\n\nBy: Sol Azirus\n\n  Acknowledgments:\n\nLemik Rexuireus-\n\nTesting of Potion of Drake's Tail\nIndex:\n\nCh. 1: Introduction\nCh. 2: Description\nCh. 3: Location\nCh. 4: Harvesting\nCh. 5: Origin of Name\nCh 6: Uses\nI. Alchemical Use\nII. Potion of Drake's\n   Tail\n-------------------Chapter 1: Introduction\n-------------------\n\nIn this book I will be explaining what Drake's Tail is, it's uses and how to identify it\n-------------------Chapter 2: Description\n-------------------\n\nDrake's tail is blackened dusky color with long thin thorns\nand almost always will be attached to a rock\n-------------------Chapter 3: Location\n-------------------\n\nDrake's tails can be found in a desert, but not just any place in a desert, it has to be near an oasis so that it can get moisture in the air and vast amounts of heat at the same time.\n-------------------Chapter 4: Harvesting\n-------------------\n\nHarvesting Drake's tail is quite tricky, you must be carefull to not get stuck by one of the thorns because it has a fever inducing poison with. Drake's tail will always be attached to a rock\nso bring the entire plant with as you will need the thorns and roots to make any sort of potion\n-------------------Chapter 5: \nOrigin of Name\n-------------------\n\nWhile I am not certain of the name I can only geuss it was named after its thorns which are attached to the tendrils of the plant which resemble the tail of a drake\n-------------------Chapter 6: Uses\n-------------------\n\nDrake's tail can be used for alchemical reasons and it can be used to create a fever inducing poison, however, in this book I will only speak about the alchemical use.\nI. Alchemical Use:\n\nDrake's tail is an alchemical reagent which is a strong fire symbol and it represents the following aspects of fire:\n\n*Heat\n*Destruction\n*Chaos\nDrake's tail can be used to create many fire accentric potions however it has its very own potion, Potion of Drake's Tail, I will be teaching you how to create this potion and it's effects and uses.\nII. Potion of \n   Drake's Tail\n\nRecipe for Potion of Drake's Tail:\n\nBase: Distilled Water\n\nReagent: Drake's Tail\n\nOnce you have collected all the ingredients begin by heating up normal \nwater then crush some coal until it is fine powder, once the water is hot enough throw in the powder and stir till it all dissolves, now you have the perfect base. Finely chop up the roots of the herb then extract the thorns and add it all into the base.\nEffects:\n\nPotion of Drake's Tail appears to burn anything it comes into contact with however, I believe this potion is infact an acid as no heat is given off when it comes into contact with material and it even eats away at things which\ncan not be burned.\n\nSince this potion is actually an acid it can't be applied to any weaponry to give a burning effect for it will chew away at the weapon\nHow to Apply:\n\nOnce this potion comes into contact with any material (except glass apparently) it will begin to eat away the material, therefore it can be applied in any way, drinking, pouring onto the material etc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dream", "Ninox", "\n\n\n          Dream\n\n\n\n\n      L. Thickfeet\n“Take this seed and find the right place. You will know it when it you find it. Plant it without any help from any source. Meditate until it grows tall. Do not return until it is done.”\n\nThis was my fifth task as a druid dedicant.\nWhat kind of task is that for a hobbit of my age? Some of the very saplings I remember as a child still are barely able to bare fruit. This was the day I realized the druids were truly masochists.\n\nWhat had I gotten myself into?\nSo of course, without much hesitation I gathered just a few things. I may or may not have emptied the entire stock of elvish lembas bread that I have ever owned, I carried with me enough pipe weed for the next century, a couple of water skins, \n and just the seed I needed to plant.\n\nI set off early morning to the north hoping to find a quiet place to start the task that would probably be the end of me. A few days past when I found myself crossing the Orcish desert.\nI knew full well the dangers of someone of my stature entering lands of danger, however I took great care to only move about at night.\n\nI found a rather easy to climb rocky hill that would allow for a much larger view of the land.\nI made my way up and as expected I gained a grand view. At night the desert can be a very beautiful place. The moon at its fullest sent its brightest light that shimmered off the sand dunes below.\n\nI should remember to appreciate all the world offers.\nAfter a few moments and realizing there was no greener lands to be found nearby I turned to leave and tripped over myself. Before I knew it I had spilled most of the contents of my bag. \n\nLost in a sea of sand is exactly what I wanted.\n There I was shaking sand off of food and luxuries when I realized the seed had gone missing. The panic that rose in me was like no other as I hurriedly checked the hill for it.\n\nA single seed in an ocean of death. Fantastic.\nI started digging into the sand to see if it had simply been covered and found something intriguing. \n\n\n\n\nDirt.\nIt was just under a short layer of sand and a small bit of stones. I am no expert on dirt but I was truly astounded to find it in a barren place such as that. Time passed and I had forfeited any chance of finding the Arch Druid’s gift. \nI had failed so soon into my journey that I frustratingly fell back and fell asleep to the stars.\n\nI woke early dawn with a sudden jolt. Once my old eyes had cleared I stared blankly at a stick in the ground.\nTime passed and I began to realize that I was staring at a sapling.  Had that damned thing been there the entire time? Had I finally gone blind? Did I possibly reveal it in my seed searching panic?\n\nIt couldn't possibly...\nIt couldn’t possibly have been the very seed I was sent to plant. I couldn’t have slept for that many days without some sort of hunger! \n\nAt the very least in my old age I'd have a sore back by now.\n\nNo such luck.\nAs if the situation hadn't been any more wild, I decided the best course of action was to do what my teachers had always dictated.\n\nI meditated.\n\n\nSee what I mean?\nI meditated next to the impossibly growing and arguably the thirstiest sapling I would ever encounter. I cleared my mind as usual, began to control my breathing, and felt the regular soothing calm that accompanied me each time.\nExcept this time something had changed. I felt as if I had opened my eyes and was drifting alone in a blank place. Had I ever used my eyes before?\n\nI couldn't see anything but darkness.\nI was completely relaxed yet aware of all the nothing that surrounded me. I was everywhere and nowhere and just as I started to analyze the situation a faint glow appeared and grew all around me. \n I then realized how cold I had been. Had I ever felt coldness on my skin before? The darkness faded swiftly and all was engulfed in light and pure warmth.\n\n\nI then felt a stirring around me. \nA wind blew softly between my hands and a long string of orbed lights fluttered and danced before me. When did I learn to feel something like the wind? My focus changed and I looked around to see that I was now sitting in an open meadow.\nThick soft grass leaned to-and-fro and wild flowers of every color bloomed in the moonlight. When had I ever seen color before? The wind picked up lovely scents and I was now aware of my sense of smell. Had I ever smelled ever before in my life?\nAs if trying to tell me not to waste time, the wind picked me up and I found myself up on my feet. I realized how it felt to use my legs. \n\n\nWhen did I obtain a body?\n I could have sworn that I had grown quite a bit. I could have been as tall as a human now. Maybe I was always that tall?\n\n\nI had no memory of it.\nThe orbs spun around me and then headed onward. They were calling to me. I heard faint whispers but could not understand them.\n\n\nWhen did I ever have hearing?\nI walked for an age. \n\n\nThe meadow stretched endlessly and the night lasted for an eternity. \n\n\nIt was an ocean of life.\nAfter a while I began to notice a rather large glow in the distance. No matter how I looked at it, I could not get a clear sight. Something inside of me told me ‘No.’\n\nIt was wrong and shouldn’t be there.\nThe orbs almost reacted to my thought and swiftly flew through me. They had gone but I felt a strange presence within.\n\nThey were with me now.\nI felt myself grow taller then. Was I as towering as an Orc? Maybe taller than a castle wall. I couldn’t remember how large that was.\n\n\nI ran.\nI sprinted towards the blur in a rage. I ran for hours, days, months, years towards the very thing that must leave this place. The blur remained and I could not pick out what its figure was. It was greater than I could have imagined but it had to leave!\nThere I was before it. It was monstrous and mysterious. The blur remained and I could not touch it. Did I even try or did fear hold my hands?\n\nI could not remember how to use my hands.\nA great anger boiled and I screamed at it to leave. It did not belong here. This was my world and it was not welcome. Nothing happened and my anger turned to rage. \nA single orb fled my body and went deep into the ground.\n I believe the earth itself responded to my rage.\n\n\nThe foundations of the world were shaking, and so was I.\nWhy was this thing here? Why didn’t it just go home? It never asked to be in this place and I knew it was going to hurt everything around it. It had to leave immediately!\nAn endless stream of fury erupted from within and the earth ripped apart. It was as if a hand of the land itself reached out and pulled the phased phenomenon deep into the reaches of the world. It had gone and the land swallowed it whole. \nI fell back into the grass but felt no weight. The flora beneath me cradled me down. I felt the roots of the flowers hug me and I was pulled deeper and deeper into a dream. I noticed that I had grown but not in a way I felt before.\n\n\nGone was my hearing, my feeling, taste, smell, and my sight.\n\n\n\nWhat then was I?\n\n\n\nI was everywhere.\n\n\n\nAll at once.\n\n\n\n\nI had grown again.\n\n\nI was at peace.\n\n\n\n\n\nI was the world.\nSunlight touched my skin softly and the warmth woke me smoothly. I sat up and recognized the salty scent of the desert. I rustled my hands and felt the soft dewy grass beneath me. Startled I was at the conflicting feelings I stood up in shock.\n Before me stood a fully grown oak wood tree. Beneath me was an area of healthy grasses and flowers. Nearby was a small pond of water.\n\nSurrounding all of this beauty was a barren and lifeless desert.\nI ran to the water and splashed my face. What had happened and how long had I been asleep? Nothing about anything made sense and I know without a doubt that nobody would ever believe this story.\nI then headed to the grove of the druids.\n\n\nI hoped I hadn't slept through the end of the world.\n\n\nOr lost my mind in the process.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dreams", "Eenhoornheid", "DREAM 1:\n\nA bunch of men dressed in weird robes and mask's weilding a staff ran at me and mah dad *A drawing of the scourge and harbringers lies here* The ran after us so we ran i fell in a hole so they jumped and tried to kill me *A few\ntear drops lay on the page and a bit of sick*\nDREAM 2:\n\nThis time the men were talking about it *He draws the same picture* one said soming about Death shall come and a new dawn shall begin i ran up to him and asked why but he came after me again this time he was different a \ndifferent master he come after me and this time spiders and dead things came after me *A larger tear lies here*\n\n\n\n\n\n-Book found by Seth Calith.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dreams of Lilies", "Lithaeril", "May you dream the dreams of Lilies, where all your worries cease. Whilst you sleep the sleep of the oak tree, full of love contentment and peace. Braids of vines tumble from the hair of the ancient walls. Flowers sprout in the fertile places whilst  the \nripples in the living pond look like friendly faces. The singing sound of the stream rolling over the stone. Beauty in the way the butterfly flutters. The soaring of the great Eagle sailing the great blue waves of the sky. Weaving through the white peaks \nand the horse galloping through amber waves of grain. Natures music, the whistle of the wind, the rustle of the branches, the hoot of the owl, the river rolling. May you dream the dreams of Lilies, where all your worries cease. Whilst you sleep the sleep \nof the oak tree, full of love, contentment, and peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drink List v2", "Ramza Mantisuku", "Ultima - Strongest Ale\n \n\"Can you handle that beast? \"  \nIt is a balanced herbal undertone, and very powering in the slightest. Nor should the anise  overwhelm, as it sometimes does particularly when badiane rather than green anise is used.\nDiamond Dust\n \n\"A Cool Temptation\" - Weak Ale\n \n This type of ale is brewed from malted barley by mixing certain amount of yeast. The yeast helps in fermenting the ale and giving a fruit flavor to the ale.\nWaltz on the Moon - Wine\n\"For the Beautiful Couple\"\n \nThis beverage is made from fermented hops. During the fermentation process, yeast absorbs the sugar in the grape juice and converts it into Alcohol.\nLiberi Fatali - Fruited Drink\n\"Fated Children\"\n \nFruits like cherry, raspberry and peach are commonly used in brewing this type of beer. Most of the breweries add a flavor of these fruits instead of fermenting these fruits.\nCactuar - Very Strong Ale\n\"1000 Nails Adventure\"\n \nThis fruit spirit is distilled from a mixture of different fruits including apple, apricot and plum.\nDivine Passion - wine\n\"Cute and Sweet\"\n \nis brewed very sweet and stored at low temperatures.\nMiss Fourtune\n\"Girl Power with a smooth new taste\"\n \nis produced by mixing a larger proportion of wheat when compared to the malted barley content.\nHero's Drink - Whiskey\n\"Pond of Eternal Life\"\n\nThis whiskey is very strong let leaves a great fruit and strong taste in your mouth leaving you feeling of a hero.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drinks Menu", "Sofetios Jayamen", " ,.-:-'Drinks Menu'-:-.,\n\n\nWater\n\nWater that has been boiled and cooled, making it cleaner.\n\nFree ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\nLight Ale\n\nAn ale that is for the light drinker.\n\n3 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\nStrong Ale\n\nAn ale that has a good kick.\n\n5 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\nHoney mead\n\nA sweet alcoholic beverage.\n\n4 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\nHerbal tea\n\nA tea made of various herbs, made to help the drinker relax.\n\n2 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\nSweet tea\n\nA tea made with various sweet herbs, made to help the drinker feel more awake.\n\n2 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\nWine\n\nA berry wine with a fine taste.\n\n6 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))\n\n        Cool Milk\n\nA mug of cold milk.\n\n2 Minas ((RP only, no actual item.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Drinks wanted", "Krilge Gorkil", "Willing to buy Irongut Ale\nor any other special drinks at the Viridian pub.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid", "Cedric Huffington", "I wish I could become a full Druid soon!", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Anthology", "Aeran Winterleaf", "      Druid Anthology\n                    \n                   By\n\n     Aeran Winterleaf\n\n\nA collection of poems\n      created by the\n        Druidic Order\n\n    Published 16th of\n     Sun's Smile, 1507\nDedicant Poem by Veren\n\nThe leaves rustle as the winds blow strong,\n\nFlowers blossom and protect the beautiful place,\n\nThe Druids protect the beautiful place,\n\nWhile the Aspects\nguide with strength and grace\n\nThe Druids watch the void grow strong,\n\nTrying to protect the things we love.\n\nAs nature listens so subtle and quiet,\n\nThe world grows on, forever strong.\nNatural Poem by Virella Deathsbane\n\nThe peaceful grass.\nThe blowing wind.\nBlooming flowers.\nAnd the tall trees.\nThe matters of them connect to one.\nNature, it's all, for us all.\n\nLinked Together.\nA Druid serves nature.\nLinked to one.\nSame as the roots with trees.\nThe sun protects with plants.\nA family with support.\nAll is linked together.\n \nDandelion Fuzz\n\nBlooming with the wind\nNothing is sinned.\nThe fuzz flies and plants.\nNewcomers join to sprout and dance.\nHaikus by Anarane\n\nFox\n\nYour coat is pretty,\n\nColours of Orange, black, and white,\n\nYour cuteness hides strength.\nTree\n\nYou hands are green\n\nYou wave hello and goodbye\n\nYour roots are endless\n\nOwl\n\nYou are large and wise\n\nSleep at day, hunt in the night\n\nYou don't give a hoot\nThe Aspects by Gi'Garun\n\nFar away in lands afar,\nThe aspects began their work.\n\nLong ago in times that passed,\nOur Nature began to stir.\n\nThe Green lady's radiance,\nBlesses the crops.\n\nThe Green Man's strength,\nBlesses the worthy.\n\nFlowers and Fruits and Seasons from her.\nPredators, tigers, hunters, from him.\n\nSaviours of the Races,\nCreators of Nature\nThe children respect them,\nThe children praise them.\nFiary Ring by Heroxis\n\nSearching the night,\nNight quietly green.\nDeep in the forest,\nNo one has seen.\n\nThe circle of fungi,\nI enter you now.\nA force I sense,\nGreeting with a bow.\n\nTo sing in the rain,\nTo write in the sun.\nTo draw in the clouds,\nAttuned as one.\nPoem by Smurgla\n\nEveryone has a purpose. Love yourself.\n\nEveryone has a trooth. Believe yourself.\n\nEveryone has a vocie. Listen to yourself.\nEveryone has a friend inside. Trust yourself.\n\nEveryone has a purpose. Stick to yourself.\n\nEveryone has a reason. Do not listen to no one else for yourself is all that matters.\nPoem by Isabella\n\nFlower Flowers!\nPretty flowers\nHow do you like to grow?\nIn rain the flowers reply, up in the Druids grove\n\nFlowers flowers \nblooming flowers\nWhy are you coloured so?\nCause we spread the joy ,the flowers sing, all around the world.\n\nFlowers flowers dying flowers\nWhy do you look so gloom?\nOur time has come, the flowers cough, and its time to go below.\nAutumn by Taynuel\n\nThe leaves are losing shade again\n\nFading to golds and reds\n\nThe flowers have all gone to sleep\n\nSweet nothings in their heads\n\nThe wind blusters o'er hill and dale\n\nThe weather quickly chilling\n\nPreparing for the winter's dawn\n\nAnd frosty cold unyielding\n\nThe bears and squirrels make final\nmoves\n\nPrepared for their long slumber\n\nFinding their caves and nests in trees\n\nIn which all will be warmer\n\nYounglings laugh and play together\nIn piles of fallen brush\n\nAll bundled up in coats and scarves\n\nNoses and cheeks all flush\n\nIt's time to say goodbye to summer\n\nThe warmth, the growth, the sunshine\nAlthough the clouds gather overhead\n\nWhat's coming can be divine\n\nSnow gathers on each rooftop once\n\nThe coloured season is through\n\nTime for loved ones to cuddle up\nTogether till spring starts anew\nAbandon by Chirr\n\nYou left me when we were young.\n\nLeft me with my falling tears.\n\nI felt like I was no one.\n\nFor so many painful years.\n\nI cried at night\nwishing you were there.\n\nHow could you do this to me?\n\nDid you not see how that was unfair?\n\nLife was a horrible mess.\n\nMy heart so bad I couldn't rest.\nFalling tears that fall.\n\nShow that I've been through it all.\n\nThe cause you leaving me.\n\nWe are together now but it isn't the same.\n\nHeart aches and you are to blame\n\nIf you saw me crying maybe you'd regret what you've done\n\nRight now I will live my life as no one.\nA Forest Poem by Nivndil\n\nPuerith'leyu\n\nThe trees they stand,\nA clamor of souls.\n\nTheir voices born on\nWinds, are old\n\nBoughs up high,\nFairy halls,\nRoots below,\nSilent foot-falls.\n\nThey stand and wait\nFor times unborn\n\nTo whisper secrets,\nBefore words were forged.\n\nAmongst their trunks.\nBeneath canopy dome.\n\n\nTo bathe in twilight,\nThe trees my home.\nFair Ethanriel by the Song Druid\n\nEthanriel\n\nIt was the perfection of the Aspects that afford me her prospects.\n\nEven as I saw her for the first time I did blush soft, as each time she held me aloft.\nAncient wisdom hanging as vines, set apart from the bird and the pine.\n\nMother and lover, mistress and wife, bark and leaf-love of mine life.\n\nI stand living while she on her side, as if am ere tree fallen by the tide.\nElandriel gives me please, come back, save us.\n\nTarry not, give no sign of hestiation, only obedience, only inclination.\n\nBlessed mother, home to our brothers, lives on in some regard.\n\n\nSacrifice greatly rendered, a loss mourned, and no payment tendered.\n\nThe Druids can never recover, from a loss like no other, but memory does push onward and strength does persist.\n\nEthanriel, Ethanriel, Mother tree of\nElandriel... keep watch from the Aspects' favour.\nHerb by Thudrin\n\nStuff it in your pipe and light\n\nSmoke all day, smoke all night\n\nRoll one, maybe two\n\nSend them clouds up into the blue.\nPetrichor by Endvani\n\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nSpice and season Petrichor,\nMay the sky kiss your cheeks,\nthe rain wash away your weeps,\ntill I am aty our side\n\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nSweet perfume of petrichor\nRainsong soft with thunder's beat,\nbring your dreams,\ntill we meet.\n\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nWinds and waves petrichor\nMoonlight will my promise keep,\nlike the bond of stubborn, faithful sleep,\ntill I am at your side.\nListen by Meiala\n\nListen.\n\nListen to the chirps.\n\nListen to the peeps.\n\nListen to the howls.\n\nListen to the creeks.\n\nListen to your heart.\nListen to your mind.\n\nIt'll all be better.\n\n    Just give it...\n\n...some time.\nAfterword:\n\nBe kind!", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Attunement", "[Drood Guide] Earendur Vym'vallei", "For a Dedicant, the attunement ceremony is the final step of initiation. This forges a link between nature, the rest of the Druidic Order, and themselves. The guide leading the ceremony must be careful to do such properly. \nI personally choose to do this ceremony by the Birch Pond. I have them close their eyes, and I begin to coax their minds into accepting the spirits of nature around them. At first, I merely whisper to their minds, hoping to soften their natural defenses. \nOnce their mind is unshielded, it is possible for enlightenment occur. It is different for everyone, but most report vivid images of the forest talking to them. In my opinion, the visions should not necessarily be told to everyone.\nThey reveal something true about a person's inner being which should only be known to them. Of course, later, they may choose to use this information when choosing a title or totem. \nThe correct chanting must be performed and not stopped until you have internally communicated with the Dedicant afterwards. Be wary of pushing on the Dedicants to forcefully, for the mind is a fragile thing.\nMake sure that while forging the link, they do not react negatively, harming your mind as well as their own. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Circle", "Leyun Kameki", "The Druidic Circle\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nThe Druidic Order and a Druidic Circle are two different groups, but are tied closely together. The Order is not of a Circle, but a Circle is of the Order. All Druids who are taught under the Druidic Order are members of the Order, but those taught under\none particular Circle are not members of another Circle.\n\nDifferent Circles are rare to exist; this is because differing Circles have differing Druidic beliefs, studies, and structures. In the Order’s past, new Circles were fored because of\ndisagreements and differing beliefs, though in the end, those disagreements and differing beliefs were realized to have been senseless and the Circles reformed and conformed to prior belief and focus.\nDuring the First and Second Age of Schisms of the Druidic Order’s history, disagreements rose and differing beliefs accumulated which resulted in the Order splitting into multiple Circles. However, it became apparent to the Druids of all Circles during\nboth ages that in order to effectively and efficiently perform the Aspects’ will they’d have to stick together in one large Circle; it was noticed that they began to fail at bringing up and teaching new Druids. The Order is strongest as one unit.\nA Druidic Circle is defined as a set group of Druids who have a particular focus; that focus could be in the lines of responsibility or it could be an entire different belief. The focus, those teachings, studies, and et cetera,\nof the Druidic Order Circle of Malinor are true and are in true allegiance with the Aspects and Nature. A word to the wise: keep close to one another, Druii, and stay true to Nature and to both Aspects; don’t begin a third Age of Schisms. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid History", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "\n\n\n\n    The History\n   of the Druids\n\n      by N. Evitan\n\nLong ago, two factions of mages fought each other to the bloody end. Good, evil, the sides mattered not, their battle devastated whole cities and forests. At this, the peak of the battle, the first dream came to a young elven girl. She began gathering\nothers around her, teaching the Druidic ways. The first druids were born from the humble beginning. Like a great wave, the young order swept across the land and surrounded the two guilds. The druids destroyed them, turning them all to mere rodents and\nanimals of the forest. The druids went on to preserve the land for a millennia afterwards.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid History I", "Briar Ophiuchus", "  Druidic Studies:\n       History\n\n         AEGIS\nThe Age Of Founding And The Before Times: During this time, Druids were brought together and the Druidic Order was founded by Wayward Druid\nRespiren Knox. The records of this time may never be fully deciphered, however. Although we know of some of the first Druids in Malinor, such as Respiren, Swifthide, and Native, very few details are known. Perhaps someday the past\nregarding these times will be revealed.\nThe First Age Of Reconstruction: The First Age of Reconstruction was ushered in by the initiation of Dragon Druid Apollan into the order. Apollan was the first to express interest\nin joining the order after reading the Myth of the Great War and spent long hours in the Druid Grotto after he was famously murdered outside the gates of Laurelin by a bandit. Apollan quickly moved up the ranks. Meanwhile, the \norder grew. After initiating Apollan, Respiren expressed interest in 'rebuilding the order.' Every day, new citizens of Aegis would show up in the grove, wanting to become Druids. Most were immediately initiated. As the order grew,\nso did a number of things including property and knowledge. During this time the order gained a lodge in Ravenhold, as well as one in the Laurelin docks. Additionally, two stalls were bought in the Laurelin marketplace and\nhundreds of books were added to the order's library.\nThe Age Of Abandonment: Unfortunately, due to extremely casual and non-uniform initiation rites of the Wayward Druid, people were joining the circle, only to wander into the\nwilderness never to be seen again. With no established hierarchy, the Order lacked organization and purpose. This was made apparent when an Elf named Rowan arrived. Archdruid Rowan arrived from a far off forest, seeking to\nreestablish his lost circle, \"The Druids of Mother Aegis.\" Rowan is most likely the only citizen to have argued with the Order's ways. His only backing for the title of Druid was that he 'had a love of nature.' Rowan became annoyed by the\nfact that he had to be initiated in order to be allowed into the inner library. He stormed off, claiming that he would start his own order somewhere else. Rowan was last seen entering the wilds outside his home in the Ravenlodge, and\nwas never heard from or seen from again. Fortunately, the dark Age of Abandonment was brought to an end by the light of Dawn Druid Maiavel.\nThe Age Of Reformation: The Age of Reformation was brought on by the ideas and\ndrive of one Maiavel. With her determination, she was able to rally the remaining Druids to create official lore, hierarchy, and a sense of order.\nThe Second Age of Reconstruction: During the Second Age of\nReconstruction, many more books were written, and a Grand Tree was planted in the Laurelin Grove. New Dedicants were brought in, but less frequently than in the first age, and the initiation process was more careful and\nuniform. During this age, the current hierarchy was established, with Apollan as Archdruid.\nThe Age Of Knowledge: The Age of Knowledge was ushered in by Petyr, the Salmon Druid. His creation of the Dedicant's\nVows and the Attunement Ceremony greatly helped the order, as well as his Order ideas.\nThe Age Of Mushroom Transgressions: This age was brought about by the conflict caused by differing ideals\nwithin the Order. Some Druids were increasingly annoyed at the restriction that came with having a Grove in a city (where trees and mushrooms could or could not be planted and the structure of the Druid Tree). Other\nDruids argued that it was their duty to promote balance, and that the runaway growth of mushrooms flowing from the Grove was nowhere near natural. Some Druids wanted a new Grove to be created faraway outside the city.\nOthers wanted the Grove to be close. Still others did not want a new grove at all. But, it is important to note that most of these arguments were caused by misunderstandings, which is why this age is sometimes called the Age of\nMisunderstanding or the Age of Confusion.\nThe Age Of Renovation: In the end, most mushrooms were removed from the Grove when Maiavel stamped her foot and the mushrooms instantly broke (but were\nthoughtlessly left on the ground, only to be swept up by Deltaro). A new, secret Grove was set up in the wilderness outside Ravenhold, (notable work from Mahten and Aeaira, who spent days working on the road to civilization). The \nLaurelin Grove continued to be renovated and improved on, with notable work contributed by Lunar Druid Bircalin and Dedicant Deltaro.\nAEGIS POST-DREAM\nThe First Age of Dreaming: For a log time, it seemed that Nature was silent. For a length of time, none had seen any feats spoken about in the ancient Druid tales. But then, as if a seed was planted, Nature began to speak,\nand each Druid began to dream mysterious dreams. It was the Aspects of Nature, Cerridwen and Cernunnos, calling to their newly found children. Wayward Druid Respiren called a Moot to discuss these dreams, \nleading into the next age.\nThe Age Of The Aspects: The Moot decided to embrace these Aspects as their primary deities.\nThe Age Of Little Occurence: Nothing happened for a while, except a few little things. There\nwas a small Hierarchy change; the Archdruid position was given to three people, and the Grand Druid's description was changed. John and Maiavel were promoted to Archdruids, but Maiavel soon retired. Her spot \nwas filled by Petyr. Cleric Druid Mahten was also promoted to the rank of Guide. A simple, new recruiting strategy was initiated.\nThe Second Age Of Renovations: During this age, the Laurelin Grove experianced a number of\nadditions. A wall was created around the Grove, with a retractable gate. This was done to keep out a number of citizens that were harassing the Druids. In addition, all entrances were  covered up, so that one must always use the\nfront gate. More additions to the Grove were a kitchen, a melon and pumpkin farm, the cultivation of the Grand Tree's roots deeper into the ground, a tree farm, an elevator system, and Druid dwellings at the top of the Grand Tree.\nThe Age Of Poor Judgement: A lot of inner-Order bad feelings culminated in this age. Multiple parties were involved, and no side was completely right. The end result was the leaving of Seeker Druid Deltaro from the Order. The bad\ntaste left in the mouths of many  Druids lead Apollan to create the Druid Code.\nThe Second Age Of Little Occurance: During this age, as its name would imply, not many things happened. The Grove was given another\nrenovation, mostly for aesthetic purposes. (In addition, a Druid Order Forum account was created, as well as a blog.) Unfortunately, during this time, Archdruid John's mental health was also starting to\nslide.\nThe Second Age Of Dreaming: During this age, Salmon Druid Petyr had a vision in which the creation myth was shown to him by the Aspects. It fortold of a time before the four races, and of a great exodus to come. A second \nMoot was called and all in attendance agreed to accept the vision as truth. The Age Of Mourning: Unfortunately, during this time, Archdruid John's mental state grew worse. One day, John snapped. Among a number of\nthings, he attacked the Dusk Druid. He then fled to his soul tree (which he named Marcus), located by the pond in the Laurelin Grove. There, he made his last stand. The Druids present at the time were Dusk, Mahten, Apollan, Respiren,\nSaviticus, and Thork the Betrayer (Thork the Blood Druid). In addition, several princes and bystanders were there. John stood on the roots of his soul tree and attacked anyone who came near. There was a standoff for some\ntime, until all at once the Druids charged the tree. While some traded blows with John, Apollan worked to purify the water around the tree for he sensed that there was a taint at work. Suddenly the Dusk Druid produced an axe\nand chopped at the soul tree until only one column was left. It was then, with the ability to see inside the tree, that Apollan discovered the taint in the form of a block of netherrack. Before Apollan could share his discovery,\nThork went into a blood lust. He cut down the last column of the tree, rendering John unconscious. Then Thork stabbed John's body, killing him. In the days that followed, Thork was shunned for violating the Druid Code. John's tree \nwas turned into the place of his burial, where his body was burned and his ashes scattered around Laurelin. His will named Mahten as his replacement as Archdruid.\nThe Age Of Expansion: During this age, the \nNature's Bounty chain was by one new store on the King's Road. The Order was also expanded by one new member. Zannith, the 10 year old son of the Dusk Druid and an unknown Elf moved into the Grove. Much to the dismay\nof one Bircalin. Zannith later left the Druid Grove to join the Wardens, and later committed suicide by jumping from the Grand Tree.\nThe Age Of Knowledge: During this age, the Druids took control of the library of the\nCloud Temple of Aegis. Petyr also retired from his position as Archdruid and became a Hierophant. Dusk Druid Aeaira was elected to fill the spot and Saviticus became Head Teacher.\nThe Second Age Of\nMourning: During this age, Archdruid Mahten transformed his entire being into a tree in the Grove. As a result of his sacrifice, Druid Dusk was named (in his will) as successor to the position of Archdruid. In this time, she had\nbegun to bring new life to the Druid Tree; ushering forth the growth and spread of new branches, and bringing in a new generation of Dedicants.\nThe Second Age Of Expansion: During this age, the Druid Order and Grand\nTree both grew exponentially.\nThe Third Age Of Mourning: During this age, Archdruids Apollan and Dusk were both killed under mysterious circumstances. Apollan's position was given to his close friend,\nHorizon Druid Makia, and Dusk's position was given to Fox Druid Valas.\nThe Age Of Poor Logic: During this age, everything the Druids knew was proven to be incorrect. Petyr proved that wood doesn't exist, and then proved that\nit does. He also proved that magic isn't real and water is fake. Unable to hold all this nonsense, Archdruid Darrin was convinced that he had gone crazy and was only dreaming. After jumping to his death from the top\nof the Grand Tree, Fey Druid Vanyariel took his position as Archdruid.\nThe Age Of Activism: During this age, many Druids had visions fortelling a coming distruction of all of Aegis. The Druids took it upon themselves to find and recover all\nancient artifacts of Aegis so that they might be saved from the end and brought with them to a new land. With the help of High Princess Indelwehn, the Druids were lead to the Druid Tree at the docks. There, she showed them the Shadow\nCircle, an underground compound created beneath the tree by Apollan and Respiren, to house the First Staff, Seed, and Sapling. \n\n\n\n[END VOLUME ONE]", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid's Paradise", "Ryn Powell", "  Druid's Paradise\nAs I walk through the grove where I learn of the Cycle,\nI take a look at the trees and realize they're really tall.\nBut that's just perfect for an Acolyte like me.\nYou know I shun voidy things like pyromancy.\n\nAt 4:30 in the mornin' I'm growin' trees.\nMy husband feeds the chickens and my family plows.\nAnd I've been growin' and feedin' so long that even he thinks that my mind is gone.\n\nI'm a woman of the land, I'm into mushroom stew.\n\nGot a staff in my hand and some leaves in my hair.\nBut if I finish all my growin' and you finish thine, \nThen tonight we're gunna party like it's 1499!\n\nWe've been spendin' most our time livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\n\nI've grown a spruce tree once or twice, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\nIt's hard work and sacrifice, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\nWe give bread out with no price, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\n\nAn Oren boy kicked me in the butt last week.\n\nI just smiled at him and turned the other cheek.\nI really don't care, infact I wish him well,\n'Cause I'll be laughing my head off while he's livin' in Hell.\n\nBut I ain't never smacked a child even if he deserved it.\n\nA Druid child abuser, you know that's unheard of.\n I never do magic but I got a cool staff and my dedicants all agree I really look good in green, Fool!\n\nIf you come to visit, you'll be havin' no fear.\n\nWe've talked to nature for over 300 years.\nBut we ain't really quaint, so please don't point and stare.\nWe're just void magically impaired.\n\nThere's no void, no undead, no necromancy\nNot a single unnatural thing.\n\nLike Druids in the old days,\nIt's as nature-y as can be.\n\nWe've been spendin' most our time livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\nWe're just nature lovin' guys, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\n\nThere's no time for evil folks, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\nWe don't die, we just join the Cycle, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\n\nWalkin' through the forest, respectin' all of Nature.\nGrew a tree on Monday.\nSoon I'll grow another.\n\nThink you're really righteous?\nThink you're a nature lover?\nWell, I know I love it a million times more than thou do.\n\nI'm the nature girl, all the little Dedicants wanna be like.\n\nOn my knees day and night plantin' wheat for the free bread.\nSo don't be vain and don't be whiney,\nor else my brother, I might have to send my vines out on your heinie!\n\nWe've been spendin' most our time livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\n\nWe're all crazy hippy guys, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\nThere's no guards or pestasides, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\nBut you'd probably think it's nice, livin' in a Druid's Paradise.\n((Parody of Amish Paradise by Wierd Al. By Melodystar/ Ryn Powell ))", ""),
