g the condensation using an alembic.)\n\n>1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n\n>1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\n\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely dull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated\nand rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish. So, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\nCreativity. Please note that I am writing here to explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something completely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in\nthe art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There comes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more \nexplanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their own extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This\nis much more difficult that it may seem... but I shan't go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but rather, an introduction to the science.\nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone who is impulsive and stupid... 'overly' enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of enthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience.\nEnthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of the list instead of the top, is simply because by\nreading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\nChapter 2:\n\nThe Life of an Alchemist\n\nThe Lifestyle.\n\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guilds need Alchemists, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the\nmost fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one location whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them.\nIn my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one's options before taking a job. This is not to say that an Alchemist /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choose a life of reclusion and \nintroversion--preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency. As an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and\nwounded. These paths will play  large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one who makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who creates healing serums as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are\nof no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of a guild. This is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing\nmuch of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could have a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however--and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of\nthe science--think of it more as a specialization. I, for example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds… even research companies.\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\n\nMany jobs seem to have a set \"morality.\" Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trustworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and is, much like\none's business opportunities dictated by the Alchemist's specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more \"evil\" morality, as they would likely find their work\nwith small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a \"good\" morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people. There are not set rules, of course, a healing\nAlchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is neutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\n\nThis section will be somewhat small, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist's abode will generally have only one constant: a lab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain\nan Alchemist's supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement… Well… The earth seems to be a bit more resistant to explosions than wooden or cobblestone walls.\nFarewell:\nI thank you, reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.\n\nAn Introduction to the Alchemist\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Ireheart Traditi", "[Yemekar's Pick] Elder Falent Ireheart", "Orc Skinning\n\nThe skinning of Orc's is a long valued tradition withing the Irehearts, beardlings are annually taught the ways of Orc skinning and it comes in handy as three different Orc hides are required in the Ireheart Trials. It is a great tradition \nwithin the Irehearts and even the most senior members go out to skin Orc's annually. The Orc skins are usually used as carpets to decorate the Clan Hall. The Irehearts most renowned Orc skinner is Olaf Ireheart.\nThe Cutting of Elf Ears\n\nThe cutting of Elf ears is also a popular tradition in the Ireheart clan, while doing the Ireheart Trials you need three different elf ears from each time of elf, usually elf ears are used to make necklaces or bracelets.\nWar Paint\n\nPainting of one's body for war and any other militaristic event is a popular tradition among the Irehearts, painting one's body can strike fear within the enemy hearts and is a great factor of war for the Irehearts.\nDungrimm/Kjellos Warshipping\n\nThe devout worship of Dungrimm and Kjellos is very popular withing the Ireheart clan and many members are known for the zealotus ways of worshipping him, before or after a kill, or even before or after battle the \nIrehearts can be heard chanting \"DUNGRIMM\", \"FER DUNGRIMM\", \"KJELLOS\" or even, \"FER KJELLOS\" showing their religious devotion for their patron god.\nHonour Duels\n\nThe Irehearts host many honour duels amongst themselves and between other dwarves in the Kingdom. They do this to prove who is a more capable fighter and who has the most honour. The Irehearts are known to be the best fighters \nin the Kingdom and nearly never lose an honour duel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ireheart Values", "[Yemekar's Pick] Elder Falent Ireheart", "Honour\n\nHonour is a great value for any dwarf and for the Irehearts in particular. They devote their lives to obtaining a strict code of honor and work very hard to keep this code. The Irehearts are known to battle with honour and are known across the \nland for their honourable deeds.\nLoyalty\n\nThe Irehearts are known to be a very loyal clan and have stuck by the Kingdom since their creation. They never think twice before thinking about the betterment of the Kingdom and always do things that will have a good effect on the \nKingdom and their clan.\nDevotion\n\nThe clan is one of the most devoted clans in Dwarven History, they have worked tirelessly for their Kingdom and have built many structures for it in the past. A lot of their members have held high positions in Dwarven Society and many will\nwill say they did it extraordinarly well.\nZealotry\n\nThe Irehearts are very well known for their religious zealotry and have often been found killing in the name of their patron god, Dungrimm. All of their members are devoted to Dungrimm and would die if their god commanded such.\nThey have followed him since the birth of the clan.\nBravery\n\nThe Irehearts are well known for their bravery on and off the battlefield and some of their members have killed thousands upon thousands of enemies. The clan is known to not fear anything and have sometimes gone into battle with nothing but \na sword and dressed in war paint.\nBrotherhood\n\nThe Irehearts were originally founded as \"The Grim Brotherhood\" and held those values high, they are known for their great respect for eachother no matter each member's past. They have always and will always have great r\nrespect for eachother and dwarves alike.", ""),
        StaticBook("Iron Corps I", "Tahjeet Mubdee", "()() Iron Corps ()()\n----Expenditures----:<><><> & Profit <><><>\nSale: 128 Iron Ingots\nProfit: 1050 Minas\nEntity: Menithrian\n\nSale: 35 Redstone Blocks\nProfit: 250\nEntity: Camo Shadd\nSale: Physical Labor\nProfit: 150\nEntity: The Bard's Guild\n\nSale: 128 Iron Ingots\nProfit: 1100\nEntity: Nation of Ker'nor\n\nSale: 45 Redstone Blocks\nProfit: 225\nEntity: Khamason\nSale: 88 Ferum Bars\nProfit: 466.4\nEntity: The Syndicate\n\nTahjeet and Ehsan\n        Mubdee\n\nReport I", ""),
        StaticBook("Isabellas Poem!", "[[Child]] Isabella Carstais Ibar'Ker", "*The poem seems to be written in childish handwriting*\n\nFlower Flowers! Pretty flowers\nHow do you like to grow?\nIn the rain the flowers reply, up in the druids grove\n\n\nFlowers flowers\nblooming flowers\nWhy are you colored so?\nCause we spread the joy, the flowers sing, all around the world\n\nFlowers flowers dying flowers\nWhy do you look so gloom?\nOur time has come, the flowers cough, and its time to go below.\n\n\n*There seems to be another page!*\n             ,-. \n    ,     ,-.   ,-. \n   / \\   (   )-(   ) \n   \\ |  ,.>-(   )-< \n    \\|,' (   )-(   ) \n     Y ___`-'   `-' \n     |/__/   `-' \n     | \n     | \n     |    -hrr- \n  ___|_____________ \n*a childs drawing of a flower!*", ""),
        StaticBook("It's Funny", "Luxeanna", "\n\n\n\n  \n        For the lady.\n      She went out in search of storm and came back with more than she had bargained for. And suddenly her hands are full of too much rain and she doesn’t know where to put it all down and she's not even sure that she wants to. Maybe she was bored, or \nmaybe she wanted to be thrown around a little. Maybe there’s something about dangerous things that reminds her of the times she was young and she touched burning flames even though she knew it would hurt. Or the first man she loved, how it was painful but\nit felt good at the same time. She knows pain now, she knows how to survive it. Maybe that's what it was. She just wanted to survive again.\n\nThe thing is, before she left, everything was gentle and safe and never overwhelming. She had time to think and \nuncoil herself. She was lazy days and sun filled afternoons that felt so good against her skin she thought she'd never want to leave that place again. And why would she? For a tempest? For a fist clutching a spark of lightning? For the burn? And now she's\nconfused because she's torn between the safe thing and the thing that will probably ruin her and it's funny because it hurts and it's funny because she did it to herself and it's not funny because it actually hurts.\n\nShe just knows that she can't have\nboth. She can either stand in the middle of all that brutal and let it wash her up or she can find that safe place and let it be soft for her. But when she's standing halfway through that storm, and she's drenched through and her skin is turning itself \ninside out, and she's shivering and it's terrifying and she's never felt more fucking alive. That's it, that's what she came looking for.\n\nShe found it. \nCongratulations.\nIs she going to hold onto it?", ""),
        StaticBook("It's funny.", "Luxeanna", "\n\n\n\n\n        For that lady.\n     Hang in there.\nShe went out in search of storm and came back with more than she had bargained for. And suddenly her hands are full of too much rain and she doesn’t know where to put it all down and she's not even sure that she wants to. Maybe she was bored, or maybe she\nwanted to be thrown around a little. Maybe there’s something about dangerous things that reminds her of the times she was young and she touched burning flames even though knew it would hurt. Or the first man she loved who broke her heart and it felt good \nat the same time. She knows pain now, she knows how to survive it. Maybe that’s what it was. She just wanted to survive again.\n\nThe thing is, before she left, everything was gentle and safe and never overwhelming. She had time to think and uncoil herself.\nShe has lazy days and sun filled afternoons that felt so good against her skin she thought she'd never want to leave that place again. And why would she? For a tempest? For a fist clutching a park of lightning? For the burn? And now she's confused because\nshe's torn between the safe thing that will probably ruin her and it's funny because it hurts and it's funny because she did it to herself and it's not funny because it actually hurts.\n\nShe just knows that she's can't have both. She can either stand in \nthe middle of all that brutal and let it wash her up or she can find that safe place and let it be soft for her. But when she's standing halfway through that storm, and she's drenched through and her skin is turning itself inside out, and she's shivering \nand it's terrifying and she's never felt more alive \n\nThat's it, that's what she came looking for. She found it.\n\nCongratulations. \n\nIs she going to hold onto it?", ""),
        StaticBook("Jabberwock", "Pippin Mousiki", "Twas brilling and the slithy toves,\nDid Shire and Gimblewood our home,\nAll mimsy were the borogoves, \nAnd the mome raths outgrabe.\nBeware the Jabberwock my friends,\nThe jaws that bite,\nThe claws that catch,\nBeware the Boggle and shun,\nThe frumious Bandersnatch!\nI sat in my burrow,\nMy hideaway,\nI looked out the window and there I saw,\nA man had Vorpal Sword in hand,\nLong time the manxome foe he sought,\nSo rested he by the grand oak tree,\nAnd stood awhile in thought.\n\nAnd as in uffish thought he stood,\nThe Jabberwock with eyes of flame,\nCame whiffling through the wooded wood,\nAnd burbled as it came! \nOne two,\nOne two,\nAnd through and through,\nThe vorpal blade went snicker-snack,\nThe boy left it dead,\nWith its head,\nHe went galumphing back.\nAnd hast thou slain the Jabberwock?\nCome to my arms,\nYou beamish boy,\nOh Frabjous Day,\nCallooh Callay,\nI chortled in my joy.\nTwas brillig and the slithy toves,\nDid Shire and Gimblewood our home,\nAll mimsy were the borogoves, \nAnd the mome raths outgrabe.\n((Jabberwock by Lewis Carroll.  I changed some words up to fit rp better. I love this poem!))", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C1", "Sofetios Jayamen", "    Jaya's Journey\n \n             -By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n     Chapter One\n A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n\n\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today. \nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head. \nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound. \nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing. \nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him. \nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped. \nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen. \nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll.\n It had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones. \nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n\n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said. \n\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\n\n Then looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again. \n\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues. \nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow.\n I then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\n As I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house. \nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.” \n\n\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\n\nEND OF CHAPTER ONE\n\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C2", "Sofetios Jayamen", "     Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios                   Jayamen \n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n      Chapter Two\n          Linink\n\nAs I woke up the next morning I couldn’t help but feel a bit afraid. Linink was one of the most important people in town and he was never really free. \nAlso, why was my Mom so worried last night? I stepped out of bed. Instead of the usual hardwood floor I was used to I was stepped on something lumpy and cold. I looked down and jumped back on my bed. \nThe weapons from last night where on the floor right next to my bed. \n\n“Jaya what’s all the racket?” Said my mom’s voice. It sounded like she was coming to my room. Quickly, I covered the weapons with my blanket.\n\n Like that would do anything, but it was worth a shot. My mom came in the door and said,\n\n“Jaya why is your blanket on the floor?” \n\n“Bad dream.” I Lied.\n\nMy mom frowned, bent over, and was about to pick up the blanket. I closed my eyes and cringed from what was about to happen. \n\n“Jaya are you ok?” Said my Mom concerned. \n\nOpening my eyes I saw my mom had folded the blanket and on the floor was nothing.\n\n“Uh, yea.” I said scratching my head. “I think I just must have hit my head.”\n\n“Well it’s a good thing your going to see Linink today.” My mom said. “Come on, breakfast is ready.”\n\nI ate very little breakfast this morning. The taste of it as usual was great, but the stress of what I thought was to come overcame my hunger.\nAfter breakfast my mom took me straight to The Adventurers Guild. \n\nAs I approached the massive building I started to get nervous. \n\n\nMy mom opened the doors, led me past staring students, rooms that where full of weapons, and many more things.\n\n Finally we reached Linink’s Office. \n\nThe large green door looked inviting enough but as to what was to happen behind it still worried me. \n\nWithout knocking a voice said, “Come in.” My mom and I entered the triangle shaped room. \n\n\nI saw Linink sitting a table in the middle, but beside the table on both sides where my friends Sofetios and Sofia.\n I relaxed a little. At least they would be here with me. “Jaya, would you please take a seat.” Said Linink coolly.  \n\nI took a seat, looked back at my mom, and Linink then said, “I need to speak to Jaya and his friends alone Madam.”\n My mom nodded and left the room quietly. Everyone was quite for a bit until I said, \n“What am I here for?” \n\n“I’d like to know that too.” Sofetios added.\n\n“Same here.” Said Sofia. After a moment Linink said,\n\n“We are here to discuss a recent series of events.”\n\n“Like what?” said Sofia. “Other then the Melonko Festival being today all that’s really happened was that Rainstorm last night. “\n\n“Exactly my point” said Linink. “A rainstorm now? In the middle of summer? I just don’t really see that as natural. There is also the Prophecy.”\n\n“You mean that old tale everyone listens to at the festival?” Said Sofetios inquiringly. \n\n“Just that.” Said Linink seriously. “From what I’ve seen happening in the last two days I’m inferring that it may be coming true.” At this Sofia laughed and said,\n“Like that would happen now. I mean the rain was probably coincidence and it’s not like the weapons have been found.” At this I felt the blood drain from my face. \n“Well from what I heard from Jaya’s Mother last night, I think they may have been found.” Said Linink. Sofia and Sofetios look right at me and Sofetios said, “You didn’t really… I mean you couldn’t have…” \n“He probably didn’t” Said Sofia, Otherwise he would be wearing them right now. It’s not like he would leave them at his house or something if he found them. Right?” I looked slightly down at this comment.\n“The weapons only appear if the owner wants them to.” Said Linink. Sofetios turns to me and said. “Well Jaya? Did you actually find the weapons?” I tell them the whole story of what happened last night and this morning. \nWhen I finish, Sofia is staring at me in disbelief, Sofetios is too, and Linink looks the same as he did before. No one said anything for a while until Linink said,\n\n“Well I guess the prophecy is coming true.” \n\n“Should we tell everyone?” Said Sofia.\n\n“No.” said Linink. “That would only raise panic. We should just tell whoever really needs to be told then you three set off after the festival.”\n\n“Us three?” I said.\n“Yes.” Said Linink “You know both Sofia and Sofetios pretty well. Except for what each they specialize in.” I didn’t actually know what Linink taught Sofetios and Sofia in the Guild and they had never shown me. \nI gave an odd face to all three of them then Linink said, “To put it bluntly Sofetios is a magician and Sofia is a fighter, in class terms that is.” \n\n“A magician?” I repeated while looking at Sofetios. \n\n“Intermediate magician.” Said Sofetios. “Sorry but Linink said we couldn’t tell anyone outside the guild.” \n\n“Wait so what can you do?” I said. “Levitate stuff or something?” Sofetios looked at Linink and Linink nodded.\n\n All of the sudden everything small in the room started to slowly floated upwards.  I froze and looked around.  Then the things in the air floated down to their original places.\n“You see Jaya, Everything we teach at this guild more or less has to do with Lin.”  Said Linink.\n\n“Lin?” I said curiously.\n\n“Yes, it is something that is in everything around us.” Said Linink. “Kind of like a fifth element so to speak. Sofetios will be teaching you about this on your travels.”\n“Wait.” I said. “There’s a whole Fifth element?”\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink simply. “Sofetios, Sofia, please get ready for your departure.”\n\n“But sir.” Said Sofetios. “We still-“\n\n“Come on Sofetios.” Said Sofia as he grabbed Sofetios on the shoulder and had him follow her. When they closed the door, Linink turned to me and Said. \n\n“You have a long journey ahead of you.”\n\n“Yes sir…” I said nervously.\n\n“I just need to make sure you really have the weapons.” Said Linink concerned.\n\n“I would sir but I don’t know how to get them to appear.” I said.\n“Just hold your hand as you would your sword and try to will them there.” Said Linink. I did so and in a second a white sword materialized there. It felt warm in my hand. Linink seemed was taken aback a little, so I asked, \n“Sir, why me?” Linink seemed back as himself and said after a moment,\n\n“Because He chose you. At least that’s what the Prophecy sais.” Linink got up and went to his bookshelf. \n\nHe picked up two books and put them both on the desk. He opened one and the inside of it was hollowed out. All there was, was a semi-clear sphere about an inch long. \nHe handed it to me and said. “This is something I’ve been working on for a long time. Use it well.”  I sheathed the sword and took the sphere and said,\n\n“Sir, what is this?”\n\n“Don’t you recognize it?” Linink said surprised. “It is object from part of the lore they tell at the Melonko festival. Well, my version of it anyway.”\n\n“I’m sorry sir, I don’t really listen to the tales they tell.” I said a little embaraced.\n\n“Well then I should probably tell you.” Said Linink. “It is my version of a water sphere. This one I would say holds about 1 week worth of water for 3 people.” Unbelieving, I stared at the sphere. \n“All you need to do is heat it in something and water will come out.”\n\n“Sir?” I said. “What did you mean by ‘your version’?”\n\n“You’ll find out soon enough.” Said Linink. Suddenly there was music outside.\n\n “The festival is starting.”\n\n“Sir, what now?” I said.\n\n“Now, you go enjoy the festival.” Said Linink. “But before you go,” Linink picked up the other book and handed it to me. \n\n“This is a book on lore of Edrot. You may want to study it.”\n\n I turned to leave when Linink said, “and Jaya, two words of advice. First, with the powers you will soon possess, Make sure you use them the right way. \n\nSecondly, I need you to will away that sword for now. The people in town don’t need to see it.”\n\n“Is that all sir?” I said.\n\n“That’s all” Said Linink.\n\nEND OF CHAPTER TWO\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C3", "Sofetios Jayamen", "    Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios                   Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n     Chapter Three\n The Melonko Festival\n\nI went to the town’s center where everyone was gathered, People where playing music and everyone was seemingly having a good time. \nThe mayor, Jedjory, appeared and walked to the center and everyone quieted down.  Then Jedjory said, \n\n“Good morning everyone, this is the 10th Melonko festival, Celebrating good fortune and peace.\n\n Now  everyone please stop and listen to the Adventurers guild orchestra!” Everyone turned to the front of the Adventurers guild where there where about 50 teenagers with all kinds of different instruments. Linink was on a piano and started to play. \nThen others joined in and more until everyone was playing.  I had heard Sofetios speak of this kind of thing before, where everyone joined in when they felt it was right. I think he called it free playing. \nThe sound was great. When they all finished there was a round of applause and Jedjory spoke again when they all quieted down.\n\n“Let the Melonko festival begin!”\n\nI met with Sofia and Sofetios a bit later in front of one of the games tents. \n\n“So, chosen one, how did you like the performance?” Said Sofia sarcastically. \n\n“Don’t call me that.” I said angrily.\n\n“Come on.” Said Sofia smiling. “Everyone is going to start calling you that once they realize what you found.”\n“Hopefully that won’t be soon” I said worried. I noticed that Sofetios was looking behind the tent. “What is it Sofetios?”\n“I think I just saw a black hooded figure behind the tent.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“Not possible.” Said Sofia. “I already know what you’re thinking and it’s not possible. They died out years ago.”\n\n“Yea, your right.” Said Sofetios turning to me. “I guess I’m just worried about the Journey.”\n\n“Wait, what died out years ago?” I said.\n\n\n“Jeez Jaya.” Said Sofia. “You really should pay more attention to lore.” I then remembered the Lore book that Linink gave me and pulled it out of my bag.\n\n“I see Linink gave you his lore book.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“That will probably help in times to come. “Look up the word ‘Omira’.”  I skimmed the book until I found the word. I then said, \n“ ‘The Omira are a clan of people dedicated to protecting the Land from any evil. They commonly wear black robes with hoods and are practiced in concealing themselves. \nThey are said to be mainly of the rouge class, but there were rumors of some being mages. They are said to have died out long ago. ‘ “ \n\n“That about covers it.” Said Sofetios. “Did Linink give you anything else?” \n I pulled out the water sphere Linink gave me. At this Sofetios’s mouth hung slightly ajar.\n\n“He gave you a water sphere?” Sofetios said in amazement. “How much did he say was in there?”\n\n“A weeks worth for three people he said.” I said.\n\n“Well then I guess we won’t need to worry about water.” Said Sofia. “Come on, let’s go to the fortune stall.” Sofia went to the fortune stall every year.\n\n The weird thing about the lady who runs it is that all her predictions seem to come true.\n\nAs we approached the purple tent. I couldn’t help but be worried. I was about to have my future laid out for me. Maybe I just wouldn’t get my fortune read. \n\nWe entered the tent. The old lady was sitting behind the usual crystal ball.\n\n“Come in.” She said as she looked up. “Ah Sofia. Come to see your fortune again I see?”\n\n“Yes Maim.” Said Sofia. \n\nThis is pretty much the only time she gets enthusiastic or manner full about anything except fighting.\n“Ok then.” Said the Lady. “Please take a seat. I will need your two friends to step outside.” Sofia looked at us and both Sofetios and I left.\n After 15 minutes, Sofia left the tent looking slightly uneasy. She was also holding a fortune cookie in her hand. The old lady also gives those out so people can have a little extra info. \n\n\n“She wants you to come in next Sofetios.” Said Sofia. Sofetios went inside the tent without saying a word.\n\n“What did she tell you?” I said.\n\n“None of your business.” Said Sofia right back.\n After another 15 minutes Sofetios exited the tent looking a bit down. \n\n“Well your next.” Said Sofetios to me. I nervously entered the tent. \n\n“Take a seat.” Said the lady. I went over and took a seat.\n “Your friends certainly had interesting fates. Now let’s see yours.” She pulled out her famous set of fortune cards and spread them out face down. “Choose four.” I picked the ones in the beginning, end, and two in the middle.\n“Now flip them over in the order you choose. One by one.” I flipped the first one. It had a picture of someone about to be shot by and arrow but there was someone behind the person who was the real one about to be shot with a dagger raised. \nThere were words printed around the sides. It said, ‘Saved by a Friend’. “It seems you have more friends then you realize.” Said the old lady. “Now the second.” \nI flipped over the second one. It showed a book with worlds spewing out of it with the word ‘Skill’. “It also seams that you will excel at learning. Now the third.”\n I flipped over the third one and it had a picture of a blanket over a bizarre shaped object with jagged edges and then a picture of a bird in a cage with the blanket on the ground, the words on this one said ‘Doubt then Understanding’. \nThe old lady seemed a little worrisome on this card. \n\n“Is something wrong?” I said nervously.\n\n“No, no.” said the old lady.\n\n “This card means that you will doubt something or be undecided, but then see the truth. Now the Fourth.” I flipped the fourth card and it showed two paths going separate from each other. \nOn one side there was what looked like woods, on the other it looked like a plain. The words on it said ‘The Choice’  “That’s the toughest one of all.” Said the lady. \n“You will have a tough choice in the future. Now for your final fortune with me. Please place your hands on the side of the crystal ball and you will see your future.” I hesitated, then was about to place my hands on the crystal ball.\n When I touched it, it exploded with light. The old lady stood up quickly and gasped and then I realized I was standing up too. As soon as my hand left the ball the light went away immediately. \n“You…” Said the lady slowly. Then she calmed down. “So the prophecy is coming true. “ \n\n“What does this all mean?” I said.\n\n“It means you have a long journey ahead of you.” Said the old lady.\n\n“Here.” She reached in a jar at the side of the table and pulled out two cookies. “Only Break and eat one. The other you are to give to a friend.”\n\n“Is that all you have to say?” I said hoping for more.\n\n“That is all.” Said the old lady. I exited the tent, sure that I looked worried.\n\n“What happened in there?” Said Sofia.\n\n“Yea.” Said Sofetios. “We saw a flash of light.” \n\nI was about to tell them when I remembered its bad luck to tell your fortunes. I needed all the luck I could get.\n\n“Sorry I don’t know myself.” I said with some truth. \n\n\nAfter some hours had passed, we went to the entrance of the village. Sofia and Sofetios had huge packs on. \n\n“Should I have brought anything?” I asked.\n\n“No we have everything here.” Said Sofetios. \n\nThen I remembered my mom.\n\n“But we can’t go yet, I need to say goodbye to my mom!” \n\n“Relax Jaya.” Said Sofetios. “Linink probably already told your mother.”\n\n“Yea, I guess your right.” I said a little down. Then it occurred to me that I didn’t even know where we were going.\n\n“Wait, where are we going?” I said.\n\n“To the temple of the Omira” Said Sofia. “You should really take a look at that lore book.” As we left I dug into my pocket and got the two fortune cookies. I picked one at random and opened it. The paper inside said one word. ‘Believe’. \nEND OF CHAPTER THREE\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C4", "Sofetios Jayamen", "    Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n      Chapter Four\n    The Power of Lin\n\nAs we set of on the path leading out from the town, Sofetios began to tell me about Lin. \n“To use Lin, you will need to be able to understand what it is.” Said Sofetios.\n\n“Ok then.” I said. “What is it?”\n\n“I think the better question is what isn’t it.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“Lin is like an elemental life force to which you can use to manipulate the area around you.\n\n For instance, Sofia uses Lin as a weapon, literally. She can make weapons out of her Lin and use it to add force to her blows.”\n\n“Wait so you mean that I could make a sword right now out of Lin?” I said astounded.\n“I don’t think you would be able to do it right away since you’re just beginning, but yes you could. I would ask Sofia to train you in that type of style since I don’t know much about it.”\n\n“Ok.” I said. “So what can you teach me?”\n\n“I can teach you another style of using Lin.” Said Sofetios. “As you saw before I levitated things around Linink’s office. But you can do much more. You can also make things into different forms.\n Imagine you holding clay with your minds hands and holding it from 5 feet away. Then being able to mold it to what you would like. Sofia can we stop for a second?” \n\n“Come on.” Said Sofia. “What for? We’re on a tight schedule.”\n\n“It will only take a second.” Said Sofetios as he picked up a pebble. He walked over to me and put it in my hand. “Something to start with. Try levitating it, transforming it, things like that.” \nAs we began walking again, I held the pebble in my hand and levitating it. I thought I saw it wiggle a bit but thought that it was just my movement walking. \n\nWe arrived at a camp site as the full moon was up. \n\nAs we set up a camp sight for the night, Sofetios walked over to me.\n\n“How is the stone coming along?” Said Sofetios\n\n“I just can’t get it to budge.” I said frustrated.\n\n Sofetios appeared to be thinking. Then he said,\n\n“I think you may be thinking about it a different way then you should for levitating. If I’m right in saying your trying to force it to, it won’t work.”\n\n“Wait why won’t force work?” I said. “I’m trying to force the stone up right?”\n\n“Force works for stuff like… well… forceful stuff.” Said Sofetios. “What you want to try to do is lifting it not with force alone, but thought.”\n\n“Thought.” I repeated.\n\n“Yes.” Said Sofetios. “Instead of the thought of trying to lift an impossible stone, just think of it as possible it might help. A lot of it is in what you believe.” There was the word again. Believe.\n\n This gave me confidence. I held out the stone in my palm and began to try to levitate it. After a moment nothing happened, and then it wiggled.\n\n“Yes!” I yelled. \n\n Just as I yelled, the stone shot into the air and then landed on the ground. “Hey Sofetios you don’t have to show off.”\n\n“That wasn’t me.” Said Sofetios. “It was you.” \n\n“I did that?” I said confused. “But all I could do was make it move a little. How could I have made it shoot in the air like that?”\n\n“Your excitement in moving the pebble while still trying to move the pebble. \n\nEmotion counts as thought when it comes to Lin.”\n\n“Hey you two.” Said a voice from behind. We turned and it was Sofia. She had a bag on her bag that seemed full of a certain type of fruit. “Dinners up.”\n\nSofetios put a metal pot on the unlit fire pit. \n\n“Hey Jaya could I get the water sphere?” Said Sofetios.\n\n“Yea, sure.” I said taking it out and giving it to him. He put it in the pot when I asked,\n\n“Who has the fire maker?” I said. Sofetios just smiled at me and said,\n\n“We don’t need one.”\n\n“But how-“I began as I saw Sofetios put his hand near the fire pit and snapped his fingers.\n\n\n Instantly, a small flame appeared on his thumb which he left sticking out. He started to light the fire until it started to flame. Then in moments there was good sized fire in the pit. “Doesn’t that hurt?”\n\n“Not when you know how to control it.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“O stop showing off Sofetios.” Said Sofia. I saw water starting to slowly rise in the pot. I got closer to get a better look. \n\nIt seemed at if the Water sphere was melting water but wasn’t shrinking in the slightest.\n\n“It’s like ice.” I said.\n\n“I guess you could look at it that way.” Said Sofetios as he picked up the water sphere out of the pot and gave it to me.\n\n“Come on guys, let’s eat.” Said Sofia tossing an apple my way. The apple had was red with an odd purplish tinge.\n\nI put the water sphere away then was about to take a bite when an arrow came from my right and hit the apple, sending it flying from my hand into a tree. We all sprang up and drew our weapons. \nSofia Looked to where the arrow came from but there was no one there. \n\n“Come out coward!” Said Sofia. There wasn’t a noise.\nThe moon was very bright, bright enough for me to make out the shadow of a figure from behind a large rock. \n\n“There!” I said pointing to the shadow. \nWe ran toward the rock and when we got to the side, No one was there. “Wait, what?” I looked down to where the shadow was and there was nothing there.\n“We’ve been tricked!” Said Sofia pointing back at the sight. “Who ever it was stole the apples!” We ran back to the camp sight and Sofetios pointed to the ground. Where he was pointing there as a piece of paper. He went down and picked it up and read, \n“ ‘I’m Sorry for having to have delayed your meal. I left some other fruits by one of your bags. Those apples where poisoned. Local hunters nearby here use the poison on those apples so that once an animal eats it, it dies in a couple of days. \nOnce the animal dies, the poison wears off. Once again I’m sorry.’ ”\n\n“Well whoever it was did leave us fruit.” Said Sofia with a smaller bag of fruit in her hands.\n\n“All there is on the bottom of the note is a big C.” Said Sofetios. \n\n\nSofia took out some of the fruits and I said,\n\n“Hey, those are the kind of berries that are in the woods back home.” \n\n“Well, I guess they are safe then.” Said Sofia.\n\n\nAfter discussing what just happened a while we ate, we agreed that I would take first watch. \nAfter a while when everyone but me was sleeping, I began to get tired so I sat on a nearby rock. \n When I sat down I felt something crinkly under me. I sat up and there was a piece of paper, Identical to the one we found a bit earlier except it had a different message. I read,\n‘If you want to learn how to use his weapons. Come see me at The Purple Café in Northenway. When you get there ask the waitress for the basement level table. I’ll be waiting there. Please do not tell your friends. I would like this to be private. C. ‘\nEND OF CHAPTER FOUR\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C5", "Sofetios Jayamen", "    Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n      Chapter Five\n\n           Cloak\n\nWhen we got up the next morning, when we finished packing up and started walking, I asked Sofetios,\n\n“Where is Northenway?” \n\n“It’s on the way to the temple.” Said Sofetios. “Why?”\n\n“It’s just there’s a place I’ve wanted to visit for a while.” I lied. “A place called the purple café? My Mom told me about it once.”\n\n“We aren’t making any un necessary stops.” Said Sofia. “We need to get to the temple.” I didn’t want to argue, so I figured I would wait until we got there to ask again.\nAs we approached the gates of Northenway, we were approached by guards.\n\n“Halt.” Said one of the guards. “What business do you have in Northenway?”\n\n“Just passing through.” Said Sofetios.\n\n“Really, do you think we were born yesterday?” Said the other guard. “You are playing hooky from school. Aren’t you?”\n\n“Relax.” Said Sofia. “We came from the Village south of here. No need to get mad.”\n\n“Hey, you better watch yourself girly.” Said the guard back. “Or Ill make you.” That was a mistake.\n\n“Girly!?” Said Sofia steaming. Sofia was about to go off.\n\n“Come on Rodrick.” Said the other guard. “Let’s just go for a bit, I think our break time is on anyway. Let’s just go to The Purple Café and relax a bit, eh?”\n“Fine, see you later miss.” The guard said with a chuckle. After the two left Sofia seemed to be trying to cam herself down. Then she said,\n\n“I think we should go to The Purple Café.”\n\nWe entered the city, which had its town square up front. In the middle there was a man in a white robe saying things to a small crowd that had gathered. He was saying,\n“The sun dims every day! Can you not feel it? It’s as though the days are getting shorter! The nights longer! Be vigilant, the time to prove ourselves comes!”\n\n“What is he talking about?” I said. \n\n“It’s part of the prophecy.” Said Sofetios. I frowned a bit as we made our way down the street to a large restaurant. There was a sign hanging from the door that showed a coffee mug with steam coming from it.\n On the top of the sign it said ‘The Purple Café’.  As we approached the door Sofia stopped and looked at a notice on the door. We gathered around it, it said, \n‘Arm wrestling day. Tournament will be in mid day. The grand champion gets 100 gold! Sign up here.’ Then there was a list of names and blank spaces. Under the notice was a pen and ink. \nSofia put her finger on the list then went down until she stopped at ‘Rodrick’.  Sofia wrote her name down so fast I thought for sure her name would be illegible. Someone came out of the door and looked at us. It was a waitress.\n“Just getting the sign up sheet.” She said taking it down and carrying it inside. We entered the café. It looked amazing. There were people at the bar drinking and the waitress cutting names off the list and putting them in a cup.\n There was also a band playing tavern music. Then I noticed another waitress staring at us. She walked up to us and said,\n\n“Are you kids going to order something or just stand there?” \n\n“I’m in the arm wrestle competition.” Said Sofia. Not waiting, Sofia walked past her and went toward a table. The waitress then looked at Sofetios and I. “We’re going to watch her compete”. Said Sofetios, The waitress sighed and said,\n“Fine, just don’t cause any trouble.”\n\n“We won’t” I said. As we went in the waitress who was cutting up the names went to the center of the restaurant, then said,\n\n“Alright! Is everyone ready to arm wrestle?” \n\n\nThere were cheers through the restaurant. “Ok then. The first two contenders are…” \nShe put her hand in the cup and drew two names. “First we have Rodrick!” There were roars from a table in the corner as the guard from before got up, Flexing. \n“Please come to the center table!” as Rodrick got there, the waitress with the names looked at the other one and said, “Second we have…” The waitress seemed to squint at the paper.\n I cringed, there was only one person that could be. “Sofia! Come to the middle table!” Rodrick was looking back at his table, which was chanting his name over and over again. \nWhen Sofia got to the table Rodrick turned to her, waited a moment as he recognized her, then laughed. \n\n“This girly is my first competition?” Said Rodrick.\n\n“You bet I am, unless you want to back down?” Said Sofia with a smile. There where “oo’s” from the crowd. \n\n“You’re on girly.” Said Rodrick as he smiled back. There were cheers throughout the restaurant again.\n\nSofia and Rodrick sat down at opposing ends of the middle table. The whole restaurant then counted, “Three!” “Two” “ONE!” There was a loud slam and a thud and it was over. The band stopped playing.\n Sofia stood over Rodrick who she had slammed his arm so hard on the table he had flipped over out of his chair to the floor. He wasn’t moving. The people from his table went over and tried to pick him up. \n“Is he dead?” The waitress said concerned.  One of them put an ear to his chest and said,\n\n“Nah, he’s just drunk. Let the tournament continue!” Everyone cheered and the tournament continued. \n\nSofia was about to step down when the waitress said,\n\n“Wait, you need to stay up here until you lose.”\n\n“Wait, what?” Said Sofia. “Well this is going to be fun then.” I then remembered why I was here.\n I went to the waitress who wanted us to order something and said,\n\n“Could I get the Basement table?” The Waitress raised an eyebrow and said,\n\n“We don’t have a basement table, but we do have an attic one. Follow me.” I followed the waitress upstairs to a door. She opened it went inside as I followed. Inside was a figure in a black hood and black robes. \n“Keep watch.” He said. The waitress nodded, went out, and closed the door.\n\n“So you’re C?” I said taking out the letters\n\n“Yes.” Said the person in the robes. “But you can call me Cloak.” \n\n“How do you know I have the weapons?” Said Sofetios. \n\n“I know how to use Lin in ways other then your friend Sofetios showed you.” Cloak said as he got up and got a bowl from a shelve and put it on the table. \nHe got a jug and poured water into the bowl.\n\n “Come look for yourself.” I went closer and looked into the bowl. I didn’t see anything. “One moment” He said. He pulled out a very small vial with white liquid in it. \n\n“What is that?” I said.\n\n“This.” He said. “Is my own lin.”\n\n“What?” I said in a slightly raised tone. There were massive cheers downstairs.\n\n“Observe.” He said as he uncorked the vial and poured it into the bowl.\n\n  The white liquid spread until it reached all sides of the bowl. Then Cloak put one finger so it was barely touching the side of the bowl and an image came in. \nIt was of Sofia In at the Middle table downstairs with a huge smirk on her face. \n\n\nThe other hand was being held up by the waitress.\n\n“It seems your Friend won another round.”\n\n“How are you doing that, and who are you?”\n\n“I am simply using my mind to see through my Lin.” Said Cloak. “I can see places nearby, or farther if my will allows me. As to who I am.” Said Cloak removing his hood. \nHe looked no older then I was. \n\n\n“I am the last member of the Omira.”\n\nEND OF CHAPTER FIVE\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("JayasJourney C1", "Sofetios", "         Jaya's\n        Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n(( This is a book I have worked on on and off for years. I've currently lost motivation to continue and hope you all will help bring it back.))\n      Chapter One\n\n A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped. \nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen. \nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll. \nIt had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones. \nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said.\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\nThen looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again.\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow. \nI then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\nAs I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house. \nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.”\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\nAlso, feedback on this story would be appreciated.\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("JayasJourney C2", "Sofetios", "         Jaya's\n        Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n\n         Linink\n\nAs I woke up the next morning I couldn’t help but feel a bit afraid. Linink was one of the most important people in town and he was never really free.\nAlso, why was my Mom so worried last night? I stepped out of bed. Instead of the usual hardwood floor I was used to I was stepped on something lumpy and cold. I looked down and jumped back on my bed. \nThe weapons from last night where on the floor right next to my bed. \n\n“Jaya what’s all the racket?” Said my mom’s voice. It sounded like she was coming to my room. Quickly, I covered the weapons with my blanket.\nLike that would do anything, but it was worth a shot. My mom came in the door and said,\n\n“Jaya why is your blanket on the floor?” \n\n“Bad dream.” I Lied.\nMy mom frowned, bent over, and was about to pick up the blanket. I closed my eyes and cringed from what was about to happen. \n\n“Jaya are you ok?” Said my Mom concerned.\nOpening my eyes I saw my mom had folded the blanket and on the floor was nothing.\n\n“Uh, yea.” I said scratching my head. “I think I just must have hit my head.”\n“Well it’s a good thing your going to see Linink today.” My mom said. “Come on, breakfast is ready.”\nI ate very little breakfast this morning. The taste of it as usual was great, but the stress of what I thought was to come overcame my hunger. After breakfast my mom took me straight to The Adventurers Guild.\nAs I approached the massive building I started to get nervous. My mom opened the doors, led me past staring students, rooms that where full of weapons, and many more things. \n Finally we reached Linink’s Office. The large green door looked inviting enough but as to what was to happen behind it still worried me. \nWithout knocking a voice said, “Come in.” My mom and I entered the triangle shaped room. I saw Linink sitting a table in the middle, but beside the table on both sides where my friends Sofetios and Sofia.\nI relaxed a little. At least they would be here with me. “Jaya, would you please take a seat.” Said Linink coolly.  I took a seat, looked back at my mom, and Linink then said,  “I need to speak to Jaya and his friends alone Madam.” \nMy mom nodded and left the room quietly. Everyone was quite for a bit until I said, \n\n“What am I here for?” \n\n“I’d like to know that too.” Sofetios added.\n\n“Same here.” Said Sofia. After a moment Linink said,\n“We are here to discuss a recent series of events.”\n\n“Like what?” said Sofia. “Other then the Melonko Festival being today all that’s really happened was that Rainstorm last night. \n“Exactly my point” said Linink. “A rainstorm now? In the middle of summer? I just don’t really see that as natural. There is also the Prophecy.”\n\n“You mean that old tale everyone listens to at the festival?” Said Sofetios inquiringly. \n“Just that.” Said Linink seriously. “From what I’ve seen happening in the last two days I’m inferring that it may be coming true.” At this Sofia laughed and said,\n“Like that would happen now. I mean the rain was probably coincidence and it’s not like the weapons have been found.” At this I felt the blood drain from my face. \n“Well from what I heard from Jaya’s Mother last night, I think they may have been found.” Said Linink. Sofia and Sofetios look right at me and Sofetios said, “You didn’t really… I mean you couldn’t have…” \n“He probably didn’t” Said Sofia, Otherwise he would be wearing them right now. It’s not like he would leave them at his house or something if he found them. Right?” I looked slightly down at this comment.\n“The weapons only appear if the owner wants them to.” Said Linink. Sofetios turns to me and said. “Well Jaya? Did you actually find the weapons?” I tell them the whole story of what happened last night and this morning. \nWhen I finish, Sofia is staring at me in disbelief, Sofetios is too, and Linink looks the same as he did before. No one said anything for a while until Linink said,\n\n“Well I guess the prophecy is coming true.” \n“Should we tell everyone?” Said Sofia.\n\n“No.” said Linink. “That would only raise panic. We should just tell whoever really needs to be told then you three set off after the festival.”\n\n“Us three?” I said.\n“Yes.” Said Linink “You know both Sofia and Sofetios pretty well. Except for what each they specialize in.” I didn’t actually know what Linink taught Sofetios and Sofia in the Guild and they had never shown me.\nI gave an odd face to all three of them then Linink said, “To put it bluntly Sofetios is a magician and Sofia is a fighter, in class terms that is.” \n\n“A magician?” I repeated while looking at Sofetios. \n“Intermediate magician.” Said Sofetios. “Sorry but Linink said we couldn’t tell anyone outside the guild.” \n\n“Wait so what can you do?” I said. “Levitate stuff or something?” Sofetios looked at Linink and Linink nodded.\nAll of the sudden everything small in the room started to slowly floated upwards.  I froze and looked around.  Then the things in the air floated down to their original places.\n“You see Jaya, Everything we teach at this guild more or less has to do with Lin.”  Said Linink.\n\n“Lin?” I said curiously.\n“Yes, it is something that is in everything around us.” Said Linink. “Kind of like a fifth element so to speak. Sofetios will be teaching you about this on your travels.”\n“Wait.” I said. “There’s a whole Fifth element?”\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink simply. “Sofetios, Sofia, please get ready for your departure.”\n\n“But sir.” Said Sofetios. “We still-“\n“Come on Sofetios.” Said Sofia as he grabbed Sofetios on the shoulder and had him follow her. When they closed the door, Linink turned to me and Said. \n\n“You have a long journey ahead of you.”\n“Yes sir…” I said tentatively.\n\n“I just need to make sure you really have the weapons.” Said Linink concerned.\n\n“I would sir but I don’t know how to get them to appear.” I said.\n“Just hold your hand as you would your sword and try to will them there.” Said Linink. I did so and in a second a white sword materialized there. It felt warm in my hand. Linink seemed was taken aback a little, so I asked, \n“Sir, why me?” Linink seemed back as himself and said after a moment,\n\n“Because He chose you. At least that’s what the Prophecy sais.” Linink got up and went to his bookshelf. \nHe picked up two books and put them both on the desk. He opened one and the inside of it was hollowed out. All there was, was a semi-clear sphere about an inch long. \nHe handed it to me and said. “This is something I’ve been working on for a long time. Use it well.”  I sheathed the sword and took the sphere and said,\n\n“Sir, what is this?”\n“Don’t you recognize it?” Linink said surprised. “It is object from part of the lore they tell at the Melonko festival. Well, my version of it anyway.”\n\n“I’m sorry sir, I don’t really listen to the tales they tell.” I said a little embaraced.\n“Well then I should probably tell you.” Said Linink. “It is my version of a water sphere. This one I would say holds about 1 week worth of water for 3 people.” Unbelieving, I stared at the sphere.\n“All you need to do is heat it in something and water will come out.”\n\n“Sir?” I said. “What did you mean by ‘your version’?”\n\n“You’ll find out soon enough.” Said Linink. Suddenly there was music outside. “The festival is starting.”\n“Sir, what now?” I said.\n\n“Now, you go enjoy the festival.” Said Linink. “But before you go,” Linink picked up the other book and handed it to me. “This is a book on lore of Edrot. You may want to study it.” \n I turned to leave when Linink said, “and Jaya, two words of advice. First, with the powers you will soon possess, Make sure you use them the right way. \nSecondly, I need you to will away that sword for now. The people in town don’t need to see it.”\n\n“Is that all sir?” I said.\n\n“That’s all” Said Linink.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Jerher's Journal", "Azorella", "*****************************\n\n\n\n This Journal Belongs To:\n             ~Jerher~\n\n\n\n\n\n\n****************************\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Day 1: It was an interesting day to say the least. Ran into a dark elf...\n\nLuckily I was able to find a place to call home for now. Too bad they don't have guards on the wall round the closk. Someo f have got locked out for quite \n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~some time.\nMet some decent company:\nArtimec Camoryn\nAdeline de Servian\nPhaedrus\nand Floragain.\n\nFraid I made a fool of my self last night while shairing a drink with Art and Adeline, its been the first time in a long time \n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~that I had a drink. \n\nDay 2: Started gathering and stockpiling food and supplise for when I move on. I even got a saddle and a few leads for when I get a horse. I will be able to travel much faster that way.\nFound a way into the \n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~c..., well never mind I better not. Don't know who's hands my journal will be in, if I should loose this.\n\nSaw the ever so pleasent High Elves...The captured a Dwarf. That was the first time I ever saw one.\n\nI think it's time to \n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~leave The Fringe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jokers Scum", "Rathrafhir Golldir", "       Jokers Scum\n\nI. This regent is one of the rarest water growing plants there is and is only obtainable at deep sea.It cannot tolerate icy water and can only be found in deep water off desert coasts. It grows thick ball like clumps and is secured to\nthe ocean floor by multiple flowing roots.  A carnivorous plant it entices fish and seabirds into its seemingly docile tangle of plants. Skeletons of small sharks have been seen floating around or in large plants tentacle mass. It is tought the plant\nsecretes large amounts of acid from bulbs that grow on the end of its kelp like tentacles.\n\nII. The tentacles  itself are almost useless except for ensnaring hapless victims that struggle,but is one is calm enough and slow enough to harvest the acid fille\nd blub itself then the lucky individual has natures answer to alchemist fire. The stems that flow from the plant is also useful for such endeavours as rope and string.\n\nIII. When an individual has had the cunning to acquire a bulb of acid from Jokers Scum\nthey have themselves  natures version of Alchemist Fire. It can disfigure one severely but does not melt anything un-organic such as Iron or Gold. The tentacle itself can be used as a medium water regent though and this is its value to an Alchemist.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Timothy McPatt", "~*~Entry 1~*~\n10th, Deep Cold, 1461\n\nTurned in my latest work today! I personally think it will be a bestseller among the other nations!\n\nFishin has been slow and so has smithing. Hope work crops up soon.\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 2~*~\n30th, Deep Cold, 1461\n\nKnox damn it all! Seems that Bubba tracked me down - my brother.\n\nHope he doesn't plan on staying long. I have a life!\n\n... sorta...\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 3~*~\n1st, Malin's Welcome, 1461\n\nToday, I learned the value of friendship. Milo and I fought, and it was fun! But now we have made friends.\n\nYou never know when or where you'll realize something!\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 4~*~\n2nd, Malin Welcome, 1461\n\nWe really showed those pointy eared, heightists who was boss! Milo and I broke in, toppled the Library and retrieved my book!\n\nAfter that, though, we broke in again! This time, our aim was to steal all\nwe could from their homes! We got off with a lot, but Milo was caught as I escaped!\n\nAfter returning home, I left Ivybend to rescue him from the beastly, pointed ears!\n\nI recruited Human members for the S.A.S., or the Spade Attack Squad!\nWe found Milo outside with guards pulling him and questioning him. I stepped into view with a call of valor, challenging all!\n\nThey prepared for battle, and I called upon the S.A.S.! They came from behind me, weapons brandished and armor worn!\nOur foes dropped their weapons and released Milo! With a hug to settle it all, Milo came back to us!\n\nSuch a grand tale to tell at parties, now. Ha!\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 5~*~\n14th, Malin Welcome, '62\n\nRealized it was a new year today. Had a little celebration for it and for our triumph over the Talls!\n\nSongs were written - by me, of course - of that heroic and awe inspiring day! Ha!\nJust hope that the pride and upbeat cheer this created lasts for a long time.\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 6~*~\n24th, Amber Cold, 1462\n\nMilo has done it! We have created a garden of peace outside the Elven capital!\n\nI fear that they will attack or attempt to remove it, being the little murderers they are now! I miss the old elves... but alas.\n-TM\n~*~Entry 7~*~\n25th, Amber Cold,1462\n\nFawking elves! They burned down the Grove in their hatred!\n\nBut do not fret, I got the Flays and Silverblades to guard our grove!\n\nWe were ran out of \nthe Grove by them, but we have decided to build near a place with little to no anger and warmongering!\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 8 ~*~\n11th, Snow Maiden, 1462\n\nCalm day since the fighting with the elves. I think I should make them some armor.\n\nAnywho, Milo is coming over soon, so I cannot write long. Says he has something to tell me.\n-TM\n~*~Entry 9~*~\n12th, Snow Maiden, 1462\n\nDamn it all, Milo! The Elves and Druids are after Milo and I, so we have left to the Silverblade's keep.\n\nMilo lives across from my Forge, so I can make sure he doesn't die. Hopefully Elves are a lot more stupid\nthan we think! If not, then Milo and I still have four traps and cobblestone walls to defend us!\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 10~*~\n24th, Snow Maiden, 1462\n\nRupert is still trying to become Mayor of Ivybend. Fumble is manipulating our systems to try and get his way with Thimble.\n\nI fear a revolt will spark, and Milo and I will head it.\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 11~*~\n25th, Snow Maiden, 1462\n\nShowed a woman named Catrina around Ivybend today! She might have been an elf, but she wasn't a heightist.\n\nGlad to see some people are still calm and collected through these times. She even told me she has a \nsister who is a Dedicant. Feel bad for the lass.\n\nDruids are being slaughtered by the Elves because of affairs. Milo and I doing what we did didn't help much, either. I just hope peace comes.\n\nAlso, fishing is slow. Like, really slow.\n-TM\n~*~Entry 12~*~\n30th,Snow Maiden,1462\n\nWe sit here, sat under the drenched trees as we wait for the Elves to attack the Druids.\n\nI lead the SAS as Captain Timothy McPatt, and I will not lose my men.\n-TM\n~*~Entry 13~*~\n6th, First Seed, 1462\n\nI currently await the coming storm, small battles lighting the field. The Druids have a plan, and I honestly feel it may end the elves.\n\nThis fight is horrid and sad to watch, but I will not let Milo and his lads \nperish at the hands of the corrupt and greedy.\n\nI do not wish to fight, but I will do so to protect the innocent.\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 14~*~\n1st, Sun's Smile, 1462\n\nBeen awhile since I wrote here! A lot has happened!\n\nI met a new lad - Phaedrus - who leads the Elves. He saved my life from a Flay attack at the Grove, and now I like to meet with him at times.\nWe fought some Orcs in Ivybend, but I just ended up beating Milo down.\n\nThimble is also becoming very uptight. I don't want him as Sheriff anymore, or to at least be less... a toad-muncher.\n\n-TM\n~*~Entry 15~*~\n15th, Sun's Smile, 1462\n\nArtimec and Ouity fought today. Artimec lost to Ouity with his amazing skills.\n\nArtimec is still stupid and smelly.\n\n-TM", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Frederick Thyrite", "1st of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================Our group has established a focus point in the southern region of the dwarven mountains. We are currently hunting something that has been plaguing the countryside. No idea as to what it is currently\n\n===================, , but I believe it has been a pack of wolves located somewhere near, as the tundra is quite the location to house wolf packs.\n\nThis scouting should hopefully be successful.\n==================\n5th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================So currently our hunt has shown very little evidence of what beasts actually reside around this area. We have been getting attacked by various bands of cultists. Quite the nuisance I must say. Nothing has-\n===================actually developed apart from a few corpses of animals strewn about the area. We have scavenged them and used them for food, but rather than that. It has become quite... Quiet\n===================\n6th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================Our band grows ever smaller, as our Orcish mercenary has fallen ill to some sort of fever. He awoke with various cuts along his body, with a trail of blood leading towards the rivers, nearby the mountains. He -\n===================claims to not remember anything, but I believe he attacked a beast and nearly died, too afraid to admit that. Perhaps we shall save this orc, or perhaps he shall be our downfall. Only the Creator knows.\n===================\n9th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================We were awoken to a corpse outside our camp, apart from the orc which passed a day before. Our band of four found a wolf corpse, torn apart. It's jaw snapped in two with various bones protruding out of it. -\n===================And it was covered in Frost?! This confuses me, because only the mountains appear to be cold enough to give water, a shape. Well, I am starting to think that something is trying to lure us. There is one thing though. This is the -\n===================creature that we have been hunting for, and we shall capture it and skin it for our reward!\n===================\n11th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================We have found a cavern up to the north of our camp, it being the exit point of a stream which flows into the river below. As we approached it yesterday, it smelt, disgusting. Bones were strewn about the -\n===================entrance and blood stained the nearby stone. I am afraid for the rest of our band that we will not be able to make it, but I have a fair idea of what has been plaguing these mountains. I have only heard of these creatures in legends. -\n===================None I have known to have appeared in Athera. \nI guess it is time to try and test judgement, Creator give me strength, for the one that resides in the mountain is stronger than us all.\n===================-Frederick Thyrite, Leader of the 4th Band of the Green Pawed Hunters.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Contract:", "I swear on Iblees himself, by my name\nCharles Junkly...\n\nI shall return to haunt those whom ever mine these mines... for they were what sought me end. *the page trails off into nothingness*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Pikel Boldshoulder", "\n\n\n      This book will\n     be a journal of\n       my travels\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLeo Oberon\n  Recently I have traveled to a few places just by aimlessly wondering and I have seen a few things. One of these places where far off the Henseti land. I have seen a dead monk covered in the red sands. He has been there for quite some time now however, \nso I did not move the body.\n((X -242 Z -662))\n\nNot far off from the dead monks I found some sort of well with healing water. Since I was fatigued, I did it anyways. The water seemed to have healed me quickly. I came out and felt brand new.\nI was gonna try to take some water, but I had no container.\n((X -31 Z -706))", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Amoss", "Grigor Grandaxe", "\n\n\n\n\n   \n      Journal Of\n        Amoss \nJeffwise sadget - suspects my corruption\n\nJacob Chapel- Believes Grigors Lies\n\nZaviel- Threat to my position\n\nGrigor- Ruined reputations \nAllies-\n\nTuvya- Close Friend and Emperor\n\nMark- Close friend \n\nEraborn- Leader of rangers\n\nFaramith- Noble brother of eraborn\nBalek Irongut- Dwarf and good friend\n\nVjek Grandaxe- Close Friend\n\nName Unknown- Lord and strong ally got me my position!\nAssasinations Required-\n\nZaviel\nGrigor\nJeffwise Sadget\nJacob Chapel\nFaramith Greymane\nYakov\nEdmund", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry", "Artorias Thannius", "17th of Snow's Maiden, 1324\n\nReports from the far away lands of Urguan's hall tell the tale that the dwarves have begun work on a terrible mechanism they call \"The Seal\". While I will not pretend to be\none who has studied the brutish and noisy mechanisms of the dwarves, I can say with utmost certainty that the power of a soul is not something that the physical mechanisms, which the dwarves create, can\n interact with.\n\nIndeed, the notion the dwarves could harness the power of a soul, when we the mages of Rivel find such a thing impossible with eldritch might is a notion that is so absurd some would say that it is even\nlaughable.\n\nI remind you, those of the Purple Circle that the efforts of the mages Torak Hergardul and Franz Astartes, who studied the nature of the soul for their entire productive lives,\nled to no remarkable discoveries and the conclusion that the soul is an intangible creation which can not even be influenced by the hand of the arcane.\n\nIt is therefore that I, Artorias\nThannius, Archmage of the Purple Circle, hereby recommend that Rivel refrain from acting on the impossible notion that dwarves will be able to harness the power of the soul. Should Rivel act on such a rumour, it would\nsimply be heeding the words of fools and madmen.\n-Artorias Thannius", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal N. 6", "Marican Barlg", "My path into the ruins of Dun'Sildur. Day 32\n\nI noticed, that the stone door opened that leads me into some sort of throne room and uncomfortable sleep areas. I also noticed an area with a lot of books, but those are behind unbreakable-\niron fences.\n\nI should sleep here for the night, in front of that giant door. Maybe it will open.\nDay 34.\n\nI woke up and the only exit is sealed. Someone or something closed the stone door.\n\nI have to wait, maybe a new door will open.\nDay 47.\n\nNothing happened, I almost have nothing to eat, I'm hungry and thirsty.\n\nI have to wait.\nDay 142.\n\nThis might be my last writing into the papers. Nothing happened, nothing, nothing, nothing at all, nothing. Everything ended here, nothing happened, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing...\nKknotos Kknotos Kknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\nKknotos Kknotos\n\nKnotos is everywhere.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 1", "Assa'rai", "My home is almost complete. As I sit here writing below the room masked as the bottom floor I think to myself it might be to my benefit to record what I am thinking right now.\n\nThis bookcase has a lock on it based on password, I have decided it would\nbe fitting to make said password 'elly'\n\nPerhaps when I die she will find this, and perhaps she will guess the password. I will leave hints.\n\n\n>--->\nMy mind is a mess. I debated even telling her of my peril but eventually I caved and decided I must.\n\nI still am absolutely terrified that... that part of myself that came out that night will return. Terrified that I will take it further than\nI hope.\n\nI am terrified of becoming a Monster. Each step I take seems to be on a fine line that at any time can leave me tumbling off into an inescapable abyss to leave me to die, falling, cold, and alone.\nNow that she knows I honestly didn't expect her to react well at all. Half of me wanted her to scream and either kill me for her and her mate's safety on the spot or never speak to me again.\n\nI wouldn't be able to harm her that way.\nRather it seems the terrifyingly opposite thing has happened - she almost considered offering herself willingly to my ritual so that I may live.\n\nMy heart hurts. The fact she would even consider such makes me both overwhelmingly happy and\nat the same time unbearably sad. My time is so limited, her fate is already chosen but... I cannot stay away. I know there is only pain in my future but I cannot stay away.\n\nShe is a flame that will burn me if I step too close but I have\nalready learned how to ignore the pain.\n\nBut oh do I hurt.\n\n\n\nPerhaps it is her sudden inavailbility that has made her seem so much more beautiful.\nTime is short, I hope to make my emotions clear and... perhaps, if in pity or perhaps another emotion, she might respond if only for a short time. One night. Even just waking to see her face in the morning would be enough, to be able to hold her and feel \nher warmth for a single night.\n\nWriting is helping to calm my mind significantly. The usual storm feels as if it is abating, calming into a light rain that could be a harbinger of times to come. Be they good or bad.\nOnly time may tell I suppose, but I hope that time is a storyteller that remains concise for if not I fear I will be teased by an early ending to my tale - never to know my true destiny.\nI have begun a catalog of all of my musings beneath my basement. I will continue to add to it to create a understandable timeline of my emotions and thoughts. Within this location there should also be another tome which is...\nless explanatory.\n\nShould Eilistrae be reading this I emplore you to ignore every word in that book. I would have burned it if I believed that those words would not burn into my mind with the destruction of the casing they are held prisoner in.\nYou see, that book was made the night after the ball. The same night I took my quest to learn Fi'hiiran'tanya. I took the necklace I gave you and in a fit of rage and fury decided to just cast it into a chest at your footstep along with a note\nto basically attempt to spitefully break your heart, in hopes that I would somehow benefit from it. Before you awoke that morning I realized my mistakes and removed the box, deciding to speak to you personally instead of jumping to conclusions.\nI hope the words burned into that accursed tome do not scar your mental image of me for they were made out of spite, jealousy, intoxication, and rage.\n\nAnd with this I wrap up my thoughts, putting my mind onto a page.\nOr rather in this case writing with blood, for there is no other substance this ink could be that it would cause me such pain to admit to these words.\n\nI love you Eilistrae,\n- Assa'rai\n\n7th of Snow's Maiden,\n1497", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 2", "Assa'rai", "I feel... light. Almost as if I should be careful to tie myself down or I might flatten against the roof from forgetting myself.\n\nGiddy. Happy. Joyious. \n\nIt... also comes with... not a little bit of confusion. Or guilt.\nLet me start from the beginning since so much has happened since the start. I cannot believe how much has changed in two elven days.\n\nA Mali'ame girl sleeps softly next to me as I write this. She's beautiful. I love her.\nHer name is Charis, and I might start calling her Cherie.\n\nI first met her when Eilistrae vanished. I don't know where she went but I have even now a bad feeling within my gut that tells me whatever her reason for vanishing was it... was not good\nPerhaps it was my stupidity. Perhaps... she realized finally that I was a danger to her. To everyone.\n\nI still am. I don't know what I will tell Charis, but... I... I can't let her heart break like mine has. I will fix this problem without involving her.\nAnyway, I met Charis within Cerulin when she first arrived within the City. I thought nothing of it, really, and she asked for where she could find a home. I pointed her to the Chancellor which was recently radified if she wanted it and she kindly thanked\nme. I thought nothing of it but eventually we had a bit more of a conversation, leading us to become friends. I enjoyed her company, she was funny and enjoyed being around me (a rarity with my sharp tongue, I assure you.) so I was rather happy.\nWe drank tea together in the Tavern one night and talked, and I came to enjoy her company even more. I learned how to make tea and that she loves sugar in her tea. A lot of it.\n\nWe talked over the next day for a bit and eventually the topic of housing\ncame up. Duncan told me to demand a home within Cerulin due to my self-proclaimed 'Prison Cell' of a home but I turned it down, saying that Charis was better suited to getting a home before I was. Eventually she said that she would go get a home but if \nI'd like I could room with her. It was... an offer I couldn't refuse because at this time I, perhaps, already was falling so hard for her. The thought of being able to be near more often was appealing, to say the least.\nIt didn't take me long however to realize that she had a pressing issue with housing, having to sleep outside alone in the cold.  As I slowly began to notice it I was appauled that she was having to live in such a way and offhandedly mentioned\nthat she could, if she enjoyed tight, freezing spaces stay in my home for the meanwhile as I wasn't going to use it for much...\n\nDid I mention I love her yet? I think I did but I was just thinking it again so I have to make sure it's written.\nWhen we got to my home for the first night she explored around the cave shortly before going downstairs and crawling into the bed. She was so concerned that I wouldn't be able to find a place sleep that she asked me to sleep with her, and I spent that\nnight holding her in my arms. It's a night I will remember for the rest of my life as I laid there holding her small and lovely form, her soft idle breathing warming my collarbone, her whole form pressed against me from the sheer lack of room...\nIt wasn't sexual in any way but my heart warmed to her that night in a way that I don't believe it has to any other. She's beautiful when she's asleep.\n\nThe next morning when I woke up she was already out and about, having slipped\nfrom my grasp sometime before conciousness entered into my head. Probably because it took me a while to finally sleep due to staring at her for so long.\n\nThat next day was also filled with firsts, with some adventure.\nShe grew bored that afternoon and even though I had warned her from strange paladins who want to take innocent females into the woods and 'Slay the Dragon' she still, when she met the Paladin man who shouted 'ADVENTURE' at the top of his lungs\nshe couldn't resist the temptation of going on journey with him. I followed behind for a little while but I ended up getting a letter that ate at my concious to not attend to - Earlier that morning I had met a nice little Mali'ker child by the name of\nInxena. I saw to her care and Dak'ir asked me to come back to the city in order to deal with her. Little did I know Charis and her paladin had gone off even further on their quest. I don't know what she did with him (and I don't believe... she did...\nanything with him... probably...) and something occured during that timeframe that upset her. I didn't even notice it until later after a whole ordeal of getting dye in my hair (children playing with dye...) and someone attempting to 'reproduce' with her\nin the most sexual of meanings (which boiled my blood, I would have murdered the Mali' if he had so much as touched her). While I was serving drinks at the bar she broke down without warning, beginning to weep in such a way that I felt like my heart was\ngoing to be torn apart. I drew to her side and she wept openly on me. Several humans entered the bar at this time and to avoid making a scene I left silently with her, taking her to the Beach thinking the sound of the waves would calm her.\nI did not expect it when she pushed me down, I dropped my coat (I was almost shirtless to my chagrin.), and she landed ontop of me, where she cried into me. We remained that way for a little while with my hand exploring her soft hair, which I know she\nfinds comfort in. Eventually I attempted to comfort her further, wiping her tears away while planting a kiss upon her temple. As this progressed eventually her lips met mine and in that moment I knew it for the first time:\n\nI love her so much.\nShe would later lead me home where we would embrace and enjoy each other's warmth in sleep.\n\nThat was yesterday, after I had started this journal. I decided to show her what I had written because... the fact I was writing these\nin secret had as of late plagued my conciousness. She smiled at the first part... creator I love her smile... but eventually she saw what I had written about Eilistrae and my... problem. I still can't explain to her the nature of my issue,\neven though part of me just wishes to break down and tell her everything right there and let her know what's wrong. Part of me wants to just curl up in her arms and let her hold me, broken and foolish... but I cannot. I... don't know how she will react.\nShe... might demand I use her. I... couldn't. I can't. If I heard those words leave her lips I might actually break the last stands of my sanity. She is my anchor, my reasoning for moving forward, she is my reason...\n\nShe is the reason I will live. I must\nlive. There is no other solution, there is no other method, there is no other compromise.\n\nThere will be a solution, and I will find it for her sake.\n\nAfter she read my journal we shared a tender moment, locked in each other's\nembrace where I finally confessed in full what I had yet to tell her;\n\nThat I loved her. I've written it so much in here, and these pages are my lifesblood. My thoughts are trapped within this tome so that they may be rendered\nuseful.\n\nShe'll probably read this. I'm not going to keep all of my books secret from her anymore, so she will absolutely read this.\n\nCharis, this note is specifically for you. If someone else would read\nthis tome I don't know what they would think but at this stage I am beyond caring.\n\nI know what you've read will concern you, and worry you. My heart breaks that I know this, but I promise Cherie it'll be fine. \nI am in danger. I will not lie to you that much, but the danger is not immedient nor is is unpreventable. It is a complicated problem, method of logic that I must work through and figure out from start to finish. I am good at logic puzzles, and the\nsolution is slowly unfolding before me. I can almost see the ending even now as I write this.\n\nWhen I die it will be in your arms of old age, having lived a long and happy life. This is my promise, and I have not lied to you yet.\nI will never lie to you.\n\n\nThese words are my Lifesblood and may they never escape this prison of a tome.\n\n- Assa'rai the Nameless,\n3rd of The Amber Cold, 1497", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 3", "Assa'rai", "I might be obsessed.\n\nI don't know what obsession is... or well, I should rephrase that. I write of it all the time, it is a wonderful tool for character development.\n\nI, personally, have never experienced it.\nI must say this puts a whole new light onto things. I feel as if before I have simply assumed obsession to be the simple act of desire, be it either... of a carnal nature or for something else.\n\nI don't describe my obsession as carnal, although\nsomeone other than myself might.\n\nI am obsessed with Charis in ways that I honestly didn't know were possible. My emotions are so conflicting, I imagined when you were dating you would find a suitable mate with some flaws\nthat you would have to simply ignore or move on, that you would have to work with both the bad and the good.\n\nI braced myself for this reality. I was mistaken.\n\nAt first I assumed there was something about Charis\nthat I simply did not know yet and when we reached that bridge I was going to welcome her into my arms without judgment or remorse, and we would work it through.\n\nI made a mistake however...\nShe has no flaw in my eyes. She is beautiful, sweet, charming, funny, smart, and any other positive adjective.\n\nWe... I blush even as I write this, I can't help it. Remembering that night might always make me blush it feels like.\nI... mentioned to her late one night after losing myself to her lips that we might end up taking it 'too far'. It was something of a joke to play toward the future for when she was more ready but she shocked me utterly when she decided that she \nbelieved herself ready then and wanted to go through with it. I almost wasn't able to do it at all from my sheer shock but... eventually the night went on and I learned more about her than I had known before.\nThe dress she wears really does not do her justice I feel, there is a certain aspect of her beauty that cannot be captured or represented through the clothing she wears.\n\nI'll save the... details for my own mind, and spare\nthe page of such thoughts. Needless to say my thoughts on her being beautiful were only reinforced thoroughly that night.\n\nIt was her first as it was mine. Later after I woke up I tended to the mess on the sheets, taking them out to burn for the time\nbeing, no use in attempting to save them I reasoned. I replaced them with some rather nice ones I managed to gather together.\n\nEven still the warmth of that night makes me shiver, it's still hard for me to believe that I had reached\nthe apex of my happiness while above the world cried in sorrow... the irony is not lost on me.\n\nI fear for us now but I will make certain that at the very least she remains safe. The Human King died on footsteps of the Mali'aheral library\nand the whole of humanity cried out in sorrow, raising their weapons to retort.\n\nAn Eye for an Eye, as they say. Humanity even now moves as a massive hulking beast of death with the pure purpose of killing anything with Mali' Blood.\nWe are in danger, technically, but it is still the greatest time of my life.\n\nCherie is still with me, and she's even more beautiful than before. \n\nI plan on taking her to a romantic mountain I had found while looking\nfor locations. It's very pretty and there are some nice hidden and close corners that I might be able to sneak a taste of her lips in.\n\nCreator, even now my mind turns back to my obsession. I might as well embrace it, at the very least I take\ncomfort that my obsession is with Charis. I have no complaints to whichever divine cursed or blessed me, for this is a fate I am willing to accept; Living with Charis in my arms.\n\nI am considering proposing.\n[!] The ink is newer [!]\n\nI am... elated. I feel that even though I stand here upon this ground it is merely an illusion of reality - In the truth of it I am soaring higher than any bird can reach. I feel as if I can gaze down from where I stand\nand see the Aenguls in their domains tending to the world, that if they might look up they might see a single speck high, high, ever so high in the sky.\n\nMy heart bursts with joy. I said I might propose to her... I never thought she would be the\none who brought it out of me. I expected to wait another week or so, it feels all so sudden... but within the mountain that we found our solace together in she told me she wished to live the rest of her life with me. Bewildered and absolutely confused I\nthought that she had beaten me to the punch with my proposal and in a strange twist of the norm she was the one asking to marry me.\n\nWhen I asked her this she pulled away from me, muttering \"Guys are the ones who propose...\"\nin a cross manner which caused me to begin to laugh not at her or even the situation but at myself, having believed she was the one asking me to marry her. It gave me the courage I needed and I summoned it all together in that moment.\nI asked Charis Alyssum to be my wife.\n\nWe sat in that state for a little bit, her soft breathing worrying me because I thought she was going to feint from the way it sounded. I had grabbed her by the waist and stood behind her, waiting for\nthe response to my request.\n\nShe said yes and in that moment I felt as if I could die by some heavenly spear and still be too happy to notice my lifes-blood spilling. I spun her around and embraced her without thinking,\nthe taste of her lips on mine and our shared passion mixed in that moment to create what can only be described as pure joy. It was then in that moment that I noticed that something touching my face was wet, and I pulled back out of realization that\nCherie was crying. My stomach bottomed out as I tried to reason why she would be crying... was something wrong? Was there something that she was going to tell me that ment we could not marry? Was there someone else? She said yes, why was she crying.\nI didn't understand it and I began to panic, the sound rimming my voice and I have no doubt I looked wild. My greatest fear was that she learned what my situation was through finding my journals and told me she wouldn't be with me if I didn't fix it.\nThat scared me to my very bones.\n\n\n\nThe relief that entered me at the moment she wiped her tears away with a smile and said it was joy is something that if I was able to transcribe on paper I would\nbe a wealthy Mali.\n\nI do not know what our plans are for the future. I need to speak with her about it all... what it means, when we'll do it, the whole... name situation. I have in the back of my head some concern as well built off of the fact that\nsome of the Mali'ker may not like the concept of our union.\n\nIt is a trival issue however. If the case presents itself where the only options are to leave Charis or to leave Ker'nor I would not hesitate to seperate myself from the population.\nI shall choose Charis every single time.\n\nI hope she doesn't tire of me too soon, I know married couples start off at a peak before dipping low after discovering... more about their mate... . . .\nShe knows of the mark. I made a mistake, there's no way she hasn't at the very least felt it when we... erm... what's the best way to write it without... Ah, yes; 'Make Love'. What a term... regardless, why hasn't she said anything about it yet?\nAh... shit.\n\nI can't keep it secret from her anymore if we are to wed what my problems are. I wish she had confonted me about it to be frank... although that's not her nature. No, she's... too sweet. I still am in disbelief that she both trusts me \nwhole-heartedly but at the same time shares the maddening love I have for her.\n\nI will... tell her of my deal. I have to. My heart hurts to have to do such a thing but I absolutely cannot keep such a thing secret from her if... we are to remain together\nfor... well, eternity.\n\nI don't know how she'll react. She won't hate me, I'm positive... although hating me is not a bad outcome. What terrifies me to the very core actually is that she may try to offer herself for the ritual. This would be... hopefully \na mere thought that a simple and firm 'no' will stop.\n\nI fear however that she may become so afraid for my sake that she will do something against her nature... either plot behind my back or seek help from sources that\nmay end up causing a problem... This is why I'm so cautious about telling her. I can see the love in her eyes and I fear that she will do anything, anything at all to keep me alive... be it at the cost of her own health and safety.\nIt is something I must work through however. It's not a problem that can be solved on my own and I cannot hold secrets from my betrothed.\n\nWe will work it out, together.\nThis ink is my lifesblood, these pages are the prison of my thought. May they never be freed.\n\n- Assa'rai, soon to be married,\n\n\n13th of The Amber Cold, 1498", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 4", "Assa'rai Rai'ari", "Rai'ari.\n\nWhat a strange name. I couldn't love it more if I tried, really; I never thought I would be called such.\n\nAssa'rai Rai'ari. Even writing it out now gives me shivers as I look upon it - a permanant and lasting\nmark Cherie has left upon me. It will never fade and upon my gravestone it shall read 'Assa'rai Rai'ari'.\n\nI'm pretty sure she chose it just so she could call me 'Rai Rai' although I don't mind, I'm actually rather fond of the name.\nRai'ari is a rather simple combination of Assa'\"rai\" and Ch\"ari\"s - she came up with it late one night when we were speaking in the bed and I thought it was perfect.\n\nWe aren't married yet technically but I don't think she\ncares, and Cherie is my guiding light; Whatever she says is what I shall do. If she says we are wed already then I am afraid we are wed already.\n\nShe has given me some interesting experiences as of late.\nDuring one of our nights she decided to switch places with me opting to stay on top.. It was rather thrilling, to be frank.\n\nShe seems to continue to surprise me in ways I thought not even possible, truly. I believe this is most likely due to my\ninexperience with not just bedding but love in general.\n\nI am, however, more than happy to let Cherie teach me.\n\nArg... Even as I write this my head hurts so much. Cherie sleeps softly below in the bedroom... oh yes,\nWe moved into Cerulin at long last! It was quite an experience and I'm glad to get Cherie out of the cold cave home I was living in. I worked hard to set up our current bedroom to be... suitable to our nightly desires. She seems comfortable with\nthe natural theme which eases my heart. She seems to almost come alive, a spring in her step, now that we've finally moved to a place suitable for a beautiful and young Mali'ame such as Cherie. \n\nThe home is built for\ntwo and on the very front it writes in Cherie's very pretty handwriting \"Rai'ari\", a marking that this home is shared by a young Mali'ker and Mali'ame madly in love.\n\nI asked her further details about the wedding and she said she wanted\nto do it upon the mountain I took her too recently, although she hadn't quite started on her dress yet. It's fine and I don't mind if she takes her time, I know she'll be beautiful no matter what she wears. I only hope that next to that brilliant sun of \nbeauty that is Cherie I might be noticable enough that I am not merely forgotten by the fates and the marriage simply does not occur.\n\nUrg... There's the pain again. I can't use my left hand at all right now; I have a terrible \nbruising pain on my left shoulder from dislocating it.\n\nLast night Cherie decided to go to the Tavern - as of late she's been speaking to Katari again attempting to mend their relationship. They seem to be doing well\nand I don't mind. I've had thoughts of jealousy, attempting to keep her all to myself and occupy every minute of her day so she could never leave me but I've made too many mistakes due to stupid masculine emotions to make that mistake once more.\nI am jealous of her beauty and I always will be, but I won't try to supress her wild and young spirit.\n\nAnyhow, She was speaking with Katari and he offered her a drink while I was watching. A large, heavy paladin in golden armor\nfor some reason sat himself upon the table they were at and to my bewilderment Cherie decided to take a drink. The result was to be expected... she's really cute when she's drunk, actually. She gets really silly and this deep red blush comes to her cheeks\nthe slur in her words just making her already cute voice just unbearable.\n\nRegardless, she doesn't take drink well. Nearly instantly after taking a sip her ears shot up and she began to wobble. I, already standing up from when she grasped the\nbottle, saw her about to fall I believed and dove to catch her, utterly scared to my soul that she would get hurt. I did not notice that at the same time Katari had decided to dispose of the Paladin on their table by dropping him off onto the floor...\nwhere I was walking.\n\nHe rammed into my shoulder and sent by face into a wall where everything went dark.\n\nI still remember hearing Cherie's voice throughout the time of my darkness and it warmed my soul, even if I don't\nremember exactly what she was saying. I woke later staring at a pool of cold water, hair a wet and soaked mess with my shoulder in extreme pain from being relocated.\n\nCherie... Have I written I love her so much it hurts? She tears into my soul\nthat is so hardened and finds my weakness, able to topple my inner goliath with nothing but a smile. It's a marvelous feat... she helped me walk home in the pain even though she could barely carry me. I can never thank her enough for everything she has\ndone for me. The warmth of our bodies as we slept (just slept) together last night still permeates through me even as I write.\n\nShe's so beautiful, warm, full of energy, young, and... she's my wife. How am I so lucky?\nThe Mali'ker aren't happy with my decision I don't believe. They are upset at me for not following hard to worship of the ancestors and even more so for taking a mate that does not worship them.\n\nI don't care. I am not going to force\nCherie to worship something I don't have faith in, the result would just be awkwardness and I don't believe I can tame that wild fire of hers in such a manner to be able to tell her what she should do.\n\nIf I must be seperate from the Mali'ker\nthen so be it; I will take the warmth between my beloved's arms over the stone caves of Ker'nor any day.\n\nCherie is my other half and without her I would be lost, I am afraid.\n\nWell...\nI believe that's the wrong thing to say. I am already lost; so lost in love I don't know forward from backward.\n\nWithout Cherie I would succumb to my inner doubts and thoughts, stewing upon my own distaste for everything\nShe brings out the best of me. She gets the best of me and I will continue to give her my best until the day I part ways with this world.\n\nUntil I die,\n\nAssa'rai Rai'ari\n2nd of the Grand Harvest, 1499", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 5", "Assa'rai Rai'ari", "My head is in a storm.\n\nThat's the theme this time. A storm. A bad storm... I write this now with Cherie softly sleeping in my arms. Her soft and gentle breaths warm my bare palms as I've removed my gloves so that there will be no border between\nmy skin and hers. She may awaken during this but... she seems content. She's still so cute when she's sleeping, I could just start kissing her and I don't think I would be able to stop. I must resist the temptation I'm afraid, even if it's hard. If she\nneeds to sleep on me then so be it.\n\nHowever, I don't feel I've earned the right to hold her like this. I still feel incapable of doing anything, a man who can't even defend what he loves... what right do I have to hold her? I detest combat.\nI wish that this world worked as simple as 'leave us alone' to get people to leave. It does not... I don't want to change. I'm afraid of change... If I grow grizzled and mean spirited due to conflict will Cherie still love me? If I change, will... will\nI still be Assa'rai?\n\nI don't know. People can change but... what happens if they change too much? Friends leave... divorces, deaths... it all comes from change. So I fear it, and it sends me into fits during the night.\nBecause I know I must change. I write... and I will try to still write... but I am a pure writer. I cannot defend what I love... I realized this when Cherie got hurt because of me.\n\nShe stepped out from our usual seat in the Red Rose tavern that day to\nlook around a bit and during that time it was quite crowded. A little boy was running around when a pair of large Uruks walked into the tavern.\n\nWhat happened next was generally the expected outcome. They marched over, grabbed the kid and\nthen turned to me. One drew out a weapon and said 'Come with me', his point clear if I did not. I stood up and resigned myself to my fate assuming Cherie would remain upstairs and out of harms way.\n\nLife isn't a book. I learned it then\nwhen she suddenly came down the stairs. She flung herself into the Uruk with the club out of fear for my safety and my entire world froze for a single second to watch what was about to happen.\n\nThe Uruk reared around and blindly\nswung his club, bashing into Cherie and sending her to the floor hard.\n\nMy breath caught and if I wasn't as furious as I was in that single moment I would have probably broken down into tears. She took that blow for me... because\nI didn't warn her. I didn't say anything, I just watched it happen like a cock-sure fool.\n[!] This particular page seems to be oddly blotched where it seems to have gotten wet. [!]\nI punched the orc and nearly started a fight, eventually bartering Cherie\n-'s and my freedom.\n\nBut I couldn't stop it. Cherie had a terrible bruise on her arm and almost broke it. I couldn't stop it. I just sat there. She got hurt and... if there was someone else who was her lover he would be able to stop them.\nI couldn't. I don't deserve her, I can't defend her, I can't. I couldn't.\n[!]The rest of the page is too blotched with what seems to be some form of liquid to be legible. Eventually it tapers out, starting again with new ink as if starting from a later\nTime [!]\n\nI have... resolved to find a method to defend Cherie in the future. I looked for a solution that allowed us to be together even if I was undergoing combat training and I believe, after speaking with her, that I shall\npursue the path of a Paladin of a holy order. Cherie herself is training to be a cleric and I don't doubt she will be an amazing Cleric. She's so soft and sweet, tender hearted and forgiving... I wouldn't be surprised if just her touch alone\nwithout any Divine assistance could heal a man mortally wounded. Any who might gaze at her visage before slipping into eternal sleep would finally do so with a smile on their face, heart warmed by the cute features of Cherie.\nSo she shall walk that road and I shall walk mine beside her. When it is done... I will either be strong enough to be able to hold her forever without letting anyone harm her or... I will be closer to that stage. It might take more effort than just\ntraining as a Paladin.\n\nI met with Eilistrae last night... we caught up a bit. It hurts to see her still with that druid but... I suppose there's nothing I should be complaining about. I have my wonderful and sweet mate Cherie and I wouldn't\ntrade her for the world. She is my pillar even if she doesn't know it or think she is strong enough to hold me. Whenever I feel desolate her face seems to always come back... that night on the beach when she told me she forgave me for my sin...\nthat night comes back to me every time. I wept into her like a broken child that night, I wept out all of my pain, all of my sorrow, and all of my jealousy. I pushed it all out and leaned upon her... and she held fast.\nShe's so strong it's unbearable. To those who do not know her she seems weak-willed and an easy target. Someone whom they can court for a week and be through with it.\n\nShe isn't though. She just loves everyone so much... \nIt's a love that has been scorned and rejected. It's a love that has been tested and tried... her childhood friends have turned on her, she's alone in this world without anyone to talk to... and she still loves people.\nShe's so strong it makes my soul weep with tears of pain when I see her putting on a strong face to hide the pain. I weep when she hurts because I know what it's like to be scorned but I can't possibly shoulder her pain for her.\nI will give her a place where she can rest, I will whisper sweet nothings to her when she is troubled, I will hold her when she feels cold, and I will sleep with her so she feels calm.\n\nBut to me, she is like my anchor in this storm.\nShe's a lighthouse to all but to me... My little dingy boat is latched to it as a storm of my own mind attempts to rip me from her. I see the light and I weep; It's so beautiful after all you've seen for months is nothing but rolling seas and black skies.\nTo me she isn't simply a lighthouse; She is the entire world. I look upon her and everything simply vanishes. Time stands still at her beauty and the sea rolls into non-existence.\n\nThis is what she serves to me and so I cling to her,\nI follow her about and let her shine as she will. I don't tug her along and instead let her lead the way unless she gets lost or occasionally turns her beautiful gaze to me and asks me to lead.\n\nThis however can't... remain this way\nforever. I follow her and I will do so, but I must... learn to be stronger than I am so that instead of being a pillow she can cry into I can be a pillar that she can lean on. I am... weak willed, physically weak, and I have been broken.\nSo I will pursue the path to strength. Until then I will hold Cherie in my arms and let the world slip away, and after I will hold her in my arms and the world will truly vanish for in those moments nothing shall seperate us.\nI'm so nervous right now, however... A pit sits in the bottom of my stomach; Not for the fear of being weak but for what approaches. I believe Cherie and I will be wedding this night and... Joy has put butterflies in my stomach just thinking\nabout it. It's so new... so... dangerous. It's exciting. I hand-made my attire and I can't wait to see Cherie in whatever dress she has managed to get her hands on. The sheer thought of her in a wedding gown gives me shivers of pleasure, \nI hope she will like what I have made thusfar. I'm working on something to give to her as a token since I didn't use a ring... I perhaps have an idea. Time will tell, really. I haven't given her anything yet because I'm afraid that anything less than what\nshe can hold on her at all times won't due; She'll try to carry it I fear. So something she can wear on her is the best but... anything less than perfect I would feel ashamed to give her. She would accept it but... No, it must be perfect.\n[!] A drawing seems to have made it's way onto the page, Assa'rai seeming to have either gotten bored of writing (unlikely) or had a mental image so strong he felt he had to draw it (more likely), It depicts a tall Dark Elf who is most likely himself\ndressed in a suit, swinging a small feminine feature in a wedding dress lightly off of her feet, her arms wrapped around his neck as their lips seem to meet, both of their ears perked up with their eyes closed. Assa'rai seems to have a silly grin on while\nkissing her.\n\nAt the bottom of the image in curly script a line is written to caption the Image.\n\n\n\"Assa'rai ♡ Charis\"\n\n10th of The Deep Cold, 1499", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 6", "Assa'rai Rai'ari", "Blood has quite a bit of symbolism. Dark magic users are known to use it for power, to others it's a sign of injury. The few authors that exist in this world have a variety of ideas for what it represents.\n\nUntil a few nights ago\nI valued blood with little more than a mild distaste and desire to not have to work with.\n\nIt's funny how a single night can change you. It's happened to me three times now. One night.. less than twelve hours. It's all it takes for my life to change\nentirely. I wonder if it's the same for others? I often wonder that; Does my sentience translate to others? Are they sentient as I am? Or is their sentience an illusion? I don't know, and this isn't the place to wonder I suppose.\nThe first night that my life changed it was with a lonely necklace in my hand with a broken heart, standing in a ballroom full of people yet entirely empty.\n\nThat was the first of three.\nThe Second night my life changed I was standing in a room with a soft waterfall with the love of my life. Within that room I worked up the courage, as spineless as I am, to propose to her.\n\nThis was the second of three.\nThe Third night that changed me was recently. I hope I don't have any nights like that again. I don't want to change any more, I want to continue with the path I'm on and keep it steady without veering.\nThis Third night I left my wife alone in bed, something I deeply regret even to this day, and I began to pour all of my thoughts into a log. When I returned, she had gone. Where she had gone... I had an idea but I didn't want to endorse it.\nI tried to follow her to no avail. I lost her, and for that night I knew that it was my fault. With this in my mind I could not sleep, I could not drink, I could not eat. I tried to distract myself with conversation only to fail. I tried to write only to\nfail. I tried everything and eventually it was too much. On the verge of my sanity fully breaking before dawn came I gathered a bow from Tristin, asked him how to use it, and then beat myself bloody.\n\nSomething broke that night. I don't know what it is\nyet. It's like waking up to a crashing sound within your home and not being able to find it, only to uncover it weeks later.\n\nI don't know what has changed, I just know that something has. I value her even more now, even though such\nshould not be possible considering my previous state.\n\nI'll remember the morning waking up with her gently holding my bloody hands for the rest of my life, as much as I'll remember our wedding for the rest of my life.\nIn that moment I fell in love with her again, like I do every morning and every night, but in this strange and changed world I was certain of nothing. I had considered leaving her for the sake of her saftey the night before... but in that moment I knew\nI wouldn't be able to speak those words if I even tried.\n\nWe might still be on rocky ground. I don't know, we have shared an intimate moment since then but even still I find myself uncertain that we're truly through the clear.\nShe made a comment that still bears with me because of how much I hate it's truth;\n\nShe said to me \"We keep hurting each other.\"\n\nThose words hurt, they hurt then and even as I bode on them\nI know they hurt more even now. They hurt because she is the source of my emotion, should she be happy then I am happy. Should she be sad then I am sad and in order to fix it I must make her happy.\n\nSo when she says that\nwe're hurting each other it's amplified onto me even more by the fact that seeing her in pain is infinitatly worse than my pain.\n\nI don't intend to hurt her again. I will tell her however if I'm cross with her, but if she seems to begin to \nhurt from my words I will quit pushing. She's the love of my life and I will do anything and everything for her.\n\nAnd so I've changed. I don't know how, but I do know why. I embrace it, but I must make certain I am changing for the better.\nWhat I do know however is I won't be leaving her side any night she needs comfort like that again.\n\nBeing cold and alone is a worse fate than death, I believe.\n\n- Assa'rai Rai'ari\n\n\n- 13th of The Deep Cold, 1500\n\n\n[!] Oddly enough, several pages exist after the dating. They're all blank except for one which in the very middle a single word is written[!]\n\"Sorry\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 7", "Assa'rai Rai'ari", "In these bodies we will live,\nIn these bodies we will die,\nWhere you invest your love,\nYou invest your life.\n\nI don't understand. I'm afraid I might never understand, and it scares me.\nI love Cherie so much but I don't know what's wrong. She won't tell me. She's gotten so defensive. What's wrong? I've cried into her so many times but she refuses to lean on me at all. She started attacking me like a cornered animal, I don't know\nwhat I should feel. My heart yearns for her so much but she doesn't want to talk to me. I'm so worried I can barely eat even now; my stomache is sick at the thought that Cherie has a problem... a bad one. She has a really bad problem but\nit hurts her to talk about. I don't understand and I don't understand... I'm panicing here, I can barely write straight.\n\nShe told me she didn't want to see me. I don't understand. Why? Why? Why?\nI want to be strong and I try to be strong but when I try my heart gets stabbed over and over and over again. It's so hard, why is it so hard?\n\nI want to hold her, I really want to hold her and I want to feel her\nbeautiful breath on my shoulder. I want her thoughts to pour from her perfect lips and I want to feel her... become mortal.\n\nShe's trying so hard and I see it now. I feel like shit because I haven't seen her pain until now and... I think... I know\nwhy she said she didn't want to see me. I fucked up. I fucked up so much. Yesterday she was in such a sad mood and when I took her around and she didn't lighten up I... I said some things and then she started smiling that smile. I got frustrated... I\nthink she opened up to me and I was too fucking stupid to realize it. In the moment I should have been the strongest I was my weakest. Why...? \nI tried redeeming myself. I wanted her to open up to me again so I could prove to her I wouldn't\nfuck up again but instead I just hurt her. Why do I have to keep hurting her? I just want her to lean on me... I want to feel her next to me, really.\n\nI'm so concerned. I don't know where she went but I don't think it was good.\nI don't think she went to train with the clerics and... She told me today something that probably pushed her away when I got jaded. I didn't want to push her away but... she treated our marriage like it wasn't special. I don't know... I love her and I vow\n-ed to be with her forever. I don't mind her going off with her big brother a whole lot and other men because I thought she valued my bond as much as I valued it.\n\nShe... said she didn't. I don't know. I CAN'T HATE HER BUT IT STILL HURTS?\nShe has a problem and I have a problem and we're just two fucked up people in a world that's too cold for us. \nWhat is the emotion when you feel like you should be crying but tears won't come? I don't know if there's a name for it. I don't know if\nthat makes me strong or... weaker than I was before.\n\nWhat's wrong with my beautiful Cherie? Why does she hurt so much? I stare at her and when I see that same smile I now know is fake it's like someone is slowly\npressing a dagger into my chest, cutting off my life and letting it seep out. I feel completely powerless. I want to hold her.. but I feel like I've lost the right to even touch her. Will she leave me? I'm so scared she'll leave me. But I've revoked my\nright to her by fucking up, how can I even be her husband when I can't even see what I'm suppose to do? Why must I be the weaker of us... I end up leaning on her so much and mistaking her continual happiness for strength when in reality it's been\nsome fucked up way of coping with something? She's just as broken as me and it makes me hurt so much to think that.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI can't think of anything else to write.\n\nI've just blanked.\n\nI only know I need to say one thing and one thing only if it means anything in this world, if I should die tomorrow at the very least it will be here;\n\n\n\n\nI'm sorry Charis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 8", "Assa'rai Rai'ari", "I've got a wide smile on my face. I don't know, I'm so happy at the moment. A much changed mood from my last journal but I write these so that I may trap my thoughts (as chaotic as they may be!) on paper so that I don't have to deal with them\nAlthough sometimes, like this one, it's to create something to mimic my joy!\n\nI have a new name for Cherie. Funny, it's odd how when you stop looking so deeply into the present things can change in moments.\nI realized that I was being selfish. I was so worried for Cherie that I refused to look at the problem; I didn't notice anything other than her pain and if I had I would have noticed it stemmed from me. I wanted her to be happy and in response\nI managed to do one of the very few things that upsets her. She loved me and I kept punishing myself without realizing that she also felt the same about me. As I beat myself up over the smallest thing she would watch and so her pain\nwas held in silence. I had, mistakenly, assumed that she would voice a concern like that to me but that's poor on my part as a Husband. I should know my wife better than that and so the fault is mine. However, I do not intend to dwell on it\nfor I have learned a trait unlike anything I've ever done; The ability to smile.\n\nIt's an odd ability. It's not like the ability to wield a sword or a bow. It's not the ability to write or throw spells, it's not the ability to deceive\nfor personal gain. It's the ability to smile no matter what is going on, to be a beacon for those who have sadness in their lives.\n\nWhen Cherie was sad I had assumed it was something other than me. I didn't realize that it was my own\nsorrow that caused her to fall into that state. I pressed her and I wanted to force her to open up to me. Cherie tries to be so strong sometimes... she didn't want me to see because (as I believe, for even though I love her I do not always understand her.\nshe is a wild a beautiful thing that no man I fear could predict. It's part of why I love her so much.) she was afraid that if I saw her fear I would leave her.\n\nYes, in my mistake I had... written in previous journals\nabout the concept of leaving her or wanting her to leave me because I honestly don't feel worthy enough to hold her. She's so sweet and perfect, innocent in nature and can always light up any hour of the day for me.\nI still don't feel worthy... I just know that I'm not the person to makes that call. Cherie has told me she loves me and... I need to stop worrying and just believe in her like she seems to believe in me.\nIt was due to this fear of us seperating that she began to feel scared or hurt. She vanished, didn't talk to me for long periods in time, and I began to grow paranoid.\n\nEventually the night happened where we went outside\nof the Red Rose tavern and I asked her what was wrong. She put on a smile and I could see the pain... And I wanted to be able to hold her. So I pushed her for her to speak to me and I, in my worry, didn't consider what was causing her\npain. I saw her reaction and I knew what she was going to do before she did it but I was powerless to stop it; She bit her lip hard enough to draw blood out of pain and then told me to leave.\n\nUtterly confused in this state I wrote\nmy last journal.\n\nAfterwards we had a light talk when she returned in which our tension was left unsettled with a armored fellow came up by the name of Raide. This fellow gave us a visit and during that visit\nI had some time to clean my mind.\n\nIn those moments of solitude to my own thoughts I realized something. I felt as if in that moment the thing that Cherie missed most from me, an expression that I had not done\nin a while;\n\nI had not smiled.\n\nIn those moments while pondering those thoughts I wondered why... and I realized it was due to worry.\n\nI decided nothing could be done about it\nthat night and I set my mind to be as happy as I could be. I resolved to be happy.\n\nI did so by remembering. Remembering the first time Cherie and I's skin touched. Our first kiss. Her scent, the sound of her voice, \nthe feeling of her light breath on my chest.\n\nThe feeling of our hands intertwined, the thought of her body pressed against mine as we held each other.\n\nThe geniune smile of happiness on her face, the tears of joy\nwhen I proposed.\n\nHow beautiful she looked in a wedding dress, when she lids her eyes out of enjoyment. The way her touch sparks a fire inside of my very soul, her cherry-glossed lips.\nHer beautiful almond eyes and her perfect frame.\n\nI love her so much and when I stopped to realize just how lucky I was I couldn't help but smiling and I wanted her to smile with me, even if in the moment.\nSo I began to teach her to live, to feel. I felt as if there was so much I hadn't shared with her that I knew of.\n\nThe feeling of grass upon bare feet. The twirling of lovers. The soft dancing to silent music as our forms met.\nShe started smiling half way through, or at least really smiling.\n\nSomething clicked in my mind and my soul at that moment. I realized... I can make her happy. I just have to try. If I don't try then no one else will;\nThis world is cold and harsh and while there are those who would hold her... I fear that they would do it out of nothing but her looks.\n\nI want her to smile. I want to live my live with her in my arms smiling like a little girl. I want to be able to\nwake up every morning and look over to see her beautiful face.\n\nThat alone makes my day perfect. There is nothing that can soil it after seeing her next to me in the early dew of morning.\nCherie, when you read this I want you and you specifically to know that I love you and everything about you.\n\nEverything you do. Every little thing makes you who you are. Your tears, your smiles, the happiness and\nmirth in your voice.\n\nKnow that I will never leave you. I will never see any other man or woman like I see you and the only thing I search for in this life is to find you in my arms; It's not power, magic, beauty, perfection...\nYou once told me pursuing magic was my dream. That's wrong.\n\nMy dream is already complete.\n\nI dreamed to live a happy life with a woman that I love.\nMy dream has already come true my Star. Thank you for helping me with it.\n\n\n\n\n\n10th of Malin's Welcome, 1502\n- Assa'rai Rai'ari", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal No. 9", "Assa'rai Rai'ari", "It's hard to write I'm shaking too much.\n\nI want to curl up in a dark corner of this bedroom and cry at the top of my lungs like a little child because I don't know what else I can do and it hurts too much.\nIt's... better than it was earlier. Earlier I had visions of drowning myself due to heartbreak. I probably would have gone through with it if she didn't cut herself up when she realized that I was thinking about it...\nShe left me. She chose her Clerical magic over me... and while we're still 'together'ish... my heart hurts.\n\nI still don't understand and I'm afraid I never will. She's promised to return to me when she's done\nwith her training but... I don't think it will ever be the same again. She broke my trust and my vows... I love her so much and... my only dream is to grow old by her side and when, in the far future, I die... I want to be buried with her.\nNow... I don't know. She told me she wanted to break up.\n\nThis came after she had been brought to the Red Rose to help with healing and had healed Cheza to an extent that she passed out and broke with fever.\nI saw that and rushed to her side... I was upset with her. She is... no, she was always thinking about other people more than herself. I loved her so much that... when I saw her like that something broke within me. I forced myself to get angry because...\nI didn't think anything else would do it. I got mad at her for treating herself like nothing and like some form of sponge to take away people's pain.\n\nI yelled at her.\n\nI'll never do that again.\nNot that I'll ever have the chance.\n\n\n\n\nShe reacted differently than I expected. She told me she couldn't be with me anymore because I was in the way of her dream to\nbecome a cleric that can heal people.\n\n[!]The ink here is new as if a pause was taken between writing. A faint trace of red might be seen in the ink.\n\nI shut down. In that moment it was like a candle being\nblown out and I... my mind spiraled. I don't even recall what I said to be frank, I was mad and angry and depressed and desolate but...\n\nmost of all I was scared out of my mind. I was scared of dying before. I was scared of rejection\nand of being alone... but in that moment I was so scared I couldn't think or even breathe. Every action felt like an eternity and I felt almost as if I should stop breathing because it hurt too much.\nI was scared the love of my life was going to leave me.\n\n[!] The writing has become steadily unstable up until this point as if the writer's hand was shaking and the final line on this page is barely readable[!]\nAnd then she did.\nMy star... my Cherie... my darling... my beautiful and wonderful partner... the light of my darkness and the apple of my eye...\n\nshe left me alone.\n\nI've never felt so cold in my life.\nI still stay with her. We're in some relationship but... even though I was sharing a bed with her I've never felt so cold in my life... so... cold...\n\nI couldn't sleep. I didn't move from the bed for her sake since she needs me but...\napparently she doesn't need me enough. I remained like that with the source of my pain so close to my heart... It was like she was teasing me... laughing at my naivety... wanting me to be close just to feel the pain...\ndigging the knife deeper into the wound... but I don't want her to hurt. It's an odd mixture...\n\nand to be fair it's born of my own stupidity. All I had to do was be a good quiet husband and she wouldn't have left me.\nshe would have not had to worry about me and we would be able to spend our time together... we would be able to laugh and sing and be happy together as a fate-locked pair...\n\nI had to fuck it up. I just... Didn't want to see her hurt... and I made her\nhurt more than she could handle by doing so and then she left me.\n\nI took my journals away... to my furture wife whoever she may be I'll let her read them. I promised myself to Charis again but... I'm still scared she'll leave me.\nShe's already shown that she doesn't think I'm a good husband... I don't imagine it would be a far flung thought to assume that there would be someone else out there who wants her as much as I do...\n\nCreator I just let out another tear. I can't keep doing\nthis, men aren't intended to cry at pain we need to remain stoic... but\n\nit\n\njust\n\nhurts\n\ntoo\n\nm...\n...u..c..h\n\nI bled a bit. I grabbed the knife I cleaned this morning and I had to just see my own blood with my eyes.\n\nThe pain was oddly calming and distant. It was actually funny how \nlittle it hurt in comparison. I'll have to clean it up before she gets back or I'll worry her again and... I don't want to do that. \nI've been staring at the wound for a while now. I don't know how long it's been. I feel facinated by it and at\nthe same time I feel repulsed. The smell of my own blood is staring to nausate me... or perhaps that's just because I'm losing blood.\n\nI think I'm going to take a nap.\n\nThe more I think on it I realize\nit's also my fault for rushing the wedding... I just... didn't think she would or could wait... mistakes...\n\n...mistakes...\n\n...mist...akes...\n\nbut... aren't we all mortal?\nI'm almost hoping I don't wake up. The pain is too great.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Rash", "Zurak Brekan", "The Lord of Dunru has ordered us to move into the deep of dun'Sildur. The forces of the races moved forward.\n\nWe keep close, all the families and children, the women and men. We follow our lord. We never will die.\nHe moved towards the end of the deep, in front of the ritual room, Drash. The forces moved inside of the keep. We will be no longer safe down here.\nOur lord moved back to us as he whispered to every single ear at once.\n\nWe will follow him, we will never die.\nThe sword of old, the forces of old bursted out as the children, the women, the old and the sick died at once. The brutal mess was enough so that the forces of old will retreat in fear from the sight of the death.\nThe plan succeded, they ran away like the children they were. We moved into the deepest part of Dun'Sildur. Into the room of old, the turn of our lord. He will be saved.\n\nWe will reside inside this room with him until it ends.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal VI", "Elorna", "Aspects help me it's happening all over again.\nThe druids and high elves are at war, or nearly. So many things have caused it. Everyone is acting like children and violent fools.\nI thought we could have peace, we nearly did. But today\neverything escalated and Ouity attacked Kalenz. Now Lucion give us their terms for peace...\n\nMilo and Ouity will be turned over to the Mali'aheral. Neither of them can die anyway, so that doesn't matter. They must be shunned. That might be difficult\nto get the Order to accept, but both endangered the Order and every druid's life with their actions. Ouity, at least, I understand what he did and why. Perhaps he would be willing to be shunned for the Order's sake.\nAnd lastly, the three druids who are\ninfluential residents of Haelun'or... Oropher, Earendur, and myself must be shunned. To ensure our loyalty to Haelun'or over the Order.\n\nThese are the terms for peace. My order or peace. My order or sanity. My order ot the high elves. I know\nwhat Callax, Dover, all of them already think of me. That I've shirked my duties to nature, abandoned my vows. This would only strengthen that belief. Earendur at least said he doesn't care. That's not surprising, he's always been more Mali'aheral than\ndruid. Oropher was shot and I can't find him...\n\nThey probably won't accept even this, but they might... I would be sacrificing my reputation, my Order, the friends in the Order - few as they may be now - in order to stop more\nbloodshed and lives lost. For peace.\n\nPeace and life.\n\nThe last promise I made to Avery was that I would live. I would survive. I want to live. I want others to live.\n\nI don't seem to have much choice. The\nultimate thing I must consider... will this help nature? Would the Aspects approve?\n\nI would abandon my Order to save it. I would abandoned my Order to keep them from abusing their gifts to bring war and plague on Tahn'siol. I would abandon my\nOrder to keep the high elves from burning the grove and killing every druid they find.\n\n\nLet us hope they accept.\nWell, it has been quite a busy few days. We've had so many moots, trips between Haelun'or and the grove. I'm exhausted. But they are finally terms that both Kalenz and the druids can agree to. So, in order to end this conflict, the druids must leave\nHaelun'or alone, turn in Milo and Ouity, and shun two of the five Kalenz originally asked. I thought they were going to shun me and either Earendur or Oropher, but Milo and Ouity actually volunteered. They've not turned themselves over yet, but they said \n\n\n*a few pages appear damaged by water and\ndust. The words are smeared into the page and impossible to read.*\nlove his company. I even called him mayilu.\n\nI'm not sure how to know when you are ready to move on. Have I already? Or will I never be. Little things still remind me of Avery, but I don't know that I would ever not remember him, or want to. Does one have\nto forget to move on? I believe Phaedrus will propose soon. He strongly suggested it, anyway. If I'm not ready to remarry now, will I ever be? I do believe I love him. Yet I don't believe I no longer love Avery. How long is long enough? Would it be unfair\nto Phaedrus to marry him while I still love the memory of Avery? I'm also worried that if I wanted to wait longer I would simply lose Phaedrus.\n\n\nI suppose I have until he proposes to think on it.\n*the next few pages are blank, smeared with grime and dust. The entire book seems rather musty and damaged by water or time.*\nWell. Hello once again. It's been several years now since I last picked up one of you. I've somehow managed to keep all my journals together despite all this hopping from place to place. I'm not sure I have the heart to read through them all again, but \nperhaps soon. This one seems to be the last place I left off, which was... in the Fringe, just before Phaedrus proposed. Well, now we're about two worlds away and we've been married for over a year! I'm not quite sure where to start but I suppose I'll\ntry to summarize the last few years.\n\nPhaedrus proposed and of course I said yes. We were very nearly robbed in the middle of it, but after all that was cleared up it was pleasant. We were planning to have the wedding in the ballroom but \nsomething happened that made us wait... I don't remember what.\n\nOh, I believe it was a drought. Or was that before? I don't remember. The drought was after the plague though, and I'm fairly certain I wrote about the plague already. Anyway, there was a\nvery bad drought near the end of the conflict between the high elves and druids, and other things that made us start to consider finally leaving the Fringe. Something happened during a council meeting and several of us were somehow teleported or had a \nvision about an altar. Something about how the elven language was too powerful and being misused by Larihei. It's rather hazy now. Anyway, we left the Fringe and settled on a little island called Thales. Every year the winters would get longer and colder,\nuntil it seemed to be perputually winter all the time. I fell very sick for a long while, I'm still not quite sure what was wrong with me. Anyway, partially because of that Lin'ame was off to a very bad start, hardly anything got done and the population \nnearly dissapeared. There was that monstrous high elf, Durion, who threatened to kill Lenniel and Naaliya several times. I believe he murdered a druid in the grove in order to start another war between us and tried to get Kalenz or Lucion to exile him,\nbut nothing came of that. At least not then, but I'll get to that part.\n\nDue to the harsh winters we left Thales, and arrived on a beautiful new content called Athera. The landscapes here are gorgeous, though there seems to be a\nlot of arcane corruption in the wildlife. The forest of Fiandria is almost completely unresponsive to any druid's attempt to commune with it, and the entire forest, trees and spiders and all, attack anyone who goes near the ruins there. Its tied in with\nthe vision we had about the alter.\n\nSo anyway, Phaedrus and I were finally married. In the middle of it some vile humans tried to push off the grove tree, and we were once again teleported by whatever beings guard the ruins in Fiandria\nand they said something about protectin the altar.\n\nWhen they returned us to the real world we fell in a mud puddle and had to walk back to the grove to finish the ceremony. But thankfully we were able to complete the wedding that same day\nand the rest of the evening was spent trying to get away from one ridiculous elf or another. Katona, one of the guards, wanted to give us a severed head as a wedding gift while we were washing off. He's quite an interesting person, though I see a lot of\npromise in him.\n\nMore recently, things have gotten tense between the Mali'aheral and other elves. The Beru'cinhir is currently the only really functional guard force in the city, and the high elves show no respect as always. Kalenz even\ninterrogated Phaedrus because he was too 'efficient' or high-elf like. Now there is a plot of some kind to simply overthrow the Mali'aheral. Phaedrus is going to present a list of demands, including making him the new Sohaer. He's gathering support from \nthe other nations, and the high elves themselves are debating what to do about it. I listened in one of their meetings, and they seem to be quite threatened by all this, but don't plan to do much.\n\nHonestly I'm simply worried something will \nhappen to him if he takes this course of action. The high elves are in a very vulnerable position right now, yet Durion, as I mentioned, attempted to take over as well and he was executed by Oren. I'm not sure who Oren will side with. The Rose have \nreturned, this time as the Flaming Rose and a different tabard, but they are the same order. They are still allied with the high elves as well.\n\nI simply don't want this to come to war. And I don't want Phaedrus hurt. I don't think I'd be able to survive \nthat again. Hopefully it won't come to that. If he succeeds I believe the Mali as a whole will be able to truly thrive.\n\n\nI cannot help but be reminded of Avery, and when he wanted to do something similar. He didn't really want to, but he felt he had to. \nPhaedrus seems to truly want to, I think. Even so it might be best to go away somewhere and live quietly. If Avery and I had done that he may never had died. I'm stronger now than I was then, and perhaps I could protect Phaedrus if something like that\nwere to happen. Because I won't let it happen again.\n\nI've read over the beginning of this journal and I seemed to be asking if I truly loved Phaedrus as I had Avery. I can answer now with yes. I can be confident in myself again knowing\nthat he'll be there for me whenever I need him, and I want to be there for him on whatever path he chooses to take. So I'll support him in this current path. However it may end, we'll end it together.\nWell.\n\nI am once again writing while bedridden. Earlier today, while I was talking with Shadow after not having seen him in some time, a child that we've had trouble with before ran up to huge me. Meanwhile, he sister came up behind me and stabbed me in\nthe back. Probably one of my more painful injuries so far, which wasn't helped when a mage cauterized it to stop the bleeding.\nI was taken to the grove and thankfully Leyun was there. One of the herbs she used though - beardweed - has added side effects..\nI have grown a beard.\n\nI'm not sure if I should laugh or cry, really. I suppose all in all it's not the worst thing that's ever happened to me, but it's very embarassing. My back is feeling a little better, at least, though I'm a bit afraid to try moving \ntoo much.\n\nSomething is going on in the city so Phaedrus has gone to check.\n\nI suppose I'm going to be hear for a while. I don't have many pages left, but I suppose I can summarize recent events. We've finally\noverthrown the high elves. It had been planned for a long while, but when Iatrilemar was elected Sohaer it seemed he would be more progssive and let the wood and dark elves have more representation. Camernor was planning to assassinate him,\nbut Phaedrus killed him in Fiandria. Some time afterwards, he was found frozen in a crystal, so Phaedrus declared martial law. The Mali'aheral didn't like that, so Kalenz tried to make Kalameet Sohaer. Ah, and I've since heard from Jakir that Kalameet is \na shade. After that Phaedrus began to hear from the dwarves, Aesterwald, the orcs, and some others that they would support him as the new leader of Haelun'or, and finally there was a battle. Before the army even arrived the high elves burned the library\nand left the city, but in place of a battle for the city Iblees attacked. He did quite a bit of damage, and the 'golden pools' under the city are tainted now. I'm planning to gather a large group of clerics, druids, and Ascended to heal them.\nThere's not much to do right now. I suppose my back is feeling better but I'd rather not wander around in public with a beard. I'll need a new journal soon, too.\n\nPhaedrus and I have been married for a while, and want children, but still \nnothing. I know the elves are cursed, byt with Avery I became a pregnant after... five or ten years, maybe a little more. I know it's been longer than that by now for Phaedrus and I. And it's been over half a century since I had Lenniel, so it can't be\nanything about that.\n\nAh well, I suppose it will happen when the Aspects will it to. I've been leaving offerings at Cerridwen's shrine in the grove.\n\nAnd I'll be holding classes to teach new druids how to harness their gifts. I should\nstart working on the curriculum for that...\n\nWell, it seems I'm on the last page. This journal was a bit more neglected than my others, and I probably missed a lot. But all in all... it has not been a bad passage of my life. Until next time, Elorna.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kafeef famly", "Riad Kaneen", "Brown ppl", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Agnar", "Grungron Irongut", "          Battle\n            Of\n        Kal'Agnar\n-------------------The Battle of Kal'Agnar was the reclaimation of the Dwarven capital of Kal'Agnar which consisted of the Dwarves and their allies against the Ironborn and Undead\n        Ironborn\n      Brief History\n-------------------The Ironborn were the Dictators that ruled over the Dwarves before we had free'd our race from their tyrannical rule. They have returned and sided with Iblees and the Undead to take back the kingdom.\nThe Battle:\nThe Orcs of Krugmar, the Humans of Oren and Aesterwald, the Elves of Laurenh'lin, the Empire of Karakatua and the Ascended fought back against the Undead with the Dwarves reclaimed the Grand Capital. The battle was fierce with much bloodshed.\nVictory: With victory against the undead under the leadership of Grand King Fimlin Grandaxe we overturned the Undead and took back the capital. The Grand Kingdom was once more, and with this the Dwarves will remain an Unconquered Kingdom and a proud race.\n       Written By:\n  Grungron Irongut\n  High Remembrancer\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Karaad Scout", "Rhyndir", "Kal'Karaad Report\n\nThe robust capital of the dwarves.\n\nScouting by Rhyndir.\nLocation:\n\nKal'Karaad is situated in a valley. It is surrounded by mountains on 3 sides, leaving the east side facing the farms and clan halls. The west side is nearly impassable due to the rugged terrain and harsh landscape. The\ncity itself is built into the mountain. Making the only way into it the gate which is heavily guarded with traps. \n§PDefenses:\n\nKal'Karaad is heavily fitted with traps and blockades that can and will prove to be effective. The first of which is at the steps to the city. At the flick of a lever, the staircase, and the surrounding platforms will be engulfed \nin flaming hot lava in a matter of seconds. REGROUPING OR RENDEZVOUSING NEAR HERE IS A HUGE MISTAKE. There is also a lever that can pull up some extra walls, denying entry to the city. All of this is controlled at a control center located at right atop \nthe gate. It is under lock and key and will no doubt be the first place the dwarves go to during an attack.\n\nIf all these fail, the central square is also a trap. With one lever, the square will have all four exits push up and deny exit. The enemies can \nthen be easily shot down or disposed of. DO NOT GROUP IN THE MIDDLE OF KAL'KARAAD.\nAlmost all open spaces in these walls can be rigged to become a trap. This usually entails a lever or switch being activated to raise up the surrounding walls. The throne \nroom is activated by clicking the gold block. \nSiege plan:\n\nIf you were to attack this city, it would have to be a blitz. You would have to overrun the guards patrolling the gates, and seize command of the control center. The best way to do this would be to split your army into three groups. \nSend one group from the east main entrance. Send the other two from the north and south mountain ranges. Give time for the other two to set up and then when they sight the first group moving in, attack. One or two men will need to be sneak in unnoticed \nand watch that the control center is not reached. This could be devastating for the attacking force. Once you are inside, make sure to run along the borders of rooms and not be trapped in the middle. \nOverview:\n\nKal'Karaad is best not to be attacked, unless necessary. They have superior base tactics and presumably a decent military. If need be, this is the way to do it.\nThis is Rhyndir,\nsigning off.\n\n*SIGNATURE*", ""),
        StaticBook("Karma", "Isengar Brockfall", "The breeze flew into the deserted inn.\nThe doors slammed shut every minute, whilst the inn keeper kept his elbow onto the counter and his hand pushed onto his face people were looking in and running off.\n\"COM' 'N 'ERE\" he would shout.\nBut they got too scared and ran off into the distance.\n\nHe would glance out the dirty window, looking at the sky until it fades dark.\nHe would then blow out the candles, put on his brown coat and walk \nhome.\nHe would always hide the key under the inn mat.\n\n\"'Lo Isengar\" they would say when he stumbled into Gimblewood.\nIsengar was never the social person so he often grumbled or moaned and kept to\nhimself.\nAs he jammed in his silver key into his burrow he would sit down on his hand made wooden chair.\nYou could count his personal items in a matter of seconds.t\n1) 2 wooden spoons\none for eating and the other one for stiring stew.\n\n2) A small handmade wooden chair with a tied on cotton pillow.\n\n3) A dusty desk with old books on it stacked Alphebetically.\n4) An old mattress that has yellow stains on it.\n\n5) A bucket full of dirty water with old socks in it.\n\n6) A small wardrobe\n\n7) Knives and forks\nAs much as Isengar seemed like he was poor from the way his house was, he was actually very rich.\nHe was very tight with his money.\n\nHe always seemed to have money in his pockets or in the bank.\nPeople teased him saying \"Yer go' 'ny dust 'n t'em notes?\"\n\nHe would sit on his chair smoking a pipe looking out his window.\nHe would then prepare his favourite food:\nA roast pork stew with some seasoning.\nHe would stir the stew until it is brown, thick and gooey.\nWhere the meat is soft and tender.\nAfter his large meal he would wash it down with some Carrot juice that he squishes with a circular cutted log.\nThen he would go straight to his wardrobe and pull out his Light blue PJ's.\n\nThen he would go bed.\n\nOne day Isengar got up at about 5:30 which gives him time to prepare the meals for his inn.\nAs Isengar slowly got out his bed stretching his arms and yawning with a glum look on his face he would get changed into his coffe stained shirt.\n\nHe would then then put on his black trousers and head to work.\n\nIsengar glanced out \nhis window, and noticed it was pouring with rain.\n\"Hmph\" he grumbled.\n\nHe would slip on his coat and wander outside.\nHe would take a right to head out of Gimblewood.\n\"Mornin' Mr Brockfall\" one of the Halflings smiled.\nIsengar gave him a fake smile and headed out.\n\"Feckin' humbug\" he whispered as he passed him.\n\nHe arrived at the inn at last the rain started to quieten down Isengar started to relax.\nHe made himself a mug of Vincenzo Ale slurping at every sip.\n\nSoon an odd man walked in with a red robe and had a strange look on his \nface.\n\n\"What ca' a'h get yer?\"\n\n\"Nothing\" he replied\n\nIsengar looked at him with a confused and solid look on his face.\n\n\"T'en ge' out yer stuped feck\" he shouted.\n\n\"Now. Now no need to get feisty little one\" he smirked.\n\nIsengar started to calm.\n\"Yer obviously 'ave a'h reason ter com' 'ere a'h s'pose?\"\n\n\"Aye\" the man said.\n\n\"T'en tell me'h or ah'll...\"\nIsengar threatened but was interupted by the man.\n\"You should learn to give your money away young man!\"\nhe smiled.\n\n\"A'h can do what a'h w'unt wit' me money yer cunt\" arthur growled.\n\n\"Aye, you can but perhaps you should learn to give some away to your fellow Halflings.\"\n\n\"'o do yer t'ink ye ar' tellin' me wot ter do wit' me mon'eh?\"\n\n\nI am Karma\nIsengar ignored his pathetic speech, and carried on cleaning his counter with a ragged cloth.\n\nLater on when Isengar finished work he noticed a man sitting on the side of the road.\nWhen Isengar passed the man gripped his\ntrousers and asked for money, Isengar refused to give his money away to a peasant.\n\n\"Ge'h a'h job yer pesant\" he shouted.\n\nThe man looked down at the dirty pavement in sorrow.\nIsengar walked off to Gimblewood.\nAs he came in he noticed his house had a big sign out front, as he read the sign aloud it said:\n\n\"Dear Mr.Isengar, a'hm afrai' we'h kickin' yer out. Yer see Gimblewood 's a'h community, we'h shar' \nour stoof, so be packed by tomorro'.\"\n\nIsengar was furious, he kicked the sign over in rage.\nAnd went over to Milo's house.\n\"Yer feckin' cunt, yer can't kic' ma'h out!!!\"\n\nMilo chuckled \n\"Isengar calm dow'\" he said in a calm voice.\n\"CALM DOW' EY? YER FECKIN' KICKIN' MA'H OU'!!!!\"\n\"A'h can see why yer angr'eh, but unti' yer learn ter shar' yer shite t'en yer ain't comin' back!\"\nAs Isengar stomped back into his house grabbing and throwing things about.\nHe packed anything important like food etc.\n\nSo as Isengar was knocking things off the shelf into his small handmade bag he panicked of where he was going to stay.\n\"'n inn perhaps\" he muttered.\nIsengar peeked under his chair and grabbed his bag of 200 minas.\n\nIsengar opened his burrow door and slung his bag's over his shoulder.\nHe took the silver key out his pocket and looked at it for a \nmoment, then he extended his arm back and threw it forward letting go of the key it plopped into the lake and sunk into the soil.\n\nIsengar had his head down with a glum look on his face, the other Halflings giggled as he stumbled out of Gimblewood.\nIsengar walked down the road to Petrus.\nHe was blinded by the light when he was out of the trees.\nSquinting his eyes he made out a figure on the end of the bridge.\nIsengar Huffed realising who it was!\nIt was the Old man, he smiled at Isengar laughing.\nA sudden voice came to Isengar's head.\n\"Had enough yet, small one?\" The voice giggled.\nIsengar did not reply but instead shook his head.\nThe man smiled with an evil grin.\n\nSuddenly the rain started to fall from the clouds!\n\n\"'S t'is Karma too yer cunt!?\"\nThe man started to chuckle.\n\"No, That's just the weather\" he says politley.\n\n((PART 2 WILL COME OUT SOON))", ""),
        StaticBook("KEEP INSPECTOR", "Jan", "OFFICIAL KEEP INSPECTOR BADGE\n\nDO NOT STEAL", ""),
        StaticBook("Ker'nor", "Giliath Haldar", "Ker'nor\n\nThe way it glistens just so,\ncrystals dazzle in soft glow.\nHues of blue caress the eyes,\nas if upon the sunlit sky.\n\nVeins of black obsidian cold,\nwhat stories does thou tell of old.\nYour strength hid in your dark core,\noh you could be so much more!\nThe sound of streams tickle mine ear,\nlike the soft whisper of vines I hear.\nStones of moss and age,\ngive me freedom in your cage.\nWritten by:\nGiliath Haldar\n\n(Razorshawl)", ""),
        StaticBook("Kha Dictionary", "Ri'Zeriko", "~ Greetings/Courtesy Words ~\n\nSa'vi - Hello/Goodbye\nMul'ta - Thank you\nTra'kul - You're welcome\n~ Pronouns ~\n\nPatta - Father\nMuuna - Mother\nMetz'al - Life Mate or Spouse\nBunn - Wife\nMunn - Husband\nPer - Son\nMaut - Daughter\nPer'ta - Brother\nMau'na - Sister\n~The Karakatuan Government~\n\nTlatlanni - A Kharajyr blessed with white fur from Metztli herself, the Tlatlanni is perfection and divinity amongst the Kharajyr. The role of the Tlatlanni is to lead the Kharajyr for Metztli.\nTultelkos - Aelkos of war. He/she deals with political or militaristic efforts, and leader of the Moonblades.\n\nTruluk - Aelkos of Crafts. He/she is director of the economy and building.\n\nVarkolu - Aelkos of Faith. The leader of the Ja’ priesthood.\n Sostelos - The Social Aelkos. This Aelkos is responsible in providing happiness to the Kharajyr.\nThe titles of the Kharajyr are bestowed upon them according to their place in society.  Every Kharajyr will have a title (Excluding kittens/cubs) that forms the prefix next to their name. \n\nTla' - Tlatlannti\nRi' - Aelkos\nDri' - Tultelkos\nDra' - Moonblade\nJa' - Priest of Metztli\nYhl' - Elder of the Kharajyr\nQi' - Hunter\nKo', Ki' - Merchants/traders\nS', Sa', So',Si' - Unemployed\n~The Wildlife~\n\nTykkan  - Alligator\n\nVena-vi - Fireflies\n\nZisban - Monkey\n\nTuark - Hyenas\n\nNehpu - Colourful breed of birds found on the kha island.\nCehkan - Blue parrots\n\nCayda - Sharks\n\nGy'Waka - The Gy’Waka are a breed of colossal majestic birds that inhabit the islandthey protect the homeland as if it were their own and are by far the lead predators of the island. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Kharajyr Guide", "Camo Shadd", "Kharajyr\n\nKharajyr are creature who share many biological qualities with cats and humans. They are completely covered in fur. They are the creations of the Deamon Metztli.\n\nSubraces\nKha’Leparda\n\nThis type of kha is known as the jack of all trades. They tend to not excel particularly in one thing. This type of kha has light brown fur with black spots all around the body.\n\n\nKha’Cheetrah\n\nThe Cheetrah is the smallest of the kha family. They are known as good runners and climbers due to their small body. This type of kha is mostly hunters and warriors. \n\nCheetrah's have\ngolden fur compared to the Leparda. They also have black spots on their body.\n\n\nKha’Pantera \n\nAre known for their skills in thievery and stealth.  They have black fur.\n\nKha’Tigrasi\n\nThis type of Kha are known as the strongest and the mightiest of all the Kharajyr. They are known for strength in battle.\nThis Kha has Orange fur with black stripes through it. \n\nCulture\n\nThe Kharajyr are a highly religious group. They are a tough race by nature. They do not care about other races but themselves. They are hunters and gatherers. They often fish and farm for food.\n\nLanguage \n\nPutta - Father\nMunna - Mother \nMuuna - Moon mother (Metztli)\nMetz’al - Life mate/spouse\nBunn - Wife\nMunn - Husband\nPer - Son\nMaut - Daughter\nPer’ta - Brother\n\nMau’na - Sister\nSa’vi - Hello/Goodbye\nMul’ta - Thank you\nTra’kul - You’re welcome.\n*In the Kha language they will often use ‘w’s and use double ‘u’s.\n*They all speak in third person.\n*They spell everything how it sound when they write.\n\nMetztli\n\nMetzli is the god of all the Kharajyr. They will do anything to worship her. They will even kill themselves under the name. Kharajyr who turn away from religion are called “ape kha”.\nApe kha are called insane by all other kha.", ""),
        StaticBook("Khaz'A'Dentrumm", "Hogarth Irongut", "            II \n Auction of the Dead\n\nWritten by Indago Stormhammer and Morgrim Grandaxe. Copied by Hogarth Irongut. Tennant from Da Ord Nar Kadrin.\nKhaz'A'Dentrumm is said to rest within the plains of the afterlife. When a Dwarf dies their souls are carred by Dungrimm to be judged by the Brathmordakin for their actions in life. Yemekar was said to have forged the moon that inhabits the gods of the \nBrathmordakin. From here, they watch over the lives of Dwarves. It is also said to bear the Great Anvil that forged our world. The moon is only accessible by the most honorable and zealous of Dwarves, who had shown either great valor in battle or great \ndiligence in their life. When a Dwarf has passed on, a select few are invited to a grand feast within the hall of the Gods, forever to eat and drink. These individuals are known as the Paragons and act as near demi-gods in the eyes of their kin. The plane\nof the afterlife is known as Khaz'A'Dentrumm and is where all Dwarves strive to go when they die. Here, the Paragons rule while ordinary Dwarves are auctioned amongst the Brathmordakin. Those unfortunate and honorless Dwarves who fail to gain a bid  \nfrom any of the gods are instead vast into Vuur'Dor, an entirely separate plane of the afterlife. \n\nThe creation of this afterlife is primarily unkown. Supposedly the void existed for as long as the Creator himself and so all of the Brathmordakin \nare believed to have devised this punishment for those Dwarves who had acted dishonorably and shameful throughout their mortal lives. This plane is otherwise known as Vuur'Dor, literally translating to Black Doom in the common tongue. When a Dwarf passes \non into this form of the afterlife, they experience an endless cycle of emotionless despair, where they wander for all eternity. It is said that honorless beings delve these depths when none of the gods have selected them to pass on into the halls of \nKhaz'A'Dentrumm. Mages are said to derive the source of their power from the void and it is further suspected that this is where Khorvad and his minions currently linger.*\n\n*Written during Asulon and therefore outdated as Khorvad \nhas returned.", ""),
        StaticBook("KITS", "Mungo Proudfoot", "\nKITS\n\n- War Kit: 64meat and a drink for each soldier  +extras.  PRICE: 50per soldier (+10 soldiers 400minas)\n\n- Daily Kit: 64meat, 10bread + extras during three days for 30minas.\n\n- Caliph Kit: 64primeRib, 64mutton, 10stews, 2cakes +extras during three days for 150minas. (extras would be cheese and other expensive stuff like vodka)\n\n- Traveller Kit: 64bread and 32 meat for 10minas.\n\n- Shahzada Kit: 64meat and vegetables + extras\n(like for example a drink) for 40minas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Knight's Code", "Lord William Harcourt", "The Knights Code of Chivalry, as revised on the 7th of The Amber Cold, 1470,  by Noble Ser Maric II Varodyr, the Winged Knight.\n\n----\n-A Knight shall live by honour, for glory, and guard the honour of fellow knights.\n-Honour The Creator and maintain His Church.\n-Keep the faith and act in righteousness.\n-He shall serve his liege lord valorously and with conviction.\n-And persevere to the end in any enterprise begun and never turn his back upon an equal foe.\n\n----\n-A Knight shall refrain from the wanton giving of offence and despise pecuniary reward.\n-Give succour to widows and orphans and regard the honor of women.\n-He shall offer that which is not needed, to those who are needy.\n\n-And safeguard the helpless and uphold the weak.\n\n----\n\n-A Knight shall respect those placed in authority but fight for the welfare of all.\n-Abstain from Injustice, cruelty and deceit.\n-He shall be vigilant and show courage, even in the face of evil.\n-Resolve not with swords what can be with words.\n-And at all times speak the truth, even if faced with death.\n----\n\n-In their blood the creator’s will shall be written.\n\n----", ""),
        StaticBook("Knldge. and Exp.", "Farley III Stafyr", "Knowledge and Experience - Elaborated\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr.\n\nUpon a recent interesting discussion about knowledge with an elf, I considered onto writing down, \nwhat the difference between knowledge and the often related experience is.\n\nTo note at this place, there are enough people who assume that knowledge and experience are the same, although this is a wrong statement, as knowledge and \nexperience are different. To point this out, an example is required.\n\nFire. Fire burns and hurts, consumes burnable things such as wood and coal.\n\nNow let's assume you learned about fire and its properties\nout of a book. You studied the texts. This merely is knowledge, theoretical knowing or to put it in different terms, theoretical experience about something, respectively fire in this example.\nOn the other hand, if you never read a book about fire and get burned heavily or see it burning in front of you, consuming something, you learn from it directly. This is experience, practical knowledge. The difference should be clearly\nvisible by now.\n\nNow we have to elaborate the relation between these two elements of wisdom, mental capabilities, sense. The origin of knowledge is clearly, through experiment and therefore through experienc.\nKnowledge is an unpractical independent manifestation of experience, written down into books, teached through them or teached through a teacher, master. That was knowledge is, to know, but not to know.\nExperience itself may not always be referred as knowledge in this case, because knowledge can go deeper than experience, although knowledge origins from it. Knowledge itself may include to know about the progress and\nprocess behind the visible, such as the burning of fire.\n\nStill, it must be said, that experience can create knowledge under circumstances, experience can also increase knowledge. Experience can support and enrich\nknowledge. The relation between these two elements is vastly huge and not to be underestimated.\n\nIt is best to acquire both of them to roughly equal terms in cases, helping you on your way through the life.\nCopied directly from an original text within the archives of House Stafyr by Farley III Stafyr.", ""),
        StaticBook("Knockback Glyph", "Noach Hughes", "Knockback Glyph\n-------------------\n\n0 = Gems\n-------------------\n\n000\n000000000\n000000000\n000", ""),
        StaticBook("Knoxxy Adventure", "Elder Eath'lur", " The adventures of Knoxxy, son of Knox.\n\nVolume I\n\nWhen Knox created the world in seven days, he created a son, made of pumpkin and courage.\n\nHis name was Knoxxy.\nBut Knoxxy din't knew\nthe purpouse of his life, so he searched for awansewers.\n\nKnoxxy din't knew much of the outer world; shield carried on his back, sword laying on his belt, heart of pumpkin, face of a king, bornt to be the pumpkin king.\nFirstly, Knoxxy went to the capital of the humans, Oren, there, Knoxxy killed an blacksmith and stole a sword and a shield, both equal in power.\n\nDon't ask me how Knoxxy killed the blacksmith. Knox will be angry, i swear.\nWith an thunderous step, the mighty creation of Knox left the forge, everyone staring at his incredible pumpkiness, some people had their minds filled of making a pumpkin stew out of the pumpkin on Knoxxy head, so Knox made pumpkins rain on their heads.\nAfter Knoxxy saw the signal of his father, he had, for once, discovered his true purpouse on the universe.\n\nThe pumpsgiving is a signal of pleading and love-sharing, if Knoxxy wanted to rule the world, he first had to give others\npumpkins, so he left on a journey, where he stood at the gates of Haelun'or.\n\n-Let me in.-\nKnoxxy roared mightly and powerfully, a roar that shaked all the Athera, creating the mightiest earthquake possible.\nThe guard, fearing the worst, opened the gates for Knoxxy.\n\nKnoxxy steped in and raised his arms, and so, his father heard his plead and made pumpkins rain on the elven city, killing the common leaf tea.\n\nRivers of pumpkiness\nbegan to flow across the large city, the walls breaching to let the pumpkin blessing get inside, they where in absolute passion with it.\n\n-Father! - Said Knoxxy. - I'll make everyone bow down at your will! The world shall tremble before you!\nAs the pumpkins filled the city, Knoxxy left it, setting himself to the elves capital. The gates where open, as he walked up to the king or whatever is it, don't question Knox will, and said for him to replant all crops with pumpkins.\nThe king refused.\n\nThen, Knoxxy threw out from the majestic and marvelous realm of beauty Knoxxária, a pumpkin towards the king head, wich enlighted him, so he ordered that pumpkins would be planted everywhere, and all the food would be\npumpkin for him and all the next kings.\n\nThen, Knoxxy moved to the capital of dwarves, the stone shaking and fearing his might as he'd step in, his pumpkin would remember the roar of the mightiest steed of Knox, Lord of Pumpkins: The mightiest \ndragon made of pumpkins.\n\nTwo dwarfs rushed towards Knoxxy, but he raised his fists and pulled both back, an army would be formed to try to stand against the might of Knox.\n\n\nKnoxxy rushed towards the 4 million dwarves alone, as he'd jump into the air and make pumpkins rain over their heads by pleading to his father, the dwarves would be then enlighted and bow down to Knoxxy as he'd fall over a bowed dwarf's back.\n-Soldiers! - Knoxxy, now King Knoxxy, Pumpkin of Knox would shout. -Enlight all of your family with my word, Knox will soon take over the word, and those whom are enlighted, shall live in a perfect world, filled with pumpkins and pumpkins!\nAll the dwarves would peasantly praise Knox, \nWe will conquest the world with all the pumpkins!\n\n§ knoxy would approach cykacykacykacykacykaWOWOWOWOWOWOWOskdoakoskdoakovjkdklskdoioqiosdkojdodljlcjljosdjdowjodjowklskdlkdlskl\nKnoxxy would chant.\n\nA portal would appear to another dimension, pumpkins would flow out of it, pumpkins of the greatest quality, as Knox would step down. The bindings with reality and fiction ripping appart, as the Mighty, Powerful, Majestic, Lord, King,\nSlayer of Titans, Slayer of Giants, Saviour of Cities,\nDestroyer of Worlds,\nBuilder of Pumpkins,\nCream Slicer,\nPumpkin Pie Best Seller\nFan of Rap'lur\nBest Pumpkin Cook,\nBoat Sinker\nExuberant, Magnificient, Beautiful His Lord Pumpkiness, Knox §\nwould start walking amongst the mortals, the world trembling before his magnificency, as he'd go to mount on his pumpkin dragon along with Knoxxy.\n~-_-~-_-~-_-~-_-~\n\"Son, you did a great job, u mak mi prowd.\"\n~<)(>~<)(>~<)(>~pumpkin\nI'd love spending my time writing about all his majesty with all the pleasure of this world, but His Pumpkiness, Lord Knox and his son Lord Knoxxy, son of His Pumpkiness, Lord Knox have an army to lead.\n\nQuestion Knox and you will be pumpkinized.\nAnd so, His Pumpkiness Lord Knox, Lord Knoxxy and the army of dwarven pumpkin warrior farmer peasants marched towards the floating city of the cats.\n\nThe dwarves began to stumble on eachother, making a bridge towards the floating\nisland filled with weird walking flying floating jealous cats.\n\nKnox obviously made pumpkins rain on the first step he took in the cat city.\n\nThe cats got together to praise Knox and destroy the altars of their fake gods, so \nthey could completely embrace the Knoxism.\n\nKnox then went to all other cities, pumpkinizing everything, until the creator came back from life and split the world in two, the one with our true reality, where Lord Knox created the world,\n[!]Drool covers the page.\nand a fake reality, where I currently live. \nKnox descended to this place aswell, to help his lost devout followers like me.\n\nI'm going to take a billion of people and sacrifice them to His Pumpkiness, Knox, children or women, soldier or dwarven\npeasant, fisher or miner. Everyone must be sacrificied to plead my pumpkiness and return to my true reality, the place i bornt and lived into, I must go back, to live under the false reality of that creator bullshit is bullshit, His Pumpkiness is all that\nI love, everyone else that isn't a devout follower of His Pumpkiness must die, if they don't die they will suffer under my hands until they are converteds, I wish to do what Knoxxy did, led armies of billions of pumpkins to pump off the world, flow rivers\nof pumpkins. I will kill anything that doesn't pleads His Pumpkiness, he's my life, he's what remains.\n\nALL\n\nPRAISE\n\nLORD\n\nKNOX\n[!] A bizarre symbol made of blood lays down in the paper, followed by large writings, made of the pencil bathed in blood\n\nSEE I'M THE CHOSEN ONE, MY BLOOD SMELLS LIKE KNOXXY, LORD OF  PUMPKINS, SON OF HIS PUMPKINESS KNOX, LORD OF PUMPKINS, I WANT\nMORE SACRIFICE, THE PUMPKIN GOD NEEDS MORE SACRIFICES\n\nPLUNDER THEIR SOULS\nSTEAL THEIR FARMS\nSABOTAGE THEM\n\nPUMPKIN\n\nPUWPKIN\n\nI MUST BE PUNISHED\nFOR WRITING PUMPKIN WRO---\n\n[!] A large pool of blood lays by this page, making it completely unreadable\n\nKNOX IS MY KI------\nKNOX IS THE FUTU---\nKNOX IS THE LIF-)**E\n\nWE MUST ESCAPE\nWE MUST ALL ESCAPE\n\nTO THE TRUE REALITY\n\nWHERE KNOX\n\nIS OUR LORD AND GOD\n\nLIKE HE IS\n[!] The page has some sort of weird writings\n\nZTRUGANOK, VRAK\nWASTAGANOK, WRAK\nZTTRAGOFF, TRAK\nGRUNDAGOND, ARAK\nDAEMUN, ZTROAK\n§.§,AEGUL, BRAK\nDROGANNON, FRAK\nZLURKAADROG, TRUK\nGRAZDAET, DREATH\n\nMY SOUL\n\nMY BLOOD\n\nMY PUMPKINS\n\nMY BODY\n\nMY APPLE PIE\n\nMY CHERRY\n\nEVERYTHING FOR HIS \nPUMPKINESS, KNOX\n\nKNOX\n             KNOX\n        KNOX\n\n                     KNOX\n   KNOX\n              KNOX\nKNOX              KNOX\n\n          KNOX\n                      KNOX\nIF THERE WASN'T KNOX, THERE WOULD BE NO FUTURE\n\nIF THERE WASN'T KNOX, THERE WOULD BE NO PUMPKINS\n\nIF THERE WASN'T KNOX, THERE WOULD BE NO LIFE\n\nTHE FUTURE OF THE \nNATION IS KNOX, YOU PRAISE KNOX OR DIE\n\nI USED SOME OF THE BLOOD OF THE DEATH TO SHOW AWE TO MY LORD, CONSIDER THIS AN EXTRA TRIBUTE\n\n[!] A large splat of blood lays on the paper's bottom\nISN'T THAT ENOUGH?\n\n[!]More blood lays on the paper, but this time, it looks like it has been shaped and somehow coagulated, forming a pumpkin\n\nI HAVE ALL THE TIME AND ALL THE BLOOD OF THE WORLD FOR YOU, MY LORD KNOX\nAND I WILL SPILL\n\n[!] A blood stream rests here\n\nSPILL\n\n[!] Another blood stream covers the paper\n\nAND SPILL!\n[!] Spouted blood.\nTHERE GOES ANOTHER WOMAN, I'M GOING FOR THE THIRD ONE, BE PLEADED, HIS PUMPKINESS KNOX, LOOK AT HER FACE\n\n[!]You can notice tear drops over the paper\n\nI SHOW IT THROUGH YOUR PORTAL, THE PORTAL TO REALITY,\nDO YOU KNOW WHAT HAPPENS IN THE VOLUME 2? KNOXXY DIES, AS THERE CAN BE ONLY ONE KNOX, OH MY LORD, I HEARD YOU ASKED FOR MORE!\n\n[!] Blood seens to be all around the paper, as the mark of a face smashed in the paper is clear as sunlight\nISN'T THAT ENOUGH? ISN'T THAT ENOUGH?!?!\n\nI STILL HAVE MORE, MY LORD, AND I'LL KEEP TAKING\n\nTAKING\n\nTAKE\nTAKE\nTAKE\nTAKE\n              TAKE MORE\nSHED BLOOD\n    YOUR NAME\n        LORD KNOX\nYOU'RE OUR RULER\nNOTHING WILL STOP US\n\nI'LL KILL AGAIN FOR YOU\n\n§[[!]A thin pool of dry blood lays in the paper\nI HEAR YOU ASKING FOR MORE\n\nI'LL GIVE YOU MORE\n\nAND MORE\n\nAND MORE\n\nAND MORE\n\nAND MORE\nAND MORE\n[!] A ritualistic symbol lays by the paper\n\nTHIS IS THE PROOF I'LL BE BACK ON OUR REALITY, I WILL RETURN, I'LL FEED FLESH TO THIS BOOK\n\nI WANT MORE BLOOD FOR MY KNOX GOD\n\nBLOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOD\n[!] All the remaining of the book are unreadable sketches and childish drawings, as you open the page, a few pieces of flesh would fall down.\n\nThe last thing you can read is\n\n         I'LL GET\n      MOREEEEEEEE...\n         MORE\nSACRIFICES\n\nLORD KNOX\n\nNEEDS MOREEEEEEEEEEEEE SACRIFICES\n\n\nMOREEEEE\nHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAAHAHA\nAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssswwww§\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\nwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", ""),
        StaticBook("Kralekianism", "people884", "The religion of Kralekism\n\n1. Your soul now belongs to Kralek.\n2. Everything you own or every will own belongs to Kralek.\n3. Animals found shall be sacrificed for the betterment of Kralek and his people.\n\n4. Men found in Kralek's land shall be forced into Kralekism, all who resist shall be decapitated. The physical remains of their body shall be eaten.\n5. All Kralekian woman\nshall be treated as horse manure. Those treated better shall be bathed in it.\n6. All teachings of Kralek shall be accepted or you shall be casterated.\n7. Casteration is illegal.\n8. We listen to Kralek\n9. Eway istenlay otay Ralekay.\n10. Twerking is illegal.\n11. Black elves are illegal.\n12. Homosexuality is illegal.\n14. We listen to Kralek.\n15. Galkais are illegal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kreyzchurz Vol 1", "TapeSauce", "DIZKLEYMUR- WHUEBR EZ REEDIN DIZ MUZT NOH DAT DIZ BUUK EZ UHBOWT DA VERYUZ FURMZ AGH TIPEZ UB KREYZCHURZ AGH REYZEZ. RULG FUR REEDIN DIZ BUUK. UHZLO, MI ROTE UHLUT UB ET EN UH ZCHEWER.\nZcheptur Un: Da Snaak. \nSnaakz ahr wyrd. Dey ez zmull. Lat kan throogh dem et wulz. Bud, dyr ez moar tu dem dan juzt myootulazchun. En diz zcheptur, lat wil lurn ub da moar zchufiztukeytd lyfztylz ub Snaakz. Dey hev uh kumplux \nkulzchur dat lat wudnt ekzpekd. Furzt, et ternz owt dat Snaakz dunt liv en hollz. Wull, dey kynd ub du, bud dyr kuld berrohz. Deyz berrohz ahr akzchuii kwyt nyz agh dekureytd. Diz ez ub kurz ef lat kan eben fet en et. Udder dan flattin, Snaakz ahr yoozful\nfur treyding, ez Mi mit menii Snaak treydurz en dah rodz. Deyr yoozchulii vurry niiz kreyzchurz, bud deyr zo zmul dat wi lyk tu meyk fun ub dem wenebur wi peep dem. Uhlzo, Snaakz meyk fur guud berdendurz, dat ez, ef dey kan eben riizch da kowntur, ryt? \nZcheptur Tuu: Da Gharat\n\nPribiiuzly, wi lurnd uhbowt da Snaakz, smul, ugli, agh wiik kreyzchurz. Tu undurztahnd uh Gharat, ez tu undurztahnd elkohol. Lat peep, deyz Gharatz fil dyr holz wit byr, lutz agh lutz ub byr.\nDey ez uh marii reyze, muzch zo lyk da Snaakz. Dey ez uhlzo zchord lyk da Snaakz. Unlyk da Snaakz doh, Gharatz ahr phaddah, agh dey lyk tu klomp uhlmozt ez muzch ez wi Bruddahz du. Uhlmozt. Tu bii onizt, dyr ez muzch tu edmyr bowt deyze kreyzchurz. Dey ez\nuh bryd ub woryurrz Ub koarz, da Gharat kant bii kumpayrd tu da ztrengf ub uh Bruddah, bud dey ziim tu be ztrungr dan eben dah bigizt Shara. Muzch lyk uz Bruddahz, Gharatz hold dyr onurr tu uh hyooj ekztent. Bote Bruddahz agh Gharatz lyk tu yooz luskz\nagh hemmurz. Tu bii onuzt, Gharatz ahr lyk tinee, uglii, zchmellii, dum Urukz en uh wai. Mi tink dat wii zchud ztil flat dem, bud, wi niid tu uhprezchyate wai deyr zo fun tu flat agh klomp. Noaw, wyr gunna zchift gyrz hyr, agh zwhizch tu uh tullur reyze. \nZcheptur Frii: Da Albaiz\n\nDiz reyze ez un ub uh dizgreyzful zenz ub onur. Da Albaiz tink deyr beddah dan uz. Mi miin, zo du dah Snaakz agh Gharatz agh udder ztuf, but dah Albaiz ziim tu heyt uz eben moar. Deyr uh gruup ub kreyzchurz dat tink deyr zo \nbootyful agh zmurt. Bud, Mi fiil dat en zum waiz, dey ekzchulli ahr zmurt. Lat peep, dey mai bi finur, zchmelliur, agh dumr dan uz, bud Mi tink dat dey en zum wai, diip enzyd, dat Albaiz hev zum digry ub endulijinz. Purhepz Albaiz kant meyk guud wepenz ur\nurmr, ur eben guud biltingz. Bud, Albaiz ziim tu grezp da mojo vurri wil. Noaw, wi gunna dyv entoo dah zchpezifek tipz ub Albaiz. \nZcheptur Foar: Da Hy Albaiz \n\nEt ez dah Hy Albai dat zukz dah mozt, en Mi upynyon. Dyr dah unz dat RILLI tink hy uhbowt demzelthz. Kunziduriin etz en deyr nymz agh ztuf. Deyz unz liiv lung, luuk tull, ahr zupr pail, dring dah teez, eet dah \nkeykz, riid dah novullz, mok dah uddah reyzez, du deyr fenzii mojo, wayzt tym en meykin ztuf pritii, (Eben dah webenz) agh teyk dyr bafz, klyn dyr klofz agh eyrz, agh..... detz prittii muzch et. Beyzikulli, dey zuk. \nZcheptur Fyv: Da Wuud Albai\n\nNeztii lidl trii hugrz, datz wub deyze Wuud Albaiz ez. Belib et ur nub, Wuud Albaiz dunt eben yooz zwordz, luskz, ur eben toylit peypr. Dey yooz bohz. Agh fur toylit peypr, Mi tink dey yooz leyvz. Uhlzo, Trii Albaiz ahr\nmuzch lyk twigz. Datz wai anuddah nym fur Albai iz Twiggeh. Deyz Wuud Twiggehz iz uh bunzch ub panzchyz. Dey hyd en dah zchadohz tu hund fur deyr prai. Bud, uz Urukz hund fur owr prai en dah opun, kynda. Uhdoh, Wuud Twiggehz ahr guud et zneekin uhrownd. \nMi heb nub ztudyd dah Wuud Twiggehz muzch, bicuz dey ez yoozchuahlii hydin frum Mi. Zo, deyr ez ztill muzch tu leern uhbowt dem. Noaw, wi gunna teyk uh peep et dah grai unz. \nZcheptur Zekz: Da Durk Albaiz\n\nDeyz Twiggehz peep lyk da nyttyme zkyz demzelfz. Dey ez pritti muzch grai agh kynda bluu. Dey ahr pritti moduzt, peepin ez dat deyr Albaiz. Dey ziim lyk da muzt humbull ub da Twiggehz. Juzt lyk deyr mizteeriuhz \nuhpyrunz, nub muzch hez biin reykordid ub dah Durk Albaiz. Meybi deyr ez, bud dey nub zchard et wit Mi. Zo, Mi juzt gunna blah lat uhbowt deyr fizchikul uhpyrunz, rathurr dan deyr riil kulzchur. Dey haz durk zkin, durk eyz, bud dey yoozchulii drezz wit \npritti buld kulurz. Ulzo, Mi meynli nohtizd peerzingz agh grai harez. Zo, Mi dun blahin uhbowt dah Twiggehz, cuz dey ez pritti leym. Zo, noaw, wi gunna zchifd geerz uhgen agh lurn uhbowt dah sharaz. \nZcheptur Zebin: Da Sharaz ub Da Nurth\n\nGriidi, zchmellii, diplohmektik, tinee, uglii, wiik, dum, agh rilli dum. Lat knoh wub wyr blah uhbowt. Da Zharaz. Bud, deyz ahr dah Zharaz en da Nurth. Mi gethurrd diz enfurmeyzchun en dah zitii ub Ubrezchi.\nDey ahr uh kumplukeytd reyze, zo Mi gunna breyk diz op ento deberint katuhgoryz. Furzt, wi gunna blah uhbowt hoaw wi peep dem, ur hoaw dey luuk. Zharaz ahr zhortah dan Twiggehz, agh phaddah dan Gharatz. Dey kal demzelfz HOO-MANZ, agh dunt kal dem\nZharaz, bikuz dey ez dum, dey dunt knoh wub et meenz. Dey blahd wit Mi, agh zed dat dey hev zumting kald \"Pulektikz.\" Mi tink etz lyk Krughai Kunfedurazchun, bud dey zed et wuz moar uglyr. Uhlzo, dey griidi, lyk Gharatz, bud dey nub griidi fur goald, dey \nwunt minaz. Agh, dey neber edmid et. Zo, beyzikly, dah Sharaz ub da Nurth ahr moar ebil dan Mi eber thowt. Az lat knoh ahlredii, da Uhbrezchi Zharaz ahr owr alliz en mozt worz, bicuz dey ez zum ub dey unlii unz whu nub bytray uz. Noaw, wi du 'Dooneeuh. \nZcheptur Eyt: Sharaz ub 'Dooneeuh\n\nTeyk noat, Mi ubteynd diz enfurmeyzchun frum da 'Dooneeun Kinggy hemzelf, Yahrl Lazchlahn Moare Ilindul. Zo ez lat kan peep, diz buuk gev Mi da onur tu meat kowntliz uhfizchuhlz en da wurld. Enywhey, da\nZharaz ub 'Dooneeuh ahr blahd tu bii da owldizt. Deyr Kinggy blahd Mi dat wuz da furzt Zharaz uhrownd, meykin' dem muzch owldar dan da Zharaz ub 'Dooneeuh. 'Dooneeunz uhlzo hev pohlektikz lyk da Uhbrezchinz, bud deyrz ez muzch deberunt. \nLat peep, en deyr kulzchur, da yungizt boarne ez da un whu ez deztind tu liid, unlyk moar popyoolahr kulzchurz weyr da eldar liidz. Deyz 'Dooneeunz hev menii deberunt reynkz tuu, lyk uh Hy Theyn, agh Hy Morzchul. Uhlzo, deyz kreyzchurz ahr da lungizt livd\nZharaz uhrownd, biicuz uhpairuhntlii, dey hev Twiggeh bluud en deyr bohdiiz. Hoaweber, dey dunt peep lyk uhn Albai. Nub, 'Dooneeunz ahr zum ub da bigizt Zharaz Mi eber peepd. Ub korz, wi Urukz ahr ztil muzch biggah dan dem, dey ez pritti tol agh meyti. \nDey nub pyoor-brid Zharaz lyk Uhbrezchinz, zo dat liidz Mi tu tink dat dey ez da mongrohl reyz ub Anthohz. Lat reymimbur da Gharatz wi blahd uhbowt urlyr? Wil, noaw wi gunna tok moar uhbowt deyr hom.\nZcheptur Nyn: Da Katz \n\nTuu knoh diz reyze, ez tuu knoh kiddunz. Dat'z wub dey ez. Katz ahr beeg kiddunz, agh dey ahr frum uh eylund kolled Kuruhkahtuh. Dey blah wyrd, zmell wyrd, agh peep eben wyrdur. Diz reyze'z eylund bloh'd uhp, agh fur uh wyoll, dey \nleeved ryt hyr en Gronkkzton, en da kiddun diztrikt. Bud, dey oll muuv'd tu Mahlinoare naow, prohbublii beekuz wi Urukz wur tuu ztrong fur dem. Dyr ez fuur tiipz ub Katz, agh wi gunna dulv entuu oll ub dem ryt naow. \nZcheptur Tin: Da Tygur Katz\n\nDeyze ahr da beegizt ub da Kiddun Krezchurz, agh zum ub dem ahr ez beeg az uh Uruk. Dey peep lyk Tygurz, agh dey klomp lyk dem tuu. Dey ahr yoozchualii da woriurz ub da Kiddunz, agh dey ahr pritii duhm.\nMi dun't knoh uhlut uhbowt da Tygur Kiddunz, zo Mi gunna guu entuu da nehzxt Kiddun reyze.\nZcheptur Eeleben: Da Zcheetuh Katz\n\nDeez unz ahr da zmullizt, bud unlyk uh phat Ztowt, dey ez rillii phazt. Da zcheetuh Kiddunz peep lyk zcheetuhz, dey guut zpotz oll obur deyr zkin. Agh tuu Mi, dey'z myk da bezt karpitz, ef lat knoh wub Mi meen. \nZcheptur Dwelv: Da Durk Katz\n\nDey peep lyk Punturz, agh dey ahr zneeki, lyk Punturz tuu. Uhweyz peep owt fur da Durk Katz, kuz dey kan zteel latz ztuf et eny mohmunt. Tuu Mi, dey kynda ahr lyk da Durk Twiggehz, en uh zenze. \nZadlii, dat'z ol Mi knohz uhbowt da Durk unz, beekuz Kiddunz ahr myzteeriuhz, agh dey nub led Mi lurn uhbowt dem. \nZcheptur Dirtyn: Da Lepurd Katz\n\nDeez unz ohbveeuhzlii peep lyk Lepurdz, bud unlyk da uddah Kiddunz, deyz unz nub exeed en eny zchpezifik zkilz, bud dey ez da bezt zooted fur duueeng enytyng. Dey ez beeger dan Zcheetahz agh \nPunturz, agh dey ez phaztur dan Tygurz agh Panturz, agh dey ez zneekeeur dan Tygurz agh Zcheetuhz. Lat gunna prohbublii peep deyz unz da mozt. Wii neber peeped et dah deberunt typz ub Ztowtz, huh? Wil, wii gunna duu  dat naow. \nZcheptur Furtyn: Da Znoh Albaiz\n\nMi nebur hurd ub dem. Deyr zkin ez whyt lyk znoh. Deyr heyr ez whyt lyk klowdz. Dey ahr Znoh Twiggehz. Dey ahr endenjurd zpechiiz. Tu bii onuzt, deyz Znoh Twiggehz ahr Ahlbynoh, agh dey nub lyk et wen Wi kul \ndem dat. Da Znoh Twiggehz halb'd da Ztowtz wen da pazht wohr, zo.... Mi nub rylii lyk da Znoh Twiggehz. Dey liiv en uh pleyzch kull'd Frohztfohl. Bud, dat'z ol Mi knoh, biicuz dey nub rylii lyk Mi. \nDiz iz unlii da furzt vohlyuum ub da Kreyzchurz. \n\n\n\nDUH UHND", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "Lori Oathcast", "Long Range Translocation Device Investigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from Archmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockets within the void to place objects and a --->\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the void, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the original void translocationist present. The void translocationist must --->\n- then re-locate himself and in the area he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stay open when powered. ", ""),
        StaticBook("L1: Mori'Quessir", "Athe'lor", "I had known of the existence of the Mori’Quessir in Asulon, yet it was not until after the fact that I was informed of the language they had spoken, unlike any other. As one who delves into Lexicology on a regular basis and prides himself in being-\nable to speak many languages, I sought the want to learn their language as well. I found it necessary to learn what I could about the race as a whole, aside from only studying the language.\nUpon scouring libraries and shops for tomes on the subject, I managed to find very few, but enough to sate my hunger nonetheless. I learned of a Deity they worshipped called Nemiisae from a poem I had bought, and of the Mori’s affinity-\nor closeness with spiders. I am not sure if it is correct for me to use the past tense when speaking of the Mori for they may still be alive, but for the sake of this minor introduction I hope the reader will condone it.\nThe Mori’s society was matriarchal, in the way that women had power over men and were allowed to have multiple slaves. After managing to track down a man who was once a slave to the Mori’Quessir, we came to the agreement that he-\nwould teach the language to me. I will include very basic words on the following pages, accompanied by three full sentences. If all words are memorized and an individual wishes to learn more, they are welcome to confront the author on the subject.\nUsstan = I/myself\nUssta = my\nL' = the\nKaas = name\nZhah = is\nXanalress = language\nTlun = am\nAglla = trying\nUlu = to\nScrea = learn\nY'sik = rather\nXull = difficult\nXal = may\nNaut = not\nTelanth = say\nWiles = words\nListrane = properly\nJhal = but\nShlu'ta = can\nInbau = get\nWun = in\nOl = it\nSevir = leave\nXuz = end\nElgg = kill\n\nVendui ussta kaas zhah Izier. \n=\nHello, my name is Izier.\n\nL'xanalress Usstan tlun aglla ulu screa zhah y'sik xull.\n=\nThe language I am trying to learn is rather difficult.\nUsstan xal naut telanth l'wiles listrane jhal Usstan shlu'ta inbau ol wun l'xuz.\n=\nI may not say the words properly but I can get it in the end.\nBy this time the reader may have noticed that the original, seperate words were put into an order very similiar to the sentences themselves. This was the intention. The language of the Mori'Quessir is structured extremely similiarly to common, to the\nextent that translated Mori words in the same exact order can probably be read aloud in common as well, retainaing the sentence's integrity. \n\nThis is all I have for you, o' pages of mine. Rest sweetly until you are awoken. \n\n-Athe'lor", ""),
        StaticBook("L2: Kharajyr", "Athe'lor", "Beneath the alias of Ja’Sirah was one accepted into the Kharajyr community, and became able to learn first-hand about their culture, language, and way of life. As might be assumed, an individual living amongst the Kharajyr would pick up the dialect-\nfairly quickly after having heard it spoken throughout the day, day after day. Ergo, I was able to master the Kharajyrian dialect before any other ‘apes’ (What the Kharajyr called non-Kharajyr), and have found myself able to still speak it to-\nthis day regardless of body. You may ask how an Elf managed to disguise himself as a Kharajyr and remain under this guise without being discovered, but that is for another book entirely.\nAll Kharajyr are born and raised to speak with their natural accent, however it is believed that a Kharajyr can speak the Common tongue properly through mere exercise. Conversely, an Elf can learn to speak with a Kharajyr accent.\nThe following page contains simple Kharajyrian words that generally sound the same spoken aloud as they are read.\nSa'vi = hello\nMul'ta = thank you\nTra'kul = you're welcome\n\nPatta = father\nMunna = mother\nMetz'al = life mate\nPer = son\nPer'ta = brother\nMaut = daughter\nMau'na = sister\nRarely will a Kharajyr speak words more advanced than these, and they will merely speak Common, though accented. However, it is believed the Kharajyr had an entire language to themselves at one point which I will not claim any mastery over.\nHowever, I will share what few words and phrases I happen to know.\n\nSo hy'sa ec…\n=\nmy name is…\n\nQuin hy'sa ec?\n=\nwhat is your name?\nFre'ma dra feht p'mufc, dra Kha' nasyeh cd'nuhk.\n=\nwhile the wind blows, the Kha stay strong.\nThe Kharajyrian accent is what distinguishes how the Kharajyr speak related to other races. Though, put simply, all Kharajyr could speak with slightly different accents, and not many would be able to notice. I will write a few sentences-\nin the accent I acquired, and if you are diligent and persistent enough you may give birth to your own. An important note to keep in mind is that all Kharajyr speak in the third-person, and this is quite unique to the language.\nHello, how are you today?\n=\nsa’vi, haw awr yu’ssah tu’day?\n\nI am very good, thank you.\n=\nja’sirah ees ver’ray guut, mul’ta.\nWhat on Athera do you think you’re doing?\n=\nwhut’tah awn Aw’ther’ah du yoo theenk yu awr du’ang?\n\nDirty humans are everywhere, I wish they would go away.\n=\nder’tay aypes awr ef’ree’way’awr, ja’sirah weeshess thay wood gu aw’ay.\nThis book should be detailed enough for any intellectual to comprehend, take the knowledge from, and use to be able to speak with a Kharajyr accent. I now retire this tome to the shelf, to be put to good use.\n\n-Athe’lor\n", ""),
        StaticBook("L3: Cervitaur", "Athe'lor", "I was first introduced to the Cervitaur language rather recently, today being 16th of The Deep Cold, 1491, by a Cervitaur nonetheless. For some reason, Plazea (The Cervitaur) was within Haelun’or but unable to speak Common, only another-\nlanguage foreign to me. I then took it upon myself to teach the half-man, half-deer how to speak Common, at least enough to be able to translate words for me.\nThis sparked our ‘friendship’ as I encouraged Plazea to translate words from Common into Cervitaur, although clearly after a few days the creature no longer wished to translate and would avoid the topic. Even still, I believe with the words I was-\ngiven are enough to for me to finish translating, and I shall explain why. Not only is Cervitaur similar to Mori’Quessir in the manner that the sentence structure is nearly identical to Common, but there is a pattern to the letters.\nMany times did I hear Plazea say the word ‘good’, or as it translates into Cervitaur, ‘Ruun’. Yet, on more than one occasion, did I hear Plazea say ‘Guun’. Was this mispronunciation? My question was answered-\nafter Plazea told me the word for language, ‘Relriera’. However, in another sentence the creature used the same word, but said ‘Lelriera’. Do you notice the pattern, reader?\nLanguage, Lelriera; language, relriera. Good, Guun; good, ruun. I believed the key to unlocking this language was in the difference between capital and lowercase letters, and my hypothesis was correct. When a letter is capitalized, it remains the same.\nHowever, in Cervitaur when a letter is lower-case, it may turn into a variety of things (or may also stay the same). The next few pages will include capitalized words, and lowercase words I have translated.\nIrrar = yes [] Yar\nLu = no [] Nu\nHarru = hello/Hello\nRuunfirra = goodbye [] Guunfirra\nFirra = bye [] Birra\n\nRserr = grass [] Gserr\nLlruwas = flower [] Fruwas\nWedas = water/Water\nSil = run [] Ril\nRunadainar = sometimes [] Sunadainar\nAir = is [] Ir\nIlnasrdeln = understand [] Ulnasrdeln\nRelriera = language [] Lelriera\nErru = also [] Arru\nEln = and [] Aln\nRdillll = stuff [] Sdillll\nFuuc = book [] Buuc\nRuun = good [] Guun\nFen = bad [] Ben\nCairr = kill [] Kairr\nAyair = evil [] Eyair\n\nAs the reader may be able to tell, translating from Cervitaur to Common is not all that difficult, you must merely know which letters replace which (and only lowercase letters are replaced). If you were to write a sentence in Cervitaur in all capital-\nletters, yes, it would seemingly translate into the exact same thing; the trick solely lies in being able to replace lowercase letters with other lowercase letters. If one seeks conversation in Cervitaur, you are encouraged to speak with the author.\nI now tuck my words to sleep, and pull the blanketed leather cover over them. Sweet dreams; may you find yourselves in the hands of those who pursue knowledge. \n\n-Athe’lor ", ""),
        StaticBook("L4: Elven", "Athe'lor", "The Elven language is perhaps the most complex and difficult to learn of all languages spoken by mortals, and will be the most arduous to overcome in this series of language volumes. Unlike the Common tongue where one word has one meaning, in-\nElven many words can combine to have multiple meanings. This book bases itself upon the foundational writings of the Elven language, mainly the manuscripts of the Elven scholar, Aerin Lissar. I personally claim no expert -\nunderstanding of the Elven language, as it is (despite the author being an elf) the language I am the worst at speaking. Nonetheless, I will re-write the information Aerin has given for you to learn from.\nAffixes are the very first thing Aerin writes of, and encourages the reader to learn these before continuing any deeper. The following pages will include affixes: first, the affixes that are meant to be attached\nto the beginnings of words, and secondly those which are meant to be placed on the ends. I will leave you to it, as truly there are not many compared to the massive size of the list to follow.\nAc/Aca- = accursed\nAh/Ahe- = reverence\nAel- = vile, beastly\nAn(a/o/i/e/u)h- = to direct (up, down, left, right, rotate)\nAv- = wandering\nAy- = for\nDiv- = empty\nEl/Ele- = changes a noun into a pronoun\nFi- = new, anew\nHey/Heya- = what, how, who\n\nIl/Ilu- = with\nIyl- = this \nIyul- = that\nMa/Mar- = very\nPar/Pra- = before\nRe/Res- = wayward, unpredictable\nTal/Tali- = part (of)\nU’- = or\nVul/Vule- = clever, deceptive\nWhat remains now is the colossal list of Elven words, to which there is no shortcut to learning and memorizing. Each word is distinct and has its own meaning, and thusly being able to grasp this language is comparable to that of-\nfirst learning Common; one must painstakingly learn all the words separately, and then learn how to apply proper grammar etc.\nIf an individual seeks to sink their roots deeper into the Elven language, I will direct them towards Aerin Lissar’s actual book: “Recovering the Ancient Tongue Of The Elves”. \nThis is where I leave the reader, with only a basic understanding of the Elven language. I regret to say that I may never master the Elven language, and I have little interest in doing so. \n\n-Athe’lor\n", ""),
        StaticBook("L5: The Blah", "Athe'lor", "Despite being an elf, for a long period of time this scholar was accepted in Krugmar and allowed to walk its sand dunes, speak with its people, and eventually become familiar with its language. It is my belief after years of study that the Uruk found-\nthemselves unable to speak Common properly (at least without tremendous effort, and those who could were deemed ‘Whitewashes’) and because of this, they found a need to create a more clear form of communication.\nWith this need, the Uruk butchered words in Common and created their own words to replace them. Because of their large, barbaric forms with tusks, orcs have difficulty saying most words and consequently they are mispronounced. The following pages-\nwill include all necessary words one must know to speak ‘Blah’ (another name for orc-speak) properly. All things aside, one could always argue that Blah is not proper in the first place but I digress.\nUg = hello\nThrom’ka = respectful greeting\nYub = yes\nNub = no\nGug’ye = goodbye\nLat = you\nMi = me\nRulg = thank you\nBlah = talk, speak\nGruk = understand\nBubhosh = great, large\nSnaga = slave\nNubhosh = small, bad\nKlomp = attack\nFlat = dead\nBlarg = home\nBruddah = friend, war nation orc\nSkah = curse word\nNubded = undead\nStowt = dwarf\nTwiggie = elf\nShara = human\nKitty = kharajyr\nAgh = and\nMojo = magic\nGoi = city\nAsh = one\nDub = two\nGahk = three\nUsing these words, all one has to do is speak with an Uruk accent which in truth is not all that difficult; it is probably easier to speak with an orc accent than a Kharajyr accent. When one of the prior words on the list is necessary in conversation, -\nall an individual has to do is substitute the orc word in (and there are not that many). Chances are learning the language will be rather useless to the reader regardless of mastery, as orcs will probably grow upset if you speak it.\nThe final and perhaps most useless book of my volumed language collection is finished. May it sit happily with its brothers and sisters, until the day comes when one can make use of it.\n\n-Athe’lor", ""),
        StaticBook("Land of Twilight", "Damien Menrow", "In the land of Twilight under the Moon, we dance for the innocents.\n\nRing around the roses jump to the moon, we sing with the Castanets.\n\nI will sing for Crescent Moon, dancing with the Castanets.\nAs the end will come so soon, in the land of Twilight.\n\nI will sing for Crescent Moon dancing with the Castanets, as the end will come so soon in the land of Twilight.\nIn the land of Twilight under the Moon, we dance for the Innocents.\n\n\nRing around the Roses jump to the Moon, we sing with the Castanets. *", ""),
        StaticBook("Larkspur affects", "Annabella", "The internal affects of Larkspur on a Chipmunk:\nUpon preperation both Chipmunks are free of external blemishes which could render tests invalid. They both frantically move around, with good speed.\nThe healthy, not poisoned chipmunk.\nThe insides are what I expected, no suprises.\n\n*A sketch of the inside of the chipmunks are here*\nHypothesis: After a few days of feeding the chipmunk poison I expect full liver failure resulting in death.\nDay 1 of feeding:\nThe chipmunk ate everything I used to hide the Larkspur seeds, but left the seeds themselves. I must be more clever with my feeding tomorow.\nDay 2 of feeding:\nToday the chipmunk was fed in a liquid form, the seeds in the liquid. It has eaten the entire thing, leaving no seeds, the process begins.\nDay 3: The Chipmunk already shows signs of not wanting to eat. It took the entire day for it to finish the entire small bowl of liquid food I gave it.\nDay 4: The chipmunk just lies there, it is still alive but today I had to force the food down it's throat with a medicine dropper. \nDay 5: Not much has changed since day 4. The chimpmunk will rarely stand up, and appears to be on it's last few days of life.\nDay 6: The chipmunk is dead, it is hard, and cold so I will begin to disect it while it is still fresh. \n\nDisection: Upon disection the liver as expected shows signs of it not functioning. The chipmunk also appears to not have fully digested most of\nthe seeds. leading me to conclude that Larkspur is not a digestible content, and as expected harms the liver. On a small dose of one time only the chipmunk may have lived longer, but the constant attack to the liver was too much for it to survive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Last Words", "-", "It happened, I knew it would. I warned Master to not keep them, they are dangerous. I’m stuck, unable to leave, with this creature looking. I’m scared, the ghosts keep coming, not even now they stop.\n\nMaster did this, it was his fault, I should have killed him. The voices spoke true, I should have killed him, him and his creations. I still hear them… The earthquakes got him loose, he’s too dangerous to have kept alive.\nIt’s watching me, that beast… it mocks me, mocks me so… I can’t breath underwater, I am harmed, I can’t leave, the door is locked. I lost one key, the Doppelganger stole the other. It wants to leave, I can sense it.\nIt’s stuck like me, wants to escape. It’s watching me for the other key, he’ll let me die, but he can forget it! It’s staying here with me, it’ll never find the other key… The noises, those noises from above… No… the other one is free.\nIt’s free… May Dungrimm... weight my soul righteous. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin", "Arinislia", "Children of Laurelin\n\nI hear the song of Laurelin;\nThe children’s laugher singing;\nOf trees, and leaves of many things,\nTo many, the sound of bells ringing;\n\nI hear the song of  Laurelin,\nNow lost in the burning flames;\nThe echos whisper in our hearts,\nNow most don’t seem the same;\n\nI heard the song of Laurelin,\nof purity and rings;\nOf ones who mix of blood,\nAre met with acid that stings.\n\nI seek the song of  Laurelin,\nOf children’s laughter and song;\n The sound almost lost to me now,\nThough somehow I continue on.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Law and Progress", "The Scribe.", "The Importance of Law.\nMany are opposed to the laws of the Mali'aheral. They decree them horrendous or barbaric. \n\nMany are opposed to the laws of the other races as well. Every individual seems to believe with a burning\npassion that only their laws are conducive to the most prosperous nation. However, I believe that law itself is prosperous to a nation or goal. How can progression exist without rules or order? The Mali'aheral are my first example of this.\nTheir laws are strict and very pointed. They are designed to weed out chaos from the state of Malinor. In doing so, science has been able to thrive within their community, and drives them towards success and prosperity. \nThe next example are the Orcs of the Rexdom. Their laws are much looser, but still maintain some integrity. The Orcs are a very violent race, but their goals are accomplished step by step. However, they progress slower than the Humans, Dwarves, and Elves \ndo. The Valah have a very stringent code of honor, and it allows them to progress quickly and militaristically. The Bortu have less stringent laws, and progress at a slower pace than the Valah do. \nLaws are conducive to progress. Without personal code, without the code of state, without the code of the realm, progress cannot be plentiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Leafy Pamphlet", "Wandering Man", "  May the Aspects bless whoevers hands this pamphlet falls into!\n\nWho are the Aspects, you may ask? Seek out the Druidic Order and find out! Find spiritual fufillment, knowledge of the ancient past and its secrets, and a new appreciation and love\nfor the Natural world around you!\n\nThe Mother Grove is found in the Oakhearth Forest, past the Sequoia Grove!\n\nSeek out the Druids today!", ""),
        StaticBook("Lean (Alchemic)", "Grim'aeldus", "The origins of Lean or more commonly known as Purple Drink (Purple Drank if you’re of Southeron dialect) precede man himself according to the legend of Lawrence Lean. \nBack in the First Era a would-be herbalist was delving far into the reaches of Aegis looking to change the face of the herbal game forever. It was after thirty years of searching that his thirst was quenched, he had discovered the Chrono root.\nIt glowed when he unearthed it on accident on a hot day in the wastes. Shocking and magnificent he gently uncovered it without severing it from its host. A perfect extraction was followed by mass excavation. \nBefore too long Lawrence Lean had a nice stockpile of Chrono and made preparations to head back to the heartland of Aegis to share his findings.\nUpon a relatively short trip back to his lab the herb fiend got to work. Mashing, grinding, and boiling Lean went wild trying to find a use for his life’s work.\nIt was in a workplace rage that he discovered the Chrono root actually grew out of root form and created a dense bush of sweetly scented buds and flowers.\nWhen a mature plant’s roots are grinded and boiled in cheesecloth Lawrence Lean found himself with a powerful elixir. It’s effects are known to slow down perceived time in the user’s mind and induce an intense warped effect about the user.\nWhen dried out the buds made for great pipe tobacco substitute. Chrono’s use as a smokable remedy has recently been made famous by Hansetians, notably avid Chrono user the late Darius “Lion”.\nLawrence Lean proclaims his elixir Lean to be the key to immortality. It has been described as a mixture that looks like the deep heavens in color and enthralling nature when staring directly into a fresh mug of Lean.\nAfter Note:\n\nTexts recovered from a Human library prior to it's closure. Original texts indicate the author was one Lion III of the Holy Oren Empire from the era of Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Learn to Read", "Saviordude", "=(^x^)= Cat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= Cat in hat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o( Cat in hat, with a bat.\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o(\n\\(     )/ Fat cat in hat, with a bat.\n*This book continues on like this for several hundred pages, allowing one to pick up the written word with the magic of Rhyme and Pictures*", ""),
        StaticBook("Leather Armor", "Kahlan Ohrpiaus", "How much is a set of leather armor? Please contact Kahlan Ohrpiaus for the price!", ""),
        StaticBook("Leatherworks", "Kamatari", "Leather Cap\n5 Minutes\n5 Tanned Leather\n\nLeather Tunic\n8 Minutes\n8 Tanned Leather\n\nLeather Pants\n7 Minutes\n7 Tanned Leather\nLeather Boots\n4 Minutes\n4 Tanned Leather\n\nSaddle\n2 Minutes\n4 Tanned Leather 1 Iron Ingot\n\nItem Frame\nNo Craft Time\n4 Sticks 1 Leather\nLead\nNo Craft Time\n3 Rope 1 Leather\n\nName Tag\nNo Craft Time\n1 Paper 3 String\n1 Leather", ""),
        StaticBook("Lenniel Div", "Lenniel", "\n\n\n\n    Lenniel Divhileia\n         Grimiore \n            of\n    Household Magic\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        Tier One\nLight Weak Fire (Evocation)- Summons a small, steady fire that can be used to light (only) flammable things. Like Greasy hair, Important paper documents, or explosives!\nPuff of Air (Evocation) - The caster summons a light puff of air that can lift up skirts and robes. Also scatter papers, blow cobwebs into people's faces, and provide a cool breeze on a hot day. For me that is.\nLight Source [Alteration] - The user creates a small and dull light using alteration. Used to dazzle freinds and blind enemies!\nIllusory Writing - The user creates glowing text for writing. This text fades in 2 elven days unless the alteration is refueled. Great for impromptu graffiti and party banners.\n\n\n\n\n\n         Tier Two\n\nLight Weak Fire [Multiple] (Evocation) – Second verse, same as the first. Only multiply the fun!\n\n\n\n\n\n       Tier Three\nLift Object (Telekinesis) – Lifts one (1) object a few feet off the ground. The object lifted cannot exceed around 2kg in weight.\nPerfect for holding a book up in lieu of a book stand.\nCommand Object (Telekinesis) – The caster commands one (1) object to perform an easy task. \nExcelent for playing with your food. Ever seen a slice of cheese and cracker do the Waltz before jumping into your mouth? It's rather entertaining.\nCreate Water (Evocation) - Creates a half a bucket's worth of water that can be used for washing, bathing, etc. Water vanishes once task is complete.\nPerfect for the classic 'drop water on somebody's head\" prank.\nCreate Earth (Evocation) - Create a half buckets worth of earth. Can make small rocks too. Vanishes when dismissed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lenniel's Task", "Lenniel'onn", "Art Camoryn: Situation- practicing lighting evocation. Shot down spark of lighting, harming himslef, and one other, the other being an innocent, simply watching the display. Art was seriously charred, and unable to speak or move, the other individual was \ncharred as well, but not to the extent of Art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Let us all unite", "Evertlas Treebeard", "Beauty lies in the sight of the Attunement Pool;\n\nWhose waters sparkle gently,\ncrisp and cool.\n\nAwe lives in the sight of an elder tree;\n\nWho houses nature lovers like you and me.\n\nAnd so we look to these \nformations of old; \n\nOf who's great stories will be forever told.\n\nFrom the gentle rabbit to the roaring lion;\n\nLet these creatures be our siren;\n\nLet us all learn to love nature dear;\nWho's awe, beauty, and love  unites us here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Let's talk", "Castien", "*a bloody hand print is shown on this page\n\nWe know what you have done, this is no death threat. We only want to talk.\n\nFind George Windfield, ask him to find the two people that started a homestead on his land. \nWe will go from there", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Freema", "[!] The letter is folded in half and lays along\nthe top of the crate.\n\n\"I'm sorry I couldn't do this face to face, but hey! I tried to find what you needed. Don't worry about paying me back, you shall do so in time. But for now, good luck with your smith\"\nThe letter is stamped with a helix and eye between it, underneath is signed with the letter F. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "flexave", "Dearest Prince Emberhard,\n\nI am rather interested in taking a room in your inn. I'd be grateful if you could reply or meet me, at the inn itself.\n\nA million thank yous,\n\n    -Fleur", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Cederick de Bolbec", "[!] The offical wax seal of House de Bolbec is stamped here.\n\n\"Dear my good friend, Emmanuel.\n\nI should like to request your aid, to speed up the process to aid the collapse of the Northern Commonwealth.\nThere is little chance of it piecing together, especially when a large number of your own men, are infact, with me, as in every major orgaisation.\n\nMy lands contributed massivly to the alliance, and I should hope to think you acknowledge that.\nYour dear friend,\n\nCederick de Bolbec of Draydon.\n\nP.S\n\n\"The Cat has been let out of the HAT\"\n\n\"TDUEHATHHATNOBOLTCTMO, PGLMEMABSUE\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Viktor 'The Grizzly' Dustin", "Dear Viktoriya Vladov,\n    I'm sorry that our whole meeting got off on the wrong foot, with you abruptly being told that you were to marry a stranger, on top of the fact that the stranger looks more like a bear than a man. I personally wish we had\nmore time to talk with one another before my patriarch, and your father had declared this marriage to occur. In this letter, I'd like to adress a few things that you had asked me during the heat of the moment. First off, I'm sorry that my lack of\ninvolvement with the military is something you see as disgraceful. I'll be sure to try and correct that by enlisting with the levy so that I do not make you feel as if I am a useless man. I tend to stay away from militaristic activities, not because I\n§§am a coward, but \nbecause I had other duties to accomplish, such as my position as Warden of the Woods of Aldersberg. Hopefully you can understand this, and do not judge me too harshly for it. I also wished to comment upon the remark \nyou made about me joining the Order of Saint Amyas to become a 'man'. I am quite certain that I am qualified to call myself a man, even though I do not partake in the usual battles and skirmishes that seem to plague the roads daily. If being a person \nis quick to draw their blade and rush out to attack other beings, then by that standard, I am no man. Though, through my work and through my mental capabilites, I'm certain I'm as manly as any who would rush out onto the battle field. This concludes the\nreflection portion of this letter, and I hope it's contents are adequate. Moving on, I'd like to state a few things about myself, as to break the metaphorical ice between the two of us. I am a well-learned man, as you might've noticed by the contents of\nletter, though it takes me quite some time to get my thoughts out in the middle of conversation. I might sometimes appear to be distant, but keep in mind that I do take notice of things, and try to correct them. \nAnother thing about me is \nthe fact that I enjoy hunting with my companion, Barnsy. I'm certain that the two of you met, considering the whole ordeal today. I'll keep in mind that you dislike dogs, having just found out today. But, nontheless, Barnsy's companionship when out \nand about is something I cannot change, and thus must inform you about it. A third thing about me is that I enjoy carving wood in my spare time. Maybe, should you wish, I could carve a wooden bust of you if you decide to enter the Alderswoods. It would \nbe a nice activity to do together, no? Anyway, a fourth thing about me is that I dislike very sweet foods, and apples. I don't understand the taste of them, but I know that quite a few people have taken a liking to the funny fruit's taste. If anything\nthings like meat and stews are much better. Nothing beats a long day of logging and patrolling the woods like a mean stew of mushroom soup with venison chunks. And lastly, another thing about me is, my favorite animal is the bear. Since I was a young \nteen, I've been called many things, but the one name that stuck with me is 'Grizzled Bear'. It is oddly fitting, once you stop to think about it, as I do quite often. Thats about it for now, Viktoriya. I hope your opinion of me has changed atleast a\nlittle. \n\n- Grizzled Bear", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter for Konig", "Martin Winter", "*After unrolling the rough parchment, you find, in the form of a charcoal scrubbing, words intended for the Konig Voron Rovin to read.*\nTo His Apostolic Majesty, Voron Rovin:\n\nI, Martin Winter of Ayr, beseech your Majesy that you pardon the knight of Vanders Ser Quinlan Campbell for his actions against my House and personal honour. 'Tis in my interest to see to it that he survives and \nremains in Vanderfell with all titles he previously held retained. My reasonings for such are few, and if you wish to understand further you may send a bird for me. Let him not suffer for his crimes. He has endured enough to my satisfaction.  \nKeep the Faith,\nMartin Winter of Ayr", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Tess", "Tessa", "Dear Lorina,\n\nI don't know what has happened, I woke up in this cloud temple place outside Oren. Everything hurt. When I finally made my way back to Dragon's peak I say my own Grave! People are told me that I died.\nI don't know what to think anymore, I barricaded myself in my room, Lady Alexandria broke open the wall with her axe. Everything is so strange, Licia's not responding to my letters and people are giving me weird looks. I know you're probably away. and you\nmight think this is some weird joke. But I really need you as a friend right now. Whenever you can come to Dragon's peak. \nPLEASE believe me, I can't come to you. I'm too scared to even cross the bridge anymore, Alexandria told me I fell.\nI'm going to try and see if I can pay a servant to deliver this. \n\nPlease come, I'm scared.\n\n~Tessa", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter of Marrow", "Unknown", "I know that you have been visited by the Order of Youth, what have you been doing to get them to notice you? Surely you are not contesting what he has done, he found it that’s for sure, and you know how his followers become when you question him. \nIblees would be jealous of their rage. You know that humans fear for their short lives, trying to remove hope of extending it will make them mad. I hope you didn’t get hurt by them, the best of health to you, may Aeriel bless your body.\nAs for what you asked me to get, I convinced the town’s people that their death were diseased. You will have the corpses sent to you in a week’s time. I am glad to hear that you have traded those foul potions for the study of anatomy and healing.\nIf you ever require any more wisdom or help in the study, do not be scared to ask me. I have been your friend for many years, and your doctor for far more.\n\n\nSafe study,\n     Doctor Marrow ", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Augl", "The Wings of Justice", "Augl, raise wisps and inhabit fallen Undead minions. Make it look as if the Undead are attacking Petrus, kill as many as possible. Raise them slightly in awareness to our goal, but toss them off trail with a plot for their minas.\nMay Tahariae forever rule, Lord over Mortal Man and Deity of All.\n\n-Hosper and Jakir", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Cersi", "Malin Mikelson", "Dear \nCersi \nThe time we spend apart must come to a end . James is dead and you need to take his place as head of the Mikelson Family . as is your birth right . \nWhat ever might of happened in the past rember i am your brother . \nWith love . \nMalin", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Hanase", "Percival Staunton", "Dear Duke Barnabov,\n\nI would like to take this time to reject your proposal of a tax.\n\nThese are our lands, and lands of the Duchy of Vanneheim and the Mighty Kingdom of Oren.\n\n\nWe are staying here.\n\nI suggest that you rethink your actions, for they disturb the stability of Oren.\n\nI suggest you speak with His Grace, the Lord Marshall of Oren, Duke Vasili Vanir.\nRegards,\n\nPercival Albert Staunton\n\n[!] The wax seal of House Staunton is at the bottom of the letter.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Lilly", "Immortal of Soth", "[!] This appears to be a journal entry.\n-------------------9th of Sun's Smile, 1489\n-------------------\nThe air is damp as I'm writing this, thus causing the Caravan to mold. It's quite the unpleasant experience if I say so myself.\nThe Caravan is nearing the Dwarf city ... We hope to find better supplies there.\n\nI ask to you, Lilly av Huwaard, how the house past the Elven city is doing? How is Koehza ... Apollo?\n\n\nSincerely,\n\nTigre av Huwaard", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Malin", "Cersi Mikelson", "Dear Malin\n\nI have a request for you \ni need you to aqure these materials. \nWith love \nCersi\nCobblestone 1764 units\nStone Brick slabs 8\nOak wood 10\nCobblestone wall 98\nFence 67\nSpruce Wood slab 350+ ( 500) \nCobblestone stars 100 +\nStone brick stairs 10+\n\nDrop them in the mikelson manor in polas . \n\n\nI cersi hereby grant him entry to the mikelson manor At Market Street 8", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to the", "_Urasept_", "*the pages lay covered in blood*\n\nMy deepest apologies for I cannot return to Malinor for some time.. several bandits had broken into my home and attacked my fiance. I had managed to fend them off but paid a terrible price. I am currently wounded \nquite severly and will not be able to move for some time. I am currently laying at home with a good portion of my body cut away... But on the bright side my fiance and daughter are safe. I will return when my body is able, I am truly sorry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lewdness", "Lucion Sullas", "\n\n\n\n\n   The Dichotomy of\n       Lewdness\n\n\n\n\n\nby L. Sullas\n-Physical fraternization outside of marriage.\n\nThis despicable crime disrespects the very nature of the matrimonial union. Unmarried elves who physically fraternize disregard the purpose of intercourse, and cause of unruly\ndistraction, emotional disruption, and in the worst case scenario--consequences of bastardization, which is the most deplorable crime of all, considering it taints the reputation of an otherwise innocent Mali’aheral child.\n\n-Physical fraternization with a minor (a minor being any Mali below the age of 50 years old).\n\nChildren are indeed the most precious safeguard of our illustrious city. Subjecting the emotionally immature mind to such matters\nis utterly unacceptable, and it disgusts this writer that it need even be listed. Let it be known that Mali under the age of 50 are -unable- to give consent, as their uninformed opinions are too juvenile to be capable of discernment.\n\n-Fraternization of any intimate sort with impures, or other races\n\nPreservation of life itself resides in the idea of purity. To lay waste to one’s untainted Mali’aheral blood is a crime no less potent than murder of another\ncitizen.\n\n-Non-consensual physical fraternization\n\nLarihei is blind to you, desecrators of this law. It is beyond reproach. The city shall expunge you as a sick stomach does its vile illness.\n-Intimate fraternization of a homosexual nature\n\nAll who express intimacy in a public space with a member of the same gender should be treated as unclean, dirtying the sights of their fellows with such a display of uncivilized,\nunproductive lust.\n\n-Incestuous intimate fraternization of any kind\n\nNo self-respecting Mali will need explanation as to why this type of behavior is both obscene and illegal.\n\nby L. Sullas\nCopied from the Mali'aheral Law\n*a pile of paper is neatly stacked*", ""),
        StaticBook("Leyu's Cookbook", "Leyu Therenal", "\n\n\n\n\n~ Leyu's Cook Book ~\n\nPage no:\n3-6\nThe Simple Loaf\n7-10\nThe Simple Cake\n11-13\nShortcrust Pastery\n15-17\nPumpkin Pie\n~ The Simple Loaf ~\nIngredients:\n- Flour\n- Hops\n- Salt\n- Oil\n- Water\n\nInstructions:\n1. Mix the flour, hops and salt in a bowl.\n2. Create a 'well' in the centre of the mixture, then add your oil and water\n\n3. Tip the dough onto a lightly floured surface, then knead it until it's smooth\n\n4. Leave the dough in the bowl to prove, until it had doubled in size\n5. Mould the dough into a ball, then allow it to prove until it has doubled in size again on an oiled tray\n\n6. Then dust the dough in flour and cut across the top of the loaf\n7. Bake the loaf in a wood fired oven for 25-30 elven minutes, or until it's golden brown\n\n8. Leave the loaf to cool and eat at your own pleasure\n\n\n~ The Simple Cake ~\n\nIngredients:\n\n- Butter\n- An egg\n- Sugar\n- Milk\n- Flour\nInstructions:\n\n1. Using a small portion of butter, grease up the sides of a tin.\n\n2. Simply crack your egg into a bowl, and beat all of your ingredients together.\n3. Move the mixture into the already greased tin and level the surface\n\n4. Bake in a wood fired oven for around 20-25 elven minutes, until the sponger springs back at the touch\n\n5. Leave the cake to cool, then if you wish you may ice it\n\n6. Either dust the surface with sugar, or a mix of water and finely ground sugar for icing instead\n~ Shortcrust\nPastery ~\n\nIngredients:\n- Flour\n- Salt \n- Butter\n- Water\nInstruction:\n\n1. Place your flour, salt and butter into a bowl, and rub the butter in with yyour fingertips\n\n2. When your mixture resembles fine bread crumbs, add your water until it binds together\n3. Leave the pastry to chill for 15-30 elven minutes\n~ Pumpkin Pie ~\n\nIngredients:\n- Pumpkin\n- Pastry\n- Sugar\n- Salt\n- Eggs\n- Melted butter\n- Milk\nInstruction:\n\n1. Place the peeled, de-seeded and cut pumpkin into a cauldron full of water and bring it to a boil\n\n2. Leave the pumpkin to simmer until tender, then it needs to be drained and left to cool\n3. Roll out your pastry on a floured surface, then line a greased tin and leave to chill for about 15 elven minutes\n\n4. Bake the pastry in a wood fired oven for around 25 elven minutes, until the base is a light golden colour\n5. Combine your salt, sugar, beaten eggs, melted butter and milk and add as icing\n(( This is for RP use only, copied from Ahern's cookbook))", ""),
        StaticBook("License Book", "Deputy Thimble Clearwater", "Pumpkin-ing License\n-------------------Thimble Clearwater\n\nThis License Entails The Owner To:\nPumpkin Wearing,\nPumpkin Carving,\nPumpkin Farming,\nPumpkin Throwing,\nPumpkin Eating, and the use of Pumpkins as a ranged weapon.\nFishing License\n-------------------\n\nThis License Entails The Owner To:\nFishing in lakes,\nFishing in rivers,\nFishing in oceans,\nFishing in ponds,\nFishing in buckets,\nFishing for bigguns,\nFishing for Hobbits,\nCatching Squids.\nLicense License\n-------------------\n\nThis License Entails The Owner To:\nOwning Licenses,\nMaking Licenses,\nSelling Licenses,\nGiving Licenses.\nBucket License\n-------------------\n\nThis License Entails The Owner To:\nWearing Buckets,\nUsing Buckets,\nFilling Buckets,\nEmpting Buckes,\nThrowing Buckets,\nEating Buckets.\nAresting License\n-------------------\n\nThis License Entails The Owner To:\nArest Bigguns\nArest Halflings\nArest Animals\nBurn Munchkins\nConfiscate Things\nDetail Whoever he wants. Do Whatever he wants.\nThis License Book is only valid while in the possesion of Thimble Clearwater, Deputy of Summerset Shire. \n-------------------Thimble Clearwater\n3\"11 and 39 years old as of\n         _____ \n        /       \\\n        ||Deputy||\n        \\_____/\nThis License Book has been issued and aproved by Thimble Clearwater, Deputy of Summerset Shire. For the use of Thimble Clearwater, Deputy of Summerset Shire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Liches.", "Jakir Axem", "[ In eloquent writing the word Liches, is spelled out on the front cover of the book. The words striking and glowing a faint golden. Under it are the words. By Jakir Axem. It seems the writing glows brighter as you get closer to it. Inviting you in.]\n[What seems to be a man shrouded in black, and clad in a dark robe. Staring out at you, watching from under his hood. The hands of the man seem to be skeletal and he is flanked by two undead zombie like figures. The words under it.] \"A Lich.\"\n[For the rest of the book, the writing seems to return to normal black ink, with less time spent on the style of writing to help the reader to clearly see the writing and understand the lessons in the tome.]\nChapter one: Introduction.\n\nFor many years Liches have roamed the earth, we do not know where they first come from. But we do know they have been around for a very long time. I myself have killed a few, but they are not to be taken lightly.\nI was gifted with the power of gods, many who read this will not be, so I decided to make this guide so you may be able to fight them without the help of others. In this book you will find the information one might need as well as my own personal.\nexperience with these dark beings so you may better survive the next encounter you may have with them. It will only have the basic knowledge for we do not know it all, and do not wish others to try to copy in their dark arts.\nChapter two: The Lich.\n\nThe Lich is a creature made of dark magic, usually necromancy. At first they were thought  to of come from the dark power of Iblees. This is true, but those Liches are long passed, today Liches are made \nfrom necromancy and many a necromancer has tried to transcend into Lichdom. But you may wonder why there is not hundreds running around. It’s because the process is deadly and requires a lot of time and effort, and also the knowledge \non creation which has been lost to most. They use the power of necromancy to move a large portion of their life-force into an object referred to as a phylactery, this is their power supply, for it connects directly to the Lich in question. \nThe only problem being it could be hidden anywhere, so the permanent death of a Lich is unlikely but it also has a time it can live, due to the removal of life-force and the tether. The Lich will die in the end and it can’t stop it.\nChapter three: Combat.\n\nAs undead creatures, the main weakness of a Lich is gold. Gold is the bane of all known undead and as such. One should use golden weaponry over all else. Liches are unable to use necromancy due \nto the lost of most of their life-force and are also unable to access voidal or divine magic. But they are strong and smart. Bound to the will of the necromancer that created them but also free to do as they please otherwise. \nThey know fear and they will target the most dangerous person first. I myself have killed only a few, and they all have tried to kill me first. Only by me being ready was I able to stop them killing me and becoming their next victim. \nA few Liches are known for ranged weapons. Due to the lack of magic they use alchemy and bows. They are the cause of the Fringe Plague for it attacked me directly with a stronger version of the plague I was only just able to bat away in time. \nSome even wear armour, but they are made of bone and dead skin, so non golden or divine weapons are almost useless when fighting them. So be careful when facing them, they are not something one should take lightly and even more so if you are alone.\nChapter four: Personal experience \n\nI am a user of divine magic, and as such I have had to face them at their most deadly and worse. They tend to enlist the help of necromancers for extra help. As such I have \nI have had to fight the beasts of the necromancers and Liches. One being a monster made of young Mali children sewn together and made alive again with the vile magics. The lich that caused the Fringe Plague \nI had to remove after it infected most of Alras killing many and infecting many others. To which I had to remove the plague from. They are deadly creatures and some of the worst beings you can find, I hope you \nnever have to use the information found within this tome, for it is a true horror what these dark beasts will do to those who mealy get in it’s way, or if it feels like having fun.\nEpilogue: \n\nI Jakir Axem made this book to help others in fighting Liches, this book will no doubt be one of many, you can tell it is of my own design by the cover. . If it does not glow, then the book is just a copy. \nThank you for taking the time and reading this tome, I hope it helps you should the worse come to pass, and I hope that you never have to use it. This is part of the collection I shall be making on this subject, \nranging from as many dark beings I have come to fight, and find within the world. Thank you once again, and if we do meet out in the world, understand that what I do, I did by choice, and that even if you do face these things\n, you can move on and you are not alone.\n\n[Once again the fancy writing returns, the small signature of Jakir Axem written in golden glowing ink pulsing lightly at the end of the book.]\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Of Batman", "Claire Lockheart", "The Story Of Batman\n------------------\nEver wanted to know how this Batmanguy lived? Well, here's your chance!\n\nA book about his life as a human, and everything else..\nTo make a long story short, the history is basically that of a young boy named Bruce Wayne belonging to a rich family whose parents were murdered during a mugging in front of his eyes. The only things the young Bruce still had left were his enormous -\ninheritance and a loyal caring butler in Alfred. Throughout the years Bruce Wayne has grown to become one of the most proficient people in just about anything, mastering not only various martial arts, but also investigative techniques and just about any -\ntopic they teach you at university; he was a genius and a wrecking machine ((i came like in a wrecking ball hehe :P)) At one point, Bruce being obscenely rich and allegedly bored out of his mind, decided that it was time to rid the city of Gotham from the\ncriminal parasite which seems to have rotten this city to core. After considering his options, possibly having a debate with Alfred about his image choice, Bruce Wayne decided that he would don a costume themed after bats, and naturally he would be called\nBatman ((dundundun))\nAt his disposal is an arsenal of various custom-made batarangs - sort of like boomerangs, but modeled after a bat -, grappling hooks, bombs, and various other accessories.. all themed after bats ofcourse.\nThroughout his never-ending crusade against the forces of evil, Batman encounters countless deranged maniacs and murderous psychopaths all of whom plot to either take control or simply destroy the city of Gotham, a place where daily\nterror attacks against innocent civilians is something of a given. Some of his most renowned enemies include the now worldwide famous Joker, the seemingly Bane, the bizarrely seductive Poison Ivy, and Scarecrow who is incredibly close to coming of as a \nshady drug dealer hanging around schoolyards. It seems that every time Batman takes down some eccentric megalomaniac plotting to destroy his city, another takes his place in the blink of an eye\nThanks for reading!\nHope you enjoyed (:\n\n-- \nThe Story of Batman?", ""),
        StaticBook("life of Goblin", "Goblin", "rickrolled", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Of Thurak", "ilikefooddude", "The Life Of Thurak'Braduk\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Thurak has only had two times in his life when he was really, undeniable happy. Two meagre, short lived moments to look back on for the rest of his life that he can safely say that he was happy. \nThe first was long ago,\nin his early childhood as a Cub of Raurna and Ghazkull Braduk. For a time, he\nlived without worry; his mother was caring, (in an Orcish way of course) and his father was there for him, training him proudly in the ways of being an \nOrc, and teaching him how to wield his chosen weapon, the hammer. Till the fourth\nyear of his infancy, such was Thurak's life, without worry or need to worry, and the days passed quickly and pleasantly. \nThe ancestors must have looked down\non Thurak, though, the day his happiness was swept away, and decided that he was\nnot destined to have this life, carefree and happy. \n\nThe air was bitter and cold on that silent desert night. Winds blew the sand\naround into small willy willies which swirled around in endless, untraceable\ncircles.\n\n'STOMP' went the boots when they clashed with the sand.\n'STOMP' went the footwear of the Orc of the Ugluk clan. Looking, searching was one pair, on patrol, was the other. The stomping stopped, as one pair neared\nthe other. A voice came, booming from the mouth of the owner of the loudest\nboots. Quieter, softer, came the voice of the Cub in response. Looking, searchin, was the cub.\n\"Where is mother? Where is father?\"\nIt asked, to be replied by the slide of a sword from its\nsheath.\n\"Follow or die,\" Accompanied the voice of the sword.\nThurak folllowed.\n\n10 years, Thurak stayed. Positions were reversed. Once his clan, now his enemy. Once his enemy, now his clan. Why\nthey did not come, he knew not. He questioned them, but did not hate them. 10 years of belief being crushed.\nMaybe tommorow, he said before he went to sleep on the dirt floor, next to the\nempty bed of his new father. Maybe next\nweek, he soon was saying. Maybe\nnever. His hope was crushed. Happiness, now such a sad memory to behold.\nArriving at the gate, another traveller.\nThurak thought nothing of the darks skinned Uruk as he entered the gates of his unwilling home, paying no more attention to him than any other of the passing by Uruks. This one was far from home, but close to\nBlood. Unrecognised, he went, by his enemies, and by his friends, until alone he was, with Thurak.\n\"What clan are you?\" He asked.\n\"Braduk,\" came the response. A name Thurak had not heard for too long.\n Hope came then,\nrushed in, the flood gates of his heart now open. \"Take me back,\" he pleaded, answered by a yes. It sounded strange, a word of hope and willingness where the young cub had thought there was none.\n\"No welcoming party for me.\" Ignored,\nhe should have expected. It hurt more now, hope of happiness is the easiest crushed. Time rushed by, though not like before. Now he strove for attention,\nwhere once he had an endless supply.\nOne Cub, two Cubs, three Cubs. Thurak was forgotton in the crowd, truly more alone than when he was alone.\n\nAt 18, Thurak was tired of holding it in. His youngest brother, Gor, was\ntroubling his Rhino, swinging his axe down on its toe. Patiently, Thurak asked\nGor to stop, an axe, flying at him, was the response. Anger, hatred. It filled Thurak, and bloodlust\nCame upon him.\nIt was a good kick; his brother must have gone a few meters.  Again, Gor troubled him, another good kick. The third time, Thurak lost all of his precious inhibitions. His brother, the leech, who stole everything Thurak needed so dearly, had\nDriven Thurak deep into bloodlust. Gor must have seen this, and had retrieved his axe, sending it spinning towards Thurak's neck. It was a good throw.\nJust as Thurak was about to launch another powerful kick at Gor, in came Durakai, pushing Thurak away, \ndepriving him of his vengeance.\nLater that day, a clan meeting was held, over what to do about Thurak. Exiled?\nNo, Thurak himself thought he deserved it, and would have accepted the punishment without complaint. Instead, the second happy \nhappy chapter in his life beginning.\n\nHe finally had a mate, Dari. Soon, along came little Sharn, a beacon of light in his once dark world. ogether, with Dari, he taught her, as his parents had done with him, and she grew to the strong age of four.\nThurak never liked that number.\nHe woke up in his Blarg, stretching and yawning, finding no one else there, not his mate, not his Cub.\nProbably hunting,\nhe though. So he thought, until two days later. No one had seen them, not a trace nor a letter of \nWhere they had gone.\nMaybe tomorrow, he said each night before he went to sleep on the empty bed. Maybe next week, he soon was saying. \nMaybe never.\nHis hope was crushed.\nHappiness, now such a sad memory to behold.\nWith them too, the eldest of his younger brothers had gone. Nazdag. He missed him as much as his mate and child, though he did not know why.\nMaybe because they shared a bloodline, they were both in line for the position of Chieftain.\nTwo years, he went without seeing those three who he held so\ndear. Why they did not come back, Thurak didn't know. He didn't question them, he didn't hate them.\nHe loved them.\n\nAnother day, another scar; Thurak hobbled around the Uzg, his injury stopping him from walking at his usual pace. The Scabbernak's stinger had plunged into his right ribcage, causing quite a bit of nerve damage.\nA growing infection was hidden underneath the thick Rhino hide bandage, unknown to him and all around him. Once he reached the gate, though, he knew the pain of the walk was worth it. here, stood his brother, bigger, stronger than when he left, but still \nHis brother. \nOne down, two to go.\nHe would restore his family, whatever the cost.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-End Of Part One\n\n\nPart Two\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The last few years of Thurak's life have been the most bloody and melancholic of them all.\n\n\nFor fifteen years, Thurak searched for a hint, a glimpse, a whisper of advice\nto direct him to what he most wanted; his life mate and cub. For fifteen years, Thurak found nothing but dead ends and false leads. From Oren to Malinor, no news of the two Uruks, mother and daughter. The men in Oren blamed the Elves, just as those \nResiding in Malinor shouted claims of slavery in Oren. From them, Thurak got nothing. From the many he paid off; knights, street urchins, assassins, he heard nothing from. The nobles in their towers knew nothing, and so neither did the\nShady groups delving in dark alleyways, even when beated to an inch of their lives.\n\nThurak killed, questioned and pleaded, all for naught for ten years, before he gave up his dignity and asked the Dwarves.\nHe had expected the result, but was disappointed nonetheless. Riducules and insults were all that awaited him at the Dwarven gates, tempting him to an action he knew he couldn't take.\nFinally, after sixteen years of searching, Thurak would find what he was looking for.\n\nA small trading group, located on the far west side of the desert, was rumoured to be trading in slaves.\nSo close, all along, Thurak though as he approached the small groups of dimly lit tents, the trusty Zpidhammah raised at the ready. Seeing a sentry, Thurak ducked under a dune, narrowly missing the sweeping gaze of the torch wielding human.\nTrying again after the man had done his rounds on his side of the camp; Thurak paced into the camp, and started looking around for any sign of the two feuruks. There, after sixteen years, Thurak caught the first glimpse of his life mate and child, \nLying face down in their blood.\nSixteen years, ten minutes late, was one of the thoughts racing\nthrough his head during the mindless bloodlust that followed. Sentries screamed warnings, and men scattered as they realised what was happening. \nNone were prepared for an attack this late at night, and none could ever be prepared for the wrath Thurak brought forth that night.\nThurak stood, panting amongst the clearing. Three days after the battle was ended, no remains of the slaving camp remained, except for the two pillars marking the remains of those he so loved. Hands splintered and bruised, Thurak sat beside the graves,\nSighing.\n\nNow he could rest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Light Illusion", "Corvo", "Illusion from what we know is the use of the void to create images into one’s mind. How this is done is simple infact, First one must connect to the endless realm that is the void, A realm of nothingness and at the same time the Void is everything\nwe so wish it to be. Now let us continue, With the use of the Void we as Illusionists are able to draw an image within it, Whether it be a small petal or that of a gigantic demon.  Once an Illusionist has done so they must simply connect to the mind\nof their opponent and place the image that they have made into their mind. Allowing them to see what you infact have seen.  However one must note that whatever you are to create you must have seen or experienced in your life,\nYou can simply create that of a demon however what is the point of you do not know how it sounds or feels.  One is of course able to make simple images from what they can think of in their own mind\nas well it is possible to simply add a feeling or sense to said image. Now in order to start learning such a power that is Illusion people tend to start the same as most Mages, Connection to the Void.\nTo do this one must simply empty their mind of all thoughts thus creating a link to the Void, this is mainly done through the simple means of mediation. However some are unlucky in their attempts to connect as some might be rejected from it.\nWhen one is rejected by the Void they may feel a small headache occur or even be knocked out from intense pain. Now once one has connected to the Void they simply draw an image in it and thus try to place that image into another entity's mind.\nSome at this stage tend to try and place the image into the mind’s of animals as an animal's mind is weak and far too stupid to even figure out that what they are seeing or feeling is an Illusion. \n Once the simple sense of images has been completed Illusionists begin to head towards the Illusions of senses, Pain and touch. This is where some Illusionist find things to be tricky, As an Illusionist must feel and how what they are creating feels,\n that intends one must be able to survive intense pain if they are so wishing to create it. To perform these sensations. it is simple they must simply draw the image of pain inside the Void and place it into that of their target.\nSimilar to how creating images of Light work. After the Illusionist has played with senses they may now head towards their end, The Illusion of emotions. This is quite hard to do in fact. To perform it they do the same as before, \n however it is much more difficult to perform as if one feels happy than angry the next moment it won’t make logical sense as they will know it is an Illusion and it shall break.  The simple way to do this is to ease the Illusion in silently,\nHow this works is if one was happy one second, it is quite easy to cause them to feel the emotion of love the next. This works quite well however from what we know emotions can not be forced upon the target only eased in.\n As such we come to an end and now I leave the rest to you, The holder of this book. \n\n((For the Light Illusion Subtype))\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Light of Life", "Tippen Oaklend", "The Light of Life\n\nA poem by\n\nTippen Oaklen\nThe wooded ways shine with light.\n\nThe light unspoken from times of old.\n\nA light unlike the sun and stars.\n\nA light no man can meausre or count.\nThe light that shines from shore to shore.\n\nThis light which speakes only in hushed tones.\n\nThis light burns bright in all that grows. \n\n\nOne Light of Life should guide your path.", ""),
        StaticBook("Like the Tree", "Callax", "           -=-=-=-=-=-\n            I Am Like\n             the Tree\n           =-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nTrees are taken for granted; so much more is the tree than a reason for Druids to spread vitality. The tree is a symbol which has lasted since the dawn of time and which will last for eternity.\nThe tree assumes many elegant forms and an outstanding array of varieties, but it is stubborn. It is unchanging. And even while it is stubborn and unchanging, it is so forgiving and gracious.\nOne cannot rid of the tree. No matter the force, the blight, or the raging fire, the tree will overcome and retain vitality, spreading across the vast lands.\nThe tree takes little but gives much. Despite the actions taken upon it by unnatural forces or by ravaging races, the tree continues to provide with grace and plenty.\nIt is a tree with which I have life. It is a tree which I shall not leave the side of. And it is a tree with which I have a love I shall never hide.\nTimes do change, as do people and factions and nations. However, the tree is stubborn and it does not change. It continues to devoutly serve the natural world. I am like the tree.\n[!] On the final page, an intricate image of an oak tree with a wizened face on its trunk is sketched.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lil' Black Book", "Netphreak", "[!] This little black book holds poems it seems, neatly written.\n\nI've got my little black book with my poems in, I've got a bag, got a toothbrush and a comb in, when I'm a good dog they sometimes throw me a bone in.\nBreak this bittersweet spell on me, how did this come to be? A life shadowed in darkness, there seems not much to profess.\n\nAre we not one with the darkness? Have we not tried to escape? The mist, they haunt, but the Flower, she holds on.\nNo one knows what it's like to be hated to be faded.\n\nHis eyes are closed, his hood is down, the cool air flowing through his always messy hair, humming slightly the tune of his lullaby, given from his mother when he would cry. His back is---\nstraight, though his head is tilted, along with roses, most have wilted, he only think and wish of a dove, that she would come back, the one he did love.\nThe footsteps on the ice as she traveled so swiftly, cut through the air with his soft lullaby so --\nbriskly. The yuletide wish that he had given to the sky itself, would not be wasted upon himself, for that Maiden with long planium hair did appear, bringing along with her a face full of cheer. In her arms was her love and atune, was she that shone in--\nthe pale afternoon. As distracted as always she did so wander, right past him, in this moment would he squander?\nHe, hearing the sounds of the ice, opens an eye to see the love of his life pass by, confused and dazed, influenced by the cold air, he---\nbegins to follow her, the long planium hair. He shouted, for the years that passed by, he never counted. Struck with emptiness without his bride, how brittle was his pride. She had returned, he was burned and scarred, life wasn't too friendly with him,--\nlife had become dim and gloomy, but now she was here, he no longer needed to fear.\nStopping dead in her tracks the little elf's ears did flick, turning around to see him, his words did the trick. Though on her face the smile had vanished, through her --\nblank face you saw that she was soon astonished. Such sudden recognition from her was rare, but the flinging open of her arms she was there, running toward him with a break-neck pace to meet him finally with such an embrace. --\nHis arms open wide, something warm grew inside, with tears forming within his eyes, he can no longer conceal his cries, finally after years they were back together, the birds of a feather they flock with each other, such a warm embrace after years of --\ncold empty feeling, now once again can start healing. \"I love you.\" he says with no stutter, as the wind around them makes him shudder. for only few can imagine this fantasy tale, lest he be blinded and all else fail. With a warm embrace he looks to her--\nface, her beautiful eyes outbeat the sky, \"Let us no longer depart.\" he says with a soft tone, for his heart is no longer stone.\n\"So, then we stay here forever, to ever starve together?\" her head lifter up from being pressed in his suffocating tether-\nYou could almost not hear her words as she said it, they were muffled. In her eyes you see not much has changed, her hair was not even ruffled. Her beauty that was the same as it's always been, but you realize now that she was drenched. The way she---\nshivered while she clenched, was the faint desperate call for warmth, warmth that is that had left her from the climate, true this was in more ways than just one, had she done this for fun? The truth was darker that could be fathomed now, for surely he--\ncould not have her death be allowed.\n\"Never starve for we have plenty.\" he says as he presses his body against the shivering girl, things about to get much better worthy of a twirl. Just to be in her arms once more, is more perfect than the Malinorian---\nshore. The warm embrace forever ahold, never to let go, but cannot be foretold. Mystery surrounds this couple's presence, but without love there is no fruitful essence. For love is the only thing worthy of this bond, one of which he is so fond. --\n\"Let us live our lives with peace.\" he says to the races, not caring about the hostile faces. To the depths they stride, forever until their final ride.\n-------------------\nEyes, like a Sea of emerald, hair white as the Northern snow, this Flower grows-\nquickly, spreading her influence across Anthos, this delicate red Flower, so confident in her power.\n-------------------\nThe Nightmare himself has nightmares, waking in a cold sweat day by day, only hoping for an escape at bay.\nLittle girl, I wish that you can see the beauty is within your heart...\n------------------- [!] A new form of handwriting is seen [!]\n\nNire zuretzat maitasuna indartsua da, bakarrik bada zuk ikusi izan bide horretatik.\nZer egiten dugu, ez da nor garen... Haunt duten Nightmares du ziur asko gainditu ditu..\n\nEzin dugu exekutatu gehiago, zergatik ez bakarrik besarkatu?\n\nFind the joy in your life, eventually you will start to heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lillian's report", "Jacob Chapel", "Upon one evening in the Deep Winter; two men were seen milling around the town fountain, their appearences unknown. The pair  then went on to speak to young girls and women alike, seemingly posing as healers or physicians of the sort. After a short while,\none of the two offered to heal a young injured woman, who kindly denied, but was then drugged and carried some distance from the town, to a blocked off cave and was tied in chains. The woman was asleep for some time, and what happened next in unclear,\nthough the pair seemed to have been practicing some sort of dark art, chanting wildly. The woman awoke soon after, and a spell was cast that she would only remember their names and actions. The two men, one reportedly called 'Hanz', left her against a\nrock where she stayed until a young man found her. She was safely returned to the Capital, and seems to be unhurt.", ""),
        StaticBook("List", "Regent Toby Williams", "Harrison Geminine\nSaik - Kha woman\nAislinn", ""),
        StaticBook("Litches", "Colette Blake", "LITCHES:\na lich is an immortal being, they obtain it's pseudo immortality through the usage of philactories. The philactory is a place where the lich holds it's soul. It rediates it's mana and it's soul through the husk of \na body that lich has chosen as it's host. Liches can only be destroyed if their philactory is destroyed.  Liches have hostile tendecies, however they remain peaceful as to not create suspicion of their existence, since they cannot stray far from their \nphilactories for they become weaker the further they get from their philactories. \n\nAs a mortal nears a lich's philactory, they feel weakness. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Little Bird", "Zane Capette", "Little bird! O little bird!\nI wonder at what thou doest,\nThou singing merry far from me,\nI in sadness all alone!\nLittle bird! O little bird!\nI wonder at how thou art\nThou high on the tips of branching boughs,\nI on the ground a-creeping!\nLittle bird! O little bird!\nThou art music far away,\nLike the tender croon of the mother loved\nIn the kindly sleep of death", ""),
        StaticBook("Little Dove", "Phaedrus", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nMountains may round to hills, rivers may descend into canyons,\n\nLong winters may fade into windy chills, yet despite all that time, I would never find a better companion,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nSoft whispers that tickle my ear, softer lips that soothe my skin, \n\nHer touch pierces me like a spear, replacing love where fear had once been,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nShe is the tinder to my spark, the hammer to my blade, \n\nMy source of light within the dark, the reason I have remained,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe trees move with the wave of her hands, the grass sways with the rock of her hips, \n\nThe wind tosses her hair in curly red strands, skin warm as sand against my fingertips,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nHer words are sweet and ease my mind, make me smile and laugh and experience love, \n\nMy hope is these words answer hers in kind, for these words are for my little dove,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n      To the love \n       of my life,\n         Elorna\n\n\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=", ""),
        StaticBook("Little Gifts", "Lelien", "\n\n\n\n\n    Little Gifts\n\n    by Acaele Lazul\n\nLittle gifts that bring good cheer\nTo ease your mind when I'm not near\nFor all the good you've done for me\nThat I'm a little too blind to see\n\nAlthough my thoughts are kept inside\nI always walk upright with pride\nTo know that you will always be\nThe only one always for me.\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("LK and the Drake", "Drake Lancefeld", "- The lady from the north, her shining sword, and the great dragon... -\n\n\"Wandering amongst the flames of her fatherland,\n\nher mournful tears wreathed the snow in sorrow.\nScattered to the wind, her love lost in the war past.\n\nEnfeebled and ruined, disaster would sweep across the world,\n\nit's eternal protectors laid to waste by the invaders.\nA blackened shadow comes from above, winged and terrible, cracked and blazing.\n\nThe blonde haired heroine faces the demon..-\"\n\nThe book stops there suddenly, followed by a note**\n->\n\"Translated from an \nancient Hansetian \nmourning song of the\nAnthosian era - eternally remembered.\n\n- Drake Lancefeld, 10th of the Sun's Smile, 1511", ""),
        StaticBook("LMJ - I", "Luthon Leyu'ilum", "LMJ\n\nLuthonian Medical Journal\n\nBy Luthon Leyu'ilum\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-\n\nSkin, tissue, or flesh as it is usually so referred to is an essential part of any mammal. \n\nThis particular journal will be written somewhat hastily,\ndue to my confinement in a Haelun'or cell due to accusation of copulation with a Mali'ker (A crime of which I am currently innocent.)\n\nMy first observation is flesh's innate weakness. If you have ever bitten into a fruit such as an apple, that is about\nthe amount of force nessicary to bite through Elven memberanous tissue. Orcish, Dwarven, and Human tissue have yet to be directly tested.\n\nI have thus been working to impliment a new medical training procedure without potential detriment to sentient\nhealth.\n\nI call this method \"apple stitching\" due to the fact that it involves literally stitching the flesh of an apple together.\n\nThe idea that initially lead me to this comparison, though not to apples specifically, I dare say that was complete chance;\nwas the comparisons between mamillian flesh and a fruit. Both house a juicy pulp within them, exuding liquid in a ripe gush when cut or bitten into. Both also have the specific purpose of holding the bag of nutrients together while in motion or under\nsome form of stress.\n\nThe procedure itself involves the incision of a needle to the supple flesh of a ripe apple. Your incision should not elicit a spray of juice or tear the surrounding skin.\n\nNext you must push the needle through the top layer of the\npulpy interior, pushing it back up approximately an inch away to meet outside of the skin. Continue this process. If the skin rips at any point in the procedure, you are stitching incorrectly.\n\nSecondly, the skin of an apple works as an applicable tool\nfor the training of precise scalpel incisions. This reduces our need to further harvest mamillian flesh or cadavers for medical study, saving any aspiring surgeon a great deal of time, effort, and money.\n\nDragging a scalpel along uneven and slightly\nrounded surface of an apple is equatable to cutting along a mammal's chest or torso, which tend to be slightly rounded in nature (particularly in females).\n\nI suggest you cut apples whenever you are about to eat one, holding a ruler or like tool along the\nincision to make absolute certain that the process is correct.\n\nDo this multiple times until you feel confident you can do so without thinking about it, and then you are ready for actual bodily testing.\n\n-End Journal I", ""),
        StaticBook("Loan Reciept", "Zane Capette", "Loan Reciept:\n\nThe bakery will pay Stebern 2 minas for each piece of wheat.\n\nThe bakery recieved 64, and will pay 128 minas to \n\nSTEBERN\n\nas soon as possible.\nSigned: Zane Capette", ""),
        StaticBook("Locks", "Roopak Khalin", "Hi can someone please lock my trapdoor in my Agriculture shop behind Valdeg's one. The trapdoor is in the corner.", ""),
        StaticBook("Log Book", "Phaedrus'Yar", "Five sets of chainmail\n\nWarhammer - 6D 40%\n\nWarhammer - 6D 36%\n\nMace - 6D 50%\n\nBattleaxe - 6D 46%\n\nBattleaxe - 6D 36%\n\n\nMace - 7D 46%\n\nBattleaxe - 6D 46%\nProfits:\n\nChainmail - 170+ minas\n15 minas base commission, five minas for every 20 minas additionally made from a single set. \n\nWeapons - 6D - 200+ minas, five minas for every 20 additionally made from a single sale.\nWeapons - 7D - 2000+ minas, no lower price, no exceptions. \n\n10 minas commission for every thirty minas increased from a single sale.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lonely Fisherman", "Arthur Caulfield", "\n\n\n        The Lonely\n         Fisherman\n\n   A short literary\n        Piece\n\"Now I don't know a whole lot about fishing,\" he confesses. \"For twenty long years been trying. They don't even notice when I cast my line into the water.\" \n    The fisherman sat alone on a boat, in the middle of a dark blue ocean that said nothing back. \n\"My bait must be cheap,\" he muttered. \"Must be me bait.\" His face scrunched up in thought. \n   His hair had started to grey, his wrinkles had become more defined. Each day it became harder to get out of bed, though he did not blame this on age.\nAfter a while the water began to ripple. Soon it gently rocked the side of his boat in waves. \n   Looking up the fisherman found another, just like him. He waved to the man in a friendly manner but was ignored.\n   Curious, the fisherman watched.\nThe man in the other boat threw his line in after a few minutes of preperation, and within seconds had caught a fish. \n   \"How unfair,\" the old man mumbled. \"Been fishing in these ponds for years and ain't caught a damn thing.\" ", ""),
        StaticBook("Looking Up", "Laura", "\n       Looking Up\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        -Laura\n    This is a tale about a badger, a badger named Sebastian. Sebastian lived in a hole in the ground, where he always looked down. And although some creatures might think that kind of life depressing, Sebastian relished every moment the familiar soil was\nabove his head. But then one day, something quite odd happened. As Sebastian awoke from a short nap, he noticed his family had up and left the hole. He roamed about the hole many times over, in search of his family, without a trace. Completely puzzled, he\nstared at the exit to the hole for a long time, before finally deciding to crawl hesitantly to the surface. Once he arrived, he looked about, spotting his family in a cluster near some flowers, all looking up. Sebastian meandered over to them, asking them\nas to why they left the hole. Sebastian's mother looked at him with starry eyes, and pointed up to the sky. Sebastian, having lived underground his entire life, had never thought to look up; once he did, he knew why his family had left the hole. He saw\nfor the first time the starry night, with the moon in the sky. The sight rendered Sebastian strucken with its beauty, and he remained there with his family until the break of dawn, where they found a modest abode above the soil, and Sebastian never looked\ndown again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Hope", "Amras Ancalimë", "Chapter One: Problem\n\"Immortality, a blessing but also a curse they say, I simply state that its an obscenity that never keeps my sanity at bay. Everything important slowly disintegrating away into ashes, that were once a well collected heart that could \nSING! Gone, ravaged into a dissapated state, only to re-occur when the feeling dawn. Need some new experiences, emotions, if only there were some differences. Stars.\"\nChapter two: Solution\n\"Stars. A bastion of hope that could free me from these bars. Brightening the night, not being able to reach so frightening. The induvidual emotion of each star is an endless fuel, keeping me going through the days like an exhausted \nmuel.\"\nChapter three: Realization\n\"I'll never reach them. Its a hopeless endeavour, lastin forever. Whats beyond? We'll never know, because we've been sompliy conned. Imprisoned within our realm, left to simply envision.\"\nFor this life without end, isn't a life at all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost journal", "-", "I earnestly love master, I really, really do; however, when he makes me do things like this, I want to strangle him. “Shovel the bodies down here” “No, there is not enough space, take them all up again” “Hold this limb while I inject this” “Go pick some\nmandragora”. Oh, how I hate picking mandragora! It is a painstaking process! Not only are they horrible to locate, but even the mature ones make you dizzy!\n\nIt gets worse! The voices, the fiends, the ghosts, the crypts! I spend more time in the crypts than in the mansion! I have become a gravedigger! The worst part is the ghosts and their voices. Oh, how I abhor those wretched creatures! \nI have told master many a time to employ the services of a cleric, but he is too lazy! \nDamn ghosts… they sometimes knock me over, fling me off the sairs, and one event tried to strangle me in my sleep! My room looks like a pantry: bags of salt, strings of garlic, bundles of sage! Yet even those do not keep these devilish fiends away!\nI cannot sleep, my eyes are bloodshot… and the voices try to bid me to do horrible things. “Kill your master” they say “Eat his heart” they say. What wretched real-estate this was to construct a mansion!\nI do not think master is doing well either. He is showing signs of insanity. It is probably all of those dead bodies he reanimates, like a necromancer! However, his morals are just. He reanimates dead bodies to test his potions on instead of doing so on\nthe living. I am surprised that someone as ardent as he would hold back. To my understanding, testing this ‘Panersea” on the living would be much easier than testing it on the damned devils we create daily, but he holds back as not to harm the living.\nBy harming the animated dead, he saves lives. He does not save our sanities, however. \nThere are these four creatures. They scare me. I refuse to go near them… and I hate when master makes me feed them. They have the worst whispers. They make friends with the most violent ghosts. I do not know how much longer I can take. \nI feel myself slipping away. The thought of killing that damned alchemist makes me happier...", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v1", "Unknown", "It seems I no longer have the skills I once had, or at least the ones I seem to recall having, once upon a dream. As a matter of fact, my skills are so far dwindled, I have difficulty with even the weakest o f monsters. As well, my ability to draw a bow\nis weakened. I can barely draw the string taut. But that is not the least concerning of my weaknesses. Aside from the consistent night horrors which plague me when I sleep, it also seems as if I can no longer practice my \"craft\" as it were. The\nloss of my powers and my skills are a surprise to me. I can remember vividly the last few hours I spent before I....wound up, here. But I am beginning to become confused, disoriented. Instead of attempting to discern why this has occurred, I have\ndecided to focus on the task at hand. I will blend in with these peoples, and hopefully, in my work, I will find the answers to my questions.  ", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v2", "Unknown", "I feel my skills are increasing, ever so slowly. They are nowhere near the level they once were. But I do feel stronger now. I, along with the Lord of Whisper Isles, have begun something of a quest. We and our two comrades, a dwarf and an Elven\nambassador, are searching for a tome. Having found the first tome here in the Whisper Isles, we now seek to find the second. It is said to lie in the High City of Laurelin, home of the elves, and concerns \"The Lost Ones.\" However, after searching the\nlibrary at Laurelin, we found nothing. The Elf's High Prince himself even assisted us, but to no avail. Yet I have seen many things, which soothes my soul somewhat, the great structures of the capital of Oren, and the beauty of Laurelin. But while these\nsites bring me pleasure, as does the knowledge I found in Laurelin, I am still yet uneasy. I feel as if I have...forgotten something. A feeling of foreboding, and confusing. If what I have read is true, then there is not much else in this land beyond\nwhat I have seen already. The home of the orcs, and the dwarves, I have yet to see, yes... But if what I have read is true...then it is not possible for me to have come from where I recall as my home. Now I lie awake and ponder, is it the history and\nknowledge of this world that is wrong? Is there perhaps something beyond it that these people are unaware of? Or...is it I, and my mind, which have failed? I will seek further answers to my questions. I cannot accept that the powers I once\nyielded, and the people I knew... And these...injuries I sustained, are mere figments of my imagination.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v3", "Unknown", "To know anything at all is to know nothing at all. After all, the very act of being a sentient being is to know that there is an obscene wealth of things you do not know. I've walked headfirst into this wall, this problem, many times now, and it blocks\nmy advance in this world at nearly every turn. I've kept quiet about the memories that I seem to have in my mind, about the things I have done, and the wars I have fought, and the things I have lost. And most importantly, about the vivid details I have\nof the time right before my arrival here in the Land of Aegis, and the man I met directly before it all went black.. Of all my memories, of fighting, killing, surviving, living, loving, those are the most  vivid. But whether what I remember was\neven real...*the text here is blotted out by some sort of dried up, red stain, which seeps through onto the next page* :: I've still no idea where the book of the Lost Ones lies. It doesn't matter. More important things have come up. I've run into a\nstrange man in the Isles. He is, by all accounts, and even my own, a Wizard. I learned this first hand when dear Rinscher, my dwarf friend, irritated the man, and he shot us both with lightning. While I can understand wanting to smoke his pipe in\npeace (Though I would have enjoyed a smoke as well), it did seem a bit of an overreaction on his part. No matter. I saved an elf later that same day, a woman named Aerovine. I had been passing through Kramoroe when I heard a few\nfellows yelling things along the lines of \"Kill! Go out, loot!\" in their home. I hid in the alley and watched as one of them, armed, left the small hut. I followed him quietly along the road to Oren, never getting too close. We passed armed men he paid\nno mind to, then came about the Elf woman. Hardly armed, she immediately ran as he attacked. I ordered for him to stop, to surrender. Alas, he did not. I was forced to slay the man. I escorted the woman, with her thanks, back to the Isles and the road\nto Laurelin. It seemed all roads pointed to Laurelin lately. An expansive library, an educated people... Although, there were a few of her residents whom I have had trouble with...", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v4", "Unknown", "My physical health has deteriorated as of late. I do not wish to go into details, but regardless whether or not my memories are fact or fiction,\nit seems the injuries I sustained are all too real. But what is worse than the physical pain is that which\nkeep me moving when it grows almost too much to bear. I wish to find out the truth, or at least a hint to it.\nI ran into the Wizard again. But what caused our meeting is what I sit in Diplomat Lafthi's home, waiting to explain. You see, I decided I\nought to move to Laurelin. It has been...calling me, it seems, for far too long.\nWhen I arrived, I ran into the elf woman I had rescued before, Aerovine. She was gracious enough to show me around the town to any properties for\nsale. I found a home I liked quite a lot, which suited my purposes well.\nPlenty of room for the piles of books I would like to accumulate, but sadly, outside of my meager price range. Aerovine however, has a kindness which knows no bounds. Or\nperhaps she is simply Virtuous enough to not know the sin of Greed. She offered to give me the money I needed to buy the home, and after some insistence on her part, I accepted, and promised to pay it back (And pay it back I shall) Afterwards, I went\nback to the Isles to turn in my Guard Uniform.\nI did not tell the others of my ailments though, and only mentioned them to Lord Tyrion. I will continue to defend people on the roads, make no mistake. A few events occured, but afterwards I\nheaded to Laurelin and purchased my new home from High Prince Native. It seems I was not the only one eyeing it. An elf named Elvador and his brothers Had also hoped to buy it. I'm afraid I got there first, though. They were not upset though, which\nmade me glad. Aerovine assisted them in looking for an apartment, when Elvador mentioned something to me as I was about to leave. On his way back from the Isles, he had heard of a plot by a group of Orcs and Elves. This plot was the kidnap the Queen\nof Oren and overthrow the Orc Leader.\nI could scarcely believe my ears when I heard it, but I knew I had to act. I sent Elvador and Aerovine to tell their High Prince, while I set out for Oren. It was as I passed through the Isles,\n\nlooking for a guard to tell my tale to, that I happened upon the Wizard again. And oh, how it vexxed me!!! He weaved and bobbed, moving quicker than light, perhaps even teleporting. He commented on the rain and mumbled to himself....and oh, how I\nwished I could speak to him, to ask him if anything I remembered could possibly be true. But I felt my wounds clawing at me, and I knew I would not last long before I had to rest. I had to reach Oren before then.\nThat duty came before my own\nwishes. So I apologized to him, stated I wished I could speak...and left. I know not if I'll run into the man again. But I had to deliver my message...", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v5", "Unknown", "As I reached Kramoroe, I ran into Sergeant Urg of the Isles' Guards. I quickly told him what I knew and bid he be on his way quickly, as would I. We parted, he for the Isles to warn Lord Tyrion, as the Isles sit dangerously close to Orc lands, and I to\nOren. But I ran into one more acquaintance on the way. A man named Dalejin. We had scarcely talked, only exchanging a few words on a pleasant basis before, but still I liked and trusted the man. I felt he could be trusted. So I told\nhim what I had to say This proved to be a good idea indeed. It seems Dalejin is a close friend of the Queen. So off we went to Oren, to find her and her guard and warn them ourselves... But...we could not find any of them. Not a soul of use in the town\nwas there. I felt my wounds again, and knew I had to leave for Laurelin before something happened. I left Dalejin to deliver my message, and headed back. The Wizard was gone from the Isles, as I expected, so I didn't even stop. I arrived in Laurelin\nagain, after a time, and collapsed in my house. Well, I assume I collapsed. I blacked out, you see. I woke up there many hours later. When I was lucid again I went out to the library to begin some work. But I ran into Lafthi on my way, which was good\nluck as he has not heard of the plot against the Queen and the Orcs yet. So I went into his office as he took care of some business, and here I wait. I can only hope he returns soon, as I feel that journey has taken more of my strength than I originally\nthought. I will continue this journal once I have informed her of the situation. wished I could speak to him, to ask him if anything I remembered could possibly be true. But I felt my wounds clawing at me, and I knew I would not last long before I had\nto rest. I had to reach Oren before then.\nThat duty came before my own wishes. So I apologized to him, stated I wished I could speak...and left. I know not if I'll run into the man again. But I had to deliver my message...", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v6", "Unknown", "I've come to the Pathfinder's new base in search of information. It seems that he has lost perhaps 3 men to banditry, and I wish to know their names.\nZevandir is one who left to become a bandit. Tailon left, but is an Elven Lord, so Kalen does not\nbelieve him a bandit. I've come here after informing High Prince Native of\nthe dangers at hand. He is quite kind, and more willing to assist me in finding the culprits. The Black Guard was started by Zevandir in hopes of converting the\nPathfinders to\nbandits. That is why I saw Val the Pathfinder claiming himself a Black Guard. Val was supposedly tricked, and Atles has agreed to vouch for him that he has\nchanged his ways. The Pathfinders are still, and always shall be, loyal to the Prince\nand the nation. Lord Atles serves in Lord Blackthorn's stead. Until his return. Lord Atles claims he found something far north of the boundaries of Oren. Some sort of dark village, with lava at the gates. But I do not know if I believe him. Pathfinder\nKalen states that town is only the town of North Alister. Kalen reports seeing strange, dark beings walking about, with cloaks pulled about their faces. Could these have been members of the Dark Brotherhood Lafthi mentioned? Kalen is a bit hard to\nunderstand, but he claims a group of the cloaked individuals Attacked Laurelin at some point. Present here are Swift Elf Alenom, Pathfinder Kalen, and Lord Atles. I've run into many of the Princes of Laurelin at Ravenhold, and the HighGuardian,\nMayctor He claims the Dark Brotherhood are no threat. He refuses to tell me how he knows of this fact, which I find very suspicious. Mayctor has informed me the Brotherhood seeks alliances with the \"do-gooder\" guilds. Could they be behind the Cripsons\nassault on a Holmes fellow? I'll have to talk to Lafthi. Macytor is a worshipper of Iblees, this much must be true. He cannot be allowed to get away with this. He guarantees the safety of the elves, on Iblees' name.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v7", "Unknown", "I grow increasingly frustrated As Prince Toren commented, \"Spider webs within Spider webs.\" I have stumbled head first into these webs, and now I am stuck. I've determined no more about my past, but that matters not now. This plot I mentioned reaches\nfurther than I imagined, clawing its way into nearly every race in Aegis. I have confirmed that this plot is being perpetrated by the Dark Brotherhood. They wish to see the empire of the humans fall, and likely the Orcs as well. It seems they plot to\nattack within the next month. Elvador also made mention of a portal they wished to create. Inside lie some sort of monsters that the Brotherhood wishes to kill. It seems the elves are the ones most manipulated by this evil. The leader of one of their\narmy branches, the Sentinels, is a worshipper of Iblees. High Guardian Mayctor... He is evil, yet his intentions appear good...he wishes to protect the Elves. So he assures me that Laurelin will remain safe, and that the Elves will not be attacked. What\nhe has done to gain this assurance, I do not know. But I believe he may be a threat to the High Prince, if the Prince decides to act against him. I have found a new ally in the Pathfinder's current leader, Atles. He also believes a great evil is\ncoming...but I will believe that when I see it. For the evil he predicts is far greater than that of what the Brotherhood could manage.  Had I the strength for it, I would go to the North, where he claims to have found a small, dark\nvillage. Yet this same village his associates say is part of Oren. But as I have mentioned, my condition worsens by the day. As I spoke to Mayctor in Ravenhold, I was prepared to fight him should he strike me. Yet in truth, I do not believe I could\nhave held my sword up. Prince Toren, who I had met at Ravenhold along with two other princes and the Princess, agreed with me that Mayctor seemed quite mad. I sent him with a book of my notes to deliver to Native, in the event I was attacked. All\nturned out fine however, and he has become a quiet ally of mine, as the other Princes are far too blinded to see Mayctor's true face. Mayctor claimed he had information I sought, but refused to tell me. He also told me that only one other knew of\nwhat he did, and that he would never talk... In addition, Atles told me that some of the Pathfinders that had deserted had become bandits. I will have to see if they have anything to do with this matter. But for now, I've but one lead... a name Lafthi\nand Prince Loren both told me. An elf by the name of Rolok, who supposedly lives in Laurelin. I must find and speak with him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v8", "Unknown", "As I ran down the King's Road towards Kal'Urguan, Mayctor always at my heels, that devilish cackle of his ringing through the air, I began to wonder to myself... Where, or when, exactly, had I gone wrong?\nI realized it was a moot question at\nthat point...I had bigger problems to worry about. Namely, the High Guardian, who I feared was drawing ever closer. But now that I think upon it, I realize it is quite obvious. I relied too much on others, and the assistance they gave. I should have\nworked for myself, done all of my research myself. I should not have involved innocents, like Prince Toren, or Atles...whom I can only hope is safe, after disobeying orders in order to assist me... But I am ahead of myself. I suppose I should start at\nthe beginning.\nI believe I had mentioned Mayctor in my last journal entry, though I have lost count of the volumes and being away from Laurelin, am unable to check the numbers. But I will assume I have mentioned him, my suspicions about\nhim, and the whirlwind of evil which seems to have engulfed the Elves of Laurelin. I will assume that I had also mentioned the Dark Brotherhood and some of their possible members. Now, I will mention the new threat that has emerged...the Undead. I\nfirmly believe, now more than ever, that Mayctor had something to do with them... That the Brotherhood at least works alongside them, if not for them. I had just finished a meeting with the  Pathfinders, along with other allies of mine, including\nDalejin.\nDalejin had left back to Oren with the news I had given him, of Mayctor's involvement in the scheme to kidnap the Queen. I believe he reached the capital in time, right as there were shrieks of horror from the North which we in\nLaurelin did not hear word of until a messenger came a bit later. As soon as we had heard it though, we left. I and a number of the Pathfinders, including Atles, headed North. Unfortunately, in my condition...I did not reach Winterfell,\nor Alstion. I am ashamed of this fact. I nearly collapsed on the road, bidding Atles to go on ahead. Yet, he returned a short time later. He had made it to Alstion, but had been ordered back to Laurelin by High Prince Native. I left with him. He told\nme what he saw, of the Undead and the chaos, as we left. When we reached the gates of Laurelin, Mayctor was standing there on top of them... Looking down on me.... I lost control, screaming at him.\nHe had to have had something to do\nwith it! He hated the humans...He sought our end. But he only laughed. I refused to enter the gates of Laurelin at that point. I would not be inside the city with that...devil. I headed to Kal'urguan after that, to make sure the dwarves were prepared.\nA merchant by the name of Algor told me Hiebe was preparing the army for war, and that he was making axes for Hiebe, but had run out of wood. I went to get him some, knowing it was the least I could do. As I headed back, I ran across a group of strange\nmen, one of whom bumped me off the road. All of them wore white robes...I had no time to question their intentions though. I can only assume they were some foolhardy, arrogant Templars. Or some other guild which thought it could defeat this evil\neasily.\nI returned to Laurelin after delivering the wood to Algor. Mayctor was no where in sight...I attempted to locate him, but failed. Then Princess Araina announced she was going to the Capital to help the wounded. I could not let her\ngo alone, and I knew I had many spare supplies I could deliver. So we set off with them. The whole of Oren was chaotic. I found Dalejin right upon entering and we gave him what supplies we had, for the soldiers. As many arrows as I had and iron for\narmor. An uproar started suddenly, the guards yelling about an escaped prisoner. One of the Undead, apparently. I ran off to search the city, but coming up empty handed, returned just as the guards were escorting the Queen up to the\nKeep....when I saw him. Mayctor, hiding in the crowd. I yelled at him and he immediately ran for the gates. I gave chase, but he leapt off the road and I lost sight of him. I desperately wished to follow, to capture and question him....but I dare not\nleave the Princess alone. I found her and we went to the Keep together. She mentioned some kind of Traveler who was going to escort her back to Laurelin. We found that Traveler in the Throne Room, causing a ruckus. He was apparently trying to convince\nthe Queen to come to Kal'Urguan, to hide. She refused, and the guards grew angry, attempting to arrest him.\nHe fled quickly, and then the escaped Undead was discovered. Dalejin, I, and the Princess moved the Queen to the Barracks, as\nshe requested. I left them there to speak, while I went to look around the city, mostly for Mayctor. I knew he was still hiding there somewhere. But then the Princess sent word that she sensed something happening in Laurelin. I immediately found\nher again and escorted her back to Laurelin... But not without running into the Traveler again. He refused to go to Laurelin with us, and the Princess refused to go anywhere without speaking to him first. By this time we were accompanied by 2\nPathfinders. So I took us to the Whisper Isles. I still had access to the Guard Barracks there. The Princess and the Traveler spoke privately inside for some time, then without a word, we left for Laurelin. When we arrived...well, I\nhad no time to rest. Mayctor was skulking about, odd as usual...then a man pulled me aside.\nI recognized him. Relok. One of the possible members of the Brotherhood... He wished to know what I knew, how much of it, what I knew about Mayctor. He\nclaimed to be a spy, who was sent to spy on Mayctor. I did not believe any of it. I refused to speak to him, and he threatened me. I do not remember the exact wording, but he ordered me to tell him \"Or feel the wrath of the Dark Brotherhood.\"\nThe Princess pulled me aside then, right as Relok claimed there was no such thing as the Dark Brotherhood. I could not comprehend what he was up to. Was it a plot to discredit me? To fool me? To drive me mad? I found out quickly what they wanted from\nme though. The Princess wished to speak to me in private about my....condition. She is quite observant, unfortunately. But I did not know what was the subject of our discussion until we reached a quiet place.\nBut before\nthat....Mayctor followed us. He crept along, hissing and making odd noises, half bent over all the while. We finally got somewhere quiet and had our conversation in whispers... And the Princess told me I should leave Laurelin. That it\nwas dangerous. That she had overheard word that the Brotherhood wanted me captured. That was when Mayctor came across us. And the Princess bade me, no....commanded me, to flee. And flee I did. I ran as fast as I could from Mayctor as he yelled for\nme to halt. Claiming I was under arrest, and cackling. As I neared the gate, one of the Princes joined him in his attempts... I could not believe he had tricked them, too. So I screamed at the Pathfinders, who guarded the gate, to open it. While the\nPrince yelled in retaliation to keep it closed. Someone, I do not know who, but someone whom I owe my life to finally opened it. And I ran out of the city. But I am injured, and slow. The young Prince caught up to me easily, as did Mayctor. I\nthought all lost. The Princess had commanded me not to let Mayctor catch me, no matter what. But I could not attack the innocent Prince. That was when Atles, my savior, arrived, demanding an explanation. Mayctor claimed I was under arrest for\nconspiracy, and Atles asked for proof... I could not stay any longer.\nI yelled an apology to Atles, then ran. Now we return to the beginning of the journal... I ran down the road from Laurelin, Mayctor cackling behind me. As I entered the\nKing's Road, I thought I saw someone familiar, up in the trees... But no. Even if it was him, I could not expect him to assist. I reached the Isles, then hung a left, running as fast as I could. I believe it was at that point Mayctor's cackles seemed\nto fade... But I could not be sure. My blood was pounding in my ears. I ran past the marketplace I had met Agnor at, down the trail... Until I finally reached Kal'Urguan and began banging on the gates, demanding to be let in. And directly behind them\nstood the Traveler, whom the Princess had bade me to meet when I arrived, saying he would help me, and I should tell him all I know. I was allowed in and we quickly retired to a private room. I told him of Mayctor, of the Brotherhood, of my wounds, of\nthe Princess... When finally the story was done, King Charles came upon us. He graciously offered me his protection…\n...ah, I drifted off. I'm afraid there are more people here, including...the Princess? And one of those men in the white robes....", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal, v9", "Unknown", "I have not felt this way as far back as I can remember. My head is cleared of my maladies, as is my body, and I feel...alive. There are many things which lead to this, and many unfortunate occurrences. But I will not bore the world with my past. It\ndoes not matter any longer. It is only the future, to which I look forward to, and the skies of Aegis which I look to for guidance.\nI will not, no, cannot explain how it came to be. But Hwaldar has played a large part in my recovery from the pits of\ndarkness. I remember not of my previous memories, which were revealed to me to be fakes. Only my recent time in Aegis lives on in my mind. I have been\nvindicated, in a way, by what Hwaldar revealed to me. It was never intentional to make me the way I\nwas, a half-full shell of a woman. It was merely necessary, to defeat evil and to spare my life. But that is not a story which needs to be revealed. The past is gone, done, and far away. Now, I search for my next calling. I was correct in my remembrance\nof my former powers, that of magic. I wish to regain those powers now, to help fight the undead and the other evils which plague Aegis. I am setting out now, on a new journey. I wish to gain more knowledge, as much as I am able. I also hope my leaving\nMalinor will draw some of the evil that haunts it to come after me. But it matters not. I feel strong enough to take on anyone who attacks me. And I will continue to protect those innocents around me, as well. I will cease to chase after my past and\ninstead chase after my future. So I have written it, and so I swear to do. I will not allow evil to corrupt me as it once almost did.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Journal,v10", "Unknown", "I've come across an interesting concept as of late. The premise of it is quite interesting. And it is quite in-depth for such a simple matter. To explain it initially is simple. The concept is that of\nequivalent exchange. The idea that you cannot have\nsomething, from nothing. You must first give up something of equal or greater value. But it is much more complex than that....and has a greater impact on the current situation than it appears. I will write more on this subject as I continue my studies.\nBut I believe it may be very useful against the undead…\nI have travelled quite a bit since my re-awakening as it were. I cannot help but take advantage of the fact that I feel well, and alive for once. I had the pleasure of speaking with Arcane Mage\nSlayer at Laurelin the other day. He's quite the gentleman, which was especially useful when that idiot Rinscher was buggering me. He was able to cast a spell on him to ward him off, which hopefully scared him away from me. Which is good, considering\nwere it not for the Monks of the Temple, Rinscher would have succeeded in killing both King Perea and High Prince Native, though I am more upset about the latter of the two. I've also travelled to Alkhazar again, take a...less travelled route, and met a\ngroup of travelling merchants who go by the names of various sins of man. I would have no trouble with them at all had one of them not sought fit to threaten me on the rooftops of Alkhazar. (I have become a bit enamored with running atop the\nroofs, I am embarrassed to admit.)\nParanoia is still at a dangerous high in Alkhazar. I can understand it, to an extent. I myself do not trust many people at all. Though I have been trying to judge people on their actions, not how I\nsee them. Yet my instinctive judgments have usually been correct, so far. Now I have set out once more, to the Valve. I have passed through before, but only now have been given a proper tour by the Grand Champion, Whurili. They seem to be well prepared\nin the event of an undead invasion. But when I first arrived, they and a few orcs were discussing alliances namely the idea that orcs and dwarves would ally, and humans and elves...but against whom? Each other? I will have to find out as much about this\nas possible. But for now, I've decided to begin officially leaving my old life behind. Or, atleast, the agony and bitterness I had because of it. In a symbolic gesture, I have decided to leave one of my journals hidden outside the Valve. I have all\nthe valuable information from them written down elsewhere. But there is no longer any need to try and recall the false memories which once plagued my mind. I leave part of my insanity here, behind me. And still, I look forward to the future and the\nseven skies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Letters, ??", "Unknown", "An unsigned letter written in careful hand. It seems to be a copy of the original.\nYou are well aware that the archives in Malinor are locked and that I am not authorized to grant you access to them. Access to the Archives requires the permission \nof a majority of Archmages as well as the express permission of the Arcane. Indeed, the Archives cannot even be opened with his presence and assistance.\n\nIt is insulting you presume I would be naive enough to\nbelieve your claim that this serves the Guild's purpose, for it would be obvious even to the most unlearned of apprentices that this serves no one's purpose but your own. I do doubt you truly wish for the Archives to be open, for to do so\nrequire your informing the Archmages of your newfound habit of pillaging and defiling graves, graves the inhabitants of which you do not and could not truly know.\n\nYou are chasing nothing more than a fantasy and I\nurge you to abandon this quest of yours, llir. I would not use such abrasive language, had you heeded my words when last we spoke at the last gathering. Your words are lost on this one, as I will not assist you in this vanity. Your\nfor I cannot grant it.\n\nWith respect,", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Parchment", "Unknown", "*a single sentance seems to be repeated throughout a single big parchment many times. It seems to have always about the same caligraphy.*\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\n\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.Order of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.", ""),
        StaticBook("LOTS Glyph", "Noach Hughes", "Luck of the Sea Glyph\n-------------------\n\n0 = Gems\n-------------------\n\n\n  00  0\n0    0\n  0 0  0\n\nBasically a fish shape.", "")
