        StaticBook("Unbreaking Glyph", "Argothin", "The Unbreaking Enchant\n-------------------\n This glyph makes it so armor and weapons 'strengthen' so to speak. The tools with this enchantment dull slower, and can take more damage before needing repair or breaking.\nGlyph\n-------------------The location to put gems on the enchantmen table to make this enchantment.\n-------------------O = A gem on the table\n----------------------O-O---\n----O----\n---O-O---", ""),
        StaticBook("Undru's Notes", "The Lord of Undru", "One will always come.\n\nIt never dissappears as long as the Sildur is up in it's hands.\n\nWe won't die.\n\nIt's not the End\n\nWe are the End.\n\n\nDeath is only the start.", ""),
        StaticBook("Unification Act", "Jacob Chapel", "Articles of Unification\nAs Issued Upon the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1477\n\nSection I: Realms & Culture\nSection II: Assurances\nSection III: War Council\nSection IV: Unification Terms\nSection V: Imperial Codex\n\nSection I: Realms & Culture\n1. Realms of Oren are to draft, adhere, and uphold their own provincial laws, whilst in adherence to existing Imperial laws.\n2. Realms of Oren are permitted to engage in territorial growth, independent of Imperial Influence\n3. Realms of Oren and their vassals are permitted to engage in foreign conflict alongside other nations, granted the Empire holds no stance in said conflict, such as in cases of rebellions in foreign nations.\n4. Realms of Oren are permitted to establish a realm-specific Knightly Chapter, in accordance with the Grand Knight’s powers and the Chivalric Code.\n\nSection II: Assurances\n1. The Electorate shall never be suspended or interfered with by Imperial influence, the duties of Emperor never to be passed on hereditarily.\n2. The wide-spread cultures of Oren shall never be infringed upon \n\nin name of Cultural Unity, whether by majority or minority, recognizing that the cultures that make up our Empire are vast and equal.\n3. Realms of Oren and their vassals shall never be targeted or ostracized for the formation of federations, \n\nwhether political or economic, so long as such formations act in no way treasonous to the Emperor and the well-being of the Empire.\n\nSection III: War Council\n1. The formation of a War Council, composed of all recognized marshals of the Empire, to ensure cooperation between martial forces.\n\n2. The formation of an Imperial Militia, composed of all Knights, sworn blades, levy-men, and militia of the Empire, to ensure a defensive body exists for the quick response to threats.\n\nSection IV: Unification Terms\n1. House Rovin and their vassals to join the Holy Empire of Oren, their existing territories made the Realm of Aesterwald.\n\n2. The Realm of Aesterwald to be recognized as the cultural heartland of all Northerners,\n\ngranted the right to be lead by their titular Konig.\n\n3. The streamlining of all Houses of Nobility, whether of Aesterwald or the Crownlands, in accordance to the Imperial Codex.\n\n4. House Rovin named as Duke Elector, to reserve a seat and vote within the Electorate.\n\nSection V: Imperial Codex\n1. The Imperial Codex to be drafted post-haste with the appropriate input and revision by Noble Lords.\n\nSignatories:\nVoron Rovin I, König of Aesterwald\n\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion, Emperor of Oren", ""),
