        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Journal\n                     of\n           Jacques Vaudrie\n\nDay 1\n\nI went looking for a job and found a bishop who wanted chairs to be delivered to him, I was then tipped off that he wasn't worth the pay. I questioned the man, who then gave me a job at Vanderfell. From then on we went to some sort of battle.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Mead:\n-Fáóláín Honey: A pure, simple mead, made from honey fermented with water, and nothing else. For The traditional mead lover.\n-Fáóláín Blue: A sweet mead, flavored with delicious blueberries.\n\n-Fáóláín Summer Mead: A tangy, refreshing mead, flavored with summer plums.\nAle:\n-Fáóláín Winter: A strongly alcoholic ale with a pleasant apple-like taste.\n\n-Fáóláín Spring: Best served on a hot day, this ale is weak, but refreshing. It possesses a somewhat bread-like taste.\n\nWine:\n-Fáóláín Silk: A rich merlot with a soft, velvety tannin and the bold taste of blackberries. Great for your more refined customers, It was my specialty back at my winery in Alras.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alchemist fire flamethrower\n\nKevin 2.0\n\nBounce Pad\n\nMake a gigantic slime.\n\nHealing salve?", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§9§89th of §lThe Grand Harvest§r§8, 1941\n\nJournal entry: 1\n\n§oToday the Orvars and all of Nezzera, including an odd bunch of invites from elsewhere, were invited to a feast within the Nezzera Keep. Other than the fact that we now live amongts the people\n\n§8§oof the Faolains now, that were once sworn enemies by there words (Due to Morvan of Orvar making Thorvarder, the leader of the Faolain, bend a knee to him from an Aesterwald order, as we were once mercs for them), are now allies. Allied pagans uniting\n\n§8§oas brethern amongst the rest of the world. The feast hall was-... extremely crowded beyond liking. So I chose to depart and remain at the camp site. Funny how the Faolain offered us the very same land we once lived on.\n. . . Fitting-.\n\nThe sun is\n\n§§§o§8§ois setting and nightfall comes.. Gorund's silver eye comes to watch as we are made to prepare for the rise of The Fallen One...\n\nThose we call Carrions are Raevir, now.. Amyas hunt 'pagans' and 'heathens'.. And Akovia is their new land. Petrus has\n\n§8§obeen over-run with Raevir... and it seems nowhere is safe for us that believe in more than one god..", ""),
