        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "SHIPMENTS§0\n§0-------------------18 bottles of Pale Ale§0\n§0126 minas at 7 apiece§0\n§04th of the Amber Cold§0\n§01497§0\n§0-------------------           SALES§0\n§0-------------------Benkowski Dystov§0\n§01 bottle of Pale Ale§0\n§08 Minas§0\n§07th of the Amber Cold\n\n          SALES§0\n§0-------------------Peter Horen§0\n§01 Bottle Of Pale Ale§0\n§01 Tea§0\n§020 Minas§0\n§021st Grand Harvest§0\n§0-------------------Elijah Alister§0\n§01 Bottle Of Pale Ale§0\n§010 Minas§0\n§09th Sun's Smile§0\n§0==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "§bViktor 'The Grizzly' Dustin", "§l§oDear Viktoriya Vladov,\n    §r§oI'm sorry that our whole meeting got off on the wrong foot, with you abruptly being told that you were to marry a stranger, on top of the fact that the stranger looks more like a bear than a man. I personally wish we had\n\n§omore time to talk with one another before my patriarch, and your father had declared this marriage to occur. In this letter, I'd like to adress a few things that you had asked me during the heat of the moment. First off, I'm sorry that my lack of\n\n§oinvolvement with the military is something you see as disgraceful. I'll be sure to try and correct that by enlisting with the levy so that I do not make you feel as if I am a useless man. I tend to stay away from militaristic activities, not because I\n\n§l§r§§§r§oam a coward, but \n§3§0§obecause I had other duties to accomplish, such as my position as Warden of the Woods of Aldersberg. Hopefully you can understand this, and do not judge me too harshly for it. I also wished to comment upon the remark\n\n§oyou made about me joining the Order of Saint Amyas to become a 'man'. I am quite certain that I am qualified to call myself a man, even though I do not partake in the usual battles and skirmishes that seem to plague the roads daily. If being a person\n\n§ois quick to draw their blade and rush out to attack other beings, then by that standard, I am no man. Though, through my work and through my mental capabilites, I'm certain I'm as manly as any who would rush out onto the battle field. This concludes the\n\n§oreflection portion of this letter, and I hope it's contents are adequate. Moving on, I'd like to state a few things about myself, as to break the metaphorical ice between the two of us. I am a well-learned man, as you might've noticed by the contents of\n\n§l§r§oletter, though it takes me quite some time to get my thoughts out in the middle of conversation. I might sometimes appear to be distant, but keep in mind that I §ldo §r§otake notice of things, and try to correct them. \nAnother thing about me is\n\n§othe fact that I enjoy hunting with my companion, Barnsy. I'm certain that the two of you met, considering the whole ordeal today. I'll keep in mind that you dislike dogs, having just found out today. But, nontheless, Barnsy's companionship when out\n\n§oand about is something I cannot change, and thus must inform you about it. A third thing about me is that I enjoy carving wood in my spare time. Maybe, should you wish, I could carve a wooden bust of you if you decide to enter the Alderswoods. It would\n\n§obe a nice activity to do together, no? Anyway, a fourth thing about me is that I dislike very sweet foods, and apples. I don't understand the taste of them, but I know that quite a few people have taken a liking to the funny fruit's taste. If anything\n\n§othings like meat and stews are much better. Nothing beats a long day of logging and patrolling the woods like a mean stew of mushroom soup with venison chunks. And lastly, another thing about me is, my favorite animal is the bear. Since I was a young\n\n§oteen, I've been called many things, but the one name that stuck with me is 'Grizzled Bear'. It is oddly fitting, once you stop to think about it, as I do quite often. Thats about it for now, Viktoriya. I hope your opinion of me has changed atleast a\n\n§olittle. \n\n- §lGrizzled Bear", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*this page seems to all be smeared and scribbled*\n\n*scribble scribble*\n\n*smear smear*\n\nThe End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Evelina's Diary", "§bEvelina Rovin", "3rd of Sun's Smile 1503~\n\nI've picked up this new diary from the book store this day, since my old one was rather broken. Several papers sticking out the book cover, as some claw marks occured yesterday, due Noni's bad mood. Anyway,\n\nI'm glad to have a new one to write in. It was Margaery's wedding today, as it would've been a total disaster for me, since I was rather late to the wedding itself. I had some troubles getting the teal corset on, as my arms were too short to reach the\n\nstrings to secure the corset with. I was already running late when I picked up this dress at Lorin's, as it costed me another two hours to get ready. Athelstan went early, since he was the one decorating the Horen castle for the wedding. Shame. Upon\n\narrival, I was surprised that the rings weren't exchanged yet. Apparently, I was not the only one being late. As I entered, I saw many familiar faces around the church, as Lorin was the first one to appear in my left eyecorner. Though I was really\n\ntempted to come sit with her, I was already  commited to sit next to Athelstan, since he was the one inviting me to the wedding. The wedding went well, as I almost saw Athelstan shedding a tear. It must've been a big surprise for him that all of his\n\ncousins were married, and he wasn't. The feast with the Vladovs after the marriage was a rather horrid place to be, as Karl's commotion wanted me to stab his leg with one of the few daggers I have in my possession. Though luckily, I didn't. Athelstan and\n\nI left the feast, as we both were intented to return to Werdenberg. We walked our way home, as we had a small chat occuring between us two. We haven't seen eachother in several months, and haven't gotten the chance to actually get to know eachother, as he\n\nwas burried inside his office downstairs. The conversation was quite pleasant, as I know much more about him now. He suddenly made a stop in his pace, as he gazed into my eyes. His hand was running through my curls, as the other was holding mine. His\n\nvoice lowered, as he was almost telling me a secret by the tone of his voice. He came closer, as the gaze remained. \"I truly see your beauty now, Lady Rovin.\" These words came as a shock to me, as it was one of the better shocks I ever experienced.\n\nHe pulled me closer to him with the hand he was holding mine, as the other moved towards my cheek. Our chests made contact with eachother. I couldn't describe the feeling I had that moment, as it was the most pleasant feeling I've ever had in my whole\n\nentire life. He lowered his head, as his hand lowered towards my chin, now gently placing his lips upon mine. I was speechless, while our kissing would've lasted forever. My first kiss, which was absolutely splendid! A broad smile pulled the corners of\n\nhis mouth. I believe he shared the same feeling that I had, due the broad smile on his face. He grabbed my hand, as we continued our way to Werdenberg. We crossed this large hill with a deep river glinting down the hill. He embraced me, as I felt\n\nweightless in his arms. \"Can you swim?\" He said, as I immediately knew that he wanted to spring into this river from this hill we were standing on. \"U-Uhh, no..\" I said, while I was peering down towards that river, seeing how deep it was. He took a firm\n\ngrip around my waist and arm, as he pulled me with him in his arms, down into the river. My face must've been horrible, since I'm absolutely afraid of heights and of water. He pulled me immediately back to shore, as we remained in the water for a mere\n\nmoment. We were playing, as his kisses runned from my back, to my neck. I knew that I was in love with him that moment, as I'd never leave him ever again, not even for father. I enjoyed every single minute of us spending time together.\n\nWe still remained in the river, as a sigh rolled down his lips. I saw that he had something to tell, and that it was difficult for him to say so. \"I think that this time is rather fitting, for my question that I have to ask you.\" I was intrigued, and\n\nalmost anxious of his question, as I fell silent for the time remaining. His hand went to go and grab something from his pocket, as it was a small box, nothing more. \"I must say, I'm in love with you, Lady Rovin. The hours we've spent today was priceless,\n\nand I'm happy that I've shared them with you. I cannot imagine a life without you any further than now.\" He said, while he slowly kneeled down, while he moved the box infront of me. \"Lady Evelina Rovin, will you marry me?\" I was speechless, /again/.\n\nI felt every little nerve in my body tingle, as a loud gasp was the only thing I was capable to say. I moved my hands infront of my mouth, jumping up and down lightly, as the water slowed me down by it's gravity. I nodded my head in a rapid pace as my\n\nrespond, as an broad smile crawled onto my face. \"Yes, yes!\" I said, as my gaze drifted towards the small box opening, as a beautifully shaped ring revealed, having a diamond in the middle. He slid the ring onto my finger, as I immediately embraced him\n\nshortly after. I felt that we both were happy, as I cannot wait until our big day occurs! I feel that my life's complete, as I've never experienced myself being that happy once in my life.\n\n10th of The First Seed 1503~\n\nI can't be more disappointed at Carr than I'm already am. It was his wedding today, and actually took the effort to wear something else than Lorin's dresses. They were wonderful, and absolutely\n\nmagnificent, but I needed something different and had to keep my hands away from her wardrobe for a while. I wore this butter yellow dress, with a silken lint flowing over my arms. It looked gorgeous. I'm blessed to have Azel to my service. The wedding\n\nwent well, as Klara, Lorin and Karl were the only Noble figures I saw. The rest were some dear friends from both Carr and Savannah, I suppose. We all took our departure towards the North. Hiebenhall, or Siegrad now, has gotten some major changes due the\n\nlast few years when I was in Werdenberg. The wall that I used to play on with Klara is demolished, and replaced by several building. They look rather.. unique. The feast occured in the tavern, as many drunk men were singing along the chants from the bard.\n\nMe, Klara and Karl were burried away in the corner with our cup of water, since they didn't serve tea in the tavern. Shame. The singing stopped, as Madam Colborn had an 'important' announcement to make. Apparently, she became impregnated before\n\nthe wedding. Father always taught me to never 'spread my legs' before marriage. I respected his command, as I found it an absolute disgrace for Carr. I admired him, and saw him as my own brother. A shame that I lost all my respect for him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Amber Cold 1493§0\n§0Queen Mary set out on an adventare through the kindom of Celeridia! She tried to find tha cassle that was stoln from her befor and she coldnt find it BUT! She found a big bensalk! She climed it and it went hier and hier till she got to tha\n\ntop of it n ther was a cloud wif tuleps n dasies groing! It was kinda spoky caus she was so hi up but she wsnt scare! Kuro was a bit scare but Mary calm him and after xplorin she climed back down tha benstalk and jumpd into tha watr down ther. She stil\n\nxplored til she got back home n went to bed§0\n§0THA NEXT DAY...§0\n§0Queen Mary went to tha cloud templ n went down tha road to a bulding that said RED ROSE TAVURN and she went in cause it was kinda colt and she herd somun talkin bout how tey wanted to\n\nchange tha world! Mary tried to spek up and tel her she wanted to change tha world to but she was talkin to gownups and ignared her fur a bit. She got sad but kep talkin. Eventaly she was goin to lead tha grop to the bas of where tha world changer were\n\nand she wantd to go wif and the lady said yes and they walkd back to tha cloud templ and then cros a brige and a demon yeled at tem to stop but they kept goin and excapd and then they went to tha snowy forsty place and went thru and then the orngey montan\n\nplace and climed over tha montan n then jumpd down n they were there. they werent demons so mary intduced hers and one of them said ther name was Kuro an Mary said he wasnt cause Kuro was Kuro. But his name still was Kuro and he was nice and so was\n\nGuarar Art and Selen, those ar tha othr peopl, and Mary looked round the place and ventualy went home aftr joinin their 'demons r bad' group.§0\n\nAmber Cold 1493§0\n§0Sam day, Jko wants to c tha benstalk so Mary goes to show him. They ventuly found it aftr seein tha towr ner it n jko said he thoht it wasn real at frst and she was a bit pset but she was fine aftr. Jko began to clim. Mary climed aftr n\n\nthey got to tha top of the cloud and mary warned him bout the holes n he fell in un like a butnukle and tried to get out but got stuk and slowly fell. i knew he was gonna go splat so i told him goodbye n he fell n then he CLIMED BACK UP cause he dosnt die\n\nand he landed in the waterer and the hole is realy deep but i want to try it so if you find this thats why, i regret nofin! well i dint do it he coninced me not to and now the rabit dols are callin me n im seein little specks n im scared im scared mary's\n\nscared she doesnt want this mary's scared [The girl's handwriting from when she started talking about her hallucinations to now would be very shaky.] scared scared scared scared i dont know what to do kuro help me kuro please stop them k- [The ink slid\n\noff the page.] sorry book! ok so then i told jko about the rabits n he piked mary up n jumped off to tha watr! splash! n then we went to find the casle but what we found was an emty feld were it was. i cryed a lot n looked round what was stil ther. a tiny\n\nhouse with a few secet spots but still no casle. im really sad. that stupid kardel irongut. that stupid stupid stupid DEMON. i will find him! well i gues thats all the advntur for tday so byby for now!\n\nDeep Cold 1493§0\n§0Quen Mary went out to try to make frends with tha peple of tha oter kindoms round Atera and she gave them bread caus she had a lot she took from a fesivel and gave people round the places tha bread cause she had nuf to eat and she went in a\n\nplace n saw to peple seting a demon strat and Queen Mary gave everywon but the demon the bred and stayd to watch §0\n§0they kep tryin to get the demon to tell the truf about what demon made them come there and it turns out to be... actuly i dont care hahaha im\n\ngonna leve this is boreng§0\n§0so queen mary went to petryus and she was goin to give bred to peple in armor but more people in armor came and ther was a lot of scremin and the peple with the armor that mary was bout to give bread to died. lotsa blud. so mary\n\ngave the life peple the bred and went on her way. she met lots of oter pepl and then went back to tha cloud templ and went to tha place she went last mont§0\n§0she was goin ther and she endd up in a toan and she herd mis Selen and they were talkin bout an\n\nalince and they went back to the place and talked.§0\n§0and they talked n it was borin and mary went to the place outsid of thera and then woke back up in her body n talked to selen caus she was bore§0\n§0they left n eventl came to tha spring\n\ngove n queen mary met princes mirabelle and made frends wif her and then there was a demon n queen mary stud up to him and he used firy magic to burn queen mary. It hurt so badly. Mary tried not scream in pain but it was too much. But she still stood her\n\nground. Eventually the flams dispered an miss selen took her to the inn and then ran into gofrey horin and she talked to him and made frends and talk bout being queen of celeridia n he said ur magesty and bowed n said she needs a jewl for her crown and he\n\ngave her a small bag and in was a prety blu-y gem and she was very happy n said thank yu a lot and then went on her way to tha equalist base\n\nSnow's Maiden 1493§0\n§0Quen Mary talked to Isbela and stuff n then she went to jkos tree n woke him up n he fel out of his tree. tday we wil go to tha Relm of Eqality n then go bak to tha Kindom of Celeridia§0\n§0so the relm of eqality was empty so they went to\n\nvorapoolool n talked to selene for a bit and mitras blew smok lik a dragen and it was werd now the to will lok round celeridia§0\n§0nothing is diferent but somun name william built a fort so rude well talk to him and then we went to tha vilage n beanstalk.\n\n[A drawing of three people is put here, a smaller one between a male and female form. The drawing is very childlike.]§0\n§0Suns Smile 1494§0\n§0spendin tim at tha new equlis base. now mary is bore§0\n§0[A doodle is scribbled in ink over here with a caption 'woops']\n\nDeep Cold 1495§0\n§0hi! ben a wile! borin adventur today. lonly.§0\n§0[random doodles of adventures are here] i wish i had a colorer§0\n§0also i met to ghosty peopl on dint talk and on was nic to me. peopl arent nice to him so i am! his name is mister aeglos... and well\n\ntwo orcs kiled the othr n im sad.§0\n§0[The previous pictures have been colored in with red, green and pink.] TEY HAD COLORERS§0\n§0[Pictures of red suns, mary with ink black hair and her green dress, and other doodles are here] im so hapy\n\nmis ros gav me anoter bok for colorin! My drawins wil b ther!", ""),
