        StaticBook("Elements of Mind", "§bFarley III Stafyr", "Elements of Mind        -:- 1 -:-\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr.\n\nUpon the writing of the Theorem of Wisdom, my very own mind came to the conclusion that there must be more to it. Every person knows\n\nof elements such as fire, earth, wind, or are and lightning. But aside from the external elements which we can feel and use, there are also other elements in a completely different range, of which we unknowingly make use and into which we tap, without\n\nrealizing it.\n\nThe Elements of Mind.\n\nThe mind is a strange frabric, giving us the ability to think, to consider, to act, react, to learn, and to remember and many things more. But the mind itself, such as the outer world\n\nwe experience, has its own elements. To underline this, an example will be given.\n\nFeelings. Feelings, such as love, guilt, hate, happiness and many more. This is one of the mind, we are able to use it, express outselves with it, to tap into\n\nthe power of this element. Further explanation is not necessary, I presume, as everyone has at least one feeling within him.\n\nOther elements do exist. Wisdom is one of them, as I aforementioned.\n\nAlso knowledge and experience are elements of the mind. But there are more!\n\nConcentration, Purity, Peace and Balance, and Common Sense.\n\nHow each of these work, will be explained in further\n\nupcoming books. For the element of wisdom, I refer myself to my work \"Theorem of Wisdom\" for further information. The book \"Knowledge and Experience - Elaborated\" may give additional hints about two further elements.\n\n-:- Primary Edition-:-\n\n\n\nCopied directly from an original text within the archives of House Stafyr by Farley III Stafyr.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting Glyph", "§bLorien Vesitza", "Unbreaking:\n\n[]  []\n  []\n[]  []", ""),
        StaticBook("Sillumir Conduct", "§bAndria Ith'ael", "§lSillumiran Conduct and Regulations§r§0\n\n\n              \nBy the Maheral\n§1Andria Ith'ael\n\n         §l Index§r§0\nPage III (hael)\n  Preface\nPage V (kulin)\n  Cooperation\nPage VIII (esun)\n  Valah \nPage XI (telu'oem)\n  Mali'aheral\nPage XVII (telu'laier)\n  Avernan \nPage XX (niut'telu)\n  Kharajyr\n\n      §l Preface§r§0\n  Our situation within the new citadel is very different from the times of Annil'sul. We are now within a new land, and while located with our allies. Due to this, the Sillumiran are in need of regulatons to allow us to continue to\n\nprogress. The children of Larihei shall be safe.\n\n  These regulations shall take affect on the 17th day (elkarin'telulaier) of the Amber Cold, in the year 1475. \n\n \n §1~Maheral\n\n     §lCooperation§r§0\n  As per our new agreement with House Savoie of Aldersberg, who are the owners of the land e currently reside on. We are to provide milltary assistance if they request it.\n\n  If there is trouble\n\nwithin their town or land, it is your duty to assist them in the removal of the trouble maker - or threat. \n  You are to cooperate with the guards of the town if required, if you do not trust them, then consider the fact that they gave us\n\n a home.\n\n  However unlikely, in the event of a war, we be obliged to provide to help both House Savoie (and House Carrion) in their battles. The Maheral is of the opinion that assistance will not be required often.\n\n       §lValah§r§0\n  As we now live within the lands of the Holy Oren Empire, more specifically the land known as Aldersberg, it is going to be a common occurence to see a Valah approach the gate. Members of both House Savoie and Carrion are to be\n\ngranted entry if requested.  This also applies to any other member of governence within Aldersberg or Oren.\n\n  The typical proceedure for allowing a Valah entry to the citadel is simple. Simply inquire as to what their\n\nname is, what their business and/or reason for entering the city is and what weaponry they are carrying. If they seem suspicous or a resident of another nation other than the Holy Oren Empire, further questioning may be needed.\n\n     §lMali'aheral§r§0\n  The Maheral wishes that only the uttermost pure Mali'aheral enter the citadel. The proceedure to allow them entry is similar to that of the Valah, however additonal questions are required.\n\n  Upon the new arrival approaching the gate, one should examine them for strange eye or hair colours, excessive jewelry, or tatoos.\n\n  Examples of 'impure' traits or signs of Mali'ata include dark coloured hair, red or black coloured\n\neyes, golden jewlery or a severe amount of tatoos. \n\n  It is recommened you do not kill such beings, for we are not on our own land. Instead, let them be unless they continue to approach the gate after being denied.\n\n  If they are indeed physically pure, you may begin the mental purity test on them. The first question to ask is simply 'Thill ito kae'leh?' or 'Are you pure?' You may provide a translation of the question in Common if they are not influent in the\n\nElven language. \n\n  After they have sucessfully answered the afforementioned question, you may begin to ask about our society, questions such as 'Who is Larihei Lomanih?' or 'What does the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya mean to you?' are adquate questions to provide to the new comer.\n\n  If they sucessfully pass, you may them entry. Though let it be known that the Maheral may overturn your judegement.\n\n      §lAvernan§r§0\n  Avernan - simply meaning 'wanderer' or 'confused person' our language is a term created to group those who are not permitted the citadel without the permission of the Maheral or are banished from our blessed society.\n\n  Avernan include Mali'ame, Mali'ker, Bortu and Uruk. All of which, with the exception of the Mali'ker or a some group of Mali'ame, are to not be granted at any time. Not even the Maheral may grant an Uruk entry.\n\n  If one of the\n\nafforementioned beings requests entry, you may contact the Maheral for judgement of the situation, for there are few who are not associated with the nation of Laureh'lin.\n\n      §lKharajyr§r§0\n  Kharajyr, much like our allies in the Holy Oren Empire, have not betrayed us. Therefore, as they once lived with us, they are to be granted entry as the Valah are.\n\n  They shall be\n\nsubject to the same regulations as Valah, though they may need to be protected better due to potential dislike of Kharajyr displayed by the Valah.\n\nay'Haelun'or Larihei'ehya\nay'maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n  Sillumiran, always remember your sacifice and your vows. Protect the children of Larihei.\n\n§1~ Andria Ith'ael, Maheral of the Mali'thill", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Eat shit", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "My Journal§0\n§0\n§0These pages are not in order of date. These are made when something interesting happens. I will now start writing the exact date.\n\nProlouge:§0\n§0 You won't remeber how you died. I or Maya will put it here:\n\nDay 1,§0\n§0 Am I falling in love with a human? This can't be true can it? I thought racial preference fordided me from loving anyone other than my knid. Perhaps it's not love. If it is, she has someone else. Besides, I have Maya. I don;t need anyones love...\n\nother than hers. But, still. If Metzali, did this to me, why? Wait, her song! I heard it, and her mother said. Then that makes sense. I just have to hold out until she gets with Gorn. Maybe it will pass then. I hope so. Or I'm doomed to lose another...\n\nloved one.\n\nDay 2,§0\n§0 Well that was intersting, I just spied on a woman, scared her, and she seemed to be eager to be alone. Well, if the dead version of me reads this, stay in your lane. Some people aren't ready for a relationship.\n\nDay 3,§0\n§0  I realized not too long ago I don't lose all memory when the monks revive me. Just how I died. I've edited the book acordingly to suit the occasion. But, still, I feel silly not knowing such a fact. Tis' not my fault though. All beings make...\n\nmistakes. To some degree they do.\n\nDay 4,§0\n§010th of the Deep Cold,§0\n§0 It would apear Elisa has attempted to cut something, or kill someone. Ishould keep an eye out for her. She may be the thief afterall. Or maybe even Thomas' killer.\n\nDay 5,§0\n§06th The Deep Cold,§0\n§0  It appears the man I had suspisions about is a killer, perhaps even of Yasmin, whom I've not seen in months. This Maia person was just talking outside my house in an alleyway. I may need more info.\n\nDay 6,§0\n§012th of Grand Harvest 1500§0\n§0  Dying is terrible, I died twice today. I lost a lot of mina and a lot of items. I'm tired of remaking that cloak... The worst part is, I don't remember doing anything to deserve dying. Ugh...", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Burk, Galendar, Agnar\nFimlin, Noobman, Hiphop\nKillerkoala,Wolfie, Strongodin\n\nBobby Grouchy me\n\nBellamy Krumples, Dagor\n\nFaunher, Sam, drake\n\nQUO, Catarh, Turret\n\nForeverGinger, Casanova. AIhumanAdambarnett", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Got an axe for you to repair.§0\n§0Ragde Greenwood§0\n§0(dkink14)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "List Of Members in the§0\n§0Falken Order§0\n§0\n§0Sergeant Elisa§0\n§0Recruit John Roger§0\n§0Recruit Thomas Columbria§0\n§0Recruit Galahad§0\n§0Recruit Luciano§0\n§0Recruit\n\nMiss Caitlyn the Maid§0\n§0requesting one bucket, please. *the writing is in beautiful Calligraphy*§0\n§0(_Caity_Cat_)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day 1: Current Events§0\n§0\n§0Dear... Diary?§0\n§0I've recently come to§0\n§0fancy a man with the §0\n§0name Dystov. A human man of a noble house.§0\n§0I've come to also find§0\n§0that his sister, is a §0\n§0decieving litle whore.§0\n§0I'll get back to you§0\n§0with more details on§0\n§0that. ~Alarica\n\n[!] The following script is in slightly messy, if precise handwriting,§0\n§0\n§0\"Beware of decieving little whore'§0s....human§0 cunt.\"§0\n\nDay 2: War§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary.§0\n§0I was invited to help the humans today. turns out a group of mercenaries was §0\n§0planning to attack the§0\n§0capital. I got my sword.. a little dirty..§0\n§0After that, me and Ivo§0\n§0spent the day mining§0\n§0~Alarica\n\nDay 3: Wandering Tinker§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary.§0\n§0Today I spent all day§0\n§0mining. But it was worth it. I managed to get a large stocks in the shop of iron. Not to mention its selling like§0\n§0crazy. I'm thinking of moving the shop to the§0\n§0main road. ~Alarica\n\nDay 4: New Roommate§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0Today a new roommate moved in with us! His name is Briar, he's a quite scrawny high elf. And he has a nest in his room... but back to the point! He's really nice! And I really like him!§0\n§0~Alarica\n\nDay 5: New Lover?§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I've recently come to fancy a man by the name of John Dystov.§0\n§0I've known him for a while. But my feelings have only awoken now. He told me we can't be a public couple since he's a human noble. But that works for me\n\ncurrently. But I'm slightly worried he may have to court, and bed other women. I'll keep you up to date on this one. Anyways I do feel some what hurt. I mean the laws that keep us apart, is what hurts me. Stupid laws that restrict love.§0\n§0~Alarica\n\nDay 6: The Offer§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary §0\n§0Today I recived a offer to become a Dread knight. I accepted but later changed my mind, but my friend Athen has chosen to accept, as he dosent have much left to live for.§0\n§0~Alarica\n\nDay 7: Snagga?§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0Today I found I had to save Ivo from Urks. I managed, to get a nice sword, and some other stuff. And I saved Ivo.. So all good. And John took my out on a date§0\n§0today! He took my to a nearby hotspring.§0\n§0~Alarica\n\nDay 8: Betrayed§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I found out today, that John Dystov, slit my past lovers, throat. §0\n§0Artemis, I can't believe he did it! I'm going back to Nicolas. I never stopped loving him, I was just alone, and scared§0\n§0~Alarica\n\nDay 9: Broken§0\n§0\n§0[!]The page seems to be ripped out. Replaced with a bunch of drawings of Nicolas, and Alarica together.§0\n§0A few visable wet spots on the small paper, they look as someone's been crying on the paper.", ""),
