        StaticBook("Thrm. Of Wisdom", "§bFarley III Stafyr", "Theorem of Wisdom\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\n\nWhat is wisdom?\n\nWisdom is not easy to define, likely similar to eternity. Every person has its own views of wisdom. To elaborate this further, a row of examples.\n\nIs knowledge wisdom? \nPerhaps.\n\nIs knowing the right thing to do wisdom? \nPerhaps.\n\nIs doing something good wisdom?\n Perhaps.\n\nIs learning wisdom? \nPerhaps.\n\nAs aforementioned you cannot simply define wisdom. Wisdom is multitude, colorful, differently shaped. Wisdom can and does exist in many of us.\n\nTo different degrees, in different shapes.  A forester can have the wisdom of knowing how to treat his plants and trees properly, when to grow what to reach the best result. As can the farmer. A sorcerer or  wizard can know a lot about the divine art of\n\nmagic and has through this his very own wisdom.\n\nStill, one would say, that in these examples wisdom turns out to be rather knowledge, which is only partially right, if it’s right at all.\n\nWisdom requires more than simply having knowledge. Wisdom requires understanding the spirit, the being, the living and many things more. The inner peace and silence may bring wisdom.  On the other side, a warrior may achieve a new level of\n\ncombat by finding his inner stability in combat. To be calm in the face of the storm and evil.\n\nAs we now scratch the evil, the darkness, I wish to bring in a small part of my very own opinion. Wisdom doesn't exist in\n\npeople who are simply evil and work for their very own profit. Wisdom requires selflessness as well.\n\nYou may now think I am taking the side of the good here, solely.  It is right. I do align myself to the good and the light, but must say , that I may be\n\nbe completely wrong with my statement about wisdom and the evilness here. Perhaps the other side may have their own kind of wisdom, being evil as it is.\n\nIs it wisdom to write a book about wisdom? No.\n\nIs it wisdom to explain what wisdom can be? Perhaps.\n\nWhy perhaps? Because wisdom is wisdom. Colorful and different. Not definable. That is wisdom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "- The Contract of Silence -§0\n§0\n§01. The signer of this contract must never speak of,§0\n§0- Lies told within an elven week of signing this contract §0\n§0- All lies told to Daniel§0\n§0- Situation previously described by Sam\n\n___________§0\n§0\n§0*A circle is here*§0\n§0\n§0\n§0 - Razh'vik nahz tur vah. Kur'ill of eric kej lezp -§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Marcy Zuberzuri§0\n§0*signed in well cursive*§0\n§0*thumbprint*", ""),
